<node id="Scale-Unit Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Scale-Unit Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale-unit architecture is a design pattern that optimizes end-to-end scalability through compartmentalization, allowing logical units to be scaled independently.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is a design pattern where regional resources are deployed as part of a deployment stamp corresponding to a scale unit.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is a key practice for achieving zero-downtime deployment in mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale-unit architecture is used in application design for building highly reliable applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980036</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Workload">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mission-critical workload is a type of application workload that requires high resilience, availability, and careful architectural design.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is an application design pattern requiring high reliability, availability, and fault tolerance, often using multi-region deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload requires rigorous testing and the highest levels of reliability, capacity, and security.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is an application that must maintain high reliability and availability, requiring rigorous deployment and testing processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is an application design approach requiring high availability, redundancy, and globally distributed active-active architecture on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is a collection of application resources that must be highly reliable, always available, resilient to failures, and operational on the platform.&lt;SEP&gt;A mission-critical workload is an application design approach requiring high availability, redundancy, and globally distributed active-active architecture on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Well-Architected Framework is a set of guiding tenets and design pillars developed by Microsoft for improving the quality of workloads on the Azure platform. Its five core pillars are Reliability, Security, Cost Optimization, Operational Excellence, and Performance Efficiency. The framework is structured in a layered approach encompassing pillars, workload guidance, service guides, and design guides, providing fundamental guidance including design principles, recommendation guides, checklists, tradeoff analysis, and maturity models. It addresses nonfunctional requirements such as operability, cost, security, and efficiency, serving as a foundation for architectural excellence in cloud workload design.

Under Reliability, the framework features checklist recommendations such as RE:09 for disaster recovery planning. Under Security, it provides recommendations including SE:01 for establishing security baselines. Under Operational Excellence, it offers guidance covering incident management, Infrastructure as Code (IaC) best practices, and safe deployment practices. It also includes detailed Performance Efficiency guidelines and a dedicated Cost Optimization checklist for optimizing cloud workload costs. Beyond these five pillars, the framework is extended by sustainability design principles, with the Cost Optimization pillar containing guidance relevant to sustainability and a dedicated series on sustainable workloads.

The framework covers workload monitoring, optimizing workload design using flows, evaluating return on investment, trade-off analysis, and review assessments. It offers a mission-critical workload series focused on designing mission-critical applications on Azure. It serves as the benchmark against which the SaaS workload assessment checks alignment, and its pillars inform application delivery guidelines and cloud workload readiness assessments.

The Azure Well-Architected Framework also provides specific guidance for multiple workload types, including Azure Virtual Desktop workloads (with networking guidelines, storage design considerations, and best practices), Azure VMware Solution customizations and cloud readiness, SAP workloads, and HPC (high-performance computing) workload design recommendations. Overall, it serves as comprehensive architectural documentation providing actionable principles, checklists, and best practices for building reliable, secure, cost-effective, efficient, and sustainable cloud workload architectures on the Azure platform.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Well-Architected Framework (WAF) provides design principles and pillars that guide architectural decisions for HPC workloads.</data>
