<node id="Deployment Stamp">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamp</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment Stamp is an architecture pattern used as a regional deployment unit for provisioning, scaling, and managing mission-critical workloads. It covers related infrastructure and application components together, functioning as a scale unit within a region. The pattern enables scaling complex workloads by treating the entire solution as a single unit rather than scaling individual components independently.

Each deployment stamp is typically placed in a dedicated subscription, ensuring that subscription limits apply only within a single stamp. A stamp can be constrained to a single availability zone, with multiple stamps deployed across zones to provide redundancy. In some implementations, deployment stamps are treated as ephemeral, short-lived units whose lifecycle is tied to a single release, with both infrastructure and application deployed together.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65b26c693a23d19a5f6c2c2910aca49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e2c1079086f316dcae858bed1190c3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Unit">
  <data key="d0">Scale Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scale unit is a logical unit or function that can be scaled independently, composed of code components, hosting platforms, and deployment stamps.&lt;SEP&gt;A scale unit is a group of resources that scale proportionately together, forming the basis of scaling and partitioning strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;A scale unit is a logical group of resources that scale together to handle increased load while being monitored independently, automatically deployed as repeatable blocks based on defined thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;A scale unit is a group of resources that scale proportionately together and can be scaled independently or together.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fb475b8b7efe4018b64a1ed512f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e912a1ac7fa5ab0139e0fac99a203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Global Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global distribution is a strategy for deploying applications in an active/active model across multiple regions to withstand regional and zone failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Global distribution is a design pattern for distributing traffic and resources across multiple Azure regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Global distribution is a feature of Azure Cosmos DB that enables deploying database instances in multiple regions closest to end users to reduce read latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a99a5a991c44794d4415bc58af98647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Landing Zone">
  <data key="d0">Azure Landing Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Landing Zone is a foundational deployment framework and conceptual architecture in Microsoft Azure that depicts the overall cloud footprint for an organization with multiple subscriptions. It provides a subscription-based environment dedicated to applications, establishing clear management boundaries and supporting integration with broader organizational network topology.

Azure Landing Zone offers connectivity to on-premises data centers and networks through technologies such as ExpressRoute or virtual networks. It includes deployment configurations such as Online and Corp. Connected variants, catering to different network connectivity scenarios. The framework incorporates security capabilities including Azure Firewall or equivalent network virtual appliance (NVA) resources, providing centralized threat mitigation.

The framework includes common design areas, reference architecture, reference implementation, and processes to tailor deployments to specific design requirements. Centralized baseline policy assignments are applied at both management group and subscription levels, and centralized storage of operational data enables data forking to both centralized tooling and application-dedicated Log Analytics workspaces.

The Azure Landing Zone model describes a partnership where workload teams rely on platform teams for shared infrastructure and services, reflecting its role as a collaborative organizational deployment pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e9fe7698a1a93cbb9d3b82e57dbe53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198</data>
