<node id="Autoscaling">
  <data key="d0">Autoscaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscaling is a best practice method for automatically adjusting computing resources in response to changing demand and load levels. It works by adding or removing resources when predefined conditions, rules, or thresholds are met, encompassing both vertical scaling (up/down) and horizontal scaling (out/in). These thresholds are configured based on service-internal and application-set parameters, involving policies, cooldown periods, and configurable maximum and minimum limits.

Autoscaling balances workload supply against demand by dynamically allocating and deallocating resources, optimizing both resource allocation and cost efficiency for flows with variable demand. It is generally preferred over manual scaling for handling unexpected load and serves to protect workloads against unanticipated bursts in activity.

Autoscaling is widely available across Azure services and platforms. In PaaS offerings, it is commonly a built-in feature. In Application Gateway v2, it scales based on application traffic requirements. In Azure Container Apps, it dynamically manages loads based on HTTP requests, TCP connections, or custom metrics, including the ability to scale to zero. For Azure Functions, it automatically adjusts capacity based on demand. In Azure Databricks, it operates as a policy-driven mechanism that adds or removes nodes based on workload demands. For compute clusters, it can scale resources down to zero nodes when idle. It is also used in model deployment environments, adjusting the number of instances of a deployed model to match demand.

Despite its benefits, autoscaling has limitations. It may not handle sudden bursts well due to provisioning time required for new resources. It can also be misconfigured, potentially leading to excess cost or uncontrolled growth. Designing precise scale-out and scale-in strategies with appropriate limits is essential to its effective operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling adds or reduces cluster nodes on demand for secondary node types to optimize resource usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling automatically adjusts application resources based on demand factors like CPU utilization and incoming requests.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling automatically increases and decreases resources based on application load to optimize performance and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65b26c693a23d19a5f6c2c2910aca49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0d4e3f080b4962999c8f4d2734bc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c387aff770332292e0a1e78af18b8fbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b047e8b449398992f0dfab15265a69c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61803d2562ce9d74f9843d45925671b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37330ee339c66455fbad4f1319377e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85416f9f4269be56820f2abc15bfb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90796296cec0f129315921be106646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937b1809a20f2b2148f344a58b016317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8fc58eb81af85bd1aa7f2b1f5ef9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca37c53f740f2b0fa041e3df2d737be8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d0c804921f6d35d43cf53a8ca5e01fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-functions.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
