<node id="AKS">
  <data key="d0">AKS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a managed Kubernetes platform on Azure that provides container orchestration capabilities for deploying, managing, and scaling containerized applications and workloads. It supports cluster and node upgrades, networking, monitoring, governance, security, and cost optimization, with extensive policy and architecture support and best practices for cluster and workload management.

AKS has a hard requirement for an underlying virtual network and requires network integration configuration. It supports both Azure CNI and Kubenet networking plugins and can be optimized with accelerated networking for query-intensive workloads. The service has a scale limit of 1,000 nodes per cluster and supports automatic scaling for consumer workloads. It is monitored for CPU utilization and deployment statuses.

AKS serves as a primary application platform and compute environment, using container images from container registries and allowing health endpoint configuration for pods. It supports deploying containerized applications to improve parallel processing. Clusters can be bootstrapped using GitOps and Flux v2 for configuration management. AKS also integrates with Application Gateway for Containers, enabling clusters to share ingress and supporting overlay pod networking.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) on Azure Local enables containerized applications to scale across multiple datacenter or edge locations, included in Azure Local pricing.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a container orchestration service with native integration in Azure Local.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) clusters are production workloads that benefit from all-flash storage solutions on Azure Local.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a deployment environment that supports cluster autoscaler for scaling to meet demand.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a deployment environment that uses a cluster autoscaler to scale to meet demand for model deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a self-hosting option for deploying models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5321cfe4fbc08d735ac5eac02e84e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b24002e6c6a1f793f274780f10d2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f08277df10a908d985f4ac74cf88b922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c957da7c0dc63ec3f07d3774c278b886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8103c464163f3ff725a5c23642a7e869&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7ebf4632700c0d791afc29f31a4749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7918938c3b3fb0cddcc9e93b114d4a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2789d17a06aaa84a6ce5fba59172ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc3e5ddb4441b86b0ef64d617182432b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245</data>
