<node id="Active/Active Model">
  <data key="d0">Active/Active Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An active/active deployment strategy that maximizes availability and provides a higher composite SLA by distributing load among all regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active model is a deployment strategy where load is distributed among all regions simultaneously to maximize resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active deployment model runs multiple regions simultaneously and is strongly recommended for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
