<node id="Azure Cosmos DB">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB is a globally distributed, fully managed NoSQL and document database service on the Microsoft Azure platform. As a PaaS offering, it abstracts infrastructure complexity and automatically distributes workloads across instances, zones, and regions. It supports multiple database types including NoSQL, relational, vector, and table databases, with flexible schema supporting both transactional and analytical workloads. It is commonly used as a managed nonrelational data store for SaaS solutions, agent state persistence, and batch inference scenarios requiring fast, globally distributed access.

Azure Cosmos DB provides multi-region read and write capabilities with transparent replication, conflict resolution options, and service-managed failover. It does not require automated failover configuration when multi-write deployment is enabled, offers higher SLAs for multiregion deployments, and is particularly recommended for applications spanning more than four regions. It includes Availability Zone redundancy and native, non-configurable global retry capabilities.

The service offers tunable consistency levels, multiple API support, and configurable authentication methods including role-based access control (RBAC), private endpoints, and virtual network endpoints. Key data management features include automatic partition rebalancing, partitioning and sharding capabilities, customizable indexing policies (including composite indexes, index aliasing, and a default policy), support for concurrency, transactional batch operations, bulk operations, and built-in Time to Live (TTL) for managing data growth and document lifecycle management.

Azure Cosmos DB natively supports vector data types and vector search capabilities. It provides a change feed capability and an analytical column store that enables large-scale analytics without impacting transactional performance. It integrates with Azure Synapse for big data analytics and is commonly used to store "hot" data actively used by applications, such as product catalogs and e-commerce orders.

Automatic backups are taken at regular intervals without affecting performance, with multiple backup modes including periodic and continuous backup with point-in-time restore. Throughput can be scaled using request units (RUs) with provisioned throughput, autoscale throughput, and serverless models, returning a 429 status code when capacity is exceeded. Server-side latency is tracked as a key monitoring metric with dedicated monitoring insights. The service is commonly used as a downstream dependency within regional deployment stamps and is referenced in mission-critical data platform guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45aecf85df05c73b4035e26a2cb04459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0be076c15399d472d831cac4c767ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefafe3b76f15cde350013dbb7911e9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af17a604206f8056ed34d52736aca636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ec