</node>
<node id="Microservices Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Microservices Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture style consistent with mission-critical requirements that facilitates high availability by preventing cascading failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices architecture is a technique for refactoring workload architecture to optimize resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices architecture separates components into independently deployable services for scalability and maintainability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Zones">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability Zones are physically separate datacenter locations within an Azure region, each equipped with independent power, cooling, and networking infrastructure. They follow a 3+1 datacenter model and are designed to provide datacenter-level fault tolerance, high availability, and fault isolation, with less than 2 milliseconds latency between them.

Availability Zones maximize resilience by distributing workloads across these physically separated datacenters within a region. This includes VMs, AKS agent nodes, data replicas, Azure Firewall instances, Application Gateway instances, log data replicas, and message data and metadata. Zone redundancy ensures resiliency to zone failures through automatic failover, routing traffic to other zones if one fails. Services including Azure Cosmos DB, Service Fabric clusters, and other regional deployments benefit from this distribution. When used with Azure Standard Load Balancer, Availability Zones enable a 99.99% SLA, and deploying Azure Firewall across multiple zones similarly provides higher SLA and resiliency.

Availability Zones are recommended for critical workloads to improve reliability and are considered fundamental infrastructure isolation units within Azure regions. They enable organizations to distribute solution components—including session hosts—for maximum availability, redundancy, and resilience, while reducing the risk of localized datacenter outages without significantly increasing cost or complexity. However, Availability Zones are limited to specific regions, and spreading resources across zones can affect performance due to inter-zone latency, which may be particularly disruptive for low-latency on-premises applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability zones are distinct locations within an Azure region used for redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability zones are separate datacenter locations used to distribute applications for fault tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zones provide an opportunity to create highly available ASCS architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability Zones are the recommended option for deploying SAP application servers for resiliency on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84a8087984070a29596b50c6ea41e0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0970265d9d614fdbdc9d79d3bcda0f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11229197c05f5be9b778a1918888ee7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a75f6abfb52e7f12669ccabfaf886c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757386a260f7f7980e2074a43870b9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8672b1e490ddaf66d06e5814d081ec72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af193ca86913bf526ac2830012c0e345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c24295afcc6630eeee9c761977e6d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b3b849ac5683c426e666e8f3f3f48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437b53743af22a4aaa11b22db9356761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edb1f343516427f2