  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Tracing">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Tracing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed Tracing is a diagnostic and observability technique used to track, monitor, and correlate requests as they flow through distributed systems and across service boundaries. It works by assigning unique activity IDs or correlation IDs to requests, enabling the linking of related events across multiple components and services. By capturing and correlating telemetry from metrics, logs, and traces across different application components or tiers, it builds end-to-end transaction flows that provide comprehensive insights into system behavior.

Distributed Tracing enables easier analysis of application performance data, helping identify performance bottlenecks, latency issues, and errors through root cause analysis. It can be applied at the transaction level to analyze bottlenecks across event delivery pipelines and other critical system flows. It also serves as a standard for propagating correlation across services to enable end-to-end traceability.

Tools such as Application Insights facilitate Distributed Tracing by providing comprehensive error messages with correlation IDs for end-to-end tracing across services, offering a unified view of system behavior. The complexity of distributed tracing increases when additional reliability components are introduced into an architecture, as more services and layers add to the volume of trace data that must be captured and correlated. Despite this complexity, it remains essential for maintaining observability in modern distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39895fc4a2ce3e45eeca7bf801519ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10f25ecc531e8935b205674b69f81d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77532f9499e43bf59e3245f6d41d3561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4aed87d4e81857a842b49249489eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7404990d0db645a738f8e03698df0941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd636d5b13ec5dfd60e1f6764089382c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-520b008ac150d01d52152b172f0a59b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Insights">
  <data key="d0">Application Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Insights is an Application Performance Monitoring (APM) tool and a feature/extension of Azure Monitor. It is an extensible service for monitoring live applications, collecting application telemetry data including logs, metrics, traces, request rates, response times, exception details, and usage and performance data. It provides deep insights into application performance, availability, reliability, and application-related issues throughout development, testing, and production.

Application Insights automatically detects performance anomalies through its smart detection feature, which can analyze memory consumption and identify memory leaks. It helps identify and optimize hot paths in code by analyzing execution times and resource usage, and can monitor application usage to identify underutilized features. It provides configurable sampling percentages to balance visibility and performance.

Application Insights provides end-to-end tracing, dependency mapping, and user behavior analytics. It supports OpenTelemetry-based distributed tracing data collection and provides correlation IDs for error tracking, enabling users to query, correlate, and visualize application traces. Its SDK collects telemetry from producer and consumer applications, enabling end-to-end transaction tracing across them, including tracing from publishers through Service Bus to consumers. It supports custom metrics tracking for consumer-specific processing times and end-to-end latency. It also provides basic availability tests and Real User Monitoring (RUM) data capture for websites, and hosts the User Flow tool for analyzing user behavior.

Key features include application map, failure and performance views, profiling, smart detection, sampling capabilities, telemetry ingestion, instrumentation, alerting, and dashboards. Application Insights is integrated with API Management as an observability tool and is used for centralized monitoring of function performance, key metrics, and detailed insights into function operations. It can also be enabled to monitor online endpoints and deployments in machine learning scenarios.

Application Insights can be deployed in a workspace-based model underpinned by Log Analytics, requiring a Log Analytics workspace to function, and is billed through that workspace. As an Azure Monitor resource, it must be deployed and configured to incorporate data collection and querying capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights is a monitoring service used alongside Azure Monitor for workload observability.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights provides a detailed view of the time that workload requests spend in the network.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights is a tool for monitoring performance in Azure Virtual Desktop environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights is a tool used for performance monitoring in Azure Virtual Desktop.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights is a monitoring tool that can be used to build application dashboards.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Insights is a tool for tracking dependencies such as databases, API calls, and external services.</data>
