<node id="Azure ExpressRoute">
  <data key="d0">Azure ExpressRoute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure ExpressRoute is a network connectivity service that provides private connectivity between on-premises networks and Microsoft Azure through dedicated circuits. It serves as a cloud connectivity solution and a typical external dependency for workloads, enabling clients outside Azure to access resources such as file shares through private networks as an alternative to public internet connections (e.g., opening TCP port 445).

Azure ExpressRoute includes components such as circuits, gateways, and Direct options. Microsoft provides guidance on resiliency and recoverability distinctions for the service, helping organizations design reliable hybrid connectivity architectures. It is commonly used to connect to on-premises services and access cloud workloads securely over private network paths.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute is a service for enterprise network flows providing dedicated connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute extends on-premises networks into Azure cloud over a private connection.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute provides private network connectivity for Remote Desktop client users to connect to virtual networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5abe8178a23baa37e13d7019242d00c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cffe100ebb087468498365a5360ea32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b3b849ac5683c426e666e8f3f3f48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161fa262de0d263c9842f3ec1f7a7795&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
