<node id="Loosely Coupled Event-Driven Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Loosely Coupled Event-Driven Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture where components operate independently via well-defined interfaces and asynchronous message processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outbox Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Outbox Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern used to guarantee consistency so that every message is processed correctly in distributed services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transactional Session">
  <data key="d0">Transactional Session</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern used alongside the Outbox pattern to guarantee message processing consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Model">
  <data key="d0">Health Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A Health Model is a layered, iterative framework used to define, quantify, and aggregate the health of individual application components and the overall workload. It serves as a graphical representation of logical entities and their relationships, where each node has a health state definition that rationalizes monitoring data. The model represents application health using traffic light states—Healthy, Degraded, and Unavailable (or Unhealthy)—by defining these states for each component, critical flow, and workload to enable fast failure detection and recovery.

The Health Model correlates various monitoring data—including indicators, KPIs, and metrics reflecting business and operational objectives—to accurately reflect the runtime state of entities or an entire workload. It uses a distinct data schema optimized for observability, leveraging key resource-level metrics and scoring functions to quantify application health in the context of availability and performance requirements. This provides operators with in-depth visibility into system health, dependencies, and business impact as part of observability and reliability strategies.

The Health Model supports proactive monitoring by spotting early warning signs and triggering appropriate recovery processes based on defined disaster thresholds. It monitors component health through health endpoints, takes corrective action for non-transient failures, and alerts responsible parties. It can be integrated with alerts and CI/CD pipelines for calculating SLO attainment, enabling teams to detect and respond to issues and measure operational efficiency. The Health Model turns operational knowledge into actionable insights and is typically developed at Level 3 maturity to represent the overall health status of a workload, also supporting vendor support scenarios through its defined thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a graphical representation of logical entities and their relationships for a given scope, where each node has a health state definition to rationalize monitoring data.&lt;SEP&gt;A model that provides operators visibility into system health, dependencies, and business impact, using a distinct data schema optimized for observability.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a comprehensive framework that correlates various monitoring data to accurately reflect the runtime state of entities or an entire workload.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a framework for quantifying and visualizing the operational health states of workloads, applications, and infrastructure components.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model labels components as Healthy, Degraded, or Unhealthy according to service level objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;The Service Fabric health model is used to continuously monitor the health of a solution, including cluster health policies and application health policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4aefadf5c38a99059d5cac5297d2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74ac1201f940bb7bb5693682e4dbc30b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb4be3d9c01e97b5b077710134d8de16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61803d2562ce9d74f9843d45925671b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44db748d8a4a0feea6626c78c05321a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c34815c939645bbbdf7eeec0352ec98f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/monitoring-alerting-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
