</node>
<node id="Health Check">
  <data key="d0">Health Check</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Check identifies non-responsive workers by assessing critical downstream dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Health check is a built-in App Service feature that periodically pings a web application path to determine application health and exclude unhealthy instances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000125</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TCP Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">TCP Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TCP port exhaustion occurs when outbound connections from a given App Service worker exceed capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;TCP port exhaustion occurs when outbound connections from a worker exceed capacity, depending on worker size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
