<node id="Geo-Replication">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-replication is a feature of Azure Container Registry that replicates registries to multiple regions, providing resiliency against regional outages and reducing latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication enables real-time asynchronous replication of events and metadata across multiple regions for Dedicated tier namespaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication replicates events and metadata across multiple regions in real time for Dedicated tier namespaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication replicates both metadata and message data across regions with synchronous and asynchronous modes, supporting planned and forced promotion scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication replicates both metadata and message data across regions with automatic failover capabilities, offering synchronous and asynchronous replication modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-replication provides automated regional failover with data replication for Service Bus namespaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d10ef40f70919a984cf031275099f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49c55356fee42f19cd603d7edc0b8b6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscale">
  <data key="d0">Autoscale</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscale is a feature in Azure that automatically adjusts compute capacity and resources based on demand and predefined configurations. It ensures adequate resources are available by scaling out when any rule is met and scaling in when all rules are met, helping prevent overprovisioning and protecting against throttling errors.

Autoscale automatically adjusts throughput between a maximum value and 10% of that maximum based on application load. It can be configured through runbook automation to ensure elasticity in response to changing traffic patterns, such as for Azure Database for MySQL/PostgreSQL.

While Autoscale can scale down aggressively to reduce costs, this behavior may cause issues with sudden demand spikes or flapping, where resources oscillate between scaling up and down rapidly.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale automatically adjusts provisioned throughput to match actual workload needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale is a platform feature that helps optimize resource use by automatically adjusting capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ec3bae0c0f185d5df0733c73840934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fb475b8b7efe4018b64a1ed512f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84a8087984070a29596b50c6ea41e0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a99a5a991c44794d4415bc58af98647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
