<node id="Geo-Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-Redundant Storage (GRS) is an Azure Storage redundancy feature that automatically replicates data to a secondary paired region, ensuring data durability and protection against regional outages. It is the default storage option for periodic backups in Azure, with data replicated to a paired region.

GRS provides higher resilience than locally redundant storage, though at a greater cost, by synchronizing data across geographically separated regions. It is used in scenarios such as dead letter destinations in Azure Event Grid to protect undelivered events from regional failures. In Azure Files, GRS is supported only by standard SMB accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;GRS is an Azure Storage redundancy option that replicates data to other regions for protection against regional failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-redundant storage (GRS) is an Azure Storage replication option for disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;GRS replicates critical datasets and final results to survive regional failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778fbb08fc2452f88b89df8ede476434</data>
