</node>
<node id="Azure Policy">
  <data key="d0">Azure Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Policy is a governance and compliance service within the Azure Resource Manager control plane. It provides a comprehensive framework for enforcing and auditing security, reliability, and organizational standards across Azure platform services at scale. It supplements Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) by restricting actions that authorized users can perform, enforcing security and reliability configurations by remediating or prohibiting deviations at configuration time. An aggregated compliance dashboard and automatic remediation capabilities enable centralized visibility and enforcement.

Azure Policy drives compliance through enforced conventions, automated management activities, and compliance reporting, offering both custom options and built-in initiatives. It serves as an automated security governance tool that streamlines resource compliance with security baselines, protecting against configuration drift. It can enforce resource configurations such as enabling service firewalls, ensuring consistent diagnostic settings, controlling subnet traffic lacking network security groups, ensuring identity components like Key Vault use RBAC, disabling Azure Cosmos DB key-based metadata write access, and routing operational data to the correct Log Analytics workspace. It also enforces security controls like private endpoint usage, SSL enforcement, encryption, and resource locks across server instances while preventing costly database configurations. Additionally, Azure Policy provides drift detection and automatic remediation for gateway SKU compliance, diagnostic settings, and network security rules.

Azure Policy provides centralized governance safeguards for AKS clusters, including pod security, resource requests and limits, configuration baselines, and supports mission-critical workloads. Beyond security, it allows limiting resource types, SKUs, compute tiers, and instances through policy rules that enforce deployment restrictions, restrict deployment regions, enforce tagging policies, required tags, allowed tiers, and zone-redundancy requirements for production instances. It is also used to require approvals for high-cost changes, mandate reviews before adding capacity, and enforce mandatory tags on resource creation for cost allocation purposes.

Azure Policy provides extensive built-in policy definitions across numerous Azure services, including App Service, Application Insights, API Management, Application Gateway, Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL, Container Apps, storage accounts, Azure Database for MySQL, Azure Databricks, Azure Disk Storage, Azure Files, Azure Firewall, Azure Front Door, Azure Functions, Event Grid, Event Hubs, ExpressRoute, Load Balancer, Log Analytics, Azure Machine Learning, Service Bus, Service Fabric, SQL Database, SQL Managed Instance, Traffic Manager, Virtual WAN, Virtual Machines, Virtual Networks, and Azure Virtual Desktop. For SQL Database, built-in policies audit authentication, zone redundancy, backups, TLS, and auditing. For Azure Databricks, policies cover network security, encryption, and compliance auditing. For Event Hubs, it enforces throughput unit limits, restricts service tiers, and defines retention period policies. For Azure Machine Learning, policies audit network access, encryption, and authentication. For Service Bus, it enforces cost management by restricting tiers, regions, and expensive features. For Virtual Machines, it provides built-in definitions affecting compute layer security and dependencies. For Azure Virtual Desktop, it promotes consistency across VM configurations, insights, tagging, can ensure monitoring agents are installed on VMs, configure diagnostics settings, and audit session host operating systems for enterprise-scale compliance.

Azure Policy is used to implement policy-driven governance to help ensure security and compliance within enterprise technical estates. It applies security controls defined by the Microsoft cloud security benchmark and automates responses to Defender for Cloud recommendations. It works alongside Azure Arc to manage security configuration and compliance auditing for Azure Local, and is used for Azure Arc-enabled servers to audit and enforce security controls on guest VMs. It also manages the guest configuration feature used by Azure Automation State Configuration and ensures resource deployments adhere to organizational best practices. Policy artifacts should be regularly backed up with versioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Policy is a tool for defining and enforcing policies to keep Azure virtual data centers continuously optimized for cost and sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Policy is a service used to enforce VM governance for SAP workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Policy enforces security baselines and compliance reporting across HPC clusters to reduce misconfigurations and configuration drift.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7c4879ffc39192c7f9e5f766b4cfd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b82e5bd8bced74ea376399d3355126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e0fe247c84a41199e470c86f0e983f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b24002e6c6a1f793f274780f10d2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c93d9704f35759a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02ed72abe4ca2d3a3487f2b3c4c1bb89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0410a251086c78865c685a5005e7ecae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e8e5e219d847f6df3d58059668695a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95454c21cf94702a963cb14772e7fc53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df0cc69c8383501073ee148f940f5d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d89d8bc1094d5427b9923c0759b965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b1775a768fc04ca64ed9caa4af5d16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195da