<node id="Azure Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor is a comprehensive, full-stack monitoring service provided by Microsoft Azure, enabled by default for all Azure subscriptions. It serves as a unified data platform for collecting, analyzing, and acting on operational data across cloud and on-premises environments, supporting three types of observability data: logs, metrics, and distributed traces. It automatically collects platform metrics, activity logs, diagnostics logs, and diagnostic data from various Azure resources, aggregating data from every layer and component of workloads across multiple Azure and non-Azure subscriptions and tenants. Pricing is based on data ingestion and retention, with Application Insights charges based on volume ingested and retention duration.

Azure Monitor is the overarching monitoring platform that includes Application Insights, alerts, workbooks, log queries, Log Analytics workspaces, and agents with data collection rules. It enables collection and analysis of telemetry data supporting capacity planning, demand forecasting, performance measurement, and cost optimization. It collects metrics, logs, and diagnostics from numerous services including AKS, Azure Cosmos DB, Azure Cache for Redis, Azure Functions, Event Grid, Event Hubs, ExpressRoute, storage, API Management, Kubernetes clusters, Azure NetApp Files, VM instances, Azure Virtual Desktop, and Azure VMware Solution, providing near real-time operational insights. It is recommended for offloading observability concerns from workloads and provides a service map feature to automatically discover and visualize application and infrastructure components.

Azure Monitor integrates with Azure Databricks for viewing logs, collecting telemetry, enabling KQL queries, and supporting automated alerting, and provides custom dashboards and end-to-end transaction tracing through Application Insights integration. It also offers insight tools such as VM insights and network insights, workbooks for performance dashboards, integration with Azure Dashboards, resource logs for security investigations, diagnostic settings to capture security events, and data transformation features.

Azure Monitor provides an extensive alerting framework through Action Groups, covering metrics such as HA status, replication lag, CPU, memory, storage, throttling events, connection failures, and capacity shortages or scaling failures. For Azure Service Bus, it enables alerting on availability, throughput, authentication failures, throttling, and message volume patterns. It supports autoscale features, self-healing mechanisms, machine learning integration, and daily caps on workspaces, and is integrated with Azure Local for health, log, and metric alerts.

For SQL Managed Instance, Azure Monitor serves as a platform telemetry service for observability of health and workload performance, provides alerting for critical reliability metrics, offers real-time log analysis for audit events, and provides workbooks to surface operation trends. For Virtual WAN, it collects hub router traffic volume metrics continuously and supports alerts for routing anomalies. It is widely used to continuously monitor performance, detect anomalies and failures, respond to events affecting reliability, and is also accessed by agent personas such as the Production Monitoring Agent for load testing and monitoring purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor is the underlying Azure infrastructure used by Azure Monitor for SAP solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor provides diagnostic logs and metrics for cluster health visibility and operational dashboards.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor provides monitoring capabilities for HPC deployments and cluster reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58687539bce004e3d6c298bc58bb0198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7595d0066e438d094afa55de7d2ba18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7c4879ffc39192c7f9e5f766b4cfd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df6e00fa9a90ca53e8d360c865875b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964d0aabb6a006eaf58781c2658f980a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a9cc1e862b6a71315c64180df14f2e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39895fc4a2ce3e45eeca7bf801519ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b502a6bff102f2e33753f38b3190d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56d3f8085e9faa95d82a0d2dfdacc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0d557186587fd7356bc48c45898548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997b67d2a5ddf57a24dd0380ce47e074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-617354e6d70206a2787d2a92e6998746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef6111a0cc4b828fa5b996fe5d89475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b32925fbb6ae4e81a734e77c9c7decb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c9