<node id="SNAT Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">SNAT Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SNAT port exhaustion is a common failure scenario in App Service involving outbound connections to public IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs when a large number of outbound requests depletes available source NAT ports, preventing new outbound connections.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion is a reliability event that can occur on an egress firewall when security tooling limitations are not accounted for.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs when a large number of outbound requests depletes available source NAT ports, preventing new outbound connections.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion is a reliability event that can occur on an egress firewall when security tooling limitations are not accounted for.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion is a potential issue with outbound traffic that can be mitigated using Azure NAT Gateway or Load Balancer.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs in multitenant applications when distinct network connections per tenant exhaust available source network address translation ports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f</data>
