<node id="Azure Kubernetes Service">
  <data key="d0">Azure Kubernetes Service</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a managed Kubernetes container orchestration service provided by Microsoft Azure that enables quick cluster provisioning with advanced networking, identity, and reliability features. It serves as a platform for deploying and managing containerized applications with high availability, scalability, and portability, commonly used in baseline mission-critical architectures for running microservices.

AKS supports a broad range of capabilities including network policies, node pools, multiple networking models, separate pod deployments on each node with updatable service definitions, and zone-redundant deployments across availability zones. As an Azure PaaS product, it offers multi-region best practices, backup capabilities, HTTP proxy support, custom certificate authority integration, and Azure CNI static block allocation. Pod CPU and memory limits can be defined to optimize performance, and it supports event-driven autoscaling via KEDA, horizontal pod automatic scaling, and cluster automatic scaling via Azure Monitor. AKS also supports resource density through namespaces and node pools, and provides configurable control plane and data plane logs.

AKS clusters host application services that use workload identities to authenticate to other components. The service requires regular Kubernetes version updates, providing a 90-day window to opt in before updates become automatic. It integrates with Container Apps for advanced networking and monitoring, and can be protected using Azure Firewall. AKS is also referenced as an example for blue-green deployment architecture.

Beyond general-purpose container orchestration, AKS serves as a model serving layer for hosting AI and machine learning inferencing workloads. It can be attached to Azure Machine Learning for self-hosting models and supports hosting deployed machine learning models with availability zone support. Additionally, AKS is a resource type that can be deployed on Azure Local, extending its reach to hybrid and edge environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) hosts custom processing logic and offers stronger reliability than Azure Logic Apps.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service is a cloud platform used for hosting inference servers with node pool isolation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service is a platform that can host inference servers and other workloads on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a hosting compute platform that can influence workflow orchestrator choice.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a general-purpose compute platform that can host web apps, AI workloads, and batch compute tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is an Azure service that should not be directly exposed to the internet without WAF protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0d4e3f080b4962999c8f4d2734bc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b502a6bff102f2e33753f38b3190d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72528a20eb854ac9dc78db25344d18e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0544ee58fb5345261d0d125500955a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7424eb960d7c722faf499211634269a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464884618643684fc043c8a50e0bf16f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b01c06cbc36f4fb17c08ab0e3baafd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079bbb48956c67b51ccb9053f7fbe162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757386a260f7f7980e2074a43870b9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1840b694f5e40fc921e2e4772b238961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03df2eaa58b6c9bb42baf709c977fdda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9a0e9b061e029f4a866b91345d9e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6c3c95f26c867cee192fcc4d9d6f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f</data>
