</node>
<node id="Cluster Autoscaler">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Autoscaler</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster autoscaler automatically adjusts the number of agent nodes in response to resource constraints in AKS.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster autoscaler automatically reduces or increases the number of agent nodes based on resource capacity demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster autoscaler automatically adjusts the number of agent nodes in response to workload demands.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c957da7c0dc63ec3f07d3774c278b886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7ebf4632700c0d791afc29f31a4749</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001866</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Pod Autoscaler">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Pod Autoscaler</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Horizontal pod autoscaler adjusts the number of pods in a deployment based on CPU utilization or other metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979407</data>
