  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proximity Placement Groups">
  <data key="d0">Proximity Placement Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Proximity placement groups minimize internode latency when colocation latency is a concern in AKS deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity Placement Groups enable submillisecond latency between services by co-locating resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity Placement Groups enable submillisecond latency between services by co-locating resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity placement groups minimize internode latency in AKS deployments when colocality requirements exist.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity placement groups ensure VMs are physically located close to each other to reduce latency and improve performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity placement groups reduce distance between SAP workloads by grouping different VM types under a single network spine, providing lower network latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Proximity Placement Groups place compute nodes within the same datacenter network segment to reduce inter-node latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea3b54c45d951e732cca09b525690b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b14a078d2121adef2ae56cc9aaead82</data>
