  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IaaS">
  <data key="d0">IaaS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) is a cloud computing model using virtual machines as the primary application hosting model.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as a service, a cloud model that may introduce extra costs for storage, server management, and configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) is a hosting model providing virtual machines with extensive control over networking and storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02ed72abe4ca2d3a3487f2b3c4c1bb89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6c3c95f26c867cee192fcc4d9d6f0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Machines is an Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) compute offering on the Azure platform for creating and running virtual machines in the cloud. It provides flexibility in SKUs, operating systems, configurations, and billing models, and serves as the primary IaaS hosting model for constrained migrations of on-premises applications.

Azure Virtual Machines use managed disks for storage and support encryption of virtual disk files to prevent unauthorized access. They can host application deployments and support automatic scaling. Azure Virtual Machines and scale sets have updated architecture best practices reflecting new Azure features and support Service Fabric nodes as the compute back end.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machines are VMs used as session hosts in Azure Virtual Desktop, with SKUs varying by region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c1dd7c66529e2ab2455ebd5bb312625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af193ca86913bf526ac2830012c0e345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets is an Azure compute service that supports deploying and managing multiple virtual machine instances directly, such as configuring a set number like five instances. The service provides automatic scaling capabilities, supported by Azure Monitor Autoscale, along with health monitoring and automatic repair of unhealthy instances. It can be configured for automatic failover as part of a self-healing infrastructure and supports zone-redundant deployments for enhanced availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets are used as back-end instances by Azure Firewall, with default deployment of two instances supporting 4,992 SNAT ports per flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets are the back-end instances used by Azure Firewall, supporting 2,496 SNAT ports per public IP address per instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets provide autoscale capabilities, automatic instance repairs, and distribute load across multiple VMs and availability zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0d4e3f080b4962999c8f4d2734bc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079bbb48956c67b51ccb9053f7fbe162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd12866b1c0a9d8fe76b6447e59f118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Workloads">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Workloads</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission-Critical Workloads are applications and systems that require the highest levels of reliability, availability, fault tolerance, and performance. They are significant in scale and complexity, and their architecture varies based on business requirements and acceptable downtime levels.

On Azure, mission-critical workloads are designed to maximize reliability, with baseline architectures recommending containerization and container orchestrators for application deployment. For the highest reliability, these workloads should leverage both multiple availability zones and multiple regions.

Mission-critical workloads prioritize real-time monitoring dashboards that site reliability engineers can quickly act on to maintain performance and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Mission-critical workloads are systems that should use both multiple availability zones and multiple regions for the highest reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Workloads requiring high reliability with design methodology focused on zero-downtime deployments and fast failure recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85dfff44e8e4c1e2d34f3f2fbc239ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999949</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud-Native Baseline Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Cloud-Native Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The North Star architecture pattern recommended for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Marketplace">
  <data key="d0">Azure Marketplace</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Marketplace is a platform for publishing, distributing, and acquiring a wide range of solutions and resources for use within the Azure ecosystem. It provides standard and trusted images for virtual machine and Azure Virtual Desktop deployments, including hardened images from CIS. Azure Marketplace offers partner firewall and web application firewall vendor products, as well as third-party queues and tools that can be integrated with Azure services to support asynchronous operations. It also serves as a platform for publishing and distributing SaaS solutions, providing support for billing, onboarding, offboarding, and customer access management, including management of billing for solutions deployed into customer environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Marketplace provides supported base images with the latest updates for use in golden image creation.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Marketplace hosts certified third-party backup solutions for SAP workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-340142470ca89eaa216bdbb33d95053a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a7fd7af178968ccbf8fd562e0e84a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d280cc7c07462216af45547cce48d2f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-661923999882010b2c5bc9a8ccb33fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da6ff7f8e8d62245d48fe850b4eb70f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb02bc2525ef384d46a37259cf6a9cf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/harden-resources.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-code-infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/resource-organization.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Functions">
  <data key="d0">Azure Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Functions is a serverless compute platform provided by Microsoft Azure that enables event-driven execution of application logic as distinct functions in response to events. It is designed for short-duration, event-driven triggers, making it suitable for background jobs, scheduled tasks via timer triggers, processing messages from queues or topics, and building orchestration with minimal code. It is positioned as a low-code/no-code tool for building serverless applications.

Azure Functions supports various deployment and reliability features, including zone-redundant deployments, virtual network injection, and multiple hosting plans with networking options. It offers Premium and Dedicated plans for autoscaling consumer applications based on incoming events, with concurrency support and the ability to bind to the change feed processor for custom backups. It is associated with App Service and features updated architecture best practices.

The service integrates with monitoring and observability tools, supporting autoinstrumentation sampling configuration for Application Insights monitoring, configurable log levels, and scope. It is central to workload design recommendations covering operational excellence, performance efficiency, security, and monitoring.

Azure Functions plays a key role in event-driven architectures, handling events and using managed identities for authentication with Event Grid. It can automate scaling responses based on Event Grid metrics and serves as a dependency that can affect event processing. It works with Azure Service Bus for planned traffic message processing and manages partitions automatically as a downstream consumer for Event Hubs. It can also configure auto-start triggers and adjust throughput units based on alert triggers for automated cost optimization.

Azure Functions serves as a key automation resource, enabling organizations to automate tasks including incident response, remediation actions, and self-healing workflows such as restarting failed jobs or scaling clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is a service evaluated for Service Bus workflow automation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is a serverless compute service used for automating Service Bus operational tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions handles operations requiring Azure Resource Manager interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Functions is an Azure native tool that can forward logs by creating listeners for incoming logs from Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e0fe247c84a41199e470c86f0e983f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0c9390a87db2dcb2296e0f0d2ad3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b24002e6c6a1f793f274780f10d2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2431ac43eabe818a5350eafb1e23d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2831164a5771887ad5de08caa27249ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464884618643684fc043c8a50e0bf16f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c1dd7c66529e2ab2455ebd5bb312625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b01c06cbc36f4fb17c08ab0e3baafd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37afa41294d82e5e5fb34db4fe81fec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd9ecc5b1e909344bcefaee765852bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9477f91dc0a48476ae389364456c73e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb68bab7c1b474f207b34f9a74328e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a75f6abfb52e7f12669ccabfaf886c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8fc58eb81af85bd1aa7f2b1f5ef9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46bd5396ccec87008471ae597a39d434&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc6dd32c7c960a85b9a30c11bc43659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493</data>
