<node id="Zone Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Zone Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone Redundancy is a built-in Azure reliability feature that distributes resources, replicas, and instances across multiple availability zones within a region to enhance availability and resilience. It ensures that workloads can withstand failures in a single availability zone by enabling automatic failover to remaining zones, providing protection against datacenter outages.

Zone Redundancy applies across multiple Azure services. For Azure App Service, it allows applications to withstand single-zone failures by provisioning instances across multiple zones. For Azure Load Balancer, it distributes traffic across zones to handle availability zone failures. For Premium tier Azure Container Registry, it provides protection against availability zone failure. As a general Azure reliability feature, it offers immediate resilience improvements by spreading instances across multiple datacenters and deploying units across multiple availability zones within a region.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone redundancy eliminates single points of failure within regional infrastructure with automatic failover during zone failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone redundancy distributes compute and storage across multiple Azure availability zones for resilience against zone outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone redundancy distributes replicas across availability zones to eliminate single points of failure within a region.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone redundancy provides datacenter failure protection with higher SLA guarantees by eliminating availability zones as single points of failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7595d0066e438d094afa55de7d2ba18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49c55356fee42f19cd603d7edc0b8b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002775</data>
