<node id="Infrastructure As A Service">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure As A Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) is a cloud computing model using virtualization and VMs as the primary hosting model for constrained migrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) solutions typically support zonal deployments in Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;IaaS provides raw infrastructure components that users must assemble and maintain themselves.&lt;SEP&gt;A cloud service model where the customer manages operating system, identity, applications, and networking.&lt;SEP&gt;IaaS database solutions can be time-consuming and resource-intensive, diverting technical teams from core tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) solutions typically support zonal deployments in Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) is the cloud delivery model used for SAP on Azure deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc27c33aba333fbae143b55b08a314fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d14511d72d14b9bf6ec7b7f61c0bc5c</data>
