<node id="Containerization">
  <data key="d0">Containerization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Containerization is an abstraction layer for application code and dependencies that enables portability and consistent execution across platforms. It packages applications and their dependencies into isolated, self-contained units, ensuring independently deployable components with improved deployment consistency.

Containerization is the strongly recommended approach for packaging and deploying mission-critical application workloads. It is used to isolate critical flows at the software or logical level, achieving performance gains through resource efficiency, fast startup times, and portability. By reducing resource allocation overhead and allowing bin packing on VMs, containerization improves server utilization, though these benefits are most fully realized when utilization is high.

Containerization also serves as a valuable development technique, enabling developers to run workloads locally, replicate production environments, and test changes quickly before deploying to production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7767ff1f3a0e2852dd0aca5f32b5671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ff8d586800116f4a9c0f2e6c0039f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c191d35e97adae9dac9c5492df49a2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite SLO">
  <data key="d0">Composite SLO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite SLO is a reliability metric calculated across user flows, with targets of 99.99% or greater requiring a minimum of three deployment regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite SLO is the overall uptime objective of a solution derived from architectural decisions and individual service SLAs.&lt;SEP&gt;A composite SLO combines multiple SLIs to define measurable targets within an observability window.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite SLO is a product distribution of contributing SLO factors, calculated by multiplying individual SLO values.&lt;SEP&gt;The overall composite SLO target is 99.45%, equivalent to approximately four hours of downtime per month.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite SLO is the overall uptime objective of a solution derived from architectural decisions and individual service SLAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6461a458cf4d4525d7fe6f8f9cfa20e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e048464dc928ee7d9ace1aae32cd84e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content Delivery Network">
  <data key="d0">Content Delivery Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Content Delivery Network (CDN) is a distributed system that caches and serves frequently accessed static content from edge nodes located closer to end users. By storing static data nearer to consumers, CDNs minimize network latency, reduce network traversal and traffic, and improve response times, particularly for distributed user bases. CDNs are a popular caching solution used to offload data and enhance performance.

CDNs can be incorporated as part of cost-optimization cloud patterns; however, their use increases the workload surface area. In many use cases, Azure Front Door's built-in cache can replace or eliminate the need for a dedicated CDN, as it provides similar edge caching capabilities for serving static content.&lt;SEP&gt;A content delivery network (CDN) is a component that can be added as part of cost-optimization cloud patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;A content delivery network optimizes data delivery for clients in distant regions.&lt;SEP&gt;A CDN feature of Azure Front Door with hundreds of edge locations that helps withstand traffic surges and DDoS attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9d6cbba3e234d9031d66c9ba1579fb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b32925fbb6ae4e81a734e77c9c7decb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c50ccf987c588887cc7df000f1e99478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5658d6f41065712f87008266f41103c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-code-infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Stamps">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamps</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment Stamps are a design pattern consisting of repeatable, self-contained units that include all resources required to deliver a workload. Each stamp represents workload-level redundancy with isolated failure domains, enabling horizontal scaling by adding one or more scale units.

These stamps are regional scale units that can be deployed across multiple regions to maximize reliability and mitigate risk. The pattern releases specific versions of an application and infrastructure as controlled deployment units, supporting immutable infrastructure and safe deployment practices. Deployment Stamps can also be used as a variation of blue-green deployment by deploying one stamp at a time, enabling reliable deployment of both application code and new infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment Stamps is a design pattern that can be used as a variation of blue-green deployment by deploying one stamp at a time.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment stamps pattern provides geo-distribution, feature deployment to specific stamps, and efficient resource utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment stamps allow deploying multiple independent instances of a solution, providing an additional scaling dimension.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment stamps pattern creates separate instances of a solution in geographically distributed locations to isolate blast radius and improve reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment stamps are a method for driving consistency across configuration and architecture, and for scaling solutions as a unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c944e9a44adf39c12919b36fa366a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cb40dd3fd0df00b3000976f92afb432</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Point Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Point Objectives (RPO) define the maximum acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a disaster recovery scenario or disruption. RPOs serve as recovery targets that should be aligned with business goals, helping organizations determine how much data they can afford to lose in the event of an outage.

In Azure Cosmos DB, RPO is configurable via consistency levels. An RPO of 0 is achievable when using strong consistency with a single-write region, meaning no data loss would occur in such a configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Time Objectives (RTO) define the maximum acceptable duration of downtime or the target time within which a workload, operations, or data must be restored after a disruption or failure. RTOs are aligned with business goals and serve as critical recovery targets in disaster recovery planning.

In the context of Azure Cosmos DB, the RTO for regional failover is approximately 10-15 minutes, with a strategic direction to reduce this to approximately 5 minutes through partition-level failovers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999561</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linux-Based Container Runtimes">
  <data key="d0">Linux-Based Container Runtimes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Linux-based container runtimes are recommended for containers due to lightweight images and frequent feature releases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The baseline architecture is a reference for mission-critical workloads accessed over public endpoints without private network connectivity requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline With Network Controls">
  <data key="d0">Baseline With Network Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An extension of the baseline architecture providing strict network controls to prevent unauthorized public access to workload resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline In Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Baseline In Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture for deploying mission-critical workloads in enterprise setups requiring integration with centralized shared services and on-premises connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure landing zones provide a subscription model for enterprise deployments that inherits from the Corp. management group.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zones represent an organizational pattern where responsibilities are split between workload and platform teams.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zones are a governed platform to help with onboarding workload teams, including platform landing zones and application landing zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardized environments in Azure including platform and application landing zones for deploying workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zones are building blocks of any Azure cloud adoption environment, used to prepare environments for hybrid cloud scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure landing zones are a conceptual architecture depicting the overall cloud footprint for an organization, with multiple subscriptions each serving a unique purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;An enterprise setup where workloads share platform resources managed by central teams, providing integration points with shared resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98ea85178a5817d9a2ef65e41464e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0aeda7bb18ec43b01e80e8a4401d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd2f8bec9d3a589a0de1d0f5ecb5745</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/architect-role/collaboration.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core Architecture Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Core Architecture Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The core architecture pattern is a design approach for mission-critical applications consisting of global resources, regional stamp resources, and regional resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Resources">
  <data key="d0">Global Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global resources are long-living, globally shared resources that distribute traffic, store geo-replicated state, and should be configured with high availability and disaster recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Stamp Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Stamp Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional stamp resources are ephemeral, stateless resources deployed within a stamp that participate in completing business transactions and can be added or removed dynamically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional resources are deployed in a region, outlive stamp resources, and share the lifetime of the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="North Star Design Approach">
  <data key="d0">North Star Design Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The north star design approach is a recommended design methodology for mission-critical architectures on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Assessment is a review tool for self-assessing the readiness of mission-critical workloads in production, organized to check alignment to best practices for resiliency, reliability, and availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4a64c702a6434c451dbfa718bffaf8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Design Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Design Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mission-critical design methodology provides foundational design principles for checking design choices of a workload's architecture and end-to-end operational approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A design methodology underpinned by five key design principles that serve as a compass for design decisions across critical design areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4a64c702a6434c451dbfa718bffaf8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Four Vs Of Big Data">
  <data key="d0">Four Vs Of Big Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Four Vs of Big Data is a framework comprising Volume, Velocity, Variety, and Veracity used to understand characteristics for designing highly available data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CQRS">
  <data key="d0">CQRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is a pattern used to optimize throughput in data platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern for asynchronous non-blocking messaging to load-level throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Command and Query Responsibility Segregation is a pattern for load-leveling through asynchronous non-blocking messaging.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern recommended for optimal Event Hubs performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db510f47656045373bcac562ba7e53ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Sourcing">
  <data key="d0">Event Sourcing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Sourcing is a persistence pattern used alongside CQRS to optimize data platform throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is an architectural pattern used for asynchronous non-blocking messaging.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is a pattern used alongside CQRS for asynchronous updates to Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern treating state changes as immutable append-only events, improving performance through atomic operations and avoidance of database locking.&lt;SEP&gt;Event sourcing is an architectural pattern applied for optimal performance with Event Hubs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db510f47656045373bcac562ba7e53ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time To Live">
  <data key="d0">Time To Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time to Live (TTL) is a feature that manages data growth by automatically deleting records after an elapsed time.&lt;SEP&gt;A caching parameter (TTL) that determines how long cached data remains fresh and relevant.&lt;SEP&gt;TTL is a mechanism used with cached data to reduce storage needs and costs by expiring data after a set period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Mission-Critical Workload">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Mission-Critical Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is a series of guidance articles for designing mission-critical systems on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;A series of articles providing guidance on designing and operating mission-critical workloads on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is an article series providing design guidance for mission-critical applications on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is an article series providing design guidance for mission-critical applications on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Write Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Write Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region write configuration enables geographically distributed writes but introduces data consistency and conflict resolution challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-region write configuration places a write replica in each deployment region to reduce latency and provide maximum redundancy at significant cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Geographical Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Geographical Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active geographical distribution is a design recommendation that introduces challenges around data consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Volume">
  <data key="d0">Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume refers to the amount of data coming in, informing storage capacity and tiering requirements, representing the size of the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume is a design consideration factor concerning data growth rates, capacity requirements, and data platform limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Velocity">
  <data key="d0">Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Velocity refers to the speed at which data is processed, either as batches or continuous streams, representing the rate of flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variety">
  <data key="d0">Variety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variety refers to the organization and format of data, capturing structured, semi-structured, and unstructured formats across multiple stores or types.&lt;SEP&gt;Variety is a design consideration factor addressing data models, data types, data relationships, and query models that affect data platform decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Veracity">
  <data key="d0">Veracity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Veracity includes the provenance and curation of data sets for governance and data quality assurance, representing the accuracy of the data.&lt;SEP&gt;Veracity is a design consideration factor for validating data accuracy, encompassing consistency, security, governance, and change management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACID">
  <data key="d0">ACID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ACID refers to full transactional semantics and traditional locking behavior, which involves trade-offs with consistency and performance in distributed systems.&lt;SEP&gt;ACID stands for atomic, consistent, isolated, and durable, representing guarantees provided by relational databases for data transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB SDK">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB SDK provides built-in error handling, retry, and reliability capabilities for client applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connection Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connection Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct connection mode optimizes network performance through direct TCP connectivity to backend Azure Cosmos DB nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partitioning Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Partitioning Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A partitioning strategy optimizes data distribution across logical and physical partitions according to the data model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Security Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Azure Security Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Security Baseline provides control guidance for Azure Cosmos DB Backup and Recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexing">
  <data key="d0">Indexing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexing in Azure Cosmos DB is crucial for performance, using index exclusions to reduce RU/s and storage requirements by only indexing fields needed for query filtering.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of creating data structures that improve the speed of data retrieval on frequently queried columns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partition Key">
  <data key="d0">Partition Key</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A partition key is an immutable property value with high cardinality that spreads RU consumption and data storage evenly across logical and physical partitions.&lt;SEP&gt;A partition key determines how data is distributed across partitions and may need to be redesigned during rebalancing.&lt;SEP&gt;The partition key for a blob consists of account name, container name, and blob name, used to partition data into load-balanced ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;A partition key determines data distribution in Azure Cosmos DB and should have high cardinality and remain unchanged.&lt;SEP&gt;Partition keys determine how data and throughput are distributed across logical partitions in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c0f1c2454a3cd326399dd189c571e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e47e51139cb584d95de7bb450c2af708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4ef1aec0a62de4cc107952af4e1f676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e48c686ed9dcbf1ebc4bd457a81b5e7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backups">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backups</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous backups provide fine granularity recovery points across the last 30 days for Azure Cosmos DB accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Failover">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic failover can be configured for single write region deployments based on a defined failover priority considering all read region replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic failover is strongly recommended for single write region Azure Cosmos DB deployments to handle write region outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Architecture Guide">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Architecture Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Application Architecture Guide provides additional data-platform guidance including decision trees and criteria for choosing data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Write">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Write</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region write is a data platform design pattern where changes to separate writeable replicas are synchronized and merged between all replicas with conflict resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last Write Wins">
  <data key="d0">Last Write Wins</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Last Write Wins (LWW) is a conflict resolution policy that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol with a system-defined timestamp property to resolve update conflicts.&lt;SEP&gt;Last Write Wins (LWW) is the default conflict resolution policy in Azure Cosmos DB that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol to resolve conflicts by selecting the item with the highest timestamp value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paxos">
  <data key="d0">Paxos</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Paxos is a consensus protocol applied by Azure Cosmos DB to achieve quorum across replicas within a region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Zone Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zone Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability Zone redundancy ensures data replicas are placed across multiple availability zones to protect against zone failures within a region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct mode facilitates connectivity over TCP to backend Azure Cosmos DB replica nodes for improved performance with fewer network hops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway mode provides HTTPS connectivity to frontend gateway nodes in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is the first-party API providing the richest feature set, typically receiving new capabilities first.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is an API variant that supports custom numerical properties for conflict resolution and custom resolution policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chaos Testing">
  <data key="d0">Chaos Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chaos testing is used to test and validate backup, restore capabilities, and failover operations within continuous delivery processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing method that injects faults into an application under load to understand how it responds to failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing injects artificial failures into the system to evaluate how it reacts and validate the effectiveness of resiliency measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing is used alongside load testing within CI/CD processes to observe and validate application health.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing is a method used to reveal undiscovered dependencies between workload components and validate recovery plans.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance test that tests resilience and stability by deliberately introducing random and unpredictable failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing is a testing approach recommended for high-availability systems to test resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6f5079bad84a35961c4d29f3694386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5fd47376a7e9081496e03cedc06a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Managed Encryption Keys">
  <data key="d0">Service-Managed Encryption Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service-managed encryption keys are recommended to reduce management complexity when applying encryption to data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer-Managed Keys">
  <data key="d0">Customer-Managed Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer-Managed Keys are encryption keys managed by the customer rather than the cloud provider, allowing users to control their own encryption keys while Azure uses them to protect data. They are stored separately from the encrypted data and provide flexibility to change, rotate, and manage keys according to organizational needs.

Customer-Managed Keys offer complete control over the encryption key lifecycle, including creation, rotation, revocation, and auditing. They support regulatory compliance requirements, including data sovereignty, and enable users to control encryption and decryption of their data in services such as Azure Storage, Event Hubs event streams and metadata, and Log Analytics clusters. For Event Hubs, using customer-managed keys requires a dedicated cluster.

Proper key management procedures are essential for customer-managed keys, including ensuring key availability, maintaining backups, and implementing regular rotation schedules to maintain security and uninterrupted access to encrypted data.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer-managed keys are encryption keys directly managed by the user, used to encrypt data at rest in Machine Learning for regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer-managed keys are encryption keys used to encrypt Machine Learning workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature allowing users to manage their own encryption keys for volumes in Azure NetApp Files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f3e7854aa5a9772017d1a8685f93f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd64e0b4a0a0a0b146d62e2b5b760fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc4795580f532b2b4baa2c23d716389</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Data Services">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Data Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized data services (Central IT DBaaS) introduce operational bottlenecks that hinder agility and should be avoided in mission-critical or business-critical contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cassandra">
  <data key="d0">Cassandra</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cassandra is one of the API options supported by Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;Cassandra is a column-oriented data store suited for vertical partitioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103386df6f9acd0832fa49dd897fcede</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MongoDB">
  <data key="d0">MongoDB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MongoDB is one of the API options supported by Azure Cosmos DB.&lt;SEP&gt;MongoDB is a nonrelational database option for SaaS solutions on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720f5dd6d7dfc922834541dcd8b45b10</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Request Units">
  <data key="d0">Request Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Request Units per second (RU/s) are the measure of throughput provisioned in Azure Cosmos DB, billed per region.&lt;SEP&gt;Request Units (RUs) are the billing unit for Azure Cosmos DB, charged per region when replicated across multiple regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Request units (RUs) are the throughput currency in Azure Cosmos DB, where exceeding provisioned RUs can cause throttling.&lt;SEP&gt;Request Units (RUs) measure throughput consumption in Azure Cosmos DB operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e48c686ed9dcbf1ebc4bd457a81b5e7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB change feed provides a time-ordered feed of insert and update operations to data in a container, excluding deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB change feed writes data to separate storage and supports continuous or periodic custom backups but does not yet reflect deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Change feed is a mechanism in Azure Cosmos DB that captures data record changes for propagation to target data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Locks">
  <data key="d0">Resource Locks</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource Locks protect Azure Cosmos DB resources against incorrect modification or deletion, applying only to control plane operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource locks are an Azure feature to prevent resources from being modified or deleted, recommended mainly for long-lived global resources rather than ephemeral regional resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource locks prevent unintended changes or deletions to important resources in Azure Resource Manager.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource locks safeguard resources from unwanted deletion or change at subscription, resource group, or resource level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft Delete">
  <data key="d0">Soft Delete</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Soft Delete is a pattern where data records are flagged as deleted rather than explicitly removed, enabling inclusion in the change feed.&lt;SEP&gt;Soft delete allows recovery of deleted data within a defined period, offered by most Azure storage services.&lt;SEP&gt;Soft delete protects Azure file shares against accidental deletion at the file share level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001488</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session">
  <data key="d0">Session</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session is the default and most widely used consistency level in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmos DB Account Reader">
  <data key="d0">Cosmos DB Account Reader</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role that enables read-only access to Azure Cosmos DB resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DocumentDB Account Contributor">
  <data key="d0">DocumentDB Account Contributor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role that enables management of Azure Cosmos DB accounts including keys and role assignments but not data-plane access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmos DB Operator">
  <data key="d0">Cosmos DB Operator</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role similar to DocumentDB Account Contributor but without ability to manage keys or role assignments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Database For PostgreSQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Database For PostgreSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Database for PostgreSQL is a fully managed, cloud-based relational database service on Microsoft Azure, built on the PostgreSQL open-source engine. It is offered in multiple deployment options, including Single Server, Flexible Server, and Hyperscale (Citus), and is designed to support mission-critical and business-critical workloads with high availability and scalability.

The service provides comprehensive backup and restore capabilities, including automated backups, point-in-time restore, and geo-redundant backup options. For performance management, it offers monitoring through Azure Monitor, query store, index tuning, intelligent performance tuning, and built-in Grafana dashboards available in the Azure portal.

Azure Database for PostgreSQL incorporates robust security and governance features, including built-in policies, confidential computing with hardware-based encryption using Intel SGX or AMD SEV-SNP secure enclaves, private networking, and Microsoft Entra ID integration. Its architecture best practices also cover cost modeling, cost optimization, automation, and operational excellence.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Database for PostgreSQL supports vector search via the pgvector extension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39895fc4a2ce3e45eeca7bf801519ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7404990d0db645a738f8e03698df0941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-400db80f7a604700a524e7328f763772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85737e4794e90bbd715857ab9acd5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cache For Redis">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cache For Redis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cache for Redis is an in-memory caching service based on open source Redis, offering Premium, Enterprise, and Enterprise Flash tiers with geo-replication and high availability capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cache for Redis had its service guide retired as the content was outdated and no longer aligned with the Azure Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999948</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse is an enterprise analytical platform combining relational and non-relational data with Spark technologies and built-in Azure service integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse brings together analytics capabilities including SQL data warehousing, Spark big data, and Data Explorer for log and time series analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse is an enterprise analytical platform that brings together relational and non-relational data with Spark technologies, including SQL data warehousing, Spark big data, and Data Explorer for log and time series analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Analytics is an analytical technology offering ML capabilities, Spark Pools, notebooks, and data integration for building AIOps models.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse is used for analysis of ingested Log Analytics operational data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperscale (Citus)">
  <data key="d0">Hyperscale (Citus)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperscale (Citus) is a PostgreSQL deployment option providing dynamic scalability through sharding, with 99.95% SLA when High Availability is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperscale (Citus) is a deployment option for Azure Database for PostgreSQL that provides dynamic scalability through sharding, with SLA 99.95% when High Availability is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperscale (Citus) is a configuration option for Azure Database For PostgreSQL that maximizes availability across multiple nodes with High Availability mode offering 99.95% SLA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Server">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible Server is a deployment option offering Availability Zone redundancy with SLA 99.99%, cost efficiencies through stop/start capability, and burstable compute tier.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible Server is a deployment option for Azure Database For PostgreSQL recommended for business critical workloads due to Availability Zone support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enterprise Flash Tier">
  <data key="d0">Enterprise Flash Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enterprise Flash tier of Azure Cache for Redis uses RAM and flash non-volatile memory, enabling cache sizes up to 13TB with clustering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-In-Time Restore">
  <data key="d0">Point-In-Time Restore</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Point-In-Time Restore (PITR) is a backup and recovery capability offered by Azure database and storage services that allows restoring data to a specific earlier state. It enables recovery to any moment with one-second granularity within the continuous backup or backup retention period, helping organizations roll back data to a previous state when needed.

PITR serves as an operational recovery method for services such as Azure SQL Database, protecting against a variety of data loss scenarios including accidental deletion, data corruption, severe configuration errors, and inadvertent changes caused by human error. For block blob data, it specifically restores data to an earlier state following accidental deletion or corruption. For databases, it returns a database to an earlier point in time to recover from unintended modifications. Additionally, deleted servers can be recovered within five days using this functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-in-time restore (PITR) is a recovery method for SQL Managed Instance that requires accounting for instance provisioning time.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-in-time restore (PITR) is a recovery method that restores to a new instance rather than an existing one, requiring account for instance provisioning time in RTO calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching For Hot Tier Data">
  <data key="d0">Caching For Hot Tier Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An in-memory caching layer that enhances data platforms by increasing read throughput and improving response times for hot tier data scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytical Scenarios">
  <data key="d0">Analytical Scenarios</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytical scenarios drive additional value from data flows in mission-critical applications, requiring different data platform capabilities than transactional workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAGA">
  <data key="d0">SAGA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAGA is a design pattern applied to manage consistency and dependencies between different datastores.&lt;SEP&gt;SAGA is a design pattern used where dependencies between datastores exist in microservice architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-To-Live">
  <data key="d0">Time-To-Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-To-Live (TTL) is a data expiration mechanism for removing data no longer required.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-To-Live (TTL) is a setting that enables Azure Cosmos DB to automatically delete expired data, used with the soft-delete pattern to ensure deletions propagate through the change feed before removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-to-live is a mechanism that sets an expiration time for data.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-to-live is a mechanism that sets an expiration time for data, allowing automatic deletion or archival.&lt;SEP&gt;TTL setting determines how long downstream DNS resolvers cache DNS responses; reducing TTL increases cache update frequency but increases DNS lookups.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-to-live (TTL) automatically deletes unnecessary data to optimize storage costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720e4839ab18a5ecc8b875712ef0f4cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e48c686ed9dcbf1ebc4bd457a81b5e7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Tiering">
  <data key="d0">Data Tiering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data tiering classifies datasets into 'hot', 'warm', and 'cold' tiers based on usage and criticality.&lt;SEP&gt;Data tiering is a storage strategy that involves categorizing data based on its access frequency and storing it on appropriate storage tiers.&lt;SEP&gt;Data tiering involves categorizing data based on importance or access frequency and storing it in different performance tiers.&lt;SEP&gt;Data tiering stores data in different tiers based on access frequency and importance to optimize storage costs and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Data tiering is a storage strategy that categorizes data based on access frequency and stores it on appropriate storage tiers ranging from hot to cold.&lt;SEP&gt;Data tiering is the practice of moving data between storage tiers (hot, cool, archive) based on access frequency and cost requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720e4839ab18a5ecc8b875712ef0f4cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f675dff830aa38bf7b60ffd30f2363d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Model">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A capacity model monitors data volume against scale limits and expected growth rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A model enabling planning of resource scale levels for a given load profile and system-wide capacity allocation planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft is a major technology company founded in 1975 and the parent company of Azure. Its cloud ecosystem encompasses Azure, Dynamics 365, Microsoft 365, Power Platform, and Fabric. Microsoft manages Azure infrastructure including data synchronization, traffic distribution, failover capabilities, serverless compute options, and DDoS L3/L4 protection. The company publishes SLAs for uptime and connectivity, RTO and RPO recovery guarantees, and offers discounted rates through various licensing agreements.

Microsoft provides comprehensive security solutions including Microsoft Sentinel, Microsoft Defender, Azure Front Door, and Microsoft Entra identity services. The company publishes threat intelligence data, implements the Zero Trust security model, integrates war game exercises into its business rhythm, and offers the Security Development Lifecycle (SDL). Microsoft discourages certain security practices such as SAS tokens in favor of more secure alternatives.

Microsoft publishes extensive documentation including the Azure Well-Architected Framework, DevOps culture guidance, and formalized processes based on industry-proven practices. The company offers Cloud Solution Architects, incident readiness training, AI and DevOps tools for incident management, cloud skills challenges, and a learning partner program with certified trainers. Microsoft provides official icons for representing its services in architecture diagrams.

Microsoft manages core Azure Virtual Desktop services including the control plane, metadata, gateway infrastructure, load balancer, session broker, and diagnostics. The company also manages Azure VMware Solution infrastructure, providing proprietary services and tools for monitoring, and offers Azure Site Recovery and Azure Backup Server. Microsoft is the provider of Azure Local and related hybrid services including Azure Arc and Azure Hybrid Benefit with validated hardware partnerships. Its broad portfolio includes Azure Blob Storage, Azure Files, and development tools for mission-critical applications. As a platform vendor, Microsoft offers support teams available during incidents and is referenced as a provider requiring mission-critical support plans.

Microsoft provides a framework for responsible AI with core principles and the Human-AI Experiences Design Library. The company also conducts research on improving edge device AI efficiency.

Microsoft is committed to sustainability, aiming to be carbon negative by 2030 and to remove all carbon emitted since 1975 by 2050. The company segments greenhouse gas emissions into three scopes, offers sustainability tools, and empowers organizations to reduce their emissions, maintaining sustainability commitments from data centers to the cloud.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft is the company that provides the SAP on Azure Deployment Automation Framework and Azure monitoring tools for SAP workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft provides Azure cloud infrastructure and builds security protections into the service at physical data center, network, host, and hypervisor levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft has hosted SAP instances in its data centers for decades and has custom built infrastructure and services to run SAP applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4a87b29a0d7646a31a3fd27442ab6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d280cc7c07462216af45547cce48d2f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654e7aada501f6fea6718cd59dbed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7277d28a361465235f16e5be124c32d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964d0aabb6a006eaf58781c2658f980a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbdc7bdb179c925972b2debe7a1d4a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8560181068572aab32ee3c98848771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf9fd57985f14c81b7d1b9d2924d1bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5200ddd62ebcb8e16dece7ddc1422557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed16a2af63252a2201b654a7b2b61614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ede2f555755748b50d3eff6168ec5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-517ef83a1fe99178ace6be8c8c95c6c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9896bbc28e252b9ce2f3f2bb74ad70f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99334db9b3c4c908652c875ca2926b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74a4365f57d52439ea79753f3bb9374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-198a3a5ea0d4ee6048ded7764b7c4702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6200584afd66d7b2ca01f9fe20d183ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb71511d377d5a69b2902c6777be774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a5d862a78e37f61b1525f212796615f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e