<node id="Microservice Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Microservice Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A microservice architecture allows individual application services to be built with distinct scenario-optimized datastores.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservice architecture is a design principle promoting loosely coupled services that can use distinct data stores and scenario-optimized data technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservice architecture is a design approach that allows scaling individual components independently, reducing resource overhead compared to monolithic applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Data Platform">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Data Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A multi-region data platform distributes replicas across regions for maximum reliability, availability, and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching">
  <data key="d0">Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Caching is a technique that stores frequently accessed or "hot" data in a fast-access storage area closer to the components or users that require it. It improves data retrieval speed, reduces latency, minimizes network traversal, and lowers the processing load on backend infrastructure and compute layers by avoiding repeated round trips to databases or origin servers.

Caching is a key design component for optimizing system performance and improving user experience. By serving static content from edge locations closer to users, caching speeds up client load times, reduces bandwidth costs, and decreases calls to origin servers. Effective caching implementations include policies for expiration and housekeeping to manage stored data. In the context of Azure Front Door, caching stores content at the edge of the network, reducing load on origin servers and improving delivery speed while lowering costs.

Beyond runtime data access, caching also applies to build processes, where it involves storing dependencies and intermediate build artifacts to avoid redundant work during subsequent builds.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching is a design technique that reduces network traversal and server load by storing data closer to where it is needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c50ccf987c588887cc7df000f1e99478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7f774cbe85718aeb4ca8377bca84b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90796296cec0f129315921be106646d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d314b16e3b2b8776b889c2beaec2890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a007dbfba3cef886b2cc00b13f46310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc7bbe0246f2fdb01b26dc432706f88</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching Layer">
  <data key="d0">Caching Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching layer is used to increase read throughput and improve user experience and end-to-end client response times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Model">
  <data key="d0">Data Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The data model, along with data types and relationships, strongly affects data platform decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The data model represents how data is structured and managed within a system, requiring evaluation and segmentation as data evolves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAP Theorem">
  <data key="d0">CAP Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAP theorem expresses the trade-off between consistency and latency in distributed applications with multiple data replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAP theorem implies tradeoffs between availability and consistency in a distributed system, with network partitions being unavoidable.&lt;SEP&gt;CAP theorem is a framework used to consider consistency, availability, and partition tolerance to explain tradeoffs in data consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997230</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PACELC Theorem">
  <data key="d0">PACELC Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The PACELC theorem extends CAP to express trade-offs between consistency, availability, and latency in distributed systems.&lt;SEP&gt;PACELC theorem is a framework considering partition tolerance, availability, consistency, and latency to explain tradeoffs in data consistency.&lt;SEP&gt;The PACELC theorem helps understand latency versus consistency tradeoff choices in distributed systems in both partitioned and nonpartitioned states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apache Spark">
  <data key="d0">Apache Spark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Apache Spark is an analytical runtime environment that may have integration restrictions for analyzing polyglot data structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Apache Spark is the underlying analytics engine that Azure Databricks is based on.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Vault">
  <data key="d0">Key Vault</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Key Vault is a global managed service provided by Microsoft Azure for securely storing and managing secrets, encryption keys, and certificates. It serves as a centralized secret management solution, handling secrets such as tokens, passwords, API keys, credentials, connection strings, storage account keys, and SSL/TLS certificates. The Premium SKU offers hardware security module (HSM) support.

Key Vault integrates with Microsoft Entra ID for access control and supports both zone and regional redundancy, implemented transparently. It provides RBAC-restricted access, audit logging, soft delete, and purge protection capabilities. Multiple vaults can be created for isolation at no added cost, and secrets can be referenced via app settings to keep them separate from application configuration. It supports secret and key rotation policies, automated secret rotation, and comprehensive auditing, facilitating key rotation without application interruption.

Key Vault is used across various Azure services and scenarios. It stores encryption keys for customer-managed key scenarios, manages certificates with simple renewal and rotation for TLS certificates, and provides secure storage for client credentials. It is often combined with API Management and stores certificates for Application Gateway, which checks for renewed certificate versions every 4 hours. It supports both client-side and server-side encryption scenarios, manages encryption keys and account keys at runtime, provides secret scopes, and plays a role in authentication workflows with enterprise-grade security controls.

Key Vault also serves as a dependent service for Azure Machine Learning and should be configured with private endpoints in such scenarios to maintain network security.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault is an Azure service that can monitor certificate expiration and send notifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault centralizes encryption key management with audit logging, soft-delete, and purge protection for SQL Managed Instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault stores certificates that are automatically refreshed by the Key Vault Windows extension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b1c021188faeb6dd44f9550bc2c4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c53b990e9918af85864a95bf9284ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f471ce6b86ced91e851ed4cd06f0521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caf8d0c8419c804f864143fd95c9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e6162eae6d61a639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608026926818db1b277afce5e06e8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7918938c3b3fb0cddcc9e93b114d4a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c50c3fc68e8ca3e2a2600f5ec515c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c34815c939645bbbdf7eeec0352ec98f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MACsec">
  <data key="d0">MACsec</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MACsec (IEEE 802.1AE MAC) is a data-link encryption method used to secure all traffic between Azure datacenters on the Microsoft backbone network.&lt;SEP&gt;MACsec is data-link layer encryption used on underlying network hardware to secure data in-transit between Azure data centers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Backbone Network">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Backbone Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft backbone network carries traffic between Azure datacenters, secured by MACsec encryption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyglot Storage">
  <data key="d0">Polyglot Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyglot storage refers to the capability of analytical datastores to support various types of data structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-side encryption is an encryption method implemented in the application layer where keys can be managed in Key Vault or another secure location.&lt;SEP&gt;Client-side encryption encrypts data before uploading as an encrypted blob, with key management done by the customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Server-side encryption is an encryption method implemented in the data layer using service-managed or customer-managed keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Default encryption method for managed disks that protects data and meets compliance commitments.&lt;SEP&gt;SSE encrypts data at rest for managed disks, snapshots, and images, enabled by default in Azure Storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conflict Resolution">
  <data key="d0">Conflict Resolution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conflict resolution addresses situations in multi-region write contexts where the same data item is changed in separate write-replicas, using policies such as Last Write Wins or custom strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Resolution Policies">
  <data key="d0">Custom Resolution Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom resolution policies allow application-defined semantics to reconcile conflicts using a registered merge stored procedure, available only with Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paxos Consensus Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Paxos Consensus Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paxos consensus protocol is applied within the hub region to achieve quorum across replicas for conflict resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Region">
  <data key="d0">Hub Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hub region is the primary single region in Azure Cosmos DB's multi-region write configuration responsible for performing all conflict resolutions, determined by the first region configured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Buffer">
  <data key="d0">Message Buffer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The message buffer stores write conflicts within the hub region to load level and provide redundancy for transient faults, capable of storing a few minutes worth of write updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Levels">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency levels in Azure Cosmos DB configure RPO and RTO trade-offs between data durability and throughput, with five levels available including strong and relaxed options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Link provides an analytical store whose data is not included in Azure Cosmos DB backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link connects Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store to Azure Synapse for performing analytics on operational data without impacting transactional performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link enables direct querying of Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store from Azure Synapse, enabling no-ETL Hybrid Transactional-Analytical Processing (HTAP).&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link is a service for complex analytical queries on Azure Cosmos DB data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a99a5a991c44794d4415bc58af98647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Factory">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Factory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Data Factory (ADF) is a cloud-based data orchestration and integration service offered by Microsoft Azure. It is a batch-oriented platform that provides workflow management, data cleansing, transformation pipelines, and orchestration capabilities, making it a recommended technology for ETL/ELT and data processing scenarios.

ADF provides pipelines to connect and process many data sources efficiently, with support for various trigger types, including triggers for automatic data refresh and indexing. It natively integrates with Azure Synapse for data extraction, transformation, and loading, and supports Azure Private Link for secure connectivity, including copying data from services such as Azure Cosmos DB.

Beyond core ETL functionality, Azure Data Factory supports workspace replication, automated backup processes, and can replicate shard map manager databases across regions, contributing to robust disaster recovery and high-availability strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcddf7ff1ed7cd474439efcf9fe04d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88acce1b2be2296ca1e97b9e9e3c8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003795</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Private Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Private Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Private Link is an Azure networking service that enables private connectivity to Azure services by providing dedicated access to Azure PaaS, SaaS, and other platform resources using private IP addresses. It connects virtual networks to platform-as-a-service and software-as-a-service resources, eliminating exposure to the public internet and enhancing confidentiality by keeping traffic on private networks.

Azure Private Link supports a wide range of Azure services and use cases. It enables private endpoints for Azure Data Factory in high network security scenarios, secures Azure Front Door connections to application origins without exposing public IP addresses (offering 99.99% SLA with Container Apps deployments), and supports SQL Managed Instance. It provides restricted private access to the API Management gateway, secures control plane connections without using the public internet, enables private connectivity between databases and virtual networks (allowing public access to be disabled), and allows creating private endpoints to extend Azure Database for PostgreSQL inside a virtual network. It is also referenced in guidance for Azure Virtual Desktop workloads, with considerations for large subnet trade-offs.

Azure Private Link is a paid service with meters for inbound and outbound data processing associated with private endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link enables private connectivity between virtual networks and Azure services such as databases.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link is a network security service for private access to Azure resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link connects to Azure resources through an internal IP address within a network.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link keeps traffic within the Microsoft network by creating private endpoints between virtual networks and services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e048464dc928ee7d9ace1aae32cd84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32bb35f93b689b12c3d63f12dc276ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d57d3c8e9b437c3bf033faee9829a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b3b849ac5683c426e666e8f3f3f48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/application-insights.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB For Nosql">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB For Nosql</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL offers the most comprehensive feature set, particularly for performance tuning.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure Cosmos DB API that supports continuous backup configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is an Azure service with updated architecture best practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is an Azure service with updated best practices including new features, policy links, and recommendations for Microsoft Entra ID, private endpoints, Azure Policy, and Azure Advisor.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is a variant of Azure Cosmos DB focused on NoSQL database workloads, serving as the primary subject of the architecture best practices guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is a database service by Microsoft Azure, with SDKs, monitoring, deployment, and performance optimization capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is a database service that supports NoSQL data models with features like global distribution, autoscale, and integrated caching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b18016c0695a884e7aacb8b1c571837&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a99a5a991c44794d4415bc58af98647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed Processor">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed Processor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The change feed processor is a component that binds to the Azure Cosmos DB change feed to process items into storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft-Delete Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Soft-Delete Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern where data records are updated with a deleted flag instead of being explicitly deleted, combined with TTL for automatic cleanup after change feed propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;A soft-delete pattern using a boolean property and TTL must be applied with the change feed since it does not yet reflect deletes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Event Grid">
  <data key="d0">Azure Event Grid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Event Grid is supported by Azure Data Factory as a trigger mechanism for backup pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid is a scalable publish-subscribe message distribution service supporting MQTT and HTTP protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid is used with Logic Apps to automate operational tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid is an Azure service whose guide was expanded to cover all five Well-Architected Framework pillars including chaos engineering and IaC.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid enables automation based on events raised by API Management instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid is a scalable, managed publish-subscribe messaging service that distributes messages using MQTT and HTTP protocols, enabling event-driven serverless architectures, data pipelines, and application integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Grid is a messaging service that supports event filtering, dead-letter destinations, private links, and logging capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0629c90da136e31cc7058b5a6a724b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/enable-automation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-Region Write Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Single-Region Write Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Single-region write configuration with globally distributed read replicas offers high reliability at a more compelling price-point with 99.999% read and 99.995% write SLAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure SQL Database">
  <data key="d0">Azure SQL Database</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL Database is a fully managed relational database engine and Platform as a Service (PaaS) offering on Microsoft Azure that handles most database management functions including upgrades, patches, backups, and monitoring. It serves as an alternative to hosting a database server and shares the SQL Server database engine with SQL Managed Instance but uses a different deployment model. The service supports multiple databases on a server for resource density and is considered a mature service recommended for relational database requirements.

Azure SQL Database offers multiple service tiers, elastic pools, reserved capacity, serverless options, and DTU-based resource metrics for various workload types. Performance management features include automatic tuning, query performance insight, index tuning, query optimization, stored procedures, partitioning, optimized locking, and sharding guidance. Connection pooling best practices and retry capabilities (via Polly or Entity Framework) are supported. The service can be monitored through Azure Monitor and database watcher.

For high availability, Azure SQL Database provides zone redundancy, geo-replication, built-in cross-region replication, automatic failover groups, and readable replicas, with an SLA of up to 99.995%. Disaster recovery capabilities include automatic full, differential, and transaction log backups, point-in-time restore, and published RTO and RPO guarantees.

Security features include options to limit or disable public and private access, built-in data classification for discovering and labeling sensitive data, Tabular Data Stream (TDS) protocol with integrated TLS handshake, and immutable storage for audit logs. The service also natively supports vector data types and vector search, and offers expanded guidance on cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL Database is a database service on Azure with query performance optimization capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39895fc4a2ce3e45eeca7bf801519ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c08b70348e6bfa97e9d7c1d1701b024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0be076c15399d472d831cac4c767ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0544ee58fb5345261d0d125500955a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefafe3b76f15cde350013dbb7911e9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af17a604206f8056ed34d52736aca636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcddf7ff1ed7cd474439efcf9fe04d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720f5dd6d7dfc922834541dcd8b45b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/consolidation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md</data>
