</node>
<node id="Auto Failover Groups">
  <data key="d0">Auto Failover Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Failover Groups replicate databases to a secondary server and allow transparent failover in case of failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Failover Groups provide transparent failover to a secondary region with geo-replication for read optimization and database redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharding">
  <data key="d0">Sharding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharding is a horizontal partitioning method that distributes data and processing across multiple identical structured databases, each holding a subset of the overall dataset while maintaining the same schema. It divides a large database into smaller, independently manageable units called shards, partitioning users, customers, or other data entities into approximately equal-sized buckets based on different application and data contexts.

Sharding directs load to specific logical destinations, isolating data or processing so that malfunctions remain contained within individual shards. This isolation reduces resource competition, enables geography-based optimization, and allows the use of multiple less expensive resources instead of a single expensive one. The approach maximizes scalability through simplified horizontal scaling, improves availability and reliability, enhances load balancing, and provides effective fault isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique of horizontally dividing data across multiple database instances or servers to improve query performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharding directs requests to logical destinations, enabling cost savings through multiple lower-spec resource instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharding replicates schema across multiple databases, storing data subsets in each instance for fault isolation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2829ddae563971c0c88cbe1829d1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0d4e3f080b4962999c8f4d2734bc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
