</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store applies a column format for optimized analytical queries with multi-region availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store is an optimized column store for analytical queries on Azure Cosmos DB operational data.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store is a schematized, fully isolated column-oriented data store that enables large-scale analytics on Azure Cosmos DB data without impacting transactional workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Traffic Manager">
  <data key="d0">Azure Traffic Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Traffic Manager is a globally distributed DNS-based routing service provided by Microsoft Azure. It operates at the DNS level, routing traffic based on configured rules without processing request payloads, and leverages DNS TTL caching for efficiency. It is not deployed into a specific region but functions as a global load balancer with built-in multi-region redundancy and availability, and can be configured across multiple regions for added resilience.

Azure Traffic Manager is particularly suited for non-HTTP/S scenarios, serving as an alternative to Azure Front Door. In the context of Azure SQL Database, it controls routing to specific gateway rings. As a DNS-level service, it directs clients to appropriate endpoints without handling actual data traffic. It supports health probes with enhanced health probing and failover practices.

Azure Traffic Manager provides functionality for capturing Real User Monitoring data for websites and enables implementation of blue-green deployment strategies. It can also be placed in front of Application Gateway when traffic exceeds 125 instances, serving as a scalable global traffic distribution solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a traffic management service for redirecting traffic during regional outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a service used for routing traffic in cross-region active-active redundancy configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager routes traffic across AKS clusters in multiregion deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a global load balancer that distributes traffic across multiple Azure regions, zones, or datacenters using DNS protocol to connect clients to workload endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Traffic Manager is a DNS-based global traffic load balancing solution supporting priority-based, weighted, performance-based, and geographic-based routing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4aed87d4e81857a842b49249489eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757386a260f7f7980e2074a43870b9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
