</node>
<node id="ETL">
  <data key="d0">ETL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) pipelines are used to extract data into separate data platforms for analytical queries, consuming throughput and impacting transactional workload performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) is a traditional data processing approach that may not scale with deployment telemetry growth.&lt;SEP&gt;ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) is a data pipeline method for moving and processing data between systems.&lt;SEP&gt;ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) is a data processing method typical for traditional data warehousing.&lt;SEP&gt;ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) is a data processing pattern common in traditional data warehousing where data is transformed before loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003554</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Sync">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-Sync is the process where operational data changes are automatically synced to the Analytical Store, usually with latency less than two minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTAP">
  <data key="d0">HTAP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid Transactional-Analytical Processing (HTAP) enables querying transactional data for analytics in near real-time without ETL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
