  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Zone-Redundant deployment model spreads Business Critical database replicas within the same region across Availability Zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserved Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Reserved Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserved Capacity provides potential cost optimizations for Azure SQL Database and Azure Database for PostgreSQL compute costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved capacity for Premium SSDs reduces total cost by prepaying for capacity at a discount.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved capacity allows pre-purchasing compute resources for one or three years, saving up to 40% or 60% respectively on compute costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved capacity commitments provide commitment-based pricing that reduces costs compared to pay-as-you-go rates for stable workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved capacity is a commitment lever that reduces SQL Managed Instance costs for predictable workloads through upfront commitment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penetration Testing">
  <data key="d0">Penetration Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Penetration testing, also known as pentesting, is a security testing methodology that simulates real-world attacks to validate and evaluate an organization's security defenses. It employs ethical hacking techniques to identify security vulnerabilities, ensuring that an application and its environment meet the requirements of an expected security posture. This includes end-to-end software supply chain and package dependency scanning for known CVEs.

Penetration testing is typically performed by third-party security practitioners or external security experts who simulate malicious actors. The process involves gathering information, analyzing vulnerabilities, and reporting results. In some cases, engagement with non-Microsoft vendors may be required for compliance purposes. Through this approach, penetration testing serves as a critical tool for identifying security gaps and strengthening overall system defenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing is performed by third-party security practitioners to assess system security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c1925896ad2776a0d0431adee7f3d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5200ddd62ebcb8e16dece7ddc1422557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6753f3d7315e92dc2b4f1d56644604</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996863</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures">
  <data key="d0">Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) is a system for identifying known security vulnerabilities that are scanned and monitored in software supply chains.&lt;SEP&gt;CVEs are tracked within utilized package dependencies as part of securing the software supply chain.&lt;SEP&gt;The Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures program is a database of known vulnerabilities used for comparing versioned assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Chaos Studio">
  <data key="d0">Azure Chaos Studio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Chaos Studio is a managed service and native suite of chaos experimentation tools within Microsoft Azure that uses chaos engineering principles to measure, understand, and improve cloud application and service resilience. It enables users to conduct chaos experiments by injecting controlled faults, failures, and malfunctions into Azure services, application components, consumers, and dependencies. This allows organizations to simulate component outages, trigger disaster recovery situations, and reproduce other unplanned failures to observe how systems respond.

Azure Chaos Studio provides a comprehensive fault and action library for fault injection testing, enabling automated failure injection to validate recovery procedures, identify resilience gaps, and discover potential failure points. It is particularly useful for practicing incident response, testing in production environments, and conducting disaster recovery (DR) testing. Azure Chaos Studio reached general availability at Microsoft Ignite 2023, offering organizations a comprehensive test suite for strengthening the reliability of their cloud applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Chaos Studio is a tool for simulating failures for resiliency testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Chaos Studio provides fault libraries to inject and simulate error conditions for testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Chaos Studio is a tool used to simulate network connectivity disruptions to test workload resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6f5079bad84a35961c4d29f3694386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997b67d2a5ddf57a24dd0380ce47e074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059dfb0d1deec0d27f10ad0c5e0f86d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2789d17a06aaa84a6ce5fba59172ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c34815c939645bbbdf7eeec0352ec98f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4889043b463029eef941a26e276c8840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cd6df2b9534dcc70f59a3fbb6607582</data>
