<node id="Infrastructure As Code">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure As Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a practice that manages, provisions, and deploys infrastructure through declarative, version-controlled code artifacts, pipelines, and templates rather than manual processes. It uses tools such as Terraform, ARM templates, Bicep, and Azure CLI to automate the provisioning of resources—including networks, virtual machines, load balancers, storage accounts, Event Hubs, Service Bus, databases, Machine Learning workspaces, compute clusters, Log Analytics workspaces, peerings, private endpoints, and connection topologies—particularly in cloud environments like Azure. IaC serves as a descriptive model that defines the desired state of all infrastructure, enabling integration with software development practices such as version control and DevOps deployment processes.

Key benefits of IaC include consistency across environments, repeatability, automation, self-documentation, change history, traceability, rollback capabilities, and reduced complexity. By treating infrastructure definitions as version-controlled source code stored in repositories (such as Git), IaC eliminates human error and provides a standardized approach to preparing resources and configurations. It favors declarative methods over imperative ones and is recommended as the preferred approach for infrastructure changes to support safe deployment practices, as well as for consistent, version-controlled management of health models. Notably, IaC minimizes human error risk in areas such as administering and operating log collection and ingestion for Log Analytics workspaces. It also drives standardization across multiple host pools, reducing overhead.

IaC is a foundational practice for disaster recovery and business continuity, introducing upfront engineering effort but supporting strong operations. It is essential for building and managing ephemeral environments—temporary environments created on demand and removed when no longer needed. A significant advantage is enabling quick redeployment into another region during a major disaster, particularly in cold disaster recovery environments. IaC tools like ARM templates, Bicep, and Terraform can save session host information and VM images for quick redeployment during recovery processes, improving resiliency. IaC is referenced as a disaster recovery option for services such as API Management (alongside APIOps), Event Grid, and Virtual WAN, where it provides version control and rollback capability through Git repositories and ARM templates, enabling repeatable deployments across environments.

IaC enables consistent deployments across numerous Azure services, including Load Balancer and other networking components, Service Bus, databases, and Machine Learning workspaces, compute clusters, and deployment environments. IaC-deployed infrastructure can be automatically scanned for security vulnerabilities and subjected to policy enforcement, and it can be used to create isolated production clones for testing purposes. However, highly layered, modularized, or heavily parameterized designs can increase the chance of accidental misconfiguration, requiring careful design and governance to maintain the reliability benefits IaC is intended to provide.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is an approach for deploying and managing Azure Virtual Desktop environments using tools like ARM templates, Bicep, and Terraform.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as code (IaC) is a strategy developed by the platform team for automating deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as code (IaC) organizes infrastructure deployments through code, enabling repeatable, auditable provisioning and configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a method used to create, update, and destroy guest VMs, working together with tags and configuration management tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is an approach to automated deployments offering benefits in knowledge, time, cost, testing, scaling, and standardization.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as code (IaC) is an approach to automate SAP workload deployments with minimal human intervention for scalable and consistent results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeefe2d63573562646e740d09fa6d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5200ddd62ebcb8e16dece7ddc1422557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4be12a3d391245ffca95ba2ca936932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddf6c44166c12054fa8380f137ab849a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2431ac43eabe818a5350eafb1e23d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a87895e99b347e4b871e414149100339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc830fbd68e22812a74bf3c788ef10f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f84fdf8398257ab3343f339b69880c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c203348328e5589b8f4b6fa4101a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-198a3a5ea0d4ee6048ded7764b7c4702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4285f3b1d912059b039db58435cd461a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b359b45da7d6b789373380187e0a7ede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9477f91dc0a48476ae389364456c73e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6949b9609e5ef191a10ce0e8da0a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2789d17a06aaa84