</node>
<node id="Azure DevOps">
  <data key="d0">Azure DevOps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DevOps is a comprehensive set of development tools and services that enable teams to plan, develop, test, and deliver software efficiently. It serves as a CI/CD platform allowing users to define pipelines and automate build, test, deployment, and reporting tasks, utilizing service connections and build agents. It functions as an orchestration tool for Infrastructure as Code (IaC) deployment and management, and supports deploying source code changes and pipeline configurations across environments, including function apps and resource deployments with consumer coordination.

Azure DevOps is hosted in a single Azure region and offers a rich feature set for deployment tooling. It supports third-party tools and plugins that can be automated as part of CI/CD pipelines, including security and performance testing to identify bottlenecks. It can serve as a repository platform for hosting catalog items for Azure Deployment Environments and provides tools for repository management, pipelines, and continuous integration, integrating with source control systems like GitHub.

Beyond CI/CD, Azure DevOps serves as a platform for backlog management, enabling teams to turn retrospective insights into actionable items. Well-Architected Review recommendations can be imported into Azure DevOps for backlog tracking. It supports work item integration with Application Insights and can be used for automated backup and workspace replication in disaster recovery scenarios. It also functions as a task management and ITSM tool that can be integrated with alerts, including Azure VMware Solution alerts.

Azure DevOps provides CI/CD pipeline technology for machine learning operations, including model deployment. It can be combined with Azure Machine Learning pipelines for ML deployment workflows and is accessed by Build Agent MLOps components for automated deployment. Additionally, it is used for automating image builds and CI/CD pipelines for Azure Virtual Desktop session hosts.

Azure DevOps has capabilities that overlap with GitHub, and the two platforms can be used together for deployment and management workflows. It is broadly described as a collection of services for building collaborative, efficient, and consistent development practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddf6c44166c12054fa8380f137ab849a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2431ac43eabe818a5350eafb1e23d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72528a20eb854ac9dc78db25344d18e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2831164a5771887ad5de08caa27249ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4285f3b1d912059b039db58435cd461a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac8f606b24c325a1ba25f35deaa3143&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb22f500a9418e75c787f58356ea6d23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c12853dd39d9a9a4beefa63014102d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b1c021188faeb6dd44f9550bc2c4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b01c06cbc36f4fb17c08ab0e3baafd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8fc58eb81af85bd1aa7f2b1f5ef9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140bb45f92c520fcbeae833dad674c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a945886318d32ffa9cc3299a5304135e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113f1dee9dacbd713204570906b3c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c45aa9611048afab38755ade22af2f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15da9f5a57c9361e9e5487fa0eea82</data>
