</node>
<node id="Stress Testing">
  <data key="d0">Stress Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress testing applies activities that overload existing resources to determine solution limits and verify the system's ability to recover gracefully.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress testing helps identify limitations of system components such as network components or databases that cannot appropriately scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress testing pushes a workload beyond its normal limits to identify breaking points and measure recovery ability, determining resilience and robustness.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress testing determines system limits, breaking points, and recovery behaviors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d20a250447d571c0a31d1f1f211c8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
