</node>
<node id="AIOps">
  <data key="d0">AIOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AIOps, or AI for IT Operations, is a methodology that applies artificial intelligence and machine learning techniques to automate, enhance, and optimize IT operations. It involves using ML models to correlate, analyze, and prioritize operational and observability data from various environments, enabling the detection, diagnosis, and prediction of system issues. By leveraging health data and application telemetry as inputs, AIOps models analyze trends and predict potential problems before they impact users.

AIOps encompasses a broad range of applications, including automating and optimizing incident triage and proactive measures within platforms such as Azure Monitor, as well as integrating AI methodologies into CI/CD pipelines to detect regressions and prevent negative deployment impacts. The approach involves continuous model training, scoring, and improvement to ensure operational procedures and triggers are continually refined, ultimately enhancing overall operational efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9f3d6861109aed1a61babb89793d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb</data>
