<node id="CI/CD">
  <data key="d0">CI/CD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CI/CD, which stands for Continuous Integration and Continuous Delivery/Deployment, is a software development practice focused on automating the build, test, and deployment pipeline. It enables teams to frequently and reliably deliver changes across environments by automating pipeline definition, execution, testing, and deployment processes.

CI/CD is a core component of DevOps and Agile development methodologies, promoting developer agility through features such as short-lived development environments and faster build times. Its pipelines are designed to support frequent deployments, including for mission-critical workloads, ensuring operational readiness and reliability.

Beyond traditional software delivery, CI/CD is also used in specialized scenarios such as AIOps, where it supports deployment updates, operational readiness tests, and real-time scoring processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous integration and continuous deployment pipelines used for automated application development lifecycle management.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous integration/continuous delivery pipeline that enables disaster recovery, preproduction testing, and resource replication.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) is a software delivery approach that can be optimized for sustainability through scaling agents, caching, and splitting repositories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddf6c44166c12054fa8380f137ab849a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf3ec0d59d6b08f5ae5935149fe9a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7f774cbe85718aeb4ca8377bca84b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f800b00991f43e7769f067d21a566bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec86357472a346e4f83fb7543b0e24c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7b8a756934ab64251ea5a23e73f2de</data>
