<node id="Azure Resource Manager Templates">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Manager Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ARM templates are infrastructure as code artifacts used for deploying Azure resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates define and deploy infrastructure using code for efficient, repeatable, and consistent resource deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates are Azure-native tools for deploying infrastructure as code.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates are declarative IaC technologies for provisioning Azure Front Door.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates enable automated Service Bus configuration backup including namespace metadata and definitions.&lt;SEP&gt;ARM templates are declarative templates for provisioning host pools, session hosts, and application groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2831164a5771887ad5de08caa27249ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb40dfedb445538dcaca461fef2278f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-code-infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tools-processes.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development Environment">
  <data key="d0">Development Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development environments are short-lived environments with lower reliability and security requirements, created for parallel feature development.&lt;SEP&gt;A sandbox space where developers write, test, experiment, build, and integrate code changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Development environments are designed for development, testing, and debugging with shorter lifecycles and lower requirements for reliability, capacity, and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Or Staging Environment">
  <data key="d0">Test Or Staging Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Test or staging environments are short-lived environments used for validation that should reflect production for reliability, capacity, and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Validation And Testing">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Validation And Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous validation and testing describes appropriate test cycles performed to ensure bug-free deployment to production for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A section describing appropriate tests for mission-critical workloads, emphasizing rigorous and ongoing testing practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous validation and testing is a critical activity for validating application code and infrastructure health across reliability, performance, availability, security, quality, and scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated testing within CI/CD processes including load testing and chaos experimentation to validate thresholds and identify risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue/Green Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Blue/Green Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model requiring at least two identical deployments where traffic is gradually transitioned from the active (blue) to the new (green) deployment, enabling zero-downtime upgrades.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a strategy that uses transient resource duplication to mitigate reliability impact during deployments, increasing costs during those periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a deployment model used in operational excellence practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model that introduces side-by-side deployments on production platforms, requiring preemptive scaling or dormant deployments for rollback support.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a strategy that uses transient resource duplication to mitigate reliability impact during deployments, increasing costs during those periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a deployment model used in operational excellence practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model that introduces side-by-side deployments on production platforms, requiring preemptive scaling or dormant deployments for rollback support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staging Environment">
  <data key="d0">Staging Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Short-lived environments that reflect production for testing and validation, destroyed after test validations are complete.&lt;SEP&gt;An environment closely resembling production used for final testing and validation before deploying to production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Production Environment">
  <data key="d0">Production Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environments requiring the highest levels of reliability, capacity, and security, with special data management needs.&lt;SEP&gt;The production environment is the real-world deployment environment that the test environment aims to mirror.&lt;SEP&gt;The production environment is the source of truth for understanding how a workload behaves in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The production environment serves customers and must be reliable, meeting specific SLAs for performance and uptime.&lt;SEP&gt;Production environment is the live environment where workloads run, serving as the baseline for preproduction similarity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0678a076bfce587ea6972a7bddad9432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Front Door">
  <data key="d0">Azure Front Door</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Front Door is a globally distributed Microsoft Azure service that functions as a reverse proxy and gateway solution, providing HTTP/HTTPS load balancing, traffic routing, content delivery, and traffic acceleration across multiple regions. It leverages Anycast protocol connectivity to route user requests to the nearest edge location, improving latency for geographically dispersed users. As a global Azure resource, it is not deployed into a specific region and provides shared public IP addresses designed to be internet-facing with built-in security filtering. It functions as a modern cloud Content Delivery Network (CDN) using the Microsoft global edge network with hundreds of points of presence worldwide, caching both static and dynamic content closer to end-users.

Azure Front Door offers Web Application Firewall (WAF) integration, TLS/SSL certificate management and renewal, health probes, session affinity, load distribution, and built-in DDoS protection. It serves as a single point of entry exposing an API for customer requests, with TLS termination, WAF policies, and routing rules. Its service tags can be used in Network Security Groups (NSGs) to validate legitimate backend traffic, and its WAF events can be analyzed through Security Copilot integration. It provides managed certificates with automatic provisioning and renewal, including wildcard domain support, along with caching, compression, and performance optimization for web workloads.

Azure Front Door supports customer domains, URL paths, private endpoints, and different plan tiers affecting cost. It supports replica-aware, priority-based global routing and can orchestrate automated traffic transitions for blue-green deployment strategies. It serves as a dedicated ingress point for easier reconfiguration during recovery steps and is commonly used for routing traffic globally across AKS clusters and other internet-facing workloads. As a networking resource, it can be shared among multiple customers to reduce costs and operational overhead, and it can affect network traffic billing in multi-region solutions.

Azure Front Door is positioned as an alternative to both Azure Load Balancer and Traffic Manager for HTTP applications, offering additional features such as WAF integration, TLS termination, and content delivery. It can be used alongside Application Gateway for additional traffic handling and WAF protection, and is often combined with API Management for comprehensive API delivery scenarios. It is well-suited for multiple-region deployments to distribute traffic across stamps and ensure high availability, including cross-region redundancy. It is also used in AI workload deployment architectures as a gateway solution.

Azure Front Door carries a 99.99% availability SLA for successful HTTP GET operations, which may be adjusted to a 99.98% SLO in practice. Its endpoints are considered internal dependencies for workloads and are identified in failure mode analysis. It is used as a front-end for applications such as e-commerce websites, delivering and protecting global HTTP/S applications spanning multiple Azure regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a global load balancer used to route traffic to closer regions and accelerate network traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a service whose TLS 1.2 cipher suites are used by Azure Virtual Desktop for encrypted connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door provides TLS 1.2 ciphers that Azure Virtual Desktop uses for encryption.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door supports file compression to reduce storage and bandwidth requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e048464dc928ee7d9ace1aae32cd84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654e7aada501f6fea6718cd59dbed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa7e37862e9b9978a85e7dde37bac4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0544ee58fb5345261d0d125500955a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd009330fd8bb700e86760925fa4ea4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eb4bf3421da46d9aac57d5ba0a0c195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443aa85fac21ccf603c8d3f8c5b909ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95454c21cf94702a9