<node id="Azure Mission-Critical">
  <data key="d0">Azure Mission-Critical</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An approach recommending blue/green deployment where infrastructure and applications are deployed together as part of a deployment stamp.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Load Generator">
  <data key="d0">User Load Generator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool provided in the Mission Critical Online reference implementation for generating synthetic user load for realistic testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue-Green Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Blue-Green Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue-Green Deployment is a deployment strategy that uses two identical infrastructure environments, referred to as "blue" and "green," to minimize downtime and mitigate performance impacts during software releases. The current production version runs in one environment (blue), while the updated version is deployed to the other (green). Traffic is then gradually shifted from the blue environment to the green environment. Once the transition is complete and the new version is verified, the old (blue) environment is decommissioned. This approach provides controlled traffic direction and enables safe, low-risk deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment is a deployment method used when no production downtime is acceptable.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment uses parallel topic configurations with traffic routing for safe deployment practices in Event Grid.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment uses parallel topic configurations with traffic routing for safe deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployments enable zero-downtime namespace transitions for Service Bus infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment is a method allowing a single endpoint to contain multiple deployments for safe rollouts.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment is a deployment strategy that enables safe rollout with traffic splitting between versions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4be12a3d391245ffca95ba2ca936932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe53a5474c5e4934795683b73b06789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc6dd32c7c960a85b9a30c11bc43659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d58b81465c40024b1e7d72578e9d17</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003847</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Testing">
  <data key="d0">Unit Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Unit testing confirms that application business logic works as expected and validates the overall effect of code changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit testing verifies individual components in isolation, runs quickly, provides immediate feedback, and is the lowest cost and highest value testing method.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit testing verifies syntax and functionality of individual code modules, should cover 100 percent of code and run in under 30 seconds.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit testing verifies syntax and functionality of individual code modules, should cover 100% of code, run under 30 seconds, and be part of continuous integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smoke Testing">
  <data key="d0">Smoke Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Smoke testing identifies whether infrastructure and application components are available and function as expected, typically testing a single virtual user session.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoke testing validates basic functionality such as API health endpoints to quickly detect infrastructure provisioning or network policy problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoke testing verifies that a workload can be stood up in a test environment and performs as expected without verifying component interoperability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UI Testing">
  <data key="d0">UI Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">UI testing validates that application user interfaces are deployed and that user interface interactions function as expected using automation tools.&lt;SEP&gt;UI testing detects visual, layout, and interaction regressions with high maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;UI testing is emphasized for customer-facing workloads alongside end-to-end testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Testing">
  <data key="d0">Performance Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance Testing is a methodology used to evaluate how a workload performs under different conditions, combining aspects of load and stress testing to validate performance and establish benchmark behaviors. It is a key capability used to define and continually evaluate application health under steady state reflective of production load.

Performance Testing encompasses various test types including load, stress, soak, spike, and compatibility tests, conducted in dedicated environments against baselines. It helps evaluate workload functionality across scenarios including response time, throughput, resource utilization, and stability.

Performance Testing involves running tests to measure and record performance metrics, monitoring health, and capturing performance issues. It serves as a method to detect performance issues and enable measure/improve cycles for workload teams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d20a250447d571c0a31d1f1f211c8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5fd47376a7e9081496e03cedc06a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0678a076bfce587ea6972a7bddad9432</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription-Scoped Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Subscription-Scoped Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subscription-scoped deployment involves using multiple Azure subscriptions as scale units to avoid single subscription scale limits for mission-critical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Level Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Service Level Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objectives (SLOs) define availability targets such as 99.9% vs. 99.999% availability for mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Level Objectives (SLOs) are measurable quality thresholds reflecting business commitments and user expectations.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantified availability targets often expressed as percentiles like 'five nines' (99.999%) used to classify criticality tiers.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Level Objectives (SLOs) represent the level of availability expected for a given workload, expressed as percentiles such as 99.99%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999133</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Time Objective (RTO) is the maximum acceptable time within which a business process, application, or solution must be restored to a working state after a disaster, failure, or other disruptive incident. It defines the target downtime threshold beyond which the impact on business operations becomes unacceptable, representing an organization's tolerance for downtime.

RTO serves as a critical metric in disaster recovery and business continuity planning, setting expectations for how quickly essential access, data, and functionalities should be recovered. It encompasses the restoration of services, systems, and operations, guiding organizations in designing appropriate recovery strategies and infrastructure to meet their defined time targets.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO is a metric defining acceptable downtime based on business needs for disaster recovery planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery time objective (RTO) defines the acceptable time to restore service after a disruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Time Objective (RTO) is a target metric defining the maximum acceptable downtime for workload recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO identifies how long Azure VMware Solution can be unavailable during a disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO defines the maximum acceptable time to restore normal operations after a data loss event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a1ff429a57f5b474e0f29cc10e052a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf77302eae466ce3d619b76c771db34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e0681994766d1adfc077b31464e02a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c634b3a2b27e4b06ab4fb93df82c41da</data>
