<node id="Recovery Point Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Point Objective (RPO) is a disaster recovery metric that defines the maximum acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a failure, incident, or disaster. It represents the target threshold indicating how much data an organization can afford to lose, essentially determining the point in time to which systems and data must be recovered.

RPO is closely tied to backup frequency, as more frequent backups reduce the window of potential data loss. It is baselined and maintained by monitoring backup and recovery processes, ensuring that the organization's data protection strategy aligns with its tolerance for data loss. RPO is defined based on business needs and is used to guide backup and replication strategies, including for specific workloads such as SAP environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a1ff429a57f5b474e0f29cc10e052a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e0681994766d1adfc077b31464e02a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c634b3a2b27e4b06ab4fb93df82c41da</data>
