<node id="Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Framework (WAF) is a comprehensive set of best practices, design principles, and guidance for building reliable, secure, scalable, and efficient cloud workloads. While particularly associated with Azure, it is applicable across cloud platforms and most workload types. It provides a structured approach to evaluating and optimizing architecture decisions across five pillars: Reliability, Security, Cost Optimization, Operational Excellence, and Performance Efficiency.

The framework guides the analysis, design, and optimization of workload architecture, recommending design patterns, setting technical targets for flows, and addressing trade-offs based on business requirements. It covers foundational principles of good design and their application to architecture components, including detailed guidance on processes, procedures, and design areas such as health modeling. The framework includes security checklist recommendations (e.g., SE:04 for segmentation) and principles relevant to quality gates across Security, Reliability, and Performance Efficiency. Advanced security measures and automation tooling should align with its pillars as part of workload design.

The Well-Architected Framework provides pillars, principles, checklists, and guides, offering rationalizations for architectural decisions with continuous improvement as a theme across all pillars. It favors simplicity, recommending off-the-shelf solutions over building in-house where appropriate. It includes a maturity model with a structured curriculum and milestones for workload teams, ensuring workloads run according to industry standards. The framework provides specific recommendations for optimizing code and infrastructure for peak performance, and guides recommendations for specific Azure services such as Azure Traffic Manager and Azure Virtual Desktop. It serves as the technical foundation for various workload-specific guidance, including SAP and mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A framework whose pillars apply to HPC workload design principles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Well-Architected Framework defines pillars for building resilient, secure, cost-effective, operationally excellent, and high-performance environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e048464dc928ee7d9ace1aae32cd84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43be904f845543056b0462aeab67302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ede2f555755748b50d3eff6168ec5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b96873d8c3872305fcc29094745223e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8e2c1079086f316dcae858bed1190c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d440b1a3c317835e0dd6ef617a4d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6200584afd66d7b2ca01f9fe20d183ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef06ef7197a8a530ba87de793b6cb9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2611a82124cb2d05996b048b560df89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d263497f5caeee5776927a85b56895&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d20533bbf7469e609a814919168f3cf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7ba45bf48a024a996731f69cab5301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d10ef40f70919a984cf031275099f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef9765311dfd798d022450d45e1c01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd12866b1c0a9d8fe76b6447e59f118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a75f6abfb52e7f12669ccabfaf886c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4057517613635840b