<node id="Active/Active Design">
  <data key="d0">Active/Active Design</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where solution components are distributed across multiple Availability Zones and Azure regions to maximize availability and achieve regional fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blast Radius Reduction And Fault Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Blast Radius Reduction And Fault Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of designing solutions in a resilient manner by anticipating failures and correlated impact from individual components to entire Azure regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Self-Healing">
  <data key="d0">Design For Self-Healing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A concept describing a system's ability to deal with failures automatically through pre-defined remediation protocols connected to failure modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Scale-Out">
  <data key="d0">Design For Scale-Out</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A concept focusing on horizontal growth by adding resource units in parallel instead of increasing existing resource sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observe Application Health">
  <data key="d0">Observe Application Health</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of monitoring application operation relative to a known healthy state to detect or predict reliability issues and enable swift remedial action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drive Automation">
  <data key="d0">Drive Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle emphasizing automation in all aspects of a cloud solution to minimize human error and improve reliability through automated testing, deployment, and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complexity Avoidance">
  <data key="d0">Complexity Avoidance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design consideration to avoid unnecessary complexity in solution design and operational processes to drive reliability and management efficiencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loosely Coupled Components">
  <data key="d0">Loosely Coupled Components</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method enabling independent testing, deployments, and updates to application components while minimizing inter-team dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automate Build And Release Processes">
  <data key="d0">Automate Build And Release Processes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of fully automating build and release processes to reduce friction, increase deployment velocity, and bring repeatability and consistency across environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Compute Services">
  <data key="d0">Managed Compute Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Using managed compute services and containerized architectures to reduce ongoing administrative and operational overhead of designing, operating, and scaling applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SIEM">
  <data key="d0">SIEM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SIEM, which stands for Security Information and Event Management, is an enterprise-grade security solution designed for advanced threat defense, security monitoring, and incident response. It functions by aggregating and consolidating security data from multiple sources into a central location, performing log analysis, correlation, and normalization of that data to detect anomalies and potential threats.

SIEM solutions offer built-in threat detection and intelligence capabilities, leveraging aggregated data and connecting to external feeds for threat intelligence. They generate alerts based on correlated and normalized data, enabling organizations to track security and audit events, manage incident notifications, and respond effectively to security incidents. SIEM can also receive streamed file access logs for unauthorized access detection and incident investigation.

As a form of specialized observability tooling, SIEM performs aggregation and threat intelligence across complex environments. It can be shared as a centralized resource across workloads, supporting centralized security log ingestion, storage, and analysis. SIEM is available on platforms such as Azure, with external security monitoring supported through Azure Event Hubs integration, and its capabilities are combined in Microsoft Sentinel for analyzing security events and logs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4a87b29a0d7646a31a3fd27442ab6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d280cc7c07462216af45547cce48d2f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c1925896ad2776a0d0431adee7f3d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbdc7bdb179c925972b2debe7a1d4a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af976d288fcb8191fe6fb55f44aaeba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0544ee58fb5345261d0d125500955a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-776c12fee2375faef068c91c8f0e42d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/establish-baseline.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/harden-resources.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/consolidation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005722</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Continuity">
  <data key="d0">Business Continuity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Planning and practice drills essential for maximizing resiliency in the event of unplanned downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Strategies for ensuring critical operations continue during and after disruptions, encompassing disaster recovery, personnel, communication, and processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Business continuity (BCuity) is a goal ensured through backup and recovery procedures, versioned backups, and reduced RTOs for Azure Databricks workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Business continuity involves implementing robust data protection to ensure availability, integrity, and recoverability during unexpected disruptions or disasters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15da9f5a57c9361e9e5487fa0eea82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disaster Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disaster Recovery (DR) is a structured set of strategies, plans, and procedures designed to restore workloads, systems, and data after failures, outages, security incidents, or other significant disruptive events. It encompasses planning, failover, failback, communication, and runbook procedures aligned with defined recovery targets to maximize business resiliency. DR is considered a mitigation strategy that all workloads must have regardless of reliability targets.

DR often involves maintaining a preserved safe system state to fail over to a secure secondary system or location, including geo-distant environment strategies to mitigate risk from large-scale geographic disasters. This includes the capability to quickly restore and redeploy critical data and configurations in another region during regional failures. It may be initiated when a system is shut down during incident response, enabling complete system recovery and restoration of workload functionality. Planning and practice drills are conducted frequently to iteratively improve procedures.

DR is distinguished from routine incident management, requiring specialized recovery efforts and a separate plan. It involves technical mitigations and processes for business continuity, including strategies for backing up and restoring infrastructure and APIs through built-in backup/restore and customer-managed options. Recovery time objectives must be aligned with business requirements, and automated backup processes should be established.

The complexity of disaster recovery can be increased by security controls. DR solutions such as backups increase workload surface area and require additional security controls. They can also lead to excess costs if they excessively satisfy recovery objectives. Organizations can optimize costs by choosing less expensive DR strategies for noncritical components, making it important to balance recovery capabilities with cost and security considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery involves implementing cross-region DR and availability zones for critical Azure Functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery involves rerouting traffic from a primary site to a backup site when the primary endpoint becomes degraded.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery (DR) involves replicating networking infrastructure across regions with consistent NSG and firewall rules for failover readiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery (DR) refers to strategies for recovering data and services after catastrophic outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery involves replicating primary data to a secondary location to ensure reliability when the primary location is inaccessible.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d20b573314239b2a88ca3deb8586c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9274b98dae68e1fda563c0a186872af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8fc58eb81af85bd1aa7f2b1f5ef9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2230ce3d7cb1e253eb90d2592e57fab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c00db143f490c3d917ea5c2345f79ef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453</data>
