</node>
<node id="Event Hubs">
  <data key="d0">Event Hubs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Hubs is an Azure messaging and event streaming platform service offering multiple tiers (Basic, Standard, Premium, Dedicated). It supports features such as throughput units, partitions, Capture, configurable retention periods, encryption, diagnostics, autoscaling, namespace-level isolation, consumer groups, and private endpoints with various security configurations.

Event Hubs is used to distribute telemetry processing, prevent single-point I/O bottlenecks, and handle log or event streams from API invocations requiring near real-time reactions. Key operational metrics include incoming and outgoing messages, and the service can provide custom metrics for autoscaling. Event Hubs is comparable to other Azure messaging services such as Event Grid and Service Bus.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Hubs is part of the Azure messaging ecosystem that integrates with Service Bus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c93d9704f35759a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0629c90da136e31cc7058b5a6a724b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb68bab7c1b474f207b34f9a74328e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Explorer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Explorer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Data Explorer is the technology that Log Analytics workspaces are based on for log storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Explorer uses Kusto Query Language (KQL) along with Log Analytics and Application Insights.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Explorer is an alternative to Log Analytics for executing queries to calculate health scores.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Explorer is a storage solution suited for trace logs.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Explorer is recommended for aggregation, analysis, exploring trends, and advanced analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Explorer is a component accessed by the Analyst persona.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7404990d0db645a738f8e03698df0941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a945886318d32ffa9cc3299a5304135e</data>
