  <data key="d5">1777005677</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correlation ID">
  <data key="d0">Correlation ID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Correlation ID is an identifier returned to callers for all calls, designed to facilitate troubleshooting and error tracking in distributed systems. It flows across service boundaries to track requests throughout an application and pinpoint the cause of failure across multiple services.

Correlation IDs are used to correlate application log events across critical application flows, such as user sign-in. They are included in telemetry data to support linking related events across system components, enabling end-to-end traceability across services in distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10f25ecc531e8935b205674b69f81d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56d3f8085e9faa95d82a0d2dfdacc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd636d5b13ec5dfd60e1f6764089382c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/monitoring-alerting-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic Light Model">
  <data key="d0">Traffic Light Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The traffic light model uses Green, Amber, and Red to represent Healthy, Degraded, and Unavailable application states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979826</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ExpressRoute">
  <data key="d0">ExpressRoute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ExpressRoute is an Azure networking service that provides private, dedicated connections between on-premises networks and Microsoft Azure, extending on-premises networks into the Microsoft cloud over private connections to reduce latency. It supports secure connectivity with bandwidths up to 100 Gbps, offering various circuit SKUs, bandwidth options, and pricing models. Each scale unit delivers 2 Gbps of guaranteed bandwidth.

ExpressRoute serves as a key Azure platform resource for on-premises communication and is commonly used in hybrid application scenarios. Through private peering, it enables access to Azure PaaS services from on-premises infrastructure, and it supports Microsoft peering connections for additional connectivity options. As a networking resource intended for shared use, it is typically placed in the hub network.

The service supports various resiliency configurations, including active-active mode, geo-redundancy, and Global Reach capabilities. ExpressRoute infrastructure encompasses circuits, ports, and gateways, each with associated metrics for monitoring and management. It delivers higher performance connectivity suited for production and mission-critical workloads requiring consistent bandwidth, though at substantially higher cost compared to other connectivity options. As a potential key dependency for hybrid architectures, ExpressRoute plays a critical role in enabling seamless integration between on-premises environments and Azure cloud services.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is a technology providing secure connections between cloud providers or to on-premises networks.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute provides a dedicated, high-performance, private connection between Azure and other cloud providers or on-premises networks with predictable performance.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is a connectivity service that introduces additional costs in hybrid networking scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is a private and resilient way to connect on-premises networks to different Azure regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a385162f5986599f4f996387e830cb95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df87985019f98b613c9173ac606646be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc00fa2fd7ff6664f6bb092b239d2134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aa82d5677c4e2d0032fac6a0dce0d32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0970265d9d614fdbdc9d79d3bcda0f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5720bc2c35e1af5035855500579a20d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8650a6bc1260a7fa43030a811f587363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d73a470d503be7e3a2f2ef63b96ec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b1ef27485e0c9c13eb1505e8179870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c00db143f490c3d917ea5c2345f79ef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51059245c825ad997eabe5a0dc767a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1a7707a8a1d8d9f53bc71b18814f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9c715c42ddea999c4f406ee448b176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea3b54c45d951e732cca09b525690b9</data>
