<node id="Azure SQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure SQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL is a relational database service offered by Microsoft Azure. It provides high-performance data storage and retrieval capabilities, and can be used to optimize dashboard data retrieval when Log Analytics query limits are reached. The service includes SQL insights capabilities for monitoring and analysis.

Azure SQL offers robust availability and security features, including auto-failover groups, failover clusters, Always On availability groups for automatic failover, and zone-redundant deployments. For security, it supports private endpoints and network security groups for protection.

Azure SQL is used in practical scenarios such as the e-commerce FMA (Failure Mode Analysis) example, demonstrating its applicability in real-world architectural patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure service that supports zone-redundant deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL is a database service supporting table partitioning, sliding window strategies, and performance advisory features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8</data>
