  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KQL">
  <data key="d0">KQL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">KQL (Kusto Query Language) is used to query and aggregate health metrics from InsightsMetrics and AzureMetrics to compute health status and scores.&lt;SEP&gt;KQL (Kusto Query Language) provides operators like 'union' to aggregate queries and mitigate Log Analytics query limits.&lt;SEP&gt;KQL (Kusto Query Language) supports obfuscated string literals to obfuscate query results displayed in workbooks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Health Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health modeling is an observability exercise and monitoring methodology that combines raw monitoring data with business context to quantify the overall health of a workload. It involves contextualizing monitoring values from infrastructure and applications to define healthy, unhealthy, and degraded states of critical flows, helping set a baseline and detect drift from expected operational states.

Health modeling is used to anticipate issues before they become incidents and affect customer experience, maximizing reliability through mapped and quantified application health states. It requires operational maturity and expertise in monitoring tools, typically implemented at higher maturity levels to integrate business insights with technical monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced monitoring and health modeling techniques that help detect and mitigate issues early before they escalate into full-scale disasters.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is an observability exercise that combines business context with raw monitoring data to quantify the overall health of a workload, helping set a baseline and detect drift from expected operational states.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling improves workload reliability by quantifying application health and building custom health models combining business context with monitoring data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4aefadf5c38a99059d5cac5297d2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e4a31ea43efb7a100f1df033cb0e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observability">
  <data key="d0">Observability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Observability is a concept and design practice focused on robust, contextualized instrumentation and monitoring to provide critical insight into application and system health. It encompasses structured monitoring capabilities including metrics, logs, traces, and telemetry data, built across infrastructure, application, and data layers. By connecting telemetry from these sources, Observability enables end-to-end system insights and deep analysis for root cause identification.

Observability operates at both the component level and aggregated across correlated user flows, providing a holistic view of system health status. It helps teams detect issues, track performance trends, and make operational decisions by understanding a system's internal state from external data. It provides meaningful alerting and supports successful incident response, ensuring operational teams can quickly identify and address issues.

Beyond reactive monitoring, Observability enables visibility into systems, supports data-driven decisions, and underpins proactive maintenance, quality and security assurance, capacity planning, and product management. It serves operational excellence by monitoring health events and validating workload design to inform future development. Observability is also treated as a feedback loop that uses production data to refine workload design, telemetry capture, and monitoring thresholds for continuous improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability enables visibility into systems, data-driven decisions, proactive maintenance, and capacity planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability refers to operations built for proactive maintenance, quality and security assurance, capacity planning, and product management.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability in testing ensures the test framework operates reliably and offers ongoing visibility into workload quality and health.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability ensures meaningful alerting and successful incident response for a workload.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability is a monitoring system design strategy focusing on aligning telemetry with health models and KPIs, standardizing data consolidation, and defining meaningful alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability in AI applications requires monitoring beyond traditional metrics, including model performance tracking, data quality monitoring, and user interaction analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeefe2d63573562646e740d09fa6d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7404990d0db645a738f8e03698df0941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c93d9704f35759a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44db748d8a4a0feea6626c78c05321a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Score">
  <data key="d0">Health Score</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A granular score calculated automatically from underlying metrics to represent the health of application components and user flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layered Application Health">
  <data key="d0">Layered Application Health</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A top-down design approach that defines application health in layered, measurable format by quantifying healthy and unhealthy states across components and user flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Level Objective">
  <data key="d0">Service Level Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objective (SLO) is a target for availability attainment calculated using the health model.&lt;SEP&gt;SLO is a target for availability attainment, calculated using the health model to distinguish service degradation from unavailability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Flows">
  <data key="d0">User Flows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User flows are mapped paths through an application whose health states are aggregated to represent overall application health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979829</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Analytics Workspace">
  <data key="d0">Log Analytics Workspace</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Log Analytics Workspace is a core Azure-native resource that serves as a centralized data sink and analytics platform within Azure Monitor. It stores and analyzes operational data, including diagnostic logs, activity logs from Microsoft Entra and other sources, Application Insights telemetry data, Azure Firewall metrics (such as throughput, health state, SNAT port utilization, and latency probe), Event Grid diagnostic data, MySQL logs, system/console logs, and Virtual WAN resource logs. Deployed into a specified Azure region, it provides capabilities for data collection, log ingestion, querying via KQL, query storage, data retention configuration, and cross-workspace queries.

Log Analytics Workspace is required to enable Azure Monitor Logs and functions as the underlying storage resource for Application Insights. It supports segmenting performance data, defining retention policies, long-term log retention, and forwarding diagnostic logs from various sources. It serves as a centralized log sink for workload monitoring data, centralized monitoring, diagnostics, and auditing. It also receives security audit events for real-time analysis using KQL queries and Virtual WAN logs for security monitoring, visibility, and troubleshooting.

Log Analytics Workspace is a designated workspace for collecting performance counters, events, and diagnostics from Azure Virtual Desktop session hosts. As an Azure resource, it features configurable access controls, security settings, pricing tiers, and data export capabilities. Log Analytics runs log queries directly against this workspace, making it the foundational component for log-based monitoring and analysis in Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics workspace is the destination for collecting logs from Azure VMware Solution private cloud guest VMs when deploying Microsoft Sentinel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d39895fc4a2ce3e45eeca7bf801519ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c93d9704f35759a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b01c06cbc36f4fb17c08ab0e3baafd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32bb35f93b689b12c3d63f12dc276ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11229197c05f5be9b778a1918888ee7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f94f551ab29e43c1a22f727367fe189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ab50ed5aab47b600c04c6b913d6a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771b01fe7618e75e298642ca2a2cb0e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d73a470d503be7e3a2f2ef63b96ec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570</data>
