</node>
<node id="Sampling">
  <data key="d0">Sampling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sampling can be enabled in Application Insights to reduce telemetry volume and optimize data ingest costs.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique to reduce telemetry volume and costs by collecting only a representative subset of data.&lt;SEP&gt;Sampling is a configuration technique to control data collection based on criticality, available in OpenTelemetry Distro and Application Insights SDKs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sampling is a technique used in Application Insights to reduce data traffic and storage costs while preserving statistically correct analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37afa41294d82e5e5fb34db4fe81fec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-552e7e27f46d45ef522cfd330748f26e</data>
