<node id="Azure Standard Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Standard Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Standard Load Balancer is an Azure load balancing SKU designed for internal traffic distribution, providing a 99.99% SLA across Availability Zones. Unlike the Basic SKU, it is backed by an SLA, making it suitable for production workloads requiring high availability.

Azure Standard Load Balancer also provides cross-region routing capabilities for managing global traffic. However, its Cross-Region feature is in preview with technical limitations and is not recommended for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DNS">
  <data key="d0">Azure DNS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DNS is a shared foundational service that serves as a global platform dependency for almost all Azure services. It is a global service providing both public and private zone name resolution with built-in zone and geo redundancy, making it resilient to regional outages through automatic redundancy across multiple regions.

Azure DNS provides alias records that couple DNS record lifecycle with Azure resources, preventing dangling DNS entries. It is also used alongside Traffic Manager for disaster recovery implementations.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS is an Azure service integrated with Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-257827ee036f98e6274522ad2bfee550&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2230ce3d7cb1e253eb90d2592e57fab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Web Application Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Azure Web Application Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) is a firewall service that provides layer 7 security for inbound HTTP/HTTPS traffic. It can be deployed on Azure Front Door at network edge locations to inspect every incoming request, supporting both built-in and custom rules in detection or prevention mode. Its capabilities include OWASP Top 10 protection, rate limiting, SQL-injection rules, and cross-site scripting prevention.

Azure WAF blocks most DDoS threats and protects ingress traffic. It also integrates with Microsoft Security Copilot for AI-powered threat analysis of events from Azure Front Door and Azure Application Gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall is a security feature available in Azure Application Gateway or Azure Front Door for filtering network traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) provides rule sets to detect and block malicious traffic, bot protection, IP restriction, geo-filtering, and rate limiting.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall is a security capability offered by Azure Application Gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa7e37862e9b9978a85e7dde37bac4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608026926818db1b277afce5e06e8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Global Backbone Network">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Global Backbone Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft global backbone network is used by Azure Front Door for optimized connectivity between edge nodes and backends.&lt;SEP&gt;The Microsoft global backbone network is used by Azure Front Door for optimized connectivity between edge nodes and backends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Traffic Routing">
  <data key="d0">Global Traffic Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global traffic routing is the practice of distributing traffic across multiple active regional deployment stamps using a global routing service.&lt;SEP&gt;Global traffic routing is the practice of distributing traffic across multiple active regional deployment stamps using a global routing service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multicloud Active-Active Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Multicloud Active-Active Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A multicloud active-active deployment approach provides broader redundancy to global outage scenarios but introduces significant operational complexities.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach using active stamps across two or more cloud providers with redundant third-party routing for global routing, though not recommended due to operational complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;A multicloud active-active deployment approach provides broader redundancy to global outage scenarios but introduces significant operational complexities.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach using active stamps across two or more cloud providers with redundant third-party routing for global routing, though not recommended due to operational complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anycast Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Anycast Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Anycast protocol is used by Azure Front Door with split TCP for optimized global connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Anycast protocol is used by Azure Front Door with split TCP for optimized global connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Application Gateway is a regional, managed Azure service that functions as a web traffic load balancer and application delivery controller, specifically designed for HTTP/HTTPS applications. It serves as an alternative to Azure Load Balancer, providing features such as TLS/SSL termination, URL-based routing, session affinity, health probes for monitoring backend availability, and the ability to choose TLS versions and cipher suites.

From a security perspective, Azure Application Gateway includes integrated Web Application Firewall (WAF) capabilities that scan for and block OWASP attack types, securing HTTP/HTTPS traffic. It provides network isolation and traffic filtering within regional deployment stamps, IDPS capabilities, and can integrate with Azure Web Application Firewall for additional protection. WAF events can be analyzed through Security Copilot integration.

Azure Application Gateway supports flexible traffic management through listeners and URL path-based routing, enabling density across deployments. It can distribute traffic across stamps in single-zone deployments and supports routing for hybrid and on-premises services. The service is used in various Azure deployment architectures, including AI workload deployments, serving as an Azure-native networking device for inbound traffic control and application traffic management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa7e37862e9b9978a85e7dde37bac4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0544ee58fb5345261d0d125500955a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc3e5ddb4441b86b0ef64d617182432b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d58b81465c40024b1e7d72578e9d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a6bdb7b9ebcb55bb58103735c0c58a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/consolidation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
