<node id="Service Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Service Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Endpoints provide connectivity to Azure services that don't support Private Link, with data exfiltration risk considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Endpoints provide connectivity to Azure services that don't support Private Link, with data exfiltration risk considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Service endpoints provide network integration without private IP addresses as an alternative to private endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Service endpoints route traffic to a service over the Azure network backbone as an alternative to private endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Service endpoints are an Azure networking feature used for connecting to resources hosted in customers' Azure environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653342d517c710c9f67df8e6155d05a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b1ef27485e0c9c13eb1505e8179870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51059245c825ad997eabe5a0dc767a97</data>
