  <data key="d5">1777004588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue-Green Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Blue-Green Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue-Green Deployments are a deployment strategy that uses parallel, duplicate resources (such as side-by-side subnets) to facilitate updated regional deployment stamps. This approach progressively rolls out changes to avoid inconsistent states, enabling testing in production without disruption.

Blue-Green Deployments are considered a safe deployment pattern that enhances flexibility and reliability during releases. They are commonly used with immutable environments, where the "blue" environment runs the current version while the "green" environment hosts the updated version, allowing seamless switchover between the two.&lt;SEP&gt;Stamp-level blue-green deployments increase confidence in releasing changes and enable zero-downtime upgrades for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployments are a release strategy to minimize downtime when deploying new model versions.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployments manage application lifecycle by using staging environments and weighted traffic distribution during updates.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployments are a deployment strategy used to validate sustainability impact and prevent inefficient workloads from reaching full production scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e912a1ac7fa5ab0139e0fac99a203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2789d17a06aaa84a6ce5fba59172ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35655a1a35d30fe6c5b864675c7afdb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908c83624526e94d8d2df8848b672966</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainable-ai-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity As A Security Perimeter">
  <data key="d0">Identity As A Security Perimeter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity as a security perimeter is a design approach that uses identity-based access control between service components instead of network-level controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Identity as a security perimeter is a design approach that uses identity-based access control between service components instead of network-level controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546</data>
