  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Azure Backbone">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Azure Backbone</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft Azure backbone is the network infrastructure ensuring connectivity between public endpoints hosted on Azure without traversing the public internet.&lt;SEP&gt;The Microsoft Azure backbone is the network infrastructure ensuring connectivity between public endpoints hosted on Azure without traversing the public internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kubenet">
  <data key="d0">Kubenet</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Kubenet is a network plugin for AKS suitable for scenarios with limited available IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight networking model where AKS nodes integrate within a virtual network but pods exist in a virtual overlay network.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubenet is a lightweight network plugin recommended for scenarios with limited IP address ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubenet is a network plugin for AKS suitable for scenarios with limited available IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A lightweight networking model where AKS nodes integrate within a virtual network but pods exist in a virtual overlay network.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubenet is a lightweight network plugin recommended for scenarios with limited IP address ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubenet is a basic network plugin option for AKS clusters, compared against Azure CNI for network model selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5321cfe4fbc08d735ac5eac02e84e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641</data>
