  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Express Route">
  <data key="d0">Express Route</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Express Route is an Azure service providing secure and scalable on-premises network connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Express Route is a connectivity method for connecting Azure regions, on-premises networks, and can be used for traffic hair-pinning to optimize costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Express Route is an Azure service providing secure and scalable on-premises network connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Express Route is a connectivity method for connecting Azure regions, on-premises networks, and can be used for traffic hair-pinning to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983281</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure NAT Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Azure NAT Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure NAT Gateway is a scalable NAT solution supporting 64,000 connections per assigned outbound IP address, with up to 16 IP addresses per gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway mitigates port exhaustion issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway is a scalable NAT solution supporting 64,000 connections per assigned outbound IP address, with up to 16 IP addresses per gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway mitigates port exhaustion issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway is used to address SNAT port exhaustion for outbound traffic, though it lacks availability zone redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure NAT Gateway helps mitigate SNAT port exhaustion by providing extra SNAT ports for outbound connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Load Balancer is a replica-aware load balancing service in Azure that provides direct internet outbound connectivity for virtual machines or compute instances. It supports health probes, whose traffic is allowed by default in network security group inbound rules. Azure Load Balancer does not require client affinity. It has limitations with high concurrent outbound traffic, which NAT Gateway helps avoid.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Load Balancer is a global load balancing service that routes traffic closer to users, supports health probes, zone redundancy, and acts as a reverse proxy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Load Balancer is an Azure-native service that performs Layer-4 load balancing for UDP and TCP, providing low latency and high availability for regional and global deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Load Balancer pings VMs to detect unhealthy VMs and reroute traffic accordingly.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Load Balancer distributes traffic across zones for high availability and fault tolerance across multiple Azure availability zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b82e5bd8bced74ea376399d3355126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Address Translation">
  <data key="d0">Network Address Translation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NAT is a compute operation in the networking stack that translates traffic from virtual networks to the internet, which can impact performance at scale.&lt;SEP&gt;NAT is a compute operation in the networking stack that translates traffic from virtual networks to the internet, which can impact performance at scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Address Translation (NAT) automatically translates IP addresses to avoid overlapping IP address conflicts in cross-network connectivity scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1a7707a8a1d8d9f53bc71b18814f3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RFC 1918">
  <data key="d0">RFC 1918</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RFC 1918 defines the address allocation for private internet IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;RFC 1918 defines the address allocation for private internet IP addresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VPN">
  <data key="d0">VPN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VPN serves as a failover connectivity mechanism providing additional redundancy alongside ExpressRoute.&lt;SEP&gt;VPN serves as a failover connectivity mechanism providing additional redundancy alongside ExpressRoute.&lt;SEP&gt;VPN provides access to on-premises or Azure environments, configured with IPSec protocol for secure communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Egress">
  <data key="d0">Internet Egress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Internet egress is a foundational network requirement for mission-critical applications to facilitate external communication including user interaction and application integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Internet egress is a foundational network requirement for mission-critical applications to facilitate external communication including user interaction and application integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
