<node id="WAF">
  <data key="d0">WAF</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">WAF (Web Application Firewall) provides centralized protection for web applications by blocking or detecting suspicious requests on publicly exposed endpoints. It defends against common exploits and vulnerabilities such as SQL injections, cross-site scripting, and file executions.

WAF offers security features including managed rules, bot protection, rate limiting, geo-filtering, and request body inspection to restrict and inspect incoming traffic. It integrates with Azure Application Gateway to protect applications at the network edge and with Azure Front Door to provide security metrics, logs, and advanced protection capabilities. WAF also supports diagnostic logs, including firewall logs, when working with Application Gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;WAF (Web Application Firewall) is a security feature for protecting HTTP applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f471ce6b86ced91e851ed4cd06f0521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df0cc69c8383501073ee148f940f5d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d314b16e3b2b8776b889c2beaec2890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a007dbfba3cef886b2cc00b13f46310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4</data>
