<node id="Zero-Trust Model">
  <data key="d0">Zero-Trust Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A security model applied in critical application environments where no standing write access is granted and operations occur only through automated processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration As Code">
  <data key="d0">Configuration As Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle requiring engineering investment where configuration settings and updates are defined as code for consistent release and update processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration as code is the practice of treating configuration changes with the same rigor as code, including testing and progressive rollouts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-222e44d67db5ca1f719f77ecd8131ebe</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/devops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Key Vault">
  <data key="d0">Azure Key Vault</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Key Vault is a secure secret, key, and certificate management service provided by Microsoft Azure. It serves as a hardened repository for managing application secrets such as passwords, connection strings, API keys, database credentials, authentication tokens, preshared keys (including Redis and third-party secrets), certificates (including TLS/SSL certificates), and cryptographic keys—all stored outside of source code in an encrypted environment with audit capabilities.

The service offers features including expiry settings, key rotation policies, seamless certificate and secret rotation to minimize performance effects, alerting for upcoming expirations, access audit logging, and secure access control through Azure RBAC and access policies for identity-based management. It stores certificates with extensions that automatically refresh them when changes are detected. It provides high availability through automatic redundancy across multiple regions, operating as a global Azure service with HSM backing, transaction limits, and a defined security boundary.

Azure Key Vault is commonly used as a typical internal dependency in cloud workloads, playing a critical role in scaling operations and overall availability. It stores customer-managed keys and secrets, manages credentials required by workloads to access services such as Blob Storage, Azure Files, and Event Hubs, and supports customer-managed key encryption of data at rest, including cross-tenant scenarios. It integrates with services like Azure Databricks for secret scopes, Azure App Configuration for secure application configuration management, and Azure Virtual Desktop as a security service. The service is a Microsoft Entra protected resource, accessible via mechanisms such as AKS Workload IDs, and is also accessed by the Discriminative AI Data Scientist as a component.

Azure Key Vault serves important roles in database security, providing unified life cycle management for TDE (Transparent Data Encryption) protectors and Always Encrypted column master keys with audit logging. It backs up TDE encryption keys for customer-managed key scenarios, protects credentials and encryption keys for SQL Managed Instance, manages certificates for Service Fabric clusters, and enables centralized management of encryption keys within dedicated instances to prevent accidental key loss.

Azure Key Vault is a recommended technology for security and access control, and a recommended approach for storing secrets needed in automated deployment processes. Beyond cloud application secrets, it serves as a secure external location for storing BitLocker recovery keys. Its centralized storage for secrets, encryption keys, and access credentials—combined with support for regular rotation, audit logging, and robust access policies—makes it an essential component of cloud infrastructure for secure management of sensitive materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Key Vault is a service used for key management, secret storage, and encryption operations in Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Key Vault is a security service integrated with Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Key Vault is a service used to securely store encryption keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Key Vault stores application secrets, customer-managed keys, and supports database encryption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31026fe6d1c4bec43b15c40b1c162e07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b24002e6c6a1f793f274780f10d2a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937b1809a20f2b2148f344a58b016317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc3e5ddb4441b86b0ef64d617182432b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653342d517c710c9f67df8e6155d05a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e36fb889991403b16d790b11d406033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af193ca86913bf526ac2830012c0e345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef