</node>
<node id="Azure VM Image Builder">
  <data key="d0">Azure VM Image Builder</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure VM Image Builder is a tool to automate build and maintenance processes for customized images.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure VM Image Builder is a tool for building VM images.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure VM Image Builder is a tool for building repeatable processes for hardened OS images.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure VM Image Builder is an infrastructure as code resource for standardized deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure VM Image Builder is a tool used to automate the build, update, system preparation, and distribution processes for golden images.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a7fd7af178968ccbf8fd562e0e84a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d280cc7c07462216af45547cce48d2f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb02bc2525ef384d46a37259cf6a9cf3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/harden-resources.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment-Time Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Deployment-Time Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment-time retrieval is a secret management approach where secrets are read from the secret store and injected into the application at deployment time, such as environment variables in Kubernetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A secret retrieval approach where secrets are injected during deployment, requiring full redeployment for updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application-Startup Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Application-Startup Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A secret retrieval approach where secrets are fetched at application startup, allowing easier rotation but creating runtime dependency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Runtime Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Runtime Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The most secure secret retrieval approach where secrets are fetched at runtime, preventing the application platform from accessing secrets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Identities">
  <data key="d0">Managed Identities</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Managed Identities are identities for Azure resources managed by Microsoft Entra ID (formerly Azure Active Directory). They allow Azure resources—including App Service instances, Container Apps, Function Apps, and AKS clusters—to authenticate to other services supporting Microsoft Entra authentication without storing secrets, managing service principal credentials, or handling credentials directly. By enabling applications to authenticate via an identity provider, managed identities help minimize the risk of credential leakage and theft.

Managed Identities automatically rotate and protect credentials, eliminating the need for manual credentials management. They remove credential management overhead for service-to-service communication patterns, application-to-instance connectivity, cross-service integrations, and database access (eliminating the need for database keys or credentials). They are favored over hard-coded secrets and are recommended as the instance identity for Azure service integration.

Managed Identities are classified as nonhuman identities and can replace human access to processes such as deployments and database changes. As non-human accounts within Identity and Access Management (IAM), they often have incorrect permissions and should be included in permissions audits to ensure proper security governance. They are recommended for automated authentication in production workloads to maintain security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31026fe6d1c4bec43b15c40b1c162e07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654e7aada501f6fea6718cd59dbed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf9fd57985f14c81b7d1b9d2924d1bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2431ac43eabe818a5350eafb1e23d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32bb35f93b689b12c3d63f12dc276ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d89d8bc1094d5427b9923c0759b965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc3e5ddb4441b86b0ef64d617182432b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8</data>
