<node id="RBAC">
  <data key="d0">RBAC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is a security method for regulating access to resources based on roles assigned to users. It follows the principle of least privilege, controlling what actions authorized users can perform and managing permissions across various contexts including Azure resources, identity components, and secret management systems.

RBAC is applied in production CD pipelines to mitigate security risks and in DevOps tooling to manage service principal access. It grants access to manage resources within segments through role assignments, ensuring role-specific visibility with appropriate security controls. RBAC can be enhanced with conditions based on context, actions, and attributes for more granular permission management. It is also used with Microsoft Entra ID to create logical access control boundaries for identity-based segmentation, such as in Event Hubs.

RBAC enforces separation between development, testing, and production environments through access control policies. It restricts access to Application Gateway's control plane to authorized identities only, limits who can create, resize, or configure database servers, and restricts access to credentials. RBAC is used to block actions that can lead to overspending on storage resources and is included in extended deployment templates for MySQL flexible server.

RBAC serves as an access control mechanism in AKS authentication and configuration policies, assigns least-privilege access roles for Event Grid operations, delegates permissions with built-in roles for platform administrators and workload operators, limits access for operations on Azure NetApp Files through custom roles, and manages workspace access permissions using the principle of least privilege.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-based access control (RBAC) controls who can modify Virtual WAN configuration using built-in or custom roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-based access control assigns permissions like Network Contributor and Reader roles to prevent unauthorized configuration changes.&lt;SEP&gt;RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) is used to block actions that can lead to overspending as part of cost guardrails.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-based access control (RBAC) is a system for managing authorization based on user roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) delegation schema implements least-privilege access using built-in Azure Virtual Desktop roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Role-based access control assigns roles and permissions based on the principle of least privilege to control access to workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caf8d0c8419c804f864143fd95c9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca94eb8d1a3fa16fe190b0f6eecd280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8103c464163f3ff725a5c23642a7e869&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd64e0b4a0a0a0b146d62e2b5b760fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec86357472a346e4f83fb7543b0e24c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570</data>
