<node id="Bicep">
  <data key="d0">Bicep</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bicep is a domain-specific, declarative infrastructure-as-code (IaC) language natively supported by Azure for deploying and provisioning Azure resources. It enables users to automate infrastructure deployments through scripted, repeatable, and consistent template-based configurations.

Bicep can be used to define and deploy a wide range of Azure resources, including storage accounts, MySQL flexible server resources, Azure SQL databases, Azure Databricks workspaces, Event Hubs namespaces, Azure Front Door instances, Log Analytics workspaces, Service Bus namespaces, Virtual WAN infrastructure, and Azure Virtual Desktop resources. Bicep files and modules can be used alongside ARM templates for consistent environment provisioning, allowing organizations to stamp out infrastructure units with repeatability and consistency.&lt;SEP&gt;Bicep is an infrastructure-as-code language used to configure Azure Virtual Desktop services.&lt;SEP&gt;Bicep is a tool for automating provisioning and configuration of resources in Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Bicep is an infrastructure-as-code language for defining and deploying Azure resources reproducibly.&lt;SEP&gt;Bicep is an infrastructure-as-code language used to automate Azure HPC deployments.</data>
