<node id="ARM Templates">
  <data key="d0">ARM Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ARM Templates, formally known as Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates, are an infrastructure-as-code (IaC) solution for automating Azure resource provisioning using declarative JSON syntax. They are Azure-native tools that enable consistent, version-controlled infrastructure deployment across a wide range of Azure services.

ARM Templates are used to define and deploy numerous Azure resources, including storage account configurations, Azure Databricks workspaces with parameterized configurations, Event Grid resources, Event Hubs resources (with property coverage and dependency management), and Log Analytics workspaces. They also support storing alerting resource configurations with alternate workspace settings to enable rapid failover scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates used to define and deploy infrastructure resources and automate deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;ARM templates are used for Service Bus namespace configuration with parameterization support for environment-specific settings.&lt;SEP&gt;ARM templates are used for consistent Service Bus infrastructure deployments as part of Infrastructure as Code.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager templates provide native Azure integration for repeatable infrastructure deployments using declarative syntax.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9477f91dc0a48476ae389364456c73e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ab50ed5aab47b600c04c6b913d6a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc6dd32c7c960a85b9a30c11bc43659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771b01fe7618e75e298642ca2a2cb0e4</data>
