  <data key="d5">1776999213</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure-As-Code">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure-As-Code</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) is a practice of deploying, configuring, and managing infrastructure and applications through code-based tools. It serves as a method for driving updates to application components via code-defined infrastructure, enabling consistent and automated provisioning across organizations.

IaC templates are maintained as a library for recovery, validation, troubleshooting, and root cause analysis during incidents. This approach is used as a standard for deploying resources, including during emergency fixes, and supports deploying clusters consistently while automating scaling, recovery, and maintenance.

IaC tools are used across organizations to streamline operations and should be aligned for consistency. They are employed across the MLOps lifecycle to manage and provision infrastructure. At more mature levels, IaC extends beyond basic deployment to include full configuration and management of infrastructure resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deb7d0f719a6be9318b32726b071565b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85dfff44e8e4c1e2d34f3f2fbc239ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d92f2138a13f47ba741d8618d3160dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/formalize-operations-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For Cloud">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For Cloud</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for Cloud, formerly known as Azure Security Center, is a comprehensive security monitoring, management, and governance service available on Azure. It functions as a security information and event management (SIEM) solution and cloud workload protection platform (CWPP), typically enabled for subscriptions containing mission-critical workload resources. It is also a default security feature included in Azure Local.

The platform provides built-in threat detection capabilities, analyzing logs, checking compromised IP addresses, and offering vulnerability scanning across various technology areas. It receives telemetry data and logs from Azure Monitor Agent to power its security insights. Microsoft Defender for Cloud triggers alerts when anomalies in activity occur, notifies administrators, and routes security detection alerts to security operations teams. It also sends Azure incident notifications to designated points of contact.

Microsoft Defender for Cloud discovers misconfigurations in Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and delivers workload protection solutions including network recommendations. It provides real-time protection for resources running in an App Service plan, security recommendations for Event Hubs namespaces, and visualization of network infrastructure and security status across virtual networks and regions. The platform also monitors security aspects of Machine Learning deployments.

Microsoft Defender for Cloud helps organizations track compliance through its regulatory compliance dashboard, monitoring baselines and alerting on deviations. It serves as an automated security governance tool to streamline resource compliance with security baselines, identifying areas of noncompliance with regulatory requirements, including those related to data storage services. The platform offers hardening capabilities, including server hardening, adaptive network hardening, and Docker host hardening.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud provides continual assessment of resource configuration against compliance controls and best practices, calculating an overall compliance score.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud is used to apply compliance standards and enable vulnerability management assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud provides cloud workload protection, vulnerability management, and compliance assessment for frameworks like PCI and ISO27001.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud provides cloud security posture management (CSPM).&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud is used for security monitoring of Azure VMware Solution workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Cloud provides advanced threat protection tools across Azure VMware Solution and on-premises VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36890a0152ce0c702b07e77948e4fe1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4a87b29a0d7646a31a3fd27442ab6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d280cc7c07462216af45547cce48d2f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d20b573314239b2a88ca3deb8586c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964d0aabb6a006eaf58781c2658f980a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-520b008ac150d01d52152b172f0a59b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea213cbc3ff82c4333ed2bb24ec62b5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c50c3fc68e8ca3e2a2600f5ec515c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc59486642305ff68ee1edaa445b8bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db16efb77d945a638ed3a142b84cba38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
