<node id="Threat Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Threat Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Threat Modeling is a structured, proactive engineering discipline and design practice used to identify, evaluate, and mitigate potential security threats to a system. It provides a risk-based approach to security design by systematically analyzing potential threats, attacks, vulnerabilities, and attack vectors that may affect a workload or application.

As a method, Threat Modeling produces reports of attack vectors prioritized by severity, enabling teams to develop appropriate security mitigations and countermeasures. It is applied early in the design phase to identify vulnerabilities and build hardening plans before they can be exploited. The practice extends beyond initial design to encompass code review and deployment pipelines, ensuring threats are identified throughout the development lifecycle.

Threat Modeling serves as a key component of maturing security practices within organizations, functioning as both an intensive exercise for building mitigation plans and a requirement for comprehensive security coverage across systems and processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Threat modeling is an exercise that points to key areas to ensure test coverage and frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9514c481f519092f6d4362611c52ecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6753f3d7315e92dc2b4f1d56644604</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/establish-baseline.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996855</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="STRIDE">
  <data key="d0">STRIDE</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">STRIDE is a lightweight risk framework for evaluating security threats across key threat vectors including spoofing, tampering, repudiation, information disclosure, denial of service, and elevation of privilege.&lt;SEP&gt;An industry-standard methodology for classifying threats to understand their nature and apply appropriate security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;STRIDE is an industry methodology used to classify threats and drive mitigation decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A threat modeling methodology that categorizes threats into six types: Spoofing, Tampering, Repudiation, Information disclosure, Denial of service, and Elevation of privilege.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense-In-Depth">
  <data key="d0">Defense-In-Depth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense-in-depth is a layered security approach applied to define and implement compensating mitigations for modeled threats.&lt;SEP&gt;A security principle applied by using localized network controls at all available network boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A security principle applied by using localized network controls at all available network boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense-in-depth is a security mentality applied alongside assume-breach in security hardening.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense-in-depth is a security strategy that applies multiple layers of controls to limit impact of breaches.&lt;SEP&gt;A security strategy that uses multiple layers of protection to safeguard systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d8a1fa2cefd5c5b3095c48727dd166b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8c5639aa16c2329aa96771580d1b65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/harden-resources.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996737</data>
