<node id="Virtual Network Injection">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Network Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual Network Injection provides dedicated private deployments for supported services such as App Service through an App Service Environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection deploys Azure services into a network, isolating applications from the internet and other services.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection provides custom network routing and private connectivity for Azure Databricks workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection provides custom network routing, private connectivity, and network-level redundancy for Azure Databricks workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection deploys Azure Databricks data plane resources into subnets within Azure Virtual Network for network isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection establishes network egress controls using custom route tables and network security groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual network injection is a method for establishing network egress controls for Azure Databricks workspaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e0fe247c84a41199e470c86f0e983f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Virtual Appliance">
  <data key="d0">Network Virtual Appliance</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Virtual Appliance (NVA) is an alternative to Azure Firewall Premium for deep packet inspection or TLS inspection requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;An NVA used for ingress to force all traffic from the internet through security inspection.&lt;SEP&gt;A network virtual appliance (NVA) is an alternative to Azure Firewall for routing internet traffic to detect and block threats.&lt;SEP&gt;A network virtual appliance (NVA) is a virtual appliance that can fail in a single zone and should be deployed with redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fa337fdf4c15ddf378bf74ac66c3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b3b849ac5683c426e666e8f3f3f48e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003346</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic Analytics">
  <data key="d0">Traffic Analytics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Traffic Analytics is a feature of Azure Network Watcher that analyzes and enriches virtual network flow logs, including NSG flow logs, to provide continuous visibility into network traffic. It surfaces actionable insights such as blocked traffic, malicious flows, active ports, suspicious traffic patterns, top talkers, threats, and misconfigurations. Traffic Analytics also uncovers trends in bandwidth usage, traffic patterns, and user flow behavior, enabling comprehensive monitoring of both internal and external traffic flows and network segmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic analytics is a feature for analyzing virtual network flow logs to surface insights such as blocked traffic and malicious flows.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic Analytics is a traffic analysis solution in Network Watcher that visualizes traffic distribution and bandwidth utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic analytics is a cloud-based solution providing visibility into user and application activity in cloud networks, helping optimize network resource allocation.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic analytics is a Network Watcher feature used to identify changes in demand, patterns, bottlenecks, and unauthorized access attempts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7c4879ffc39192c7f9e5f766b4cfd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9641143ef161c630f4c2735baa058dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f01a2d2b2e2dfa5053288e4cf9593f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0d557186587fd7356bc48c45898548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b83068a0b2e1184a046db5ce56e2cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71183984350fc59c93d9704f35759a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6554b8dac9d13f8d208f0bad6db30cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/monitoring-alerting-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Tags">
  <data key="d0">Service Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Tags can be applied to Network Security Groups to facilitate connectivity with Azure PaaS services.&lt;SEP&gt;Named groups that summarize source and destination IP address ranges for Azure services, with responsibility offloaded to Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Service tags are used alongside FQDNs when defining network rules to simplify management.&lt;SEP&gt;Service tags define access controls based on service names rather than specific IP addresses, automatically managed and updated by Microsoft.&lt;SEP&gt;Service tags are used instead of specific IP addresses when defining routes, ensuring reliability as IP addresses change.&lt;SEP&gt;Service tags replace specific IP addresses for Azure services, reducing complexity of updating network security rules and lowering costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Service tags are used in place of specific IP addresses to simplify rule management and reduce misconfiguration risk in network security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b82e5bd8bced74ea376399d3355126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fa337fdf4c15ddf378bf74ac66c3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e496d3c1901ebb6e0f0add1d59b5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eb78b84d41322da30efb8dd70aafc73</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Key Vault Managed HSM">
  <data key="d0">Azure Key Vault Managed HSM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A dedicated managed HSM offering for scenarios requiring FIPS 140-2 Level 3 compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Integrity Protection">
  <data key="d0">Data Integrity Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data integrity protection involves encryption and key management to safeguard data without compromising application reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Policy-Driven Governance">
  <data key="d0">Policy-Driven Governance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Policy-driven governance uses Azure Policy to enforce security and reliability conventions across mission-critical application services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual Machines are IaaS resources that require specific security considerations including hardening, update management, and access control.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual machines (infrastructure as a service) require collection of operating system performance data.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual Machines allow hosting background tasks in a dedicated VM, suitable for Windows services or Windows Task Scheduler.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Machines allow running background tasks with flexibility and precise control over deployment, scheduling, and resource allocation.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual Machines are compute resources that can be protected, secured, and managed using various Azure features and best practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual Machines are cloud computing resources that can be configured with different sizes, SKUs, and billing models on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Virtual Machines (VMs) are Azure compute resources that can be monitored, scaled, and configured for various workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56d3f8085e9faa95d82a0d2dfdacc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464884618643684fc043c8a50e0bf16f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deploy If Not Exist">
  <data key="d0">Deploy If Not Exist</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deploy If Not Exist (DINE) is an Azure Policy execution mode that can take several minutes to occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission Critical Reference Implementation">
  <data key="d0">Mission Critical Reference Implementation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Mission Critical reference implementation contains a wide array of security and reliability centric policies to define and enforce a sample common engineering criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateways">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateways</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateways operate at Level 7 to filter and restrict egress traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Engineering Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Common Engineering Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common engineering criteria captures secure and reliable configuration definitions for all utilized Azure services, mapped to Azure Policy assignments to enforce compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Criticality">
  <data key="d0">Criticality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Criticality refers to determining the importance of each component to design appropriate reliability levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Criticality refers to determining the importance of each component to design appropriate reliability levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A qualitative label indicating the relative importance of a flow to business operations, typically rated as low, medium, or high.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fault Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Fault Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fault isolation is a strategy to prevent noncritical component failures from cascading to other components.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault isolation is a strategy to prevent noncritical component failures from cascading to other components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blast Radius">
  <data key="d0">Blast Radius</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blast radius refers to the scope and intensity of widespread effect that a failure, fault, or compromise can have across a workload's flows and components. It describes how far-reaching the impact of a malfunction or security breach can be within a system.

The blast radius can be expanded by factors such as co-location and increased density of resources. Conversely, it can be reduced through various strategies, including partitioning (which isolates failures to individual shards), constraining access permissions to minimize damage from compromised identities, and applying reliability practices designed to limit the scope of failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Blast radius refers to the scope of impact when a compromise or error occurs, increased by co-location and density.&lt;SEP&gt;Blast radius refers to the scope of impact from a malfunction, which reliability seeks to limit and which increased density can expand.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent of impact when a component fails, which architecture should aim to limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Blast radius refers to the scope of impact when a component fails, which architecture should limit.&lt;SEP&gt;The scope of impact or affected area when an incident occurs, which containment strategies aim to limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2829ddae563971c0c88cbe1829d1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Preservation">
  <data key="d0">Self-Preservation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-preservation capabilities use design patterns and modularization to prevent problems from affecting downstream components.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-preservation refers to built-in measures that help a workload remain functional during incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-preservation refers to built-in measures that help a workload remain functional during incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-preservation capabilities use design patterns and modularization to prevent problems from affecting downstream components.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a workload to be resilient against potential problems, reducing the likelihood of full outage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Out">
  <data key="d0">Scale Out</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scaling out critical components to handle variable capacity spikes and fluctuations across supported regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Scaling out critical components to handle variable capacity spikes and fluctuations across supported regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale out is a horizontal scaling strategy that adds instances to provide more resources to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Redundancy is a fundamental reliability strategy involving the deployment of multiple identical instances of workload components to ensure continued operation if one instance fails. By implementing redundancy across layers and application tiers, organizations minimize single points of failure through active-active or active-passive deployment configurations. This approach extends to deploying components across multiple regions, containing problems and ensuring overall system reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Building duplicate components and infrastructure to avoid single points of failure and handle faults efficiently.&lt;SEP&gt;Redundancy provides resiliency but incurs costs; it should be evaluated against service-level objectives to avoid unnecessary complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overprovisioning">
  <data key="d0">Overprovisioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Overprovisioning immediately mitigates individual failure of redundant instances and buffers against runaway resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning is a risk when teams allocate too much supply relative to demand, often caused by misjudged capacity planning or incident response scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning is deploying more instances of a resource so that some remain available while others are upgraded.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning immediately mitigates individual failure of redundant instances and buffers against runaway resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning is a risk when teams allocate too much supply relative to demand, often caused by misjudged capacity planning or incident response scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning is deploying more instances of a resource so that some remain available while others are upgraded.&lt;SEP&gt;Overprovisioning reduces deployment times and cost by provisioning extra VMs that aren't billed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Design For Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design for recovery ensures workloads can anticipate and recover from failures with minimal disruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Design for recovery ensures workloads can anticipate and recover from failures with minimal disruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Plans">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured, tested, and documented recovery plans aligned with negotiated recovery targets for quick recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Structured, tested, and documented recovery plans aligned with negotiated recovery targets for quick recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Healing">
  <data key="d0">Self-Healing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-Healing refers to the ability of a workload or system to automatically detect, respond to, and recover from failures and incidents without human intervention. It encompasses automated mechanisms such as recovering affected components, failing over to redundant infrastructure, using checkpoints for long-running transactions, and executing automated remediation actions.

Automated self-healing capabilities reduce risks from external factors and shorten the break-fix cycle by safely automating responses to common incident patterns. Proper monitoring and manual override options are maintained to ensure safety and control throughout the process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df6e00fa9a90ca53e8d360c865875b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61b04e78e2d91d6d0df8535ea9be2c6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/respond-live-performance-issues.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immutable Ephemeral Units">
  <data key="d0">Immutable Ephemeral Units</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stateless components replaced with immutable ephemeral units that provide repeatability and consistency.&lt;SEP&gt;Stateless components replaced with immutable ephemeral units that provide repeatability and consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Operations">
  <data key="d0">Design For Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design for operations shifts left to anticipate failure conditions through testing and observability.&lt;SEP&gt;Design for operations shifts left to anticipate failure conditions through testing and observability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observable Systems">
  <data key="d0">Observable Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Observable systems correlate telemetry for monitoring, diagnostics, and holistic health status views.&lt;SEP&gt;Observable systems correlate telemetry for monitoring, diagnostics, and holistic health status views.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Site Reliability Engineers">
  <data key="d0">Site Reliability Engineers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Site reliability engineers prioritize remediation efforts based on observability data and respond to actionable alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Site reliability engineers are professionals responsible for mitigating live site incidents and proactively addressing potential failures.&lt;SEP&gt;SREs are personnel who integrate business insights and technical skills for recovery planning to meet reliability targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Site reliability engineers prioritize remediation efforts based on observability data and respond to actionable alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Site reliability engineers are professionals responsible for mitigating live site incidents and proactively addressing potential failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Site reliability engineers are professionals who act on real-time monitoring dashboards for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Site reliability engineers focus on critical problems during downtime events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb4be3d9c01e97b5b077710134d8de16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85dfff44e8e4c1e2d34f3f2fbc239ab2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backups">
  <data key="d0">Backups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Backups are essential for restoring the system to a working state using a trusted recovery point such as the last-known good state, ensuring immutable and transactionally consistent data.&lt;SEP&gt;Backups are essential for restoring the system to a working state using a trusted recovery point such as the last-known good state, ensuring immutable and transactionally consistent data.&lt;SEP&gt;Backups consume workload resources like processing power, network bandwidth, and disk I/O, and should be optimized using strategies like incremental backups and off-peak scheduling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root Cause Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Root Cause Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Root Cause Analysis (RCA) is the process of identifying the underlying cause of failures, problems, or performance issues in applications and systems. It is a systematic method for uncovering deficiencies in processes or implementations that contribute to these issues.

RCA involves a structured approach including hypothesis testing through systematic steps: gathering information, defining problems, investigating causes, correlating data, testing hypotheses, implementing solutions, and monitoring results. When failures occur, RCA is enabled by correlated telemetry from distributed tracing, which helps pinpoint issues across complex systems.

Effective root cause analysis requires shared visibility across teams regarding dependency status and ongoing failures, making it essential for incident management. This cross-team collaboration ensures that the right context is available to quickly identify and resolve underlying issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Cause Analysis (RCA) is the investigation and identification of underlying causes of an incident to prevent recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;A thorough analysis conducted after incidents to identify underlying causes and contributing factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Root cause analysis (RCA) is performed when failures occur, enabled by correlated telemetry from distributed tracing.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic process of investigating an incident to identify underlying factors responsible for the problem and prevent recurrence, abbreviated as RCA.&lt;SEP&gt;RCA is a post-incident analysis method to identify the underlying cause of an incident, supported by documentation from incident closure.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Cause Analysis (RCA) is a deep technical analysis process to pinpoint the cause of an incident and contain its impact, using observability data, telemetry dashboards, system logs, and change histories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61b04e78e2d91d6d0df8535ea9be2c6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef6111a0cc4b828fa5b996fe5d89475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/monitoring-alerting-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/respond-live-performance-issues.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disaster Preparedness">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Preparedness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disaster preparedness approaches in architecture design and workload operations are needed even for highly resilient systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster preparedness approaches in architecture design and workload operations are needed even for highly resilient systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8047163c921812913ce249dbb081c0d2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automation">
  <data key="d0">Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Automation refers to the practice of replacing repetitive manual tasks with software-driven processes that execute faster, with greater consistency and accuracy. It encompasses routine operations such as provisioning, scaling, deployments, testing, maintenance, and security, minimizing human error and reducing associated risks.

Automation is a critical dependency of workloads and should be treated as integral to system design. It supports at-scale operations, relieves management burden, and reduces technical debt. By integrating automated processes, organizations gain efficiency across operational tasks, cost optimization, and security.

Beyond routine execution, automation adds self-healing and self-prevention qualities to workloads, enabling them to respond to common recurring performance issues. At the highest maturity levels (Level 5), automation serves as a key strategy for reducing operational friction and achieving consistent, reliable outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Automation replaces repetitive manual tasks with software that completes them quicker, with greater consistency and accuracy, reducing risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Automation is a critical dependency of workloads that should be treated as integral, supporting at-scale operations and reducing repetitive tasks and technical debt.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef6111a0cc4b828fa5b996fe5d89475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddf6c44166c12054fa8380f137ab849a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deb7d0f719a6be9318b32726b071565b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/respond-live-performance-issues.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/enable-automation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/formalize-operations-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997972</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplicity">
  <data key="d0">Simplicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Simplicity in architecture design reduces surface area for control, minimizing inefficiencies and potential misconfigurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Simplicity in architecture design reduces surface area for control, minimizing inefficiencies and potential misconfigurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Predictive alerts identify potential failures before they become live incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive alerts identify potential failures before they become live incidents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failure Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Failure Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure simulation involves running tests in production and pre-production environments to set realistic recovery expectations.&lt;SEP&gt;Failure simulation involves running tests in production and pre-production environments to set realistic recovery expectations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A checklist document used to drive actions after setting a reliability strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The reliability checklist is a next-step resource referenced for ensuring reliability practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A checklist document used to drive actions after setting a reliability strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The reliability checklist is a next-step resource referenced for ensuring reliability practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reliability checklist is a complete set of recommendations for reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability checklist is a complete set of recommendations for ensuring reliability in system design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9ef91f9cdfc70b6b3be61ee475dc1c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b934336b9f0ae48abbe56045f1da0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Routine Operations">
  <data key="d0">Routine Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routine operations include application revisions, security and compliance audits, component upgrades, and backup processes that impact system stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Routine operations include application revisions, security and compliance audits, component upgrades, and backup processes that impact system stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incident Learning">
  <data key="d0">Incident Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Incident learning involves continuously learning from production incidents to drive improvements based on real-life failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Incident learning involves continuously learning from production incidents to drive improvements based on real-life failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Learning from incidents involves using past incidents as opportunities for future improvement through retrospectives and enhanced observability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb32778b5a44a1a37ca0f92518c49c6e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standards">
  <data key="d0">Standards</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standards in code implementation, deployment, and processes provide consistency, minimize human errors, and support troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;Standards in code implementation, deployment, and processes provide consistency, minimize human errors, and support troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Design Principles">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Design Principles</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A set of guiding principles for building reliable workloads that can survive outages and malfunctions while continuing to provide intended functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability design principles are documented guidelines that inform workload design decisions for achieving reliability goals.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of guiding principles for building reliable workloads that can survive outages and malfunctions while continuing to provide intended functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability design principles are documented guidelines that inform workload design decisions for achieving reliability goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resilience">
  <data key="d0">Resilience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ability of a workload to detect and withstand faults while continuing to operate.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a workload to detect and withstand faults while continuing to operate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recoverability">
  <data key="d0">Recoverability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ability to restore a workload within agreed recovery targets when disruption exceeds resiliency measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability to restore a workload within agreed recovery targets when disruption exceeds resiliency measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Recoverability is the ability to restore normal operations after a disruption within agreed RTO and RPO targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Recoverability refers to the ability to get back online after a disruption, involving backup storage, disaster recovery tooling, and recovery testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Recoverability focuses on restoration within recovery time objective (RTO) and RPO targets, restoring operations after failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f082730bb91f06b04e3b6f39138f774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/cost-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability">
  <data key="d0">Availability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ensuring users can access the workload during the promised time period at the promised quality level.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability is a security principle focused on preventing or minimizing system downtime and degradation during security incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability measures uptime from the perspective of customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Ensuring users can access the workload during the promised time period at the promised quality level.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability is the amount of time that an application workload runs in a healthy state without significant downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability is a security principle focused on preventing or minimizing system downtime and degradation during security incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A design goal for partitions that eliminates single points of failure and enables independent management of data subsets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a879a1f2cc37839210f7fa1a38c26a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6461a458cf4d4525d7fe6f8f9cfa20e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f5c02d75cf91d6692adb66113df89eb</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Business Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Design For Business Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle focused on aligning workload design with clear, documented business goals and stakeholder promises.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle focused on aligning workload design with clear, documented business goals and stakeholder promises.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Resilience">
  <data key="d0">Design For Resilience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle focused on ensuring workloads continue to operate with full or reduced functionality through fault tolerance and graceful degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle focused on ensuring workloads continue to operate with full or reduced functionality through fault tolerance and graceful degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graceful Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Graceful Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design approach where a system continues operating with reduced functionality when components fail.&lt;SEP&gt;Graceful degradation is a strategy for maintaining partial system functionality during overload or failure, supported by the Throttling pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy to continue serving users despite failures by disabling nonworking parts and adjusting the user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy that includes temporary fixes when parts of a system don't work properly, continuing to serve users by disabling nonworking parts and adjusting the user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;A design approach where a system continues operating with reduced functionality when components fail.&lt;SEP&gt;Graceful degradation is a design approach that minimizes the blast radius of component malfunction while maintaining partial functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Path">
  <data key="d0">Critical Path</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The set of components essential to workload operation that must be distinguished from those that can function in a degraded state.&lt;SEP&gt;The set of components essential to workload operation that must be distinguished from those that can function in a degraded state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fault Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Fault Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ability of a system to continue operating properly in the event of failure of some of its components.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a system to continue operating properly in the event of failure of some of its components.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault tolerance is a reliability concept for ensuring infrastructure and storage resilience, such as three-way mirror configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault tolerance centers on high availability and disaster recovery principles for Virtual Desktop environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault tolerance includes fault-tolerant storage to safeguard integrity and availability of user data during failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edb1f343516427f2303f45fae771d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RTO">
  <data key="d0">RTO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Time Objective (RTO) is a key reliability and disaster recovery metric that defines the maximum acceptable amount of downtime before services, systems, applications, or workloads must be restored after a disruption or outage. It serves as a target for how quickly recovery procedures must be completed, establishing the tolerable window of time between a failure event and the resumption of normal operations.

RTO is determined through failure mode analysis and disaster recovery planning processes. It applies to individual systems, applications, and operational flows, guiding organizations in designing their resilience strategies and ensuring that restoration efforts meet defined business continuity requirements.

RTO is also used as a practical benchmark in operational testing and validation. It is verified through incident response testing and restore drills to ensure recovery performance meets defined targets. Additionally, RTO serves as a criterion in failback data synchronization processes, ensuring that data recovery and system restoration align with acceptable downtime tolerances.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Time Objective, the target time for restoring a solution after an outage.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Time Objective (RTO) is a metric used to determine the appropriate redundancy level for data storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery Time Objective defines the maximum acceptable downtime for recovery after a failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37330ee339c66455fbad4f1319377e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443aa85fac21ccf603c8d3f8c5b909ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059dfb0d1deec0d27f10ad0c5e0f86d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RPO">
  <data key="d0">RPO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Point Objective (RPO) is a reliability and recovery metric that defines the maximum acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a disruption. It represents the threshold for how much data an organization can afford to lose, applicable to individual systems, applications, and data flows.

RPO is determined through failure mode analysis and disaster recovery planning, and is directly controlled by backup frequency—more frequent backups result in a lower RPO and less potential data loss. It is also used to determine the appropriate redundancy level for data storage. As a key recovery metric, RPO is used to define recovery targets for workloads and to validate data integrity during recovery. It is verified through incident response testing to ensure systems meet their defined objectives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37330ee339c66455fbad4f1319377e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059dfb0d1deec0d27f10ad0c5e0f86d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000766</data>
