</node>
<node id="SLO">
  <data key="d0">SLO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objective (SLO) is a measurable, agreed-upon target for service reliability that defines the desired level of service along with specific quality attributes. SLOs serve as critical health signals for applications, setting targets for critical flows such as availability and response time. For example, an SLO might target 99.45% availability or specify response time thresholds at the 75th percentile for an API, with some targeting criteria as stringent as 99.999% uptime.

SLOs should be achievable and clearly communicated. They can be composite values calculated from multiple contributing factors. SLOs are used to evaluate whether potential downtime falls within tolerable limits and serve as the basis for calculating error budgets, enabling teams to balance reliability with development velocity.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Level Objectives are critical health signals that define the desired level of service along with quality attributes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67df0f5abb1d6d875958c4732f3ab63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d531693488b5e9a3be349c75f47f4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354f0a4ce38a1d015d0e524baae4a06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6461a458cf4d4525d7fe6f8f9cfa20e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
