<node id="Chaos Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Chaos Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chaos Engineering is a discipline and practice centered on deliberately injecting faults, failures, and real-world stresses into systems to test their resilience, improve reliability, and validate recoverability. It involves conducting controlled experiments—often in production environments, though also in nonproduction environments—to confirm that applications and services can recover gracefully under adverse conditions. Through active malfunction simulation and load testing, Chaos Engineering helps teams build confidence in system robustness, test incident response processes, and validate event processing resilience during simulated infrastructure failures.

Considered a gold standard for resilience validation, Chaos Engineering is typically reserved for mature systems that have safeguards in place to limit the blast radius of experiments. By proactively subjecting infrastructure to realistic failure scenarios, organizations can systematically identify resilience gaps and weaknesses, validate mitigation and recovery procedures, and prevent unexpected outages. It is widely used to measure, understand, and improve cloud application and service resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos engineering is a testing approach to identify points of failure before outages occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos engineering is a testing method that introduces faults to improve workload reliability, resilience, and fault handling while considering sustainability impacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61803d2562ce9d74f9843d45925671b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7b8a756934ab64251ea5a23e73f2de</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Tradeoffs">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Tradeoffs</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A guide exploring concepts related to tradeoffs in reliability design decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A document covering tradeoffs related to the reliability pillar of architecture design.&lt;SEP&gt;A guide exploring concepts related to tradeoffs in reliability design decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A document covering tradeoffs related to the reliability pillar of architecture design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Replication">
  <data key="d0">Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Replication is a key reliability strategy that duplicates components, data, or geographic presence to handle concurrent node failures, but increases surface area and costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Replication is a key reliability strategy that duplicates components, data, or geographic presence to handle concurrent node failures, but increases surface area and costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero Trust Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Zero Trust Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero Trust Architecture is a security framework whose three principles can be eroded by using overly broad security rules to mitigate reliability-related configuration complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust Architecture is a security framework whose three principles can be eroded by using overly broad security rules to mitigate reliability-related configuration complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incident Response Plan">
  <data key="d0">Incident Response Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An Incident Response Plan (IRP) is a well-documented plan that defines standard operating procedures for preparedness, detection, containment, mitigation, and post-incident activity. It unifies threat detection and mitigation strategies while standardizing security incident management, enabling rapid detection and recovery from potential and active security compromises. The plan includes guidance for triage, recovery, and post-incident reviews, making it vital for maintaining reliable workload operations.

The Incident Response Plan is a living document that is continuously refined through real-world production incidents, retrospective learning sessions, and lessons learned from past security events. This iterative improvement process ensures the plan remains current and effective in addressing evolving threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The incident response plan is a predefined plan followed exactly during disaster recovery emergencies to ensure fast, coordinated action.&lt;SEP&gt;The incident response plan documents key roles, communication structures, core procedures, and supplemental procedures for managing incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured plan for responding to incidents, dependent on monitoring, testing, and continuous improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;The incident response plan is a predefined plan that outlines severity classifications, criteria for response levels, and mitigation steps during incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A documented plan that defines processes for incident reporting, severity assignment, triage, and response procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A proactive plan defining how to respond to major incidents, including escalation paths, severity levels, and communication strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727509da0a6c0effe0339afa582c8da4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d20b573314239b2a88ca3deb8586c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9514c481f519092f6d4362611c52ecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deb7d0f719a6be9318b32726b071565b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd8f7b0b2f8f309054b1fccac7b1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b111334644545025473a63cd0bd3a289</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/formalize-operations-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Replication">
  <data key="d0">Data Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data replication is a reliability pattern that copies data to survive replica malfunction, introducing additional latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication is a reliability pattern that copies data to survive replica malfunction, introducing additional latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication involves creating multiple copies of data and storing them in other geographic locations or zones for reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication involves creating multiple copies of data and storing them in other geographic locations or zones for reliability and availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Balancing">
  <data key="d0">Resource Balancing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource balancing distributes or redistributes load to healthy replicas, affecting performance of requests being balanced.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource balancing distributes or redistributes load to healthy replicas, affecting performance of requests being balanced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic scaling adjusts resources in response to demand but cannot instantaneously handle sudden spikes, necessitating over-provisioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic scaling adjusts resources in response to demand but cannot instantaneously handle sudden spikes, necessitating over-provisioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic scaling adjusts resources based on demand, with maximum scaling limits to avoid costly spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic scaling is a resource configuration that adjusts resources dynamically, requiring maximum scaling thresholds to avoid cost overruns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf77302eae466ce3d619b76c771db34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-component-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Call Rotation">
  <data key="d0">On-Call Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">On-call rotation is a rapid response process requiring technical team members to be available, incurring personnel and opportunity costs.&lt;SEP&gt;On-call rotation is a rapid response process requiring technical team members to be available, incurring personnel and opportunity costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Over-Provisioning">
  <data key="d0">Over-Provisioning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Over-provisioning is a reliability tactic of using larger or more instances than currently needed to absorb demand bursts, countering performance efficiency goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Over-provisioning is a reliability tactic of using larger or more instances than currently needed to absorb demand bursts, countering performance efficiency goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Support Contracts">
  <data key="d0">Support Contracts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Support contracts with technology providers are a key component of reliable workloads, but can incur waste when the level of support is over-provisioned.&lt;SEP&gt;Support contracts with technology providers are a key component of reliable workloads, but can incur waste when the level of support is over-provisioned.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Cold Standby">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Cold Standby</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-passive cold standby is a recovery strategy where the secondary environment is not running until needed.&lt;SEP&gt;A DR deployment pattern where the secondary region has minimal infrastructure until failover, requiring full deployment during a disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-passive cold standby is a recovery strategy where the secondary environment is not running until needed.&lt;SEP&gt;A DR deployment pattern where the secondary region has minimal infrastructure until failover, requiring full deployment during a disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;An environment that isn't running and requires provisioning and data restoration when activated, offering lowest cost but longest recovery time.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment strategy where secondary region compute resources remain stopped until needed, suitable for Tier 2 or Tier 3 workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A recovery strategy where the secondary region remains inactive until manually activated during a disaster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443aa85fac21ccf603c8d3f8c5b909ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Warm Standby">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Warm Standby</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-passive warm standby is a recovery strategy with minimal pre-deployed resources for rapid failover.&lt;SEP&gt;A DR deployment pattern where the secondary region has pre-deployed infrastructure at reduced capacity for faster failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-passive warm standby is a recovery strategy with minimal pre-deployed resources for rapid failover.&lt;SEP&gt;A DR deployment pattern where the secondary region has pre-deployed infrastructure at reduced capacity for faster failover.&lt;SEP&gt;A partially provisioned environment running minimal services that can scale up quickly during failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A recovery strategy that maintains a minimally provisioned secondary environment that can scale quickly during failure events, balancing cost and resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443aa85fac21ccf603c8d3f8c5b909ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synchronous Replication">
  <data key="d0">Synchronous Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synchronous Replication is a data replication approach where data is written and committed to multiple locations simultaneously, requiring acknowledgment from each location before a transaction is considered complete. This method distributes data copies across multiple availability zones, ensuring all writes complete across zones before confirming the transaction. Synchronous Replication ensures zero data loss but potentially introduces higher latency due to the requirement of waiting for acknowledgment from all locations.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous replication ensures data consistency across datacenters in a stretched cluster.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous replication commits database transactions to instances in two separate zones or regions to achieve zero data loss (RPO of 0).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c634b3a2b27e4b06ab4fb93df82c41da</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005925</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Replication">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data replication where changes are written to the primary location first then copied to secondary locations, allowing some data loss but lower latency.&lt;SEP&gt;A data replication approach where changes are replicated to another location at a later time.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication where changes are written to the primary location first then copied to secondary locations, allowing some data loss but lower latency.&lt;SEP&gt;A data replication approach where changes are replicated to another location at a later time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Criticality">
  <data key="d0">Business Criticality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Classification of workloads based on importance to business operations, influencing recovery priorities and investment levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Classification of workloads based on importance to business operations, influencing recovery priorities and investment levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="War Room">
  <data key="d0">War Room</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A centralized location or communication channel where key personnel coordinate during disaster recovery operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A centralized location or communication channel where key personnel coordinate during disaster recovery operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DR Drill">
  <data key="d0">DR Drill</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A planned exercise to test disaster recovery procedures and validate recovery capabilities under controlled conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A planned exercise to test disaster recovery procedures and validate recovery capabilities under controlled conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failover">
  <data key="d0">Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failover is the process of switching operations from a primary environment to a secondary or standby system when the primary becomes unavailable due to a failure or disaster. It involves the automated and/or manual shifting of production workload traffic from an unavailable region to an unaffected geographical region, ensuring continuity of service.

As a reliability technique, failover redirects work or data access to healthy components when malfunctions occur. It can be implemented through patterns such as Leader Election, Index Table, and Scheduler Agent Supervisor. For mission-critical workloads, automation of the failover process is recommended to minimize downtime and reduce the risk of human error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failback">
  <data key="d0">Failback</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failback is the process of restoring operations to the original environment after a failover, treated as a separate process from failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Failback is the automated and/or manual shifting of production workload traffic from a failover region back to the primary region.&lt;SEP&gt;Failback is the process of restoring operations to the original environment after a failover, treated as a separate process from failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Failback is the automated and/or manual shifting of production workload traffic from a failover region back to the primary region.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of returning workloads to the original primary environment after incident resolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Failback is the process of returning operations to the primary site after failover, often involving more complexity than failover itself.&lt;SEP&gt;Failback is the process of returning operations to the primary site after a disaster, often involving more complexity than failover and recommended to be managed through a controlled process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999133</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-In-Time Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Point-In-Time Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Point-in-time recovery is the ability to restore data to a specific moment in time, typically used to recover from data corruption or accidental changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-in-time recovery is the ability to restore data to a specific moment in time, typically used to recover from data corruption or accidental changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backup">
  <data key="d0">Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A backup is a copy of data stored separately from the primary system to enable data recovery if loss, corruption, or disaster occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;A backup is a copy of data stored separately from the primary system to enable data recovery if loss, corruption, or disaster occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;A value-added backup service that integrates with Azure Files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca94eb8d1a3fa16fe190b0f6eecd280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DR Activation Criteria">
  <data key="d0">DR Activation Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Predefined thresholds and conditions that determine when to declare a disaster and trigger recovery procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Predefined thresholds and conditions that determine when to declare a disaster and trigger recovery procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Site Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Azure Site Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Site Recovery is an Azure service designed to provide disaster recovery capabilities by automating failover and recovery for IaaS systems. It protects applications by replicating them to a secondary location with continuous replication and automated failover. The service enables disaster recovery for Azure VMs between availability zones and supports protecting VMs running on Azure Local. In advanced scenarios, Azure Site Recovery can be used for self-healing, enabling failover and recovery drills to ensure business continuity.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Site Recovery is a service used to replicate session hosts from a primary region to a secondary region for disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Site Recovery is a disaster recovery solution that automates failover and failback to minimize VM downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Site Recovery is a disaster recovery solution for SAP workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15da9f5a57c9361e9e5487fa0eea82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Backup">
  <data key="d0">Azure Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Backup is a cloud-based Azure service that provides comprehensive data protection through backup and restore operations across a wide range of Azure resources. It supports backup for virtual machines (including host-level and VM guest-level backups for Azure Local), Azure Files, SMB file shares, Azure Blob Storage, Azure Managed Disks, SQL Database, AKS clusters, Azure Database for PostgreSQL, and FSLogix profiles stored in Azure Files or Azure NetApp Files. It is also integrated with Azure VMware Solution.

Azure Backup uses incremental backups, compression, and encryption to minimize performance impact. It offers capabilities such as native database backup, storage backup, virtual machine backup, long-term retention (up to 99 years in Recovery Services vault), centralized backup management, soft delete, and recovery point management. For Azure Database for PostgreSQL, backup policies support recovery point retention up to 10 years. The service provides vaulted backup to protect data from threats such as ransomware attacks and offers geo-redundant backup capabilities.

For disaster recovery, Azure Backup vaults in a secondary region can protect persistent data without requiring standby infrastructure. It supports cross-region restores, stores recovery points in Backup vaults for AKS cluster disaster recovery, and provides centralized business continuity and disaster recovery management for services like SQL Database.

Azure Backup offers storage with reserved capacity, providing discounts for one-year or three-year commitments. For services like Azure Database for PostgreSQL, it incurs protected instance fees and backup storage fees. The service continues to receive new features enhancing disaster recovery guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Backup is the native backup solution in Azure providing database backups, storage backups, VM backups, long-term retention, and backup management for SAP workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Backup is a service that can take database backups for HANA and SQL Server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757386a260f7f7980e2074a43870b9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe464ce8a55b32a868b7ba10711df9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85737e4794e90bbd715857ab9acd5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005928</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Managed Redis">
  <data key="d0">Azure Managed Redis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Managed Redis is an Azure caching service that stores frequently accessed data closer to the application for faster retrieval, reducing the need for repeated requests to the backend by keeping copies of data in front of the main data store. It offers reliability and disaster recovery capabilities. Azure Managed Redis is often combined with API Management and can provide custom metrics for autoscaling, including in Container Apps.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Managed Redis is a secure shared storage option for agent state persistence.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Managed Redis is an Azure-hosted caching solution for caching frequently accessed data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eb4bf3421da46d9aac57d5ba0a0c195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c53b990e9918af85864a95bf9284ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Files">
  <data key="d0">Azure Files</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Files is a Microsoft cloud file storage solution that provides fully managed file shares accessible via both SMB and NFS protocols. These file shares can be mounted by cloud and on-premises clients, offering flexible connectivity options across environments.

Azure Files supports various performance tiers, including SSD file shares, and features metadata caching capabilities. The service offers three billing models: pay-as-you-go, provisioned v1, and provisioned v2, along with multiple access tiers, reservations, snapshots, and soft-delete features. Various redundancy and security configurations are available, including configurable settings for SMB protocol versions and encryption.

Azure Files includes backup capabilities and follows architecture best practices covering SMB and NFS file share administrative control, making it a comprehensive storage service within the Azure ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Files is a storage service that supports premium zone-redundant storage for FSLogix profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Files is a fully managed Azure-native file share storage solution recommended for housing FSLogix profile containers, supporting up to 100,000 IOPS per share.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Files is a cloud storage service that can be used for App Attach file shares.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Files is a storage service supporting NFS and SMB for SAP high-availability configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5720bc2c35e1af5035855500579a20d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6949b9609e5ef191a10ce0e8da0a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca94eb8d1a3fa16fe190b0f6eecd280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e39ac746628d7273f799262e7cf7dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0723b9dd0fc297957da0041030d0b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785fcaaef274ecc977b30c815a92374a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FMA Documentation">
  <data key="d0">FMA Documentation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure Mode Analysis documentation captures how the system behaves during disasters and how to respond.&lt;SEP&gt;Failure Mode Analysis documentation captures how the system behaves during disasters and how to respond.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DR Plan">
  <data key="d0">DR Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The DR plan is a living document that defines recovery procedures, activation criteria, and is reviewed regularly with stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The DR plan is a living document that defines recovery procedures, activation criteria, and is reviewed regularly with stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The disaster recovery (DR) plan is a document that should be regularly updated to reflect the current system state, incorporating lessons from drills and incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A disaster recovery plan that requires regular testing to move beyond theoretical status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855b48574d32952d11c2de78f45cb1a0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabletop Exercises">
  <data key="d0">Tabletop Exercises</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabletop exercises are drills where the team practices their roles, builds familiarity, and trains new members without impacting production.&lt;SEP&gt;Tabletop exercises are drills where the team practices their roles, builds familiarity, and trains new members without impacting production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Production Drills">
  <data key="d0">Production Drills</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Production-level drills are the only way to verify that a DR plan meets RTO and RPO targets in real conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Production-level drills are the only way to verify that a DR plan meets RTO and RPO targets in real conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backup Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Backup Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Backup strategies involve choosing tailored solutions for each service, defining retention periods, and using multi-region storage for cross-region recoverability.&lt;SEP&gt;Backup strategies involve choosing tailored solutions for each service, defining retention periods, and using multi-region storage for cross-region recoverability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partial Failover">
  <data key="d0">Partial Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial failover allows individual components to fail over independently, reducing complexity, cost, and RTO while maintaining partial availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial failover allows individual components to fail over independently, reducing complexity, cost, and RTO while maintaining partial availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Failover Group">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Failover Group</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-failover group is a mechanism in Azure SQL that fails over to a secondary region during regional outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto-failover group is a mechanism in Azure SQL that fails over to a secondary region during regional outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mitigation">
  <data key="d0">Mitigation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitigation strategies fall into two categories: building more resiliency and designing for degraded performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities identified to address problems either proactively or reactively.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation strategies fall into two categories: building more resiliency and designing for degraded performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities identified to address problems either proactively or reactively.&lt;SEP&gt;Actions to reduce or remove the impact of an incident, including rollback, fallback, bypass, or emergency fixes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Degraded Performance">
  <data key="d0">Degraded Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Designing for degraded performance involves identifying failure points that disable some components while maintaining end-to-end flow functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Designing for degraded performance involves identifying failure points that disable some components while maintaining end-to-end flow functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failure Mode">
  <data key="d0">Failure Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of problem that can cause one or more workload components to be degraded or severely affected to the point of being unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of problem that can cause one or more workload components to be degraded or severely affected to the point of being unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single Point-Of-Failure Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Single Point-Of-Failure Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An analysis method for identifying workload dependencies that could serve as single points of failure.&lt;SEP&gt;An analysis method for identifying workload dependencies that could serve as single points of failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detection">
  <data key="d0">Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detection refers to infrastructure, data, and app monitoring and alerting processes and procedures used to identify failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Detection refers to infrastructure, data, and app monitoring and alerting processes and procedures used to identify failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Detection is the process of identifying that an incident has occurred or is occurring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active deployment maximizes availability by running multiple instances simultaneously, each actively handling traffic with immediate failover capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-active deployment maximizes availability by running multiple instances simultaneously, each actively handling traffic with immediate failover capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-region deployment method enabling instant recovery with no interruption to users.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-active deployment means multiple environments serving traffic simultaneously across regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efaee6ae92cff9320730dd7f435d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5658d6f41065712f87008266f41103c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-passive deployment is a cost-effective DR approach where a primary instance handles traffic while secondary instances remain on standby for failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-passive deployment is a cost-effective DR approach where a primary instance handles traffic while secondary instances remain on standby for failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-passive deployment means only the primary region handles traffic, failing over to the secondary region when necessary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5658d6f41065712f87008266f41103c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Spare">
  <data key="d0">Warm Spare</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Warm spare is an active-passive configuration where the secondary location runs with minimum compute and data sizing, scaled up after failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm spare is an active-passive design pattern that offers shorter recovery time but higher operating costs compared to cold spare.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm spare is an active-passive configuration where the secondary location runs with minimum compute and data sizing, scaled up after failover.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm spare is an active-passive design pattern that offers shorter recovery time but higher operating costs compared to cold spare.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Spare">
  <data key="d0">Cold Spare</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cold spare is an active-passive configuration where secondary location compute resources are fully scaled but stopped, requiring startup before use.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold spare is an active-passive design pattern with one primary location and secondary locations where compute resources are stopped and must be started before failover, offering lower operating costs but longer recovery time than warm spare.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold spare is an active-passive configuration where secondary location compute resources are fully scaled but stopped, requiring startup before use.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold spare is an active-passive design pattern with one primary location and secondary locations where compute resources are stopped and must be started before failover, offering lower operating costs but longer recovery time than warm spare.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DNS Private Resolver">
  <data key="d0">Azure DNS Private Resolver</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DNS Private Resolver supports hybrid name resolution between on-premises and cloud environments with zone redundancy and automatic self-healing.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS Private Resolver is a service that supports resilient hybrid name resolution, with self-healing capabilities during zone-wide outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS Private Resolver supports hybrid name resolution between on-premises and cloud environments with zone redundancy and automatic self-healing.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS Private Resolver is a service that supports resilient hybrid name resolution, with self-healing capabilities during zone-wide outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DNS Failover">
  <data key="d0">DNS Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DNS failover is achieved by assigning primary and secondary DNS servers using private resolvers across different regions.&lt;SEP&gt;DNS failover is achieved by assigning primary and secondary DNS servers using private resolvers across different regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CanNotDelete Locks">
  <data key="d0">CanNotDelete Locks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CanNotDelete locks are Azure resource locks that prevent accidental deletion to preserve redundancy and resiliency.&lt;SEP&gt;CanNotDelete locks are Azure resource locks that prevent accidental deletion to preserve redundancy and resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Storage Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Azure Storage Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Storage redundancy provides data replication options for Azure Storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage redundancy provides data replication options for Azure Storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Database Active Geo-Replication">
  <data key="d0">SQL Database Active Geo-Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Database active geo-replication enables replication of databases across regions for resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;SQL Database active geo-replication enables replication of databases across regions for resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc31c34dd7feec455a5b2a2d551c3a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Expressroute">
  <data key="d0">Azure Expressroute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure ExpressRoute is a networking service that may require manual configuration of multiple circuits for redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute is a networking service that may require manual configuration of multiple circuits for redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute is a service that enables private connections between Azure data-centers and on-premises or colocation infrastructure, offering more security, faster speeds, and lower latencies than internet connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute is a Microsoft Azure service for private network connectivity between on-premises networks and Azure virtual networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6da263826443aba6bd2ff3b90cd482c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840c9812065b0dae17f67ebda4bb6ea9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-expressroute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Stamps Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamps Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Deployment Stamps pattern is an architectural approach that creates repeatable, self-contained units (called stamps) containing all resources required to deliver a workload. This pattern shifts the focus from component-level to workload-level redundancy by bundling workload components into templates as units of scale, enabling easy and repeatable deployments.

The pattern is used to provision, manage, and monitor varied resources to host multiple workloads or tenants, with each copy referred to as a stamp. It is particularly suitable for multi-zone, multi-region deployments and is well-suited for SaaS providers. The Deployment Stamps pattern is a proven practice for scaling predictably while providing failure isolation and performance at scale.&lt;SEP&gt;The Deployment Stamps pattern compartmentalizes App Service into immutable, self-contained units that can be quickly scaled.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployment stamps pattern achieves workload-level redundancy across regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Deployment Stamps pattern involves deploying dedicated infrastructure for each customer.&lt;SEP&gt;The Deployment Stamps pattern deploys multiple independent instances of a solution, providing an additional scaling dimension.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment Stamps pattern is a deployment model where separate stamps can share an identity provider rather than requiring one in each stamp.&lt;SEP&gt;The Deployment Stamps pattern enables deploying dedicated or identical resources across multiple Azure regions, either customer-specific or shared.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e912a1ac7fa5ab0139e0fac99a203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b1c021188faeb6dd44f9550bc2c4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da6ff7f8e8d62245d48fe850b4eb70f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/resource-organization.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command Query Responsibility Segregation">
  <data key="d0">Command Query Responsibility Segregation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CQRS pattern separates read-write and read-only data models to add redundant read-only database instances for resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS pattern separates read-write and read-only data models to add redundant read-only database instances for resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Partitioning">
  <data key="d0">Database Partitioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Database partitioning improves scalability and availability by splitting data into shards so failure in one shard only disrupts a subset of transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Database partitioning improves scalability and availability by splitting data into shards so failure in one shard only disrupts a subset of transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eventual Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Eventual Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eventual consistency is a data consistency approach that reduces tight coupling and improves throughput when data is distributed.&lt;SEP&gt;Eventual consistency is a data consistency approach that reduces tight coupling and improves throughput when data is distributed.&lt;SEP&gt;A consistency model that enhances performance by allowing data to be slightly dated, reducing immediate demand on CPU cycles and network bandwidth.&lt;SEP&gt;Eventual consistency is a data synchronization model allowing temporary inconsistency in data replicas before they eventually sync.&lt;SEP&gt;Eventual consistency is a consistency level where changes spread gradually, boosting responsiveness and performance while introducing short-lived inconsistencies.&lt;SEP&gt;A consistency model where data updates propagate across partitions over time, guaranteeing all replicas eventually converge to the same state.&lt;SEP&gt;Eventual consistency is a common approach in distributed systems where data in each partition is updated separately and consistency is achieved over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c0f1c2454a3cd326399dd189c571e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc8280bb50c2a5f4a589617c1bed437</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-code-infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub-And-Spoke Model">
  <data key="d0">Hub-And-Spoke Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub-and-spoke model is a network topology pattern used to organize cloud infrastructure into logical patterns that make redundancy design easier to build and scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Hub-and-spoke model is a network topology pattern used to organize cloud infrastructure into logical patterns that make redundancy design easier to build and scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyglot Persistence">
  <data key="d0">Polyglot Persistence</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyglot persistence is the concept of using different storage technologies within the same application to take advantage of each component's best capabilities. Rather than relying on a single database system, this approach employs a combination of data store technologies to handle different data types appropriately, leveraging the strengths of each for optimal performance and scalability. It is applicable to cloud workloads and supports segmentation by matching specific data needs with the most suitable storage solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyglot persistence stores different data types in technologies suited for their specific use patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-230e614bb0d26b9bf3245480dced7db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f01a2d2b2e2dfa5053288e4cf9593f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9d6cbba3e234d9031d66c9ba1579fb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7404990d0db645a738f8e03698df0941</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VPN Gateway">
  <data key="d0">VPN Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VPN Gateway is an Azure networking service that provides VPN connectivity through site-to-site and point-to-site VPN tunnel connections. It serves as both a standalone Azure resource and a component of Virtual WAN, offering secure connectivity for clients outside Azure to access resources such as file shares without opening TCP port 445.

VPN Gateway throughput varies based on SKU, with zone-redundant SKU options available for select configurations. It supports configurable IPsec policies and SKU-based capacity limits.

As a Virtual WAN component, VPN Gateway provides monitorable metrics including throughput, connection counts, tunnel availability, TunnelEgressPacketDropCount, TunnelIngressPacketDropCount, TunnelBandwidth, and connection status metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771b01fe7618e75e298642ca2a2cb0e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d73a470d503be7e3a2f2ef63b96ec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3f86dbbc0e68845a4cfbd563dcaafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c74dac0959c495ccca3e91ce252cb225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142487c37cb4da71ab0fecf01ad7e10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Flows">
  <data key="d0">Critical Flows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical Flows are essential workload paths and processes that are vital to primary business activities and operations. They represent the most important and high-priority workflows within a workload, typically characterized as business critical, time-sensitive, latency sensitive, and having a direct effect on revenue generation.

Critical Flows are assigned criticality levels based on multiple factors, including frequency, criticality, risk, data intensiveness, and architecture intensiveness. These classifications help determine the required components, resiliency approaches, and performance optimization strategies needed to support them.

Given their importance, Critical Flows require redundancy to meet reliability targets and must remain operational during outages. They demand prioritized resource allocation and performance optimization to ensure continuous operation and support of high-priority business processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7595d0066e438d094afa55de7d2ba18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720e4839ab18a5ecc8b875712ef0f4cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43be904f845543056b0462aeab67302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-617354e6d70206a2787d2a92e6998746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997386</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shard">
  <data key="d0">Shard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A shard is a horizontal database partitioning strategy that supports multiple storage instances with a common schema.&lt;SEP&gt;A shard is a horizontal database partitioning strategy that supports multiple storage instances with a common schema.&lt;SEP&gt;A horizontal partition that contains a subset of data rows from a larger dataset, sharing the same schema but containing different data.&lt;SEP&gt;A shard is a SQL database that holds partitioned data, addressed via shard maps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e47e51139cb584d95de7bb450c2af708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc8280bb50c2a5f4a589617c1bed437</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure OpenAI">
  <data key="d0">Azure OpenAI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure OpenAI managed endpoints abstract underlying infrastructure complexity behind capacity units.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure OpenAI managed endpoints abstract underlying infrastructure complexity behind capacity units.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure OpenAI is a language model service that can be accessed through an AI gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure OpenAI is a platform recommended for foundation model hosting, offering both batch and online inferencing capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
