  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Data Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data consistency is the measure of how in sync or out of sync a given dataset is across multiple stores.&lt;SEP&gt;Data consistency is the measure of how in sync or out of sync a given dataset is across multiple stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partitioning">
  <data key="d0">Partitioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Partitioning is the process of physically dividing data into separate data stores or smaller, manageable subsets. It is a data management and redesign strategy used to improve performance, scalability, and reliability, particularly as data growth occurs in production systems.

Partitioning enables parallel processing and reduces contention by distributing workload across segments. It can be implemented in several forms, including horizontal, vertical, or functional partitioning. By simplifying data management and ensuring reliable access and maintenance, partitioning serves as a key technique for enhancing overall system performance and efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Partitioning involves dividing a workload into smaller manageable units to distribute data and processing across multiple resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Partitioning is the process of dividing a large dataset or workload into smaller, more manageable parts called partitions, enabling parallel processing and reducing contention.&lt;SEP&gt;Partitioning is a data management strategy that distributes data across multiple partitions to improve performance and scalability, requiring careful planning around data distribution, query patterns, and workload requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique of dividing a large dataset into smaller subsets called partitions for parallel processing and improved query performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Partitioning involves structuring partition keys with hash characters to improve list, query, and read performance for blobs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2829ddae563971c0c88cbe1829d1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c944e9a44adf39c12919b36fa366a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fb475b8b7efe4018b64a1ed512f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region">
  <data key="d0">Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A region is an Azure datacenter location used for deploying redundant resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A region is an Azure datacenter location used for deploying redundant resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A geographic perimeter containing a set of datacenters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc27c33aba333fbae143b55b08a314fd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless">
  <data key="d0">Serverless</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless is a cloud computing model that allows adding redundancy without managing data replication or failover operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless is a cloud computing model that allows adding redundancy without managing data replication or failover operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless computing is a managed service approach that relieves operational burden and supports automatic scaling for cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;A computing model considered for architecture optimization to use fewer resources and reduce costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless is a SQL Database service tier option for workload cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless is a cloud computing model considered as an option for modernizing legacy code.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless workloads are highly optimized managed services that contribute to better sustainability posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9274b98dae68e1fda563c0a186872af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d57d3c8e9b437c3bf033faee9829a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Database">
  <data key="d0">SQL Database</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL Database is a Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) relational database service offered by Microsoft Azure. It supports elastic scaling and pooling, allowing flexible resource management, and can host shards, though it does not support cross-database joins.

The service provides robust high-availability and disaster recovery features, including automatic failover groups and active geo-replication. It offers transparent data encryption to encrypt database files at the page level, along with various security and networking configurations for cost optimization.

Azure SQL Database supports automatic tuning features for performance optimization and provides retry mechanisms through ADO.NET, Entity Framework, and Entity Framework Core. It is commonly discussed in the context of operational excellence, monitoring, performance tuning, backup, and deployment best practices.&lt;SEP&gt;SQL Database is an Azure database service that differs from SQL Managed Instance in available controls and capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbfe826fe19c233eb2d1b279f7950e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-428d5f718f38d153cbe16fd48c1637de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e47e51139cb584d95de7bb450c2af708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d57d3c8e9b437c3bf033faee9829a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe464ce8a55b32a868b7ba10711df9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Distant Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Distant Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-distant deployments spread workloads across regions hundreds or thousands of miles apart to protect against large-scale disasters, introducing higher latency and complex data consistency requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-distant deployments spread workloads across regions hundreds or thousands of miles apart to protect against large-scale disasters, introducing higher latency and complex data consistency requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Posture">
  <data key="d0">Security Posture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security posture refers to the overall security state of a system that must be continuously improved and not allowed to degrade over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Security posture refers to the overall security state of a system that must be continuously improved and not allowed to degrade over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996677</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assume Breach">
  <data key="d0">Assume Breach</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Assume Breach is a foundational security principle and Zero Trust concept that presupposes systems may already be compromised or that an attacker may eventually gain access. Rather than relying solely on perimeter defenses, this mindset guides organizations to design compensating controls that limit risk and damage if primary defenses fail. Key strategies associated with Assume Breach include encryption, containment, and other defensive measures that minimize the blast radius of a potential compromise. By planning accordingly from the outset, organizations adopting this principle build more resilient security architectures capable of detecting, containing, and responding to threats even after initial infiltration.&lt;SEP&gt;Assume breach is a security mindset that plans for control failures and applies layered defenses to limit impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727509da0a6c0effe0339afa582c8da4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a879a1f2cc37839210f7fa1a38c26a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verify Explicitly">
  <data key="d0">Verify Explicitly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Verify Explicitly is a foundational Zero Trust security principle that requires explicit verification of all access, actions, and data changes. It ensures that only trusted identities perform intended and allowed actions from expected locations, using trusted sources for validation. The principle focuses on right-sizing security measures and minimizing vulnerabilities through explicit validation, rejecting any implicit trust in users, devices, or network locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727509da0a6c0effe0339afa582c8da4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a879a1f2cc37839210f7fa1a38c26a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vulnerability Scanning">
  <data key="d0">Vulnerability Scanning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vulnerability scanning detects exploits in infrastructure, dependencies, and application code.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerability scanning is a security check performed in deployment pipelines to identify security weaknesses.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerability scanning is incorporated into pipelines during pre-deployment and continues post-deployment to detect security vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerability scanning detects exploits in infrastructure, dependencies, and application code.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-080b0147971910915ed740faf5b69284</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/establish-baseline.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996679</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIA Triad">
  <data key="d0">CIA Triad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The CIA triad refers to the interrelated security principles of confidentiality, integrity, and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;The CIA triad represents confidentiality, integrity, and availability security assurances that must be preserved during and after attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The CIA triad refers to the interrelated security principles of confidentiality, integrity, and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;The CIA triad represents confidentiality, integrity, and availability security assurances that must be preserved during and after attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996679</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Development Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">Security Development Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Development Lifecycle (SDL) is a set of best practices for maintaining security features and workload asset inventories.&lt;SEP&gt;Security Development Lifecycle (SDL) is a set of best practices for maintaining security features and workload asset inventories.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of practices provided by Microsoft that supports security assurance and compliance requirements, aligned throughout the software development lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of practices provided by Microsoft that supports security assurance and compliance requirements, including tests that catch vulnerabilities in code.&lt;SEP&gt;SDL practices apply security review to API policy changes similar to application code changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5200ddd62ebcb8e16dece7ddc1422557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asset Inventory">
  <data key="d0">Asset Inventory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A comprehensive asset inventory includes classified information about resources, locations, dependencies, and owners relevant to security.&lt;SEP&gt;Asset inventory involves identifying stakeholders of workload assets, classifying them by security requirements and criticality.&lt;SEP&gt;A comprehensive asset inventory includes classified information about resources, locations, dependencies, and owners relevant to security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/establish-baseline.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996679</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root-Cause Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Root-Cause Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Root-cause analysis is a post-incident activity that provides insight into the impact of breaches and drives improvements in defenses and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Root-cause analysis is a structured post-incident review method to identify weaknesses and areas for improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Root-cause analysis is a post-incident activity that provides insight into the impact of breaches and drives improvements in defenses and operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d20b573314239b2a88ca3deb8586c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Posture Management">
  <data key="d0">Security Posture Management</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Security posture management is a platform-provided feature for quantifying current security state against established baselines and setting remediation priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Security posture management is a platform-provided feature for quantifying current security state against established baselines and setting remediation priorities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Threat Intelligence">
  <data key="d0">Threat Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Threat intelligence powered by security analytics enables dynamic detection of threats.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy for interpreting threat detection data to detect suspicious activity by examining patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Threat intelligence powered by security analytics enables dynamic detection of threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Threat intelligence uses Microsoft's threat intelligence feed to automatically alert and block traffic from known malicious IP addresses, domains, and URLs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af976d288fcb8191fe6fb55f44aaeba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e496d3c1901ebb6e0f0add1d59b5b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/monitor-threats.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Security Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Checklist is a document containing a complete set of security recommendations. It serves as a resource for driving security actions after setting a security strategy and is recommended as a next step for implementing security practices. It can be referenced for ongoing guidance on security measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7277d28a361465235f16e5be124c32d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9641143ef161c630f4c2735baa058dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8560181068572aab32ee3c98848771</data>
