  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation is a security strategy used to plan and enforce security boundaries within workload environments, processes, and team structures to isolate access and function. It involves isolating workload resources from other parts of the organization to enhance security and management, containing the blast radius through identity, network, and other isolation approaches.

Segmentation enables fine-grained security controls and distinct performance characteristics but can increase total ownership costs. It includes exercises to identify firewall injection points on communication paths of network segments, supporting controlled access across different segments for stronger overall security posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f01a2d2b2e2dfa5053288e4cf9593f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6503993c6e8852f14500c5e6630b88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d</data>
