<node id="Least-Privilege Access">
  <data key="d0">Least-Privilege Access</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Least-privilege access limits permissions to the right identities, right set of permissions, right duration, and right assets.&lt;SEP&gt;A Zero Trust principle that aims at minimizing a set of permissions to complete a job function.&lt;SEP&gt;Least-privilege access limits permissions to the right identities, right set of permissions, right duration, and right assets.&lt;SEP&gt;A security principle where identities are granted the minimum level of access needed, limiting negative effects if compromised.&lt;SEP&gt;A Zero Trust principle that aims at minimizing a set of permissions to complete a job function.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle of least-privilege access grants users only the necessary permissions to perform their tasks, used as a basis for defining access policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6503993c6e8852f14500c5e6630b88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
