<node id="Identity And Access Management">
  <data key="d0">Identity And Access Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity And Access Management (IAM) is a security discipline focused on authenticating and authorizing identities accessing workload resources. It provides strict, conditional, and auditable management of access across workload users, team members, and system components.

Identity is the cornerstone of cloud security, forming the foundation of access management in SaaS solutions. IAM is a critical area for SaaS workloads, serving as the first line of defense for protecting data. As a design area, it addresses identity management challenges in multitenant SaaS environments, including federation with customer identity systems.

IAM configurations are refined as part of Level 4 security hardening strategies. Additional guidance on identity controls is provided through referenced documentation such as identity-access.md.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d8a1fa2cefd5c5b3095c48727dd166b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9514c481f519092f6d4362611c52ecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6503993c6e8852f14500c5e6630b88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a0beb0360defdd62600690749d5e142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96969696039ca4d7daf8f0eaa36cb1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/governance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004508</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Design Principles">
  <data key="d0">Security Design Principles</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Design Principles are guidelines referenced during the design phase of a workload. They provide a high-level design strategy for achieving confidentiality, integrity, and availability goals by applying approaches to technical design.

These principles are applicable across various Azure services, including App Service, Container Apps, Azure Front Door, and Azure Functions. For example, they guide technical design around hosting on App Service, restrict traffic coming through Azure Front Door, and inform security design for Azure Functions and Container Apps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
