<node id="SDLC">
  <data key="d0">SDLC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SDLC (Software Development Lifecycle) requires security validation that usually needs specialized tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Development Lifecycle, a framework of practices that may need to evolve as workloads and external factors change.&lt;SEP&gt;The Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) encompasses development and deployment phases that require security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The Software Development Lifecycle is an iterative process where security practices must be continuously applied from development to decommission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Software Development Lifecycle is the process into which routine security tests should be integrated.&lt;SEP&gt;SDLC (Software Development Lifecycle) requires security validation that usually needs specialized tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Development Lifecycle, a framework of practices that may need to evolve as workloads and external factors change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf9fd57985f14c81b7d1b9d2924d1bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6753f3d7315e92dc2b4f1d56644604</data>
