</node>
<node id="Latency">
  <data key="d0">Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latency refers to the time delay between when a request is initiated and when the result becomes available. It is a common response time metric, with example targets such as 200 milliseconds, and broadly measures the responsiveness of systems and operations.

In the context of networking and distributed systems, latency represents the time data takes to travel from source to destination, which increases the further services are from each other. Architectural components such as gateway routing, messaging brokers, and anti-corruption layers introduce additional latency that draws against performance target budgets.

In security contexts, latency is the delay added to requests by security controls such as inspection, identity verification, and encryption in workload flows. In storage systems, latency measures how long storage operations last, indicating the responsiveness of the storage system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6461a458cf4d4525d7fe6f8f9cfa20e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56d3f8085e9faa95d82a0d2dfdacc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4e354767f44f79da40710542ed5310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84a8087984070a29596b50c6ea41e0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Firewalls">
  <data key="d0">Firewalls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Firewalls are inspection security controls that add latency and can impact performance through rule ordering, complexity, and quantity.&lt;SEP&gt;Firewalls are inspection security controls that add latency and can impact performance through rule ordering, complexity, and quantity.&lt;SEP&gt;Firewalls control access to databases by defining rules for allowed network traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030</data>
