<node id="Performance Testing Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Performance Testing Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy for conducting various types of performance tests including manual, low-effort tests and automated routine performance tests in pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy for conducting various types of performance tests including manual, low-effort tests and automated routine performance tests in pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Gates">
  <data key="d0">Quality Gates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality Gates are checkpoints integrated into deployment, release promotion, and code promotion processes that ensure changes meet defined criteria and performance standards before advancing to the next stage or higher environment. They serve as enforcement mechanisms that block a release if performance falls below expectations, requiring changes to pass tests and receive approval before proceeding.

Quality Gates enforce best practices to reduce risks, with artifacts gaining confidence each time they pass through a gate. They also serve as mechanisms that enforce coding standards and catch potential issues early, including through automated code reviews and static code analysis. By functioning as checkpoints in the deployment and testing pipeline, Quality Gates help avoid deploying unsustainable solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb4be3d9c01e97b5b077710134d8de16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ff8d586800116f4a9c0f2e6c0039f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66676114d38f71040fa212c5425b398e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Planning">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Capacity Planning is the process of forecasting workload demand and determining the resources required to meet that demand while balancing cost and performance. It involves proactively measuring, estimating, and provisioning computing resources—such as CPU, memory, storage, and network bandwidth—to address anticipated changes in capacity and meet workload performance targets.

Capacity Planning is an iterative process that shifts organizations from reactive to proactive resource management. It relies on performance models and predictive modeling based on the capability of selected resources to forecast future needs. This includes analyzing trends and continuously updating predictions to match workload goals and user demand, ensuring sufficient resources are available for a defined period.

Capacity Planning is a key strategy for achieving performance efficiency by aligning resource supply with demand. It is also one of the primary purposes served by operations built for observability, leveraging monitoring and measurement data to inform resource planning decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning involves assessing current utilization, projecting future needs, and planning infrastructure changes for Virtual WAN.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning involves understanding resource consumption when onboarding new customers, accounting for scaling limits such as networking or storage constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning refers to managing resource utilization including CPU, memory, storage, and IOPS.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning involves monitoring Azure subscription limits and scaling strategies to ensure smooth Azure Virtual Desktop operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3baca1f2978b6321676e22c33fba6cf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a9cc1e862b6a71315c64180df14f2e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43be904f845543056b0462aeab67302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4aed87d4e81857a842b49249489eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3f86dbbc0e68845a4cfbd563dcaafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proof Of Concept">
  <data key="d0">Proof Of Concept</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A validation approach to confirm proposed design choices can meet performance targets and anticipated load.&lt;SEP&gt;A POC is a small-scale validation conducted to assess the usability, features, and effectiveness of testing tools in a specific testing scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;A proof of concept (POC) can be used for performance testing when production code isn't ready.&lt;SEP&gt;A validation approach to confirm proposed design choices can meet performance targets and anticipated load.&lt;SEP&gt;A proof of concept (POC) is a method to validate understanding of billing factors and increments through hands-on experience, helping refine workload design for cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;A proof of concept (POC) is used by architects to inform design decisions and assess feasibility, but POC code should never be considered production-ready.&lt;SEP&gt;A method to validate high-risk or novel components with working code before finalizing a design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d20a250447d571c0a31d1f1f211c8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5fd47376a7e9081496e03cedc06a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76c4bb7431f02f35a05848683404dfc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98ea85178a5817d9a2ef65e41464e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d263497f5caeee5776927a85b56895</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/architect-role/collaboration.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/architect-role/fundamentals.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Model">
  <data key="d0">Performance Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A model that is updated based on tested and monitored metrics, indicating increased, reduced, or no effect on performance of flows.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance model considers usage patterns, business impact, and operational costs to calculate initial performance targets and supports strategic resource planning.&lt;SEP&gt;A model that is updated based on tested and monitored metrics, indicating increased, reduced, or no effect on performance of flows.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance model considers usage patterns, business impact, and operational costs to calculate initial performance targets and supports strategic resource planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Techniques used to forecast anticipated changes in capacity, helping avoid resource shortages or overprovisioning.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive modeling builds mathematical models using historical data and machine learning algorithms to predict future demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Techniques used to forecast anticipated changes in capacity, helping avoid resource shortages or overprovisioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a9cc1e862b6a71315c64180df14f2e6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Pillars">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Pillars</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A framework whose optimizations in various pillars can cause changes that strain workload resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A framework whose optimizations in various pillars can cause changes that strain workload resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The evaluation of scaling needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic scaling evaluates elasticity needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of dynamically adjusting capacity by scaling up when demand increases and scaling down when no longer needed.&lt;SEP&gt;The evaluation of scaling needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic scaling evaluates elasticity needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of dynamically adjusting capacity by scaling up when demand increases and scaling down when no longer needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Performance Efficiency Checklist is a complete set of recommendations for optimizing performance efficiency. It is used to validate workload design against performance efficiency principles and serves as a recommended next step resource for performance efficiency guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a complete set of recommendations for performance efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a complete set of recommendations for performance efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a complete set of recommendations related to performance efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a complete set of recommendations for performance efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a complete set of recommendations for performance efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0d557186587fd7356bc48c45898548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997b67d2a5ddf57a24dd0380ce47e074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0c9390a87db2dcb2296e0f0d2ad3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df125b1159752fb88280cd8ef02f3320&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef6111a0cc4b828fa5b996fe5d89475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ec3bae0c0f185d5df0733c73840934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b32925fbb6ae4e81a734e77c9c7decb</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/respond-live-performance-issues.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Targets">
  <data key="d0">Performance Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance targets are negotiated benchmarks aligned with business requirements and user experience expectations, refined iteratively through testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance targets are benchmarks used to measure the current performance of a workload or flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance targets are measurable, realistic thresholds for metrics like response time and error rate, aligned with workload objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance targets are metrics that define performance objectives, expressed as a single numerical value or a numerical range, serving as a foundation for improvements.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance targets are negotiated benchmarks aligned with business requirements and user experience expectations, refined iteratively through testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance targets ensure essential flows receive adequate resources and are continuously adjusted to meet evolving demands.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77532f9499e43bf59e3245f6d41d3561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0d557186587fd7356bc48c45898548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4e354767f44f79da40710542ed5310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef06ef7197a8a530ba87de793b6cb9e5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/collect-performance-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Performance Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance optimization is a practice of dedicating time to monitor and continuously improve system performance throughout the development lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance optimization is a practice of dedicating time to monitor and continuously improve system performance throughout the development lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonfunctional Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Nonfunctional Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonfunctional requirements are targets that can be revisited and updated by analyzing historical production trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonfunctional requirements are targets that can be revisited and updated by analyzing historical production trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonfunctional requirements include response time, resource utilization, and cost considerations that guide autoscaling optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonfunctional requirements include latency, throughput limitations, cost management, model accuracy, compliance, and data privacy challenges inherent to AI technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6791a2ed934654a8da6b225e44dac9e3</data>
