  <data key="d5">1776998144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Partitioning And Sharding">
  <data key="d0">Data Partitioning And Sharding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data partitioning and sharding help avoid performance issues in large datasets but increase complexity due to consistency requirements across additional resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Data partitioning and sharding are techniques that can complicate routine operational tasks like backups and key rotations when teams try to ensure data consistency.&lt;SEP&gt;Data partitioning and sharding help avoid performance issues in large datasets but increase complexity due to consistency requirements across additional resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Data partitioning and sharding are techniques that can complicate routine operational tasks like backups and key rotations when teams try to ensure data consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Culture Stress">
  <data key="d0">Culture Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Culture stress is a tradeoff associated with Operational Excellence, relating to impacts on team morale from blame and inconvenient work schedules.&lt;SEP&gt;Culture stress is a tradeoff associated with Operational Excellence, relating to impacts on team morale from blame and inconvenient work schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997521</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denormalization">
  <data key="d0">Denormalization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Denormalization optimizes data access patterns for performance but introduces complexity from keeping multiple data representations synchronized.&lt;SEP&gt;Denormalization optimizes data access patterns for performance but introduces complexity from keeping multiple data representations synchronized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Bus">
  <data key="d0">Message Bus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A message bus is used for load leveling, introducing a critical stateful component to the workload.&lt;SEP&gt;A message bus is used for load leveling, introducing a critical stateful component to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Load Balancer is a networking service that distributes incoming traffic across multiple back-end instances to ensure reliability and availability. In Azure, Load Balancer operates as a Layer 4 network service supporting TCP and UDP traffic load balancing, though it does not support SSL/TLS termination. It is available in Basic and Standard SKUs and supports up to 5,000 VMs in a single back-end pool.

Load Balancer plays a critical role in autoscaling scenarios by distributing traffic across autoscaled replicas, requiring reliable operation. When built into zone-redundant services, it disperses requests across instances in multiple availability zones and redirects traffic during outages, enhancing fault tolerance.

Additionally, Load Balancer can serve as a global traffic management mechanism used to control traffic shifting between blue and green environments, supporting deployment strategies that minimize downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Performance Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Application Performance Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">APM is a system that enables teams to learn from active environments through instrumentation of application code or hosting environment.&lt;SEP&gt;APM tools provide deep insights into applications, helping trace individual transactions and map paths through workload services.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Performance Monitoring (APM) tools monitor application performance, tracking response times, errors, and other performance metrics for flow optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;APM is a system that enables teams to learn from active environments through instrumentation of application code or hosting environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Application performance monitoring (APM) is an observability tool used to detect and diagnose performance issues during deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d20a250447d571c0a31d1f1f211c8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense In Depth">
  <data key="d0">Defense In Depth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense in depth is a security approach establishing controls across multiple layers, sometimes redundantly, which may be compromised by performance optimizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense in depth is a security approach using multiple layers of segmentation and controls at various network boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A security approach maintaining end-to-end control of security affordances across all hops and internal segments.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense in depth is a security approach enabled by segmentation based on Zero Trust model principles.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense in depth is a security approach establishing controls across multiple layers, sometimes redundantly, which may be compromised by performance optimizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Defense in depth deploys security controls at multiple network layers for comprehensive protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Transactions">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Transactions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthetic transactions are used in performance testing on active environments, carrying the risk of causing malfunctions.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthetic transactions consistently test real-world user experience to identify problems before users are affected.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthetic transactions are used in performance testing on active environments, carrying the risk of causing malfunctions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Pillar">
  <data key="d0">Security Pillar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security pillar is an architecture framework component focused on establishing and strengthening workload security posture through multiple levels. It provides confidentiality, integrity, and availability guarantees to workloads.

The Security pillar prioritizes a reduced and contained surface area to minimize attack vectors, along with strong segmentation to enable fine-grained security controls, support targeted security measures, and reduce blast radius. Key priorities include isolation, strong authorization, uniform application security, and modern protocols. The Security pillar also encompasses security testing as part of its framework responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security pillar provides confidentiality, integrity, and availability guarantees to workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security pillar provides confidentiality, integrity, and availability guarantees to workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security pillar provides confidentiality, integrity, and availability guarantees to workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cf91e067df302cf4a6958a130fa0fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fa337fdf4c15ddf378bf74ac66c3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6c79bd6c72543235e9a779851e5641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb40dfedb445538dcaca461fef2278f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4889043b463029eef941a26e276c8840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c24295afcc6630eeee9c761977e6d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cd6df2b9534dcc70f59a3fbb6607582</data>
