</node>
<node id="Multitenancy">
  <data key="d0">Multitenancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multitenancy is a core business methodology and technical strategy for designing SaaS workloads, where multiple tenants share resources to maximize cost efficiency through increased density. It is an architecture in which careful isolation and authorization of data access are required to serve multiple customers from shared infrastructure. However, multitenancy can lead to security concerns, such as unauthorized lateral movement between tenants, making robust security controls essential.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitenancy is a core business methodology for designing SaaS workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitenancy refers to keeping tenant (customer) data separate in an application, driven by effective user authentication and authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitenancy is a core methodology for SaaS workloads where multiple tenants share a platform while maintaining data isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitenancy is a core business methodology for designing SaaS workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Multitenancy is a core business methodology for designing SaaS workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926d040bafb1c4ed2780ed2173357dfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77fdbd68a5283ca0d7625c8716f1b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead72caffece10babff69d75d2a2b12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94d10f8b3b5b59147b8608dc6f63cb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a0beb0360defdd62600690749d5e142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc63217f8e41f1a8e15dac9427efa323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51059245c825ad997eabe5a0dc767a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da6ff7f8e8d62245d48fe850b4eb70f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/devops.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/resource-organization.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Performance Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance-centric cloud design patterns may introduce extra components to improve performance but add complexity and cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance-centric cloud design patterns may introduce extra components to improve performance but add complexity and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A monitoring system is built with its own stack and flows, decoupled from the workload, covering infrastructure, application health, and build and release processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A monitoring system is built with its own stack and flows, decoupled from the workload, covering infrastructure, application health, and build and release processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Telemetry is emitted from application code to correlate key points of execution flow and provide end-to-end views at different granularity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Collective term for logs, metrics, traces, and events that provides the foundation for observability.&lt;SEP&gt;Telemetry is emitted from application code to correlate key points of execution flow and provide end-to-end views at different granularity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational signals generated from systems, referring to logs, traces, and metrics that provide insight into system behavior and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44db748d8a4a0feea6626c78c05321a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metrics are monitoring signals prioritized for triggering actions that rely on numeric measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Numerical values collected at regular intervals that describe aspects of a system at a particular time.&lt;SEP&gt;Metrics are numerical values that describe the state of a system at a particular point in time.&lt;SEP&gt;Numerical values collected at regular intervals that describe system performance and help identify trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Metrics are monitoring signals prioritized for triggering actions that rely on numeric measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Numerical measurements of a system or resource at a specific point in time, often accompanied by tags or dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77532f9499e43bf59e3245f6d41d3561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44db748d8a4a0feea6626c78c05321a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f</data>
