<node id="Continuous Improvement">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Improvement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous improvement is a goal driven by learning from experience and collected data to iteratively enhance workload operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous improvement is an environment where teams learn from production and listen to feedback to optimize performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous improvement is a goal driven by learning from experience and collected data to iteratively enhance workload operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fostering an environment where the workload team is empowered to explore and propose cost-saving measures through open dialog, training, and team-building.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous improvement is a theme across all Well-Architected Framework pillars, encouraging a progressive mindset toward new approaches and technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-517ef83a1fe99178ace6be8c8c95c6c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
