  <data key="d5">1776999609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Management">
  <data key="d0">Change Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Systematic change management is used to track progress and success in development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of managing changes in production environments to maintain system reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Change management is Level 4 focus area involving maintaining and improving a live system through efficient day-2 operations such as triage, maintenance, upgrades, and troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;Change management is the priority focus at this maturity level, encompassing triage, maintenance, upgrades, and troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;Systematic change management is used to track progress and success in development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Change management practices are crucial for mitigating performance, security, and reliability impacts when making cost-saving adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Change management involves making the process of implementing change smooth and accepted through coaching and continuous learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e4a31ea43efb7a100f1df033cb0e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe53a5474c5e4934795683b73b06789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d440b1a3c317835e0dd6ef617a4d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb32778b5a44a1a37ca0f92518c49c6e</data>
