  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Development Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">Software Development Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) is a multistage, systematic process framework for developing software systems, spanning from ideation to delivery. It encompasses planning, design, development, testing, deployment, and monitoring activities, and can be implemented through various frameworks such as Scrum, Kanban, or Waterfall. The SDLC provides rigor, consistency, specificity, and prioritization to change management in a workload, reflecting industry-proven processes that enhance development efficiency.

The SDLC serves as the foundation into which baseline security practices and threat modeling should be integrated. Performance tests should also be conducted as early as possible within the SDLC to catch issues earlier. As architecture, business requirements, and team structure change, SDLC practices may need to evolve accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5200ddd62ebcb8e16dece7ddc1422557&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5fd47376a7e9081496e03cedc06a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1c379f7c96adb8c669329b1ce128b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f84fdf8398257ab3343f339b69880c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb32778b5a44a1a37ca0f92518c49c6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5</data>
