<node id="Gateway Routing">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An access pattern used in deployment models that can introduce latency affecting performance targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway Routing routes incoming network requests to various backend systems based on request intents, business logic, and backend availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway Routing routes incoming network requests to various backend systems based on request intents, business logic, and backend availability to balance load.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that routes incoming network requests to various backend systems based on request intents and business logic, supporting advanced deployment models.&lt;SEP&gt;An access pattern used in deployment models that can introduce latency affecting performance targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway routing is a pattern for routing requests through a gateway.</data>
