</node>
<node id="Continuous Integration">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Integration (CI) is a software development practice where code changes are regularly integrated into shared repositories, with automated builds and tests triggered on every code commit. This approach helps identify conflicts early, reduces risky merges, and provides quick quality feedback to development teams. CI encompasses automated processes to validate, secure, and package code as it moves through the development lifecycle, including running unit tests as part of routine builds. It integrates source control systems with software deployment pipelines to provide automated build, test, and feedback mechanisms. CI is supported by platforms such as GitHub and Azure DevOps.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous integration in release engineering includes source control, automated testing, and best practices for modern software development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e8f0e5af9ce702f31e5d4baa1c048d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac8f606b24c325a1ba25f35deaa3143&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb22f500a9418e75c787f58356ea6d23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c12853dd39d9a9a4beefa63014102d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/formalize-development-practices.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/release-engineering-continuous-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
