</node>
<node id="Return On Investment">
  <data key="d0">Return On Investment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Return on investment (ROI) is a financial metric that architecture design must factor in alongside financial constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on investment (ROI) is a measure of business value that cost optimization aims to maximize for workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on investment (ROI) is a measure of business value that cost optimization aims to maximize for workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on investment measures what percentage of revenue goes into system operation and other ROI metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on Investment (ROI) is a measure used to evaluate the value of each environment, even if the environment does not generate direct profit.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on investment (ROI) is a financial metric that architecture design must factor in alongside financial constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21e41edd72b9157b512d1a210db4941b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54ab6df34391dde2f99128ba16bd1f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Model">
  <data key="d0">Cost Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cost model is a fundamental exercise and decision-making aid that estimates the total cost of ownership for a workload by segmenting and breaking down all associated expenses. These expenses typically include infrastructure, software licenses, personnel, data storage, platform services, user and system flows, operations, maintenance, support, and implementation costs.

A cost model serves as a foundational tool for expense forecasting and budget planning. It predicts combined costs of services and associated expenses, projects future expenses, allocates funds, adjusts for deviations, and evaluates the financial impact of business changes. It is used alongside the budget to review spending with stakeholders, identify cost trends, and uncover optimization areas.

Additionally, a cost model supports budgeting, scenario analysis, and resource optimization, enabling informed decision-making about workload expenses.&lt;SEP&gt;A cost model helps understand, forecast, and optimize costs, and make informed architectural decisions based on COGS effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A cost model represents the marginal cost per customer and identifies how business metrics influence costs in SaaS development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02ed72abe4ca2d3a3487f2b3c4c1bb89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76e6af9e7f0b10472ec2406ba2334d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f082730bb91f06b04e3b6f39138f774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80555797ec0044df18cccee521a04c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d440b1a3c317835e0dd6ef617a4d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd009330fd8bb700e86760925fa4ea4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-661923999882010b2c5bc9a8ccb33fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/cost-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
