  <data key="d5">1776998900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Guardrails">
  <data key="d0">Cost Guardrails</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost guardrails are architectural enforcement mechanisms that keep resources within upper and lower budget limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost guardrails are architectural enforcement mechanisms that keep resources within upper and lower budget limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SDLC Environments">
  <data key="d0">SDLC Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Software development lifecycle environments that should be treated differently to save costs, with nonproduction environments having different features and SKUs.&lt;SEP&gt;Software development lifecycle environments that should be treated differently to save costs, with nonproduction environments having different features and SKUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost-Management Discipline">
  <data key="d0">Cost-Management Discipline</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost-management discipline is a principle focused on building a team culture with awareness of budget, expenses, reporting, and cost tracking.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost-management discipline is a principle focused on building a team culture with awareness of budget, expenses, reporting, and cost tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accountability Model">
  <data key="d0">Accountability Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An accountability model is an effective but flexible governance structure with properly assigned roles and responsibilities to enforce functional expectations and prevent unnecessary expenditure.&lt;SEP&gt;An accountability model is an effective but flexible governance structure with properly assigned roles and responsibilities to enforce functional expectations and prevent unnecessary expenditure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Cost Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A cost baseline includes projected growth and ensures design choices work within allocated budget to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A cost baseline includes projected growth and ensures design choices work within allocated budget to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Showback">
  <data key="d0">Showback</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Showback is a process for reporting and attributing costs to business units without direct billing.&lt;SEP&gt;Showback refers to providing cost visibility throughout an organization without charging individual teams or departments for their cloud costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Showback is an accounting model where departments are shown the cost of their workload usage without receiving payment from them.&lt;SEP&gt;An accounting model where departments are shown the cost of their workload usage without receiving payment from them.&lt;SEP&gt;Showback is a process for reporting and attributing costs to business units without direct billing.&lt;SEP&gt;Showback is a cost allocation method where centralized platform costs are displayed to workload teams without direct billing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b44c13ce2128c3df84d5bcf4f8f763a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54ab6df34391dde2f99128ba16bd1f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76e6af9e7f0b10472ec2406ba2334d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/cost-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chargeback">
  <data key="d0">Chargeback</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chargeback is a process for directly billing business units for their resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Chargeback involves billing internal teams or departments for their respective cloud costs based on actual usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Chargeback is an accounting model where departments are charged for their workload usage and payments are received from them.&lt;SEP&gt;An accounting model where departments are charged for their workload usage and payments are received from them.&lt;SEP&gt;Chargeback is a process for directly billing business units for their resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Chargeback is a cost allocation method where workload teams are billed for platform services, often cheaper due to economies of scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b44c13ce2128c3df84d5bcf4f8f763a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54ab6df34391dde2f99128ba16bd1f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76e6af9e7f0b10472ec2406ba2334d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/cost-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Right-Sizing">
  <data key="d0">Right-Sizing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Right-sizing involves adjusting resource allocation to match actual usage, reducing costs by resizing or removing underutilized resources or changing SKUs.&lt;SEP&gt;Right-sizing is the practice of adjusting resources to match workload requirements, helping align to billing increments and reduce costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Right-sizing is the process of adjusting resource allocation to better match actual usage needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Right-sizing involves adjusting resource allocation to match actual usage, reducing costs by resizing or removing underutilized resources or changing SKUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd0de7f853795f167d30d84ede72282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbf77302eae466ce3d619b76c771db34</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-component-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Cost Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost alerts are proactive notifications implemented when spending approaches predefined budget thresholds to prevent budget overruns.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts notify users when consumption reaches predefined thresholds for proactive spending monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts are proactive notifications implemented when spending approaches predefined budget thresholds to prevent budget overruns.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts are notifications set for budgets, cost anomalies, and commitment-based plan utilization to provide visibility into cloud spending and enable proactive cost management.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts are configurable notifications with multiple threshold levels at subscription, resource group, and topic levels to prevent cost overruns.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts notify users about unexpected cloud spend or when approaching predefined limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost alerts help monitor cloud spend through budget alerts, anomaly alerts, and scheduled alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd0de7f853795f167d30d84ede72282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96969696039ca4d7daf8f0eaa36cb1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad653e4d2f68d336a1fa1654643a4bb</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/governance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Usage Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Design For Usage Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design principle focused on maximizing the use of resources and operations to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements of a solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A design principle focused on maximizing the use of resources and operations to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements of a solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Rate Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Design For Rate Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design principle focused on increasing efficiency without redesigning or sacrificing requirements, by optimizing utility and costs of existing resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A design principle focused on increasing efficiency without redesigning or sacrificing requirements, by optimizing utility and costs of existing resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor And Optimize Over Time">
  <data key="d0">Monitor And Optimize Over Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle of continuously right-sizing investment as workloads evolve with the ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle of continuously right-sizing investment as workloads evolve with the ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Model">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where all provisioned resources are actively used, preferred over active-passive to avoid idle resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model where all provisioned resources are actively used, preferred over active-passive to avoid idle resources.&lt;SEP&gt;An active-active deployment model where workloads are deployed across multiple regions with all instances actively serving traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;A disaster recovery configuration using two host pools in separate regions, both active during normal operations, requiring no administrator intervention for failover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumption-Based Pricing">
  <data key="d0">Consumption-Based Pricing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing model where users pay for what they use, suitable when resources are not expected to be fully utilized.&lt;SEP&gt;A billing model where users pay for what they use, suitable when resources are not expected to be fully utilized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fixed-Price Billing">
  <data key="d0">Fixed-Price Billing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing model that usually costs less when utilization is high and predictable.&lt;SEP&gt;A billing model that usually costs less when utilization is high and predictable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Model">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where some provisioned resources remain idle as standby, which can lead to underutilization of paid resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model where some provisioned resources remain idle as standby, which can lead to underutilization of paid resources.&lt;SEP&gt;An active-passive deployment model where a primary instance serves traffic and a secondary instance becomes active upon failure.&lt;SEP&gt;A disaster recovery configuration where fewer compute resources are active in the secondary region, with failover requiring resource activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commitment-Based Discounts">
  <data key="d0">Commitment-Based Discounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Discounted resources obtained through prepurchase commitments, prioritized for developing new features or setting up additional environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Discounted resources obtained through prepurchase commitments, prioritized for developing new features or setting up additional environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Use">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A licensing alternative that gives usage rights to the same or comparable technologies at a lower cost without additional licensing.&lt;SEP&gt;A licensing alternative that gives usage rights to the same or comparable technologies at a lower cost without additional licensing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
