<node id="Queue-Based Load Leveling Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Queue-Based Load Leveling Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A cloud design pattern that smooths costs by introducing a message bus.&lt;SEP&gt;Queue-Based Load Leveling pattern uses a queue as a buffer between producer and consumer components to handle peaks in demand.&lt;SEP&gt;A cloud design pattern that smooths costs by introducing a message bus.&lt;SEP&gt;Queue-Based Load Leveling pattern uses queues as buffers to handle variable load on background tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Queue-Based Load Leveling pattern is an Azure architecture pattern for managing load distribution using queues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Queue-Based Load Leveling pattern queues work items as a buffer to smooth out traffic spikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e31fdc4d1c3251e67cb0588dd3047a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b934336b9f0ae48abbe56045f1da0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7faed93ac7c8b81fc0be047d2c1f773f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c</data>
