<node id="Health Probes">
  <data key="d0">Health Probes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Probes are configured checks that explicitly monitor application health, responsiveness, and availability by measuring response time and detecting failures. They ensure traffic is only routed to healthy endpoints by triggering automatic rerouting when issues are detected.

Health Probes encompass several types, including liveness, readiness, and startup probes, which serve distinct purposes: detecting failures, ensuring traffic routes to healthy containers, allowing proper initialization, and enabling self-healing mechanisms.

In the context of Azure services, Health Probes are used by Application Gateway to detect back-end unavailability and ensure traffic only routes to healthy back ends. Similarly, Azure Front Door configures Health Probes to conduct health checks on origin instances, determining their availability and readiness to receive requests, and assessing origins within a group to impact routing decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes detect unhealthy instances using HTTP or TCP to route traffic only to healthy back-end pool instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes using HTTP or TCP are used to monitor workload instance health and route traffic only to healthy back-end instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes monitor application readiness during scaling operations, ensuring smooth scale-out and scale-in without disrupting ongoing operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes ping endpoints from various locations to check availability, available in fast and slow ping options with different cost implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes are used by Traffic Manager to ping endpoints from various locations to check their availability, with options for slow or fast pings that trade off cost and detection speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Health probes monitor the health of back-end VMs and indicate when to remove unhealthy resources from rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443aa85fac21ccf603c8d3f8c5b909ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a007dbfba3cef886b2cc00b13f46310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-257827ee036f98e6274522ad2bfee550&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c2320d6f192d51ba7461cdb73ef6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
