<node id="Workload">
  <data key="d0">Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A workload refers to a cloud application and its subsystems whose runtime health is assessed through health modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A workload is a system that generates outputs and contains flows supporting business processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A workload is a discrete capability or computing task that can be logically separated from other tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A workload refers to a cloud application and its subsystems whose runtime health is assessed through health modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;A system composed of multiple use cases and flows, designed to fulfill business requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A workload refers to the product or system that architects design and continue to support through its lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection of application resources, custom code, AI models, data, and supporting infrastructure that function together to achieve defined business outcomes.</data>
