<node id="Azure Service Bus">
  <data key="d0">Azure Service Bus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Service Bus is a fully managed enterprise message broker within the Microsoft Azure platform that enables reliable messaging between distributed applications and services. It provides queue-based asynchronous communication capabilities, supporting queues, topics, subscriptions, and sessions for flexible messaging operations. The service is available in multiple pricing tiers, including Premium and Standard.

Azure Service Bus offers a rich set of features including duplicate detection, dead letter queues, auto-forwarding, partitioned entities, and advanced routing capabilities. It supports ReplyTo and CorrelationId properties for background task communication, as well as message schemas with attached metadata for classification purposes. The service facilitates asynchronous programming patterns such as priority queue processing.

For reliability and resilience, Azure Service Bus supports zone-redundant deployments, geo-disaster recovery, and replication patterns. It provides native programmatic retry capabilities and ETW (Event Tracing for Windows) telemetry. Architectural best practices cover authentication, private endpoints, tier selection, and autoscaling. The service also includes built-in policies for security and governance, supporting high-throughput messaging scenarios.

Azure Service Bus can provide custom metrics for autoscaling in Container Apps and serves various workloads across Azure architectures. In practical usage, it functions as a message-bus technology whose implementation details can be abstracted in block diagrams. For example, in an e-commerce scenario, a spike in failed messages on Azure Service Bus caused payment failures, illustrating the importance of monitoring and resilience. The service also provides guidance on failure modes to help ensure reliable messaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74ac1201f940bb7bb5693682e4dbc30b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df6e00fa9a90ca53e8d360c865875b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57aaf36552634a062a8c85ab22d4022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0c9390a87db2dcb2296e0f0d2ad3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0f7011b209ee2d53115a29ddfa186f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af17a604206f8056ed34d52736aca636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ddb1fca24e8f66e1403bf34e0339ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4e1326f308873031b3e530e46d8478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653342d517c710c9f67df8e6155d05a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e36fb889991403b16d790b11d406033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb40dfedb445538dcaca461fef2278f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-806209f42e9e5bd900cd963777ef796f</data>
