<node id="Service-Level Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Service-Level Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service-Level Objectives (SLOs) are target values for service-level indicators that define acceptable performance and reliability levels for applications, business processes, and workloads. They serve as business metrics used to establish availability and recovery targets for workload flows, setting accountability for workload teams.

SLOs have cost implications, as higher objectives can generate revenue and reduce costs by avoiding downtime. They are integral to defining platform reliability targets and ensuring that expected performance levels align with business requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) are targets that define acceptable levels of workload performance and reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) define acceptable performance thresholds for workloads and guide redundancy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) are percentage-based availability targets used to evaluate workload reliability on Azure Local.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) are specific reliability and performance targets for a service.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) measure reliability requirements using metrics like uptime, recovery time, and recovery point.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74ac1201f940bb7bb5693682e4dbc30b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7fdbb7d6c79a6437952833a6e0ac9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76e6af9e7f0b10472ec2406ba2334d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f082730bb91f06b04e3b6f39138f774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5158d59c7d2bc03597e0221545a1a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6c3c95f26c867cee192fcc4d9d6f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
