<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone-Redundant Deployment is a deployment model in Microsoft Azure that distributes resources, including application and storage tiers, across multiple availability zones within a single region. This approach provides high reliability and resiliency by ensuring that if one availability zone experiences an outage, the workload continues operating in the remaining zones.

Key features of Zone-Redundant Deployment include built-in load balancing, synchronous replication, and automatic failover, all managed by Microsoft. This eliminates the need for customers to manually handle synchronization and failover processes, simplifying operations while maintaining robust availability.

Zone-Redundant Deployment offers high reliability at moderate cost and is recommended for many production workloads. As a single-region strategy, it serves as an effective redundancy approach for organizations seeking resilient infrastructure without the complexity of multi-region architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An approach extending zone-redundant deployment by performing regular backups to a secondary region, providing protection against full region outages.&lt;SEP&gt;An approach extending zone-redundant deployment by performing regular backups to a secondary region, providing protection against full region outages.</data>
