</node>
<node id="Data Residency">
  <data key="d0">Data Residency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data residency refers to restrictions and compliance requirements governing the physical geographic locations where data can be stored and processed. These requirements are often driven by legal and regulatory mandates that dictate data must remain within a specific location or jurisdiction. Data residency is critically important for industries such as healthcare and banking, where strict regulations govern the handling and storage of sensitive information.

From an architectural perspective, data residency is a key concern that varies depending on the deployment approach and region selection. In Microsoft Azure environments, data residency compliance is achieved in both zonal and zone-redundant deployments by ensuring that data is stored within the selected Azure region. This allows organizations to meet their geographic data storage obligations while leveraging cloud infrastructure for resilience and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency refers to regulations governing where user data is stored, which can affect identity provider choices and require separate deployment stamps for different geographies.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency refers to requirements about where customer data can be stored, often driven by data sovereignty laws.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437b53743af22a4aaa11b22db9356761</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/resource-organization.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
