</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach that extends locally redundant deployment by performing regular backups of infrastructure and data to a secondary region for extra protection against primary region outages.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach that extends locally redundant deployment by performing regular backups of infrastructure and data to a secondary region for extra protection against primary region outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zonal Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zonal Deployment, also known as zone-pinned deployment, is a deployment model where resources are deployed into a specific availability zone. This approach reduces latency between components by co-locating them within the same zone. However, zonal deployment requires manual failover handling during outages, as resources are pinned to a particular zone rather than distributed across multiple zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture in which one primary instance processes traffic and secondary instances serve traffic if the primary is unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;A traffic routing approach where one instance handles traffic while others remain on standby for failover.&lt;SEP&gt;An architecture in which one primary instance processes traffic and secondary instances serve traffic if the primary is unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;A traffic routing approach where one instance handles traffic while others remain on standby for failover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture in which multiple instances of a solution actively process requests at the same time.&lt;SEP&gt;A request distribution model where multiple instances simultaneously handle traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment pattern where two or more environments are fully operational and serving live traffic simultaneously across multiple regions with zero or near-zero disruption on failure.&lt;SEP&gt;An architecture in which multiple instances of a solution actively process requests at the same time.&lt;SEP&gt;A request distribution model where multiple instances simultaneously handle traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d</data>
