  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Datacenter">
  <data key="d0">Datacenter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility containing servers, networking equipment, and other hardware to support Azure resources and workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A facility containing servers, networking equipment, and other hardware to support Azure resources and workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Region">
  <data key="d0">Paired Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired regions support certain types of multi-region deployment approaches in Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired regions support certain types of multi-region deployment approaches in Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Responsibility Principle">
  <data key="d0">Shared Responsibility Principle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle describing how responsibilities are divided between the cloud provider and the customer.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle describing how responsibilities are divided between the cloud provider and the customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform As A Service">
  <data key="d0">Platform As A Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Platform as a Service (PaaS) is a cloud service model where the provider manages the operating system and shares responsibility for identity, applications, and networking. PaaS is easier to configure and administer compared to Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), removing the need for virtual machine setup and maintenance tasks.

PaaS offerings provide built-in autoscale features and handle load balancing, client-request handling, and state management. PaaS database solutions are more cost-effective and efficient than IaaS by reducing manual scaling, backups, and infrastructure maintenance. In Azure, PaaS solutions typically support zone-redundant deployments.

PaaS is recommended to minimize operational burden for AI workloads and is preferred over self-hosted options to simplify design and automate workflow orchestration.&lt;SEP&gt;PaaS is a fully managed platform that handles scaling, availability, and performance, optimizing hardware efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ed64d4db4b1d8cf5e3ba5c43f2faf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b047e8b449398992f0dfab15265a69c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc27c33aba333fbae143b55b08a314fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea600d3306dde466b8e4fa453de97e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d7c0f28c3ae2bf90186c890ee840779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c191d35e97adae9dac9c5492df49a2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/simplify.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/select-services.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Data Replication">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Data Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Asynchronous data replication is a method where changes are committed in the primary region and replicated to secondary regions later, minimizing latency impact but risking some data loss during outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Asynchronous data replication is a method where changes are committed in the primary region and replicated to secondary regions later, minimizing latency impact but risking some data loss during outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synchronous Data Replication">
  <data key="d0">Synchronous Data Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synchronous data replication requires write operations to complete in each Azure region before a transaction is considered complete, providing very high reliability but potentially low performance due to inter-region latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous data replication requires write operations to complete in each Azure region before a transaction is considered complete, providing very high reliability but potentially low performance due to inter-region latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999554</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Region Network Latency">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Region Network Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-region network latency is the delay in data transmission between geographically separated regions, significantly affecting solution design.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-region network latency is the delay in data transmission between geographically separated regions, significantly affecting solution design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999554</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region architecture involves deploying solutions across multiple Azure regions for resilience, with trade-offs in cost, performance, and operational complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-region architecture involves deploying solutions across multiple Azure regions for resilience, with trade-offs in cost, performance, and operational complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Region Pairs">
  <data key="d0">Azure Region Pairs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure region pairs are paired Azure regions where some services automatically replicate data between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure region pairs are paired Azure regions where some services automatically replicate data between them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Object Replication">
  <data key="d0">Object Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used to replicate data across regions when geo-redundant storage is not available.&lt;SEP&gt;Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used as an alternative when GRS is not available.&lt;SEP&gt;Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used to replicate data across regions when geo-redundant storage is not available.&lt;SEP&gt;Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used as an alternative when GRS is not available.&lt;SEP&gt;Object replication is used to optimize data access for clients in regions far from the data source.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48</data>
