  <data key="d5">1776999524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal (Pinned) Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zonal (Pinned) Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach where resources are pinned to a specific availability zone, with passive deployments across other zones for in-region DR.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach where resources are pinned to a specific availability zone, with passive deployments across other zones for in-region DR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Deployment With Backups Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Deployment With Backups Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A low-cost deployment approach with significant risks, using local redundancy and cross-region backups.&lt;SEP&gt;A low-cost deployment approach with significant risks, using local redundancy and cross-region backups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployment With Backup Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployment With Backup Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach providing multiple layers of resiliency with high performance through zone redundancy and cross-region backups.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach providing multiple layers of resiliency with high performance through zone redundancy and cross-region backups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Hub">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reliability Hub is an Azure resource providing guidance on specific deployment options and approaches for each Azure service.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reliability Hub is an Azure resource providing guidance on specific deployment options and approaches for each Azure service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Level Objective">
  <data key="d0">Service-Level Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A service-level objective (SLO) represents the expected uptime target for a solution, such as 99.9% uptime.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of performance and reliability of a workload, representing a specific measurable target for customer interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;An internal target for service performance and reliability that helps teams meet or exceed SLA commitments.&lt;SEP&gt;A service-level objective (SLO) represents the expected uptime target for a solution, such as 99.9% uptime.&lt;SEP&gt;Service-level objectives (SLOs) are targets offered to the workload's users regarding performance and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;A service-level objective (SLO) is a target for system performance that index update strategies must not breach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a1ff429a57f5b474e0f29cc10e052a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee8f06f69405c135c99cf295eda608c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/grounding-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geodes Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Geodes Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Geodes pattern is an approach for deploying workloads across multiple regions to bring applications closer to users.&lt;SEP&gt;The Geodes pattern is an approach for deploying workloads across multiple regions to bring applications closer to users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Risk Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk tolerance refers to the varying degrees of acceptable risk within organizations, differing by workload and influencing resiliency strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk tolerance refers to the varying degrees of acceptable risk within organizations, differing by workload and influencing resiliency strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-Region Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Single-Region Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Single-region deployment is an approach that simplifies operational requirements and reduces costs but may not meet high reliability requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-region deployment is an approach that simplifies operational requirements and reduces costs but may not meet high reliability requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999558</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal Pinned Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zonal Pinned Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach where resources are pinned to a specific availability zone, offering high performance but high operational requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach where resources are pinned to a specific availability zone, offering high performance but high operational requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Principle Of Simplicity">
  <data key="d0">Principle Of Simplicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A reliability principle advising to keep solutions simple to improve security and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A reliability principle advising to keep solutions simple to improve security and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Region DR">
  <data key="d0">In-Region DR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In-region DR (also called metro DR) refers to active-passive deployment across multiple availability zones within the same region for disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;In-region DR (also called metro DR) refers to active-passive deployment across multiple availability zones within the same region for disaster recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Offloading">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Offloading</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway Offloading is a design pattern that offloads request processing to a gateway device before and after forwarding requests to backend nodes. This approach centralizes functionality—such as security features like web application firewalls and TLS connections—reducing the complexity of application code and shifting per-node processing costs to a centralized processing model. By consolidating these responsibilities at the gateway level, organizations can use fewer resources per node and benefit from centralized configuration management of offloaded functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geode">
  <data key="d0">Geode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geode deploys systems in active-active availability modes across multiple geographies using data replication to withstand regional outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Geode deploys systems in active-active availability modes across multiple geographies using data replication, reducing latency by serving from the closest region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Index Table">
  <data key="d0">Index Table</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Index Table optimizes data retrieval in distributed data stores by enabling metadata lookup to avoid full data store scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Index Table optimizes data retrieval in distributed data stores by enabling metadata lookups to avoid full data store scans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leader Election">
  <data key="d0">Leader Election</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Leader Election establishes a leader among distributed application instances to coordinate responsibilities and implement failover via consensus algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pipes And Filters">
  <data key="d0">Pipes And Filters</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pipes and Filters breaks down complex data processing into independent stages with single responsibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Pipes and Filters is a design pattern that distributes processing tasks across multiple resources and promotes scalability and flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4f212602314ae8aa68b2a4631872d3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Priority Queue">
  <data key="d0">Priority Queue</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Priority Queue ensures higher-priority items are processed before lower-priority items to focus reliability on critical work.&lt;SEP&gt;Priority Queue ensures higher-priority items are processed before lower-priority items, focusing performance on time-sensitive work.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Publisher/Subscriber">
  <data key="d0">Publisher/Subscriber</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Publisher/Subscriber decouples architecture components by replacing direct communication with an intermediate message broker or event bus.&lt;SEP&gt;A pattern decoupling components via an intermediate message broker, introducing security segmentation between publishers and subscribers.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher/Subscriber decouples architecture components by replacing direct communication with an intermediate message broker or event bus.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that decouples architecture components by replacing direct communication with an intermediate message broker or event bus.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern used to decouple components in system architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher/Subscriber pattern decouples architecture components using an intermediate message broker, enabling event-driven approaches with consumption-based billing.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher/subscriber pattern decouples components using an intermediate message broker, enabling event-driven and consumption-based billing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ec8d1aedbc1588b6b1ad6ff2df36aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rate Limiting">
  <data key="d0">Rate Limiting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rate Limiting controls client request rates to reduce throttling errors and avoid unbounded retry-on-error scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate limiting is the act of limiting how many requests can access a resource.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate limiting caps the number of requests lower-priority flows and users can make to constrained resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate limiting is a strategy to reduce demand by controlling the rate of incoming requests to prevent undesired scaling costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate-limiting rules for Azure WAF prevent clients from sending too much traffic to applications, avoiding problems like retry storms.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate limiting restricts the number of requests clients can send to prevent excessive traffic and issues like retry storms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-617354e6d70206a2787d2a92e6998746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001690</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saga Distributed Transactions">
  <data key="d0">Saga Distributed Transactions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Saga decomposes long-running transactions into smaller independent transactions with compensating actions to maintain consistency and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheduler Agent Supervisor">
  <data key="d0">Scheduler Agent Supervisor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scheduler Agent Supervisor distributes and redistributes tasks using health metrics to detect failures and reroute tasks to healthy agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Scheduler Agent Supervisor distributes tasks across a system using performance and capacity metrics to detect utilization and route tasks efficiently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sequential Convoy">
  <data key="d0">Sequential Convoy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequential Convoy maintains concurrent messaging ingress while supporting processing in a defined order to eliminate race conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strangler Fig">
  <data key="d0">Strangler Fig</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Strangler Fig systematically replaces components of a running system with new components incrementally to mitigate migration risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Strangler Fig is an architecture design pattern that provides an approach for systematically replacing components of a running system with new components during migration or modernization.&lt;SEP&gt;Strangler Fig pattern systematically replaces components of a running system during migration, maximizing existing investments while modernizing incrementally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-686a674e18aea8177f756b4cd627bcd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b268cbd7205ca95583d2d4692a80828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Architecture Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Architecture Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industry patterns used in workload architecture design to address common challenges, optimize outcomes, and mitigate risks affecting reliability, security, performance, cost, and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Industry patterns used in workload architecture design to address common challenges, mitigate risks, and support security goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996189</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Pillar">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Pillar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture pillar that prioritizes workload availability, self-preservation, recovery, data and processing integrity, and containment of malfunctions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reliability pillar is a framework component related to testing strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reliability pillar is one of the pillars that must be balanced against cost optimization trade-offs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reliability pillar is a component of the Azure Well-Architected Framework covering disaster recovery strategies and availability requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cf91e067df302cf4a6958a130fa0fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4c20a753377d79a1b6e9a6ac4090a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b9f43effe85bb4f106ab0a823c7d4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambassador Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Ambassador Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern that encapsulates and manages network communications by offloading cross-cutting tasks, providing opportunities to add reliability patterns like retry or buffering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backends For Frontends Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Backends For Frontends Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern that creates separate backend services exclusive to specific frontend interfaces, isolating malfunctions so one client's issues don't affect another's availability.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that minimizes the number of requests and reduces costs by creating separate backends for different frontends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85416f9f4269be56820f2abc15bfb29</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bulkhead Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Bulkhead Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bulkhead Pattern is a design pattern that introduces intentional segmentation between components of a system to isolate failures and contain their blast radius. By partitioning a system into isolated groups or pools, it prevents failures in one component from cascading to other parts, ensuring that only affected sections experience problems while the remaining components continue to function normally.

The pattern can be applied in various ways, including partitioning service instances into pools based on consumer load and availability requirements, or restricting customers to specific regions by treating multiregion deployments as separate stamps. It also serves to isolate services from each other, ensuring independent lifecycles. Overall, the Bulkhead Pattern is a fundamental approach to achieving fault isolation and resilience in system architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bulkhead pattern is a design pattern that isolates failures and prevents cascading failures in systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0075254306371deed306288e9b95eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef12664b5845bb63109916b6e16079b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03df2eaa58b6c9bb42baf709c977fdda</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/metrics.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cache-Aside Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Cache-Aside Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern that introduces an on-demand cache for frequently read data, providing data replication and fallback capability when the origin data store is unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that improves performance by caching frequently accessed data to reduce expensive computations or external calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Circuit Breaker Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Circuit Breaker Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Circuit Breaker Pattern is a resilience-oriented design pattern that prevents an application from repeatedly attempting operations likely to fail. It works by monitoring failures against a threshold within a specified time window; once that threshold is exceeded, the circuit "opens," immediately returning errors instead of making further requests to malfunctioning dependencies. This prevents unnecessary resource consumption and avoids cascading failures caused by continual retries to external dependencies.

The pattern enables graceful degradation and is often coupled with automatic recovery mechanisms, allowing the system to self-heal when the underlying dependency becomes available again. By handling failures in a controlled manner, the Circuit Breaker Pattern increases overall system availability, optimizes resource utilization, and enhances architectural resilience. It is closely related to retry and fault-handling strategies, serving as a complementary safety measure for building robust, fault-tolerant systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Circuit breaker pattern is applied to consumer applications to prevent cascading failures.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that stops sending requests to failing consumers after consecutive failures to prevent cascading failures.&lt;SEP&gt;The circuit breaker pattern is used to protect traffic during recovery scenarios and implement client-side throttling protection in Azure Event Hubs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Circuit Breaker pattern avoids continued retries when quotas are exceeded or services are unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;Circuit breaker pattern is a design pattern that prevents applications from performing operations likely to fail, reducing unnecessary processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0150f1d7a68414d68f2d36fee4a0389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbfe826fe19c233eb2d1b279f7950e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8602faa58c6ec0ac39453f0668455f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d10ef40f70919a984cf031275099f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claim Check Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Claim Check Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern that separates data from messaging flow, providing increased reliability for underlying data and enabling message queue recovery after disasters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compensating Transaction Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Compensating Transaction Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern providing recovery from failures by reversing effects of previously applied actions through compensation actions like rolling back data changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Compensating Transaction pattern manages recovery for task steps that fail by undoing work in eventually consistent operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Compensating Transaction pattern is a design pattern for undoing work performed by a series of steps when one or more steps fail.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7faed93ac7c8b81fc0be047d2c1f773f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbfe826fe19c233eb2d1b279f7950e7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Competing Consumers Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Competing Consumers Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern applying distributed concurrent processing for queue items, building redundancy by treating consumers as replicas so instance failures don't block processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing Consumers pattern describes how to handle scenarios where multiple service instances process messages from a queue.&lt;SEP&gt;The Competing Consumers pattern is a solution for distributing background tasks that require substantial time or resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing Consumers pattern is an architecture pattern relevant to partitioning background jobs.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing Consumers pattern is an architecture pattern for handling multiple consumers processing messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c387aff770332292e0a1e78af18b8fbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b047e8b449398992f0dfab15265a69c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0f7011b209ee2d53115a29ddfa186f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7faed93ac7c8b81fc0be047d2c1f773f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Workload Configuration Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Edge Workload Configuration Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern managing configuration for distributed edge workloads using cloud as source of truth while maintaining local availability during connectivity disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Sourcing Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Event Sourcing Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern treating state changes as events in an immutable append-only log, facilitating reliable change history and state reconstruction for recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federated Identity Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Federated Identity Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern delegating trust to an external identity provider, shifting reliability for user management and authentication to a high-SLA provider.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Aggregation Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Aggregation Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern simplifying client interactions by aggregating calls to multiple backend services, centralizing transient fault handling.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that reduces the number of requests by aggregating multiple individual requests into a single request.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85416f9f4269be56820f2abc15bfb29</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Offloading Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Offloading Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern offloading request processing to a gateway device, reducing backend complexity and replacing functionality with reliable platform-provided features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Routing Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Routing Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern routing incoming network requests to various backend systems based on request intents, business logic, and backend availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e687b13375238447a37923a69d1d0adb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Adoption Framework">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Adoption Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cloud Adoption Framework is a comprehensive framework that provides guidance across multiple aspects of cloud adoption and management. It offers strategies for preparing environments for cloud adoption, including hybrid and multicloud scenarios, and provides perspectives for a holistic approach to cloud readiness, including operating model comparisons.

The framework addresses organizational governance by helping central teams set up spending guardrails across an organization and improving portfolios of workloads through centralized controls. It provides guidance for workloads requiring business criticality classification and offers best practices for resource naming.

Additionally, the Cloud Adoption Framework covers enterprise-scale landing zones and connectivity best practices in Azure, and provides guidance on creating AI strategy for AI integration planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cloud Adoption Framework provides best practices and recommendations for network topology and connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure guides deployment including custom RBAC role definitions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cloud Adoption Framework provides perspectives incorporated into Azure VMware Solution guidance for a holistic approach to cloud readiness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cloud Adoption Framework provides cost policies and guidance for governing cloud resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-839c6849bb3baf2d3e29441a3b61a033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4285f3b1d912059b039db58435cd461a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-387611e470f83bbe5d875c098db01fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc00fa2fd7ff6664f6bb092b239d2134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7a8cd71f19bd38f8998b0a51811a72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad653e4d2f68d336a1fa1654643a4bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0aeda7bb18ec43b01e80e8a4401d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9c715c42ddea999c4f406ee448b176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9afa79a4fdffd13927a0fd86422a26</data>
