<node id="User Flow">
  <data key="d0">User Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User flows are the paths or sequences of actions that users take within an application or system, focusing on user interface, interactions, and decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Paths or sequences of actions that users take within an application or system.&lt;SEP&gt;User flow is the sequence that a user follows to accomplish a task.&lt;SEP&gt;User flow is the path or sequence of actions that users take within an application or system.&lt;SEP&gt;A flow that determines how users interact with the workload, defining the sequence of actions users take to accomplish specific tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae4f38f75c43fbb89e4aa72f0afd7c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4e354767f44f79da40710542ed5310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9c98557d8b38582c1462aa9d0fd3e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Flow">
  <data key="d0">System Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System flows are the flow of information and processes within a system, focusing on data movement, processing, and interactions among workload components.&lt;SEP&gt;System flow is the flow of information and processes within a system that automatically enables user flows or workload functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;System flow is the flow of information and processes within a system that automatically enables user flows or workload functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;A flow that determines communication and data exchange between workload components, operating independently of direct user interaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae4f38f75c43fbb89e4aa72f0afd7c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9c98557d8b38582c1462aa9d0fd3e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Flow Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A flow catalog is a compiled list of all identified user and system flows in a workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae4f38f75c43fbb89e4aa72f0afd7c9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Process">
  <data key="d0">Business Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business processes are a series of tasks to achieve an output, such as order fulfillment or customer service management.&lt;SEP&gt;A series of sequential actions or stages that fulfill a business requirement, such as selling products online or processing customer support requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae4f38f75c43fbb89e4aa72f0afd7c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Criticality Scale">
  <data key="d0">Criticality Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A criticality scale is used to prioritize flows based on business requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eae4f38f75c43fbb89e4aa72f0afd7c9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process Owner">
  <data key="d0">Process Owner</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The individual responsible for the successful execution of a given process and the flows that support it.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for the business process that a flow supports, with authority over business requirements and priorities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Escalation Path">
  <data key="d0">Escalation Path</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Channels for escalating issues related to a flow, ensuring timely and effective resolution of urgent updates, security concerns, degradations, or technical incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;A defined sequence of individuals or teams to contact to resolve flow problems, where each level has broader scope and authority.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Impact">
  <data key="d0">Business Impact</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">How each flow contributes to key business objectives such as revenue generation, customer satisfaction, or operational efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The effect that a flow's availability or unavailability has on revenue, reputation, operations, or compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Criticality Rating">
  <data key="d0">Criticality Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A rating assigned to each flow based on its importance relative to overall business impacts, categorized as high, medium, or low criticality.&lt;SEP&gt;Criticality rating is a classification method using High, Medium, and Low levels to prioritize flows based on business impact and performance demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Responsibility Assignment Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Responsibility Assignment Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A matrix (RAM or RACI) that identifies process owners and stakeholders for processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flow">
  <data key="d0">Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A flow is a component of a workload that supports business processes and can be evaluated for criticality, business impact, and escalation paths.&lt;SEP&gt;A sequence of operations in a workload that performs a specific function, involving data movement and process execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A flow is the sequence of actions that performs a specific function in a workload, involving data movement and process execution between components.&lt;SEP&gt;A flow is the sequence of actions that performs a specific function in a workload, involving data movement and process execution between components.&lt;SEP&gt;A sequence of actions that supports workload functionality, used to optimize workload design by segmenting and prioritizing different parts of a workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4e354767f44f79da40710542ed5310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0ca00b92b2b19805cdb05c0d7a7e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9c98557d8b38582c1462aa9d0fd3e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-targets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/prioritize-critical-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stakeholder">
  <data key="d0">Stakeholder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stakeholders are individuals involved in a workload, having dependencies on a flow, or managing dependencies that a flow has.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Criticality">
  <data key="d0">High Criticality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High criticality flows are integral to core business functions, directly affecting customer experience, financial transactions, security, health, and safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medium Criticality">
  <data key="d0">Medium Criticality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medium criticality flows are important for system functionality but do not directly interface with customers or critical business operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Criticality">
  <data key="d0">Low Criticality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low criticality flows do not have a direct or significant effect on core business functions or customer experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3ed77bd2b12302d74feb0a92d79de9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/identify-flows.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customization Lock-In">
  <data key="d0">Customization Lock-In</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A situation where custom extensions to a bought solution make updates and modernization impractical.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7595d0066e438d094afa55de7d2ba18c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lift-And-Shift">
  <data key="d0">Lift-And-Shift</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A migration approach that moves workloads without redesign, potentially missing modernization benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7595d0066e438d094afa55de7d2ba18c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graceful Degradation Testing">
  <data key="d0">Graceful Degradation Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing method that evaluates how a system runs with reduced functionality during failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third-Party Failure Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Third-Party Failure Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method that disables or throttles calls to external APIs to test fallbacks and retries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disaster Recovery Drills">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery Drills</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DR drills assess the resilience of process controls by validating procedures, coordination, and human actions during recovery from major failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hot-Cold Partitioning">
  <data key="d0">Hot-Cold Partitioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hot-cold partitioning applies different levels of data management to each storage tier, separating archival data from active workload data.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that divides data based on access patterns, separating frequently accessed data from infrequently accessed data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2829ddae563971c0c88cbe1829d1e1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Game Days">
  <data key="d0">Game Days</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preparatory exercises run in nonproduction environments using synthetic transactions to identify process gaps and architectural flaws.&lt;SEP&gt;Game days are planned events where faults are introduced to test a team's ability to detect and resolve problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe53a5474c5e4934795683b73b06789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61803d2562ce9d74f9843d45925671b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Center Of Excellence">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Center Of Excellence</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An organizational team with specialized expertise in multiregion design, failover strategies, and cloud services.&lt;SEP&gt;A centralized board (CCoE) that provides governance and guidance for cloud workloads within an organization.&lt;SEP&gt;The CCoE team provides standards and guidelines for compliance, security, application architecture, and operational processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c45aa9611048afab38755ade22af2f4f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Horizontal scaling, also known as scaling out, is a scaling approach that adds more instances of a given resource type to distribute workload across multiple servers or compute nodes. It requires a load balancer to distribute traffic across these instances, and smaller instances can be added or removed based on demand, offering cost savings.

Partitioning strategies simplify horizontal scaling. For example, sharding can divide users into equal-sized buckets, and partitioned entities can distribute messages across multiple message brokers, improving throughput with trade-offs in ordering and consistency.

Horizontal scaling is generally considered simpler, more reliable, and more cost-effective than vertical scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Horizontal scaling is the ability to dynamically span workloads across multiple VMs for high availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13f58bb87b8f13eaa0fc8be64f114a5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2829ddae563971c0c88cbe1829d1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c387aff770332292e0a1e78af18b8fbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c944e9a44adf39c12919b36fa366a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fb475b8b7efe4018b64a1ed512f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/scaling.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Service Health">
  <data key="d0">Azure Service Health</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Service Health is used to check platform-level health status of Azure services.&lt;SEP&gt;A platform-level health monitoring service provided by Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Service Health provides notifications about maintenance events and service incidents for Azure services.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Service Health is used to monitor Azure Firewall health and detect service state degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Service Health provides a view of the health of Azure services and regions, including notifications about outages and planned maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b359b45da7d6b789373380187e0a7ede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11229197c05f5be9b778a1918888ee7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/monitoring-alerting-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/monitoring.md</data>
