<node id="Azure Resource Health">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Health</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Resource Health is used to check resource-level health status.&lt;SEP&gt;A resource-level health monitoring service provided by Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Health provides health status monitoring for Azure resources including Azure Firewall.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Health distinguishes Azure service problems from customer-side connectivity problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Health helps diagnose and get support for service problems affecting Azure resources, reporting current and past health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b99a62e53e59edcc42c5c691f68045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11229197c05f5be9b778a1918888ee7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b</data>
