  <data key="d5">1777004898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Monitor Action Groups">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor Action Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor action groups are configured for both infrastructure and application alerting.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor action groups are Azure-native options used to set up triggers that automatically initiate various tasks for self-healing automation.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor action groups are Azure-native options used to set up triggers that automatically initiate various tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor action groups are used for notifications (email, voice, SMS) and to trigger automated actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor action groups automatically run self-healing operations when alerts trigger, using runbooks, Azure functions, or webhooks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor action groups route critical reliability alerts to appropriate notification channels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-707a8f0435e28285c9cf77ad7c3898c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fcebbf5c193f6fa1d943e2af2fe05b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
