<node id="Retry Logic">
  <data key="d0">Retry Logic</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retry logic is a design pattern used in client-side logic to handle transient network failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Retry logic improves application resilience to temporary infrastructure failures by retrying failed calls with backoff delays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6086bb426312de9978645863ba67d2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4</data>
