</node>
<node id="Level 4">
  <data key="d0">Level 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 4 is a maturity level requiring improvements in operational and technical controls for system reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 4 is a maturity level where performance monitoring and testing in production should be well-developed.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 4 maturity focuses on advanced monitoring, fine-tuning alerting, automating maintenance, and operational efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 4 is a maturity level where architecture likely meets business requirements effectively and safe deployment practices are established.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adeaccdaf088dd43cb5b66e1bb18c9ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e912a1ac7fa5ab0139e0fac99a203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61803d2562ce9d74f9843d45925671b</data>
