<node id="Disaster Recovery Plan">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Disaster Recovery Plan (DR plan) is a comprehensive, process-based living document designed to respond to catastrophic failures and other major incidents. It provides detailed, executable procedures for recovering specific systems after major failures, including step-by-step recovery actions, roles, responsibilities, failover sequences, and communication workflows.

The plan covers recovery architecture components, failover mechanisms, user and data flow impact, and operational recommendations to meet Recovery Time Objective (RTO) and Recovery Point Objective (RPO) goals. It is activated when incidents meet disaster-level thresholds based on severity evaluation, and addresses technical artifacts alongside communication and recovery steps.

A Disaster Recovery Plan evolves from basic graceful degradation strategies at more mature organizational levels. It also serves as a guide for building recovery strategies for multi-region deployments—such as those on Azure—based on business priorities and reliability objectives, covering approaches including backup and restore, active-passive, and active-active strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;A well-documented disaster recovery plan defines recovery steps, RPO, and RTO targets for business continuity.&lt;SEP&gt;A comprehensive disaster recovery plan involves creating a plan and deciding on recovery technology, including handling dependencies and stateful components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45aecf85df05c73b4035e26a2cb04459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec310894211cb31c51a678d1c91d5a8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e0681994766d1adfc077b31464e02a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/architect-role/architecture-design-specification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level 1">
  <data key="d0">Level 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The first maturity level focused on establishing a solid groundwork for resiliency through bootstrapping basic reliability capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 1 introduces methods for addressing transient failures and basic reliability practices including monitoring, testing, and risk mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 1 is a baseline monitoring setup focusing on infrastructure, basic analysis, and basic alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 1 of the Security pillar focuses on baseline security configuration and securing the development phase of the SDLC.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 1 represents the initial stage of DevOps adoption focused on building foundational vocabulary, processes, and tools for stable operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f84fdf8398257ab3343f339b69880c7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level 2">
  <data key="d0">Level 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 2 focuses on self-preservation strategies to prevent, detect, and recover from longer-lasting failures, with advanced monitoring and recovery plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 extends monitoring with advanced observability, structured analysis, and operations around the monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 of the Security pillar focuses on threat prevention, strengthening deployment security, and hardening workload infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 represents process standardization, focusing on structured approaches to streamline decision-making and define deployment and monitoring requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 is a process standardization stage that focuses on streamlining decision-making responsibilities and defining requirements for system deployment and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e556a5a0ce1ce8e99bdd9ba80921a8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c271e52ca02be4b8bdb801ea111d9be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85dfff44e8e4c1e2d34f3f2fbc239ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f84fdf8398257ab3343f339b69880c7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Maturity Model">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Maturity Model</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A five-level structured model that helps teams assess their current reliability state and offers a path for progressive improvement in system resilience and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar-specific maturity model focused on reliability within the Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7ba45bf48a024a996731f69cab5301</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disaster Recovery Plans">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comprehensive plans prepared to ensure systematic preparation for various failure scenarios and maintain system reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48e6023a56c54a7dd2d0d74d805223e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure App Service WebJobs">
  <data key="d0">Azure App Service WebJobs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure App Service WebJobs is an Azure feature for background jobs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995763</data>
