</node>
<node id="Checkpointing">
  <data key="d0">Checkpointing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Checkpointing is a technique for saving the state of a process at specific points, useful for long-running tasks that might be disrupted.&lt;SEP&gt;A fault tolerance strategy for HPC workloads that enables jobs to resume reliably after failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d92f2138a13f47ba741d8618d3160dc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idempotency">
  <data key="d0">Idempotency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idempotency ensures that if a background task fails, another instance can pick it up and continue processing without problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A property ensuring that repeating an operation produces the same result, preventing data inconsistencies during retries.&lt;SEP&gt;Idempotency is a design principle ensuring functions can be safely retried without causing unintended side effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af17a604206f8056ed34d52736aca636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a75f6abfb52e7f12669ccabfaf886c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-functions.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SRE">
  <data key="d0">SRE</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Site Reliability Engineers (SREs) use health model dashboards to quickly pinpoint problems by focusing on unhealthy or degraded flows.&lt;SEP&gt;SREs (Site Reliability Engineers) use automated playbooks built from triggers and automated responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776995763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Background Tasks">
  <data key="d0">Background Tasks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Background tasks are workload components that don't directly support user flows but play critical roles such as email confirmation, data cleanup, and backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Background tasks offload CPU-intensive and I/O-intensive operations from the main application to handle increasing workload when scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Background tasks are asynchronous jobs that can be complex, require orchestration, and need resilience features like checkpoints and graceful restarts.&lt;SEP&gt;Background tasks process messages from queues, should be idempotent, scalable, and can create challenges for data synchronization and user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504668d189fb583478dc96b97aa36487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b047e8b449398992f0dfab15265a69c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c1dd7c66529e2ab2455ebd5bb312625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7faed93ac7c8b81fc0be047d2c1f773f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domain Name System">
  <data key="d0">Domain Name System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DNS is a system for resolving domain names; pointing DNS records directly to applications can cause delays during recovery due to propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;DNS implementations are driven by specific hub-spoke infrastructure configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;DNS is the protocol used by Azure Traffic Manager to establish communication paths between clients and workload endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002855</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actionable Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Actionable Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerts that are set to be actionable, helping teams respond to reliability issues effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Actionable alerts are clearly defined alerts with sufficient information for quick troubleshooting, configured with appropriate severity and thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4dc888d546b77a45fccbd5a3b4695b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a61083a07976793cf6cee9da2a51bdf</data>
