<node id="Throughput">
  <data key="d0">Throughput</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Throughput measures minimum data transfer rate during a certain time period, such as transactions per second.&lt;SEP&gt;Throughput measures the amount of data read from or written to a storage system over a period of time.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability to handle a specific number of transactions within a given time period, a capacity metric.&lt;SEP&gt;The amount of data that can be transmitted over a network in a given time.</data>
