<node id="Transient Faults">
  <data key="d0">Transient Faults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transient faults are temporary failures like network timeouts common in cloud workloads, typically handled with retry mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Transient faults are temporary failures that are expected to resolve on their own and are typically handled through retry mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Transient faults are temporary failures in cloud applications addressed through retry strategies and best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df6e00fa9a90ca53e8d360c865875b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8602faa58c6ec0ac39453f0668455f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/self-preservation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/handle-transient-faults.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Background Jobs">
  <data key="d0">Background Jobs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Background jobs are tasks decoupled from the user interface to enhance system reliability, including CPU-intensive, I/O-intensive, batch, and long-running workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Background jobs are tasks that run independently of the UI, including batch jobs, processor-intensive tasks, and long-running processes such as workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Background tasks that run independently of the UI, including batch jobs, processor-intensive tasks, and long-running processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Background jobs are tasks like batch processing and workflows that minimize UI load, improve availability, and reduce response time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df6e00fa9a90ca53e8d360c865875b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e31fdc4d1c3251e67cb0588dd3047a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e</data>
