<node id="Bounded Context">
  <data key="d0">Bounded Context</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A bounded context is a domain-driven design concept that defines an explicit boundary around a domain model and maps to a subdomain of the business domain.&lt;SEP&gt;A distinct business area or domain that defines clear boundaries for data and functionality, often the basis for functional partitioning decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A bounded context is a distinct business area in an application that can be identified for functional partitioning.</data>
