<node id="Scaling Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Scaling Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scaling strategy defines how a workload responds to changes in load patterns and spikes in usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Scaling strategy involves advanced techniques like scheduled scaling and automation to optimize resource usage.&lt;SEP&gt;A well-defined scaling strategy ensures applications can handle various loads without compromising performance, involving autoscaling and overprovisioning resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8947b14829678f0e3a98c01dd0b8ff35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fault-Injection Testing">
  <data key="d0">Fault-Injection Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fault-injection testing follows chaos engineering principles to test a workload's ability to react to component failures across infrastructure and application layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault-injection testing in production can be disruptive and potentially cause downtime, requiring safeguards and rollback plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e6f5079bad84a35961c4d29f3694386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Test Plans">
  <data key="d0">Azure Test Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Test Plans is a browser-based test management solution providing capabilities for manual testing, user acceptance testing, exploratory testing, and stakeholder feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Test Plans is a browser-based test management solution providing capabilities for planned manual testing, user acceptance testing, exploratory testing, and gathering feedback from stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Test Plans is a browser-based test management solution for manual testing, UAT, exploratory testing, and stakeholder feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Test Plans is a browser-based test management solution for manual testing, user acceptance testing, and exploratory testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e6f5079bad84a35961c4d29f3694386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c203348328e5589b8f4b6fa4101a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2831164a5771887ad5de08caa27249ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7987518df69e1ecaaed650861e7e6e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tools-processes.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ignite 2023">
  <data key="d0">Ignite 2023</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Ignite 2023 is the event where Azure Chaos Studio reached general availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e6f5079bad84a35961c4d29f3694386</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Error Budget">
  <data key="d0">Error Budget</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An error budget is the difference between 100% SLO achievement and the agreed-upon SLO, used as an investment in chaos and fault injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Directly Responsible Individual">
  <data key="d0">Directly Responsible Individual</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A directly responsible individual (DRI) is a person assigned to take ownership of an incident.&lt;SEP&gt;The DRI makes final decisions with input from key stakeholders and technical decision-makers during emergency deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;A person or working group accountable for driving AI initiatives and ensuring cohesion across teams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fb455e5de9f1067bb91e069db8c9a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e4a31ea43efb7a100f1df033cb0e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7a8cd71f19bd38f8998b0a51811a72</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/reliability/testing-strategy.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/ai-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hardware Security Module">
  <data key="d0">Hardware Security Module</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hardware Security Module (HSM) is a hardware-based security system that provides a higher level of security for secret management, offered at a higher cost.&lt;SEP&gt;HSM provides higher security for secret storage compared to software-based stores, at higher cost.&lt;SEP&gt;A hardware security module (HSM) is a store offering higher restrictions for protecting highly sensitive secrets, supporting FIPS 140-2 Level 3 protection.&lt;SEP&gt;A managed HSM used to store highly sensitive data and encryption keys with identity-based access and least-privilege access control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Managed HSM">
  <data key="d0">Azure Managed HSM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Managed HSM is an Azure service for key management and secret storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secret Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Secret Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secret rotation is the process of retiring and replacing secrets frequently to reduce attack vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of regularly updating secrets to limit exposure time if compromised.&lt;SEP&gt;Secret rotation is the practice of frequently rotating keys, secrets, and certificates to make it more challenging for attackers to access encrypted data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15da9f5a57c9361e9e5487fa0eea82</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Least-Privilege Approach">
  <data key="d0">Least-Privilege Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The least-privilege approach restricts permissions to the minimum necessary for authorized identities and services.&lt;SEP&gt;A security principle of removing unnecessary role assignments and performing regular access reviews for management processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654e7aada501f6fea6718cd59dbed297</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/harden-resources.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Access Tokens">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Access Tokens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth access tokens require careful handling with consideration of their time to live and exposure window.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996114</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secret Injection Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Secret Injection Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Secret injection patterns insert secrets into application code or configuration at runtime to prevent accidental exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refresh Tokens">
  <data key="d0">Refresh Tokens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refresh tokens must be stored securely with limited exposure to the application and can be secured using OAuth 2.0 On-Behalf-Of patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Git Precommit Hooks">
  <data key="d0">Git Precommit Hooks</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Git precommit hooks scan for credentials before source code commits deploy to prevent exposed secrets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secret Management System">
  <data key="d0">Secret Management System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dedicated secret management system stores, distributes, and controls access to application secrets for authorized identities and services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-940b923de959bc1ad2624536ebc72dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996115</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Identity">
  <data key="d0">Managed Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An identity assigned to resources and managed by Azure, used to handle credentials without embedding access information in connection strings.&lt;SEP&gt;Managed identities allow Azure to manage all credentials for applications and can be extended to Azure resources for authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure feature that provides applications with an automatically managed identity in Microsoft Entra ID, eliminating the need to store credentials in code.&lt;SEP&gt;An authentication method between Machine Learning and other services that eliminates the need to store credentials manually.&lt;SEP&gt;Managed identities allow Service Fabric applications to authenticate to Azure resources without saving credentials locally or in source control.&lt;SEP&gt;Managed identity is an identity assigned to VMs or scale sets that enables secure authentication when communicating with other Azure resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d45ee5353204fd65637dc950ee85715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c50c3fc68e8ca3e2a2600f5ec515c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24da17048f52e4eee422a69ff4b58769</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Credential Scanning">
  <data key="d0">Credential Scanning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of validating source code to ensure secrets aren't included.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X.509">
  <data key="d0">X.509</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard defining the format of public key certificates.&lt;SEP&gt;X.509 is a standard that defines the format of public key certificates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preshared Keys">
  <data key="d0">Preshared Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distinct keys created for each consumer to control access, enabling independent revocation and rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;Preshared keys are a type of secret shared between a provider and consumer used through a secure and agreed upon mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Secrets">
  <data key="d0">Application Secrets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential components of a system that facilitate communication between workload components, including credentials, API keys, OAuth tokens, SSH keys, certificates, and digital signature keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Application secrets such as preshared keys are vulnerable points in systems that should be dynamically managed, rotatable, and avoided when possible in favor of identity-based authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Application secrets are confidential components such as passwords, API keys, and certificates that facilitate communication between workload components.&lt;SEP&gt;Application secrets are confidential components that facilitate communication between workload components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Tokens">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Tokens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Open Authorization tokens used as credentials, which can be dynamically created at runtime but still need safeguarding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60be6d579871b518c685612e6a815820</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/application-secrets.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Role-Based Access Control">
  <data key="d0">Azure Role-Based Access Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure RBAC is a method to assign permissions to users, groups, and applications at a certain scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure RBAC is an access management method applied to networking flows using managed identities between network components.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure RBAC is an authorization method where security principals are authenticated via Microsoft Entra ID without passwords or keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure RBAC is used to control identities and manage access in Azure Virtual Desktop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-31026fe6d1c4bec43b15c40b1c162e07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020</data>
