<node id="Metadata">
  <data key="d0">Metadata</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metadata is an implementation for applying taxonomy to assets.&lt;SEP&gt;Metadata can be used to group data and generate meaningful cost reports, enabling identification of high-cost areas and implementation of accountability measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Metadata is used to organize, categorize, and track resources, helping avoid orphaned resources and unexpected costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bfa9de462a82f93657efb2d63f7e3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54ab6df34391dde2f99128ba16bd1f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97489185a44dcbeac38d0a5a48e1097</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/collect-review-cost-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-component-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIPAA">
  <data key="d0">HIPAA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIPAA is a compliance standard relevant to data classification scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act is a regulatory compliance framework supported by enhanced security settings.&lt;SEP&gt;HIPAA is a regulatory compliance standard supported by Azure Policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act is a regulatory requirement relevant to Azure Virtual Desktop security and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act is a regulatory requirement for security compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;HIPAA is a regulatory requirement for organizations processing health-related data in HPC environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bfa9de462a82f93657efb2d63f7e3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc59486642305ff68ee1edaa445b8bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778fbb08fc2452f88b89df8ede476434</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/governance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006203</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PCI">
  <data key="d0">PCI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PCI is a compliance standard relevant to data classification scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Payment Card Industry standards are regulatory requirements relevant to security and governance in Azure Virtual Desktop.&lt;SEP&gt;Payment Card Industry (PCI) is a compliance framework that can be assessed using Microsoft Defender for Cloud.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bfa9de462a82f93657efb2d63f7e3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db16efb77d945a638ed3a142b84cba38</data>
