<node id="Segmentation Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Segmentation Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation strategy is an architectural approach influenced by classification labels, including traffic isolation boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy to minimize network visibility by segmenting networks and starting with least-privilege network controls.&lt;SEP&gt;A segmentation strategy defines how logical units should be separated from other units with their own set of security requirements and measures.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy for grouping components based on functional areas, workloads, and ownership to identify segment owners.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bfa9de462a82f93657efb2d63f7e3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
