<node id="Microsoft Purview">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Purview</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Purview is a family of data governance, risk, and compliance solutions that helps organizations govern, protect, and manage their entire data estate. It unifies Azure Purview and Microsoft Purview solutions to provide comprehensive visibility into data assets across environments.

Microsoft Purview offers capabilities including autodiscovery, cataloging, classification, and lineage tracking. It supports automated Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies and provides tooling for content safety and data traceability. The platform serves as a centralized solution for data governance and compliance needs across an organization's entire data landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Purview provides features for data discovery, lineage tracking, and governance, integrated with Azure Machine Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Purview is a tool that helps label data and add time-based purging to delete data after a retention period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c1925896ad2776a0d0431adee7f3d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6fe01d5e4f3c9a2a28525facf5534c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ee2e21cbfcb93f01ab71fb4f3f1e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed98fc331eceb219bf3e4e782eb6e340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/responsible-ai.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Analytics">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Analytics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Analytics is a Microsoft analytics service designed for high-volume data storage, processing, and transformation. It supports data extraction, transformation, loading (ETL), and complex analytical queries, including serverless query capabilities for analyzing logs and blob inventory reports.

The service offers built-in classification features for sensitive data and supports Spark jobs for distributed data processing. It is recommended as a technology for aggregated data storage and can run complex analytical queries on data from sources such as Azure Cosmos DB's analytical store.

Azure Synapse Analytics also serves as a tool for visualizing inventory data and creating reports for stakeholders, making it a comprehensive platform for end-to-end data analytics workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Analytics combines big data and data warehousing, supporting data lakes, Apache Spark, and Azure Synapse SQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a2c3c1077bbf94e3d952e330c6f922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88acce1b2be2296ca1e97b9e9e3c8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003791</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Database For Postgresql">
  <data key="d0">Azure Database For Postgresql</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Database for PostgreSQL supports confidential computing to provide hardware-based encryption for data in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Computing">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Computing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential Computing is a security technology that protects data while in use by performing computation within hardware-based, attested Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs). Unlike traditional encryption that covers data at rest and in transit, Confidential Computing addresses the protection of data during active processing operations through hardware-based encryption and attestation mechanisms.

This technology is particularly crucial for highly confidential workloads in regulated industries, including healthcare, financial services, and government sectors. In the Azure ecosystem, Confidential Computing provides encryption of data-in-use for virtual machines, enabling organizations to process sensitive data with enhanced security guarantees.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c1925896ad2776a0d0431adee7f3d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24da17048f52e4eee422a69ff4b58769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dace10a501d3c2b544e137b224cd683</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PCI-DSS">
  <data key="d0">PCI-DSS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PCI-DSS is a compliance standard that mandates the use of FIPS 140-2 Level 3 protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FIPS 140-2 Level 3">
  <data key="d0">FIPS 140-2 Level 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FIPS 140-2 Level 3 is a cryptographic protection standard mandated by PCI-DSS, available only with hardware security modules.&lt;SEP&gt;FIPS 140-2 Level 3 is a cryptographic security standard that can be met through customer-managed keys with automatic rotation policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure SQL Server">
  <data key="d0">Azure SQL Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL Server has a built-in classification engine, supports dynamic masking, and can generate reports based on metadata.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6949410eeaa7d29fe48e0341815607d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/data-classification.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996164</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambassador">
  <data key="d0">Ambassador</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern that encapsulates network communications by offloading cross-cutting tasks, providing a mediation point to augment security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996189</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backends For Frontends">
  <data key="d0">Backends For Frontends</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern creating separate backend services exclusive to specific frontend interfaces, reducing API surface area and lateral movement.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern creating separate backend services exclusive to specific frontend interfaces, enabling client-specific performance optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claim Check">
  <data key="d0">Claim Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern separating sensitive data from messaging flow, keeping it in a secured data store with stricter authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern separating data from messaging flow to improve efficiency when handling large data payloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Claim Check pattern separates data from messaging flow, enabling cheaper messaging solutions by reducing message body size.&lt;SEP&gt;Claim check pattern separates data from messaging flow to reduce message size and support cost-effective messaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998884</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federated Identity">
  <data key="d0">Federated Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern delegating trust to an external identity provider for user management and authentication using modern protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Federated Identity is a design pattern that delegates trust to an external identity provider for managing users and providing authentication, freeing application resources for other priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern delegating authentication to an external identity provider, freeing application resources for other priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Federated identity, also known as single sign-on (SSO), allows users to sign in with credentials they already use elsewhere by establishing trust relationships between identity providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Federated identity involves establishing trust relationships between identity providers using protocols like OIDC or SAML.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc63217f8e41f1a8e15dac9427efa323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0166aac21580feb08a54d6067d8103</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004504</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gatekeeper">
  <data key="d0">Gatekeeper</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern offloading request processing for security and access control enforcement, centralizing firewalls, DDoS protection, and authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Gatekeeper is a design pattern that offloads request processing for security and access control enforcement before and after forwarding requests to backend nodes, often used for gateway-level throttling.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern offloading security and access control processing before forwarding requests to backend nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Aggregation">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Aggregation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern aggregating calls to multiple backend services in a single request, reducing public surface area and authentication points.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway Aggregation simplifies client interactions by aggregating calls to multiple backend services in a single request, reducing latency and enabling caching.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that simplifies client interactions by aggregating calls to multiple backend services in a single request.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway Aggregation is a design pattern that reduces the number of incoming requests to improve operational efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Gateway aggregation is a pattern for aggregating multiple requests or responses through a gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quarantine">
  <data key="d0">Quarantine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern ensuring external assets meet quality levels before consumption, serving as first security validation in a segmented environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Quarantine is an architecture design pattern that ensures external assets meet a team-agreed quality level before being authorized for consumption in the workload.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that ensures external assets meet quality levels before consumption, as part of software development lifecycle and safe deployment practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b268cbd7205ca95583d2d4692a80828</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sidecar">
  <data key="d0">Sidecar</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern extending application functionality via a companion process, reducing surface area of sensitive processes and adding cross-cutting security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidecar extends application functionality by encapsulating cross-cutting tasks in a companion process alongside the main application.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidecar is an architecture design pattern that extends application functionality by encapsulating nonprimary or cross-cutting tasks in a companion process alongside the main application.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that extends application functionality by attaching auxiliary processes alongside the main application.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b268cbd7205ca95583d2d4692a80828</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valet Key">
  <data key="d0">Valet Key</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Valet Key is an architecture design pattern that grants security-restricted access to a resource without using an intermediary resource to proxy the access, limiting access in both scope and duration.&lt;SEP&gt;A pattern granting security-restricted, time-limited access to resources without intermediary proxies or long-lasting credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Valet Key is a design pattern that grants security-restricted access to a resource without using an intermediary proxy, offloading processing as a direct client-resource relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Valet Key pattern grants security-restricted access to resources without an intermediary proxy, reducing processing overhead for frequent or large client requests.&lt;SEP&gt;Valet key pattern grants secure access to resources without intermediary components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90dd8914d5ed47ea7dd3fc98eec8c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bc0f8073e4729b7a291e64a078ac827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec74bc9a6ceebb7c4ce58c9f06c2063c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Data Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data encryption is the process of using cryptography algorithms to make data unreadable and lock it with a key to guard confidentiality and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Data encryption implements encryption for data at rest and in transit to ensure confidentiality and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Data encryption protects Azure VMware Solution workloads from unauthorized access, covering data at rest and in transit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data At Rest">
  <data key="d0">Data At Rest</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data at rest refers to all information kept in storage objects that needs encryption protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data In Transit">
  <data key="d0">Data In Transit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data in transit refers to information transferred between components, locations, or programs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data In Use">
  <data key="d0">Data In Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data in use refers to data actively being worked on in memory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BitLocker">
  <data key="d0">BitLocker</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">BitLocker is a tool used to encrypt data saved to storage on a disk.&lt;SEP&gt;BitLocker provides volume encryption as a default security feature in Azure Local.&lt;SEP&gt;BitLocker provides data-at-rest encryption on infrastructure and workload data volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;BitLocker provides volume encryption using XTS-AES 256-bit encryption for data-at-rest protection on Azure Local.&lt;SEP&gt;BitLocker is a native encryption tool used to encrypt guest VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft-Managed Encryption Keys">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft-Managed Encryption Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft-managed encryption keys are the default keys Azure services use to encrypt and decrypt data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Double Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Double encryption is the process of encrypting data using two or more independent layers of encryption, providing enhanced security for highly sensitive data. This strategy increases attacker costs by employing separate customer-managed keys across independent encryption layers.

In the context of Azure NetApp Files, double encryption operates at both the storage hardware level (using encrypted SSD drives) and at the software layer (volume level) to protect sensitive data at rest. It can be enabled by setting the encryption type to "double" when creating a capacity pool.

Double encryption also applies in other contexts, such as namespace-level configurations, where it provides an extra layer of data protection and must be enabled at namespace creation time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9514c481f519092f6d4362611c52ecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc4795580f532b2b4baa2c23d716389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002361</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cipher Suite">
  <data key="d0">Cipher Suite</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cipher suite is a set of algorithms used to encrypt and decrypt information to secure a network connection over TLS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hashing">
  <data key="d0">Hashing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hashing is the process of transforming data to text or numbers with the intent of hiding information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e507b943962b0d36b3563fef00c4090</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SHA-2">
  <data key="d0">SHA-2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SHA-2 is a family of hash algorithms including SHA-256, SHA-384, and SHA-512, recommended for security hashing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Encryption Key">
  <data key="d0">Key Encryption Key</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A KEK is used to protect the data encryption key (DEK).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Encryption Key">
  <data key="d0">Data Encryption Key</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A DEK is the key used to directly encrypt data, protected by a key encryption key.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Encryption Standard">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Encryption Standard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AES is a symmetric block cipher used in cipher suites, with variants AES-128, AES-192, and AES-256.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) is a symmetric block cipher used in cipher suites, with AES-128, AES-192, and AES-256 as acceptable variants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HSTS">
  <data key="d0">HSTS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HTTP Strict Transport Security is a policy ensuring HTTPS transport is maintained, protecting against man-in-the-middle attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entropy">
  <data key="d0">Entropy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entropy is injected during encryption to strengthen algorithms and make it difficult for attackers to extract information, with tolerable thresholds to balance security and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Checksums">
  <data key="d0">Checksums</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Checksums are produced by hash functions and used to compare data to verify its integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data At Rest Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Data At Rest Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Encrypting stored data using native options provided by storage services, including temporary and backup data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data In Transit Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Data In Transit Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Encrypting data during transmission using secure protocols like TLS for client-server communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabular Data Stream">
  <data key="d0">Tabular Data Stream</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TDS is a protocol used by Azure SQL Database that integrates a TLS handshake for secure database connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b663f0176e526e5a609a0de282882878</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Disk Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Azure Disk Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Disk Encryption protects and safeguards virtual disk data during the export process.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Disk Encryption protects and safeguards data during the export process for virtual machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Disk Encryption is an extension for Windows and Linux VMs enabling disk encryption and data-at-rest encryption.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Disk Encryption encrypts disks but does not support all SAP operating systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24da17048f52e4eee422a69ff4b58769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006021</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential Virtual Machines run inside a TEE with encrypted memory and CPU contents, offering lift-and-shift for high-security applications. Each has a dedicated virtual TPM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Confidential Computing">
  <data key="d0">Azure Confidential Computing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure confidential computing enables data protection while being computed within the physical CPU and memory of a host.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure confidential computing provides high-security controls like double encryption to protect data-in-use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trust Platform Module">
  <data key="d0">Trust Platform Module</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TPM is a dedicated virtual security module in each Azure confidential VM for encryption during secure boot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Enclave">
  <data key="d0">Application Enclave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Enclave solutions use Intel SGX CPU extensions for granular Trusted Compute Base but require specifically coded applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intel SGX">
  <data key="d0">Intel SGX</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intel Software Guard Extensions are CPU extensions used for confidential computing and secure enclaves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secure Key Release">
  <data key="d0">Secure Key Release</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Secure Key Release ensures encrypted data is only decrypted inside a TEE verified through attestation.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure Key Release supports a policy ensuring a key is only released to a workload that can cryptographically prove it is executing inside a Trusted Execution Environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attestation">
  <data key="d0">Attestation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attestation provides hardware-based, cryptographically signed evidence that data is being encrypted while in use.&lt;SEP&gt;Attestation is a process that proves a TEE provides the required level of protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Containers">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Containers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential Containers run unmodified containers inside a TEE on AKS or ACI, built upon Confidential Virtual Machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AMD SEV-SNP">
  <data key="d0">AMD SEV-SNP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AMD SEV-SNP is a secure enclave technology used for hardware-based encryption in confidential computing services.&lt;SEP&gt;AMD Secure Encrypted Virtualization-Secure Nested Paging (SEV-SNP) is a security technology that hardens guest protections and encrypts data in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dace10a501d3c2b544e137b224cd683</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trusted Execution Environment">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Execution Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Trusted Execution Environment (TEE) is a hardware isolation boundary within which encryption and decryption of data occurs securely.&lt;SEP&gt;A TEE is a secure environment where virtual machines and containers run with encrypted memory and CPU contents for data-in-use protection.&lt;SEP&gt;A Trusted Execution Environment (TEE) is a security concept for protecting data-in-use through confidential computing.&lt;SEP&gt;A hardware-based trusted execution environment (TEE) provided by confidential VM series to protect data in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a6f56b52ae33dfac75b83ed7575dc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dace10a501d3c2b544e137b224cd683</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Disk Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Managed Disk Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure offers several encryption options for managed disks to protect data at rest.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22441c67d26ebe79c34774a5792e33e6</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/encryption.md</data>
