<node id="Security Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Security Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A security baseline is a set of minimum security standards and recommendations that covers development processes, operations, training, and architectural components to ensure workload security.&lt;SEP&gt;A security baseline is a structured document specifying an organization's minimum security requirements and expectations across a range of areas.&lt;SEP&gt;A security baseline represents an organization's foundational IT environment security configuration, serving as an example for other recommendation guides.&lt;SEP&gt;The security baseline captures minimum security requirements anchored in industry standards and regulatory framework guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuously reviewed and refined set of security standards that must be kept up-to-date as workloads evolve.&lt;SEP&gt;A security baseline is a set of security configurations that should be continuously reviewed and refined as workloads evolve.&lt;SEP&gt;The security baseline maps MySQL flexible server capabilities to Microsoft cloud security benchmark controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4a87b29a0d7646a31a3fd27442ab6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9514c481f519092f6d4362611c52ecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957</data>
