<node id="Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark (MCSB) is a comprehensive security best practice framework used as a starting point for security baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft cloud security benchmark (MCSB) is a platform-driven standard used as a starting point for security baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Microsoft cloud security benchmark specifies security recommendations implemented in the Azure Databricks security baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark provides controls for Event Hubs covering encryption, network isolation, and access control.&lt;SEP&gt;The Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark version 1.0 provides recommendations on securing cloud solutions on Azure, serving as the basis for the ExpressRoute security baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;MCSB is a set of compliance controls provided by Microsoft recommended as a baseline standard for security and compliance-based practices for most workloads on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft cloud security benchmark provides recommendations for securing cloud solutions on Azure, with version 1.0 controls applied to Azure Policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb722448087dee173a263b0b147b058d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-245038d4b86625c6550cd7ef29cef86c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840c9812065b0dae17f67ebda4bb6ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc59486642305ff68ee1edaa445b8bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570</data>
