<node id="Multifactor Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Multifactor Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multifactor authentication (MFA) is an authentication requirement specified in security baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;Multifactor authentication is a modern access protocol used to protect privileged access.&lt;SEP&gt;MFA is required for privileged operations like topic creation and policy changes in Event Grid.&lt;SEP&gt;Multifactor authentication strengthens identity verification to deter unauthorized access attempts.&lt;SEP&gt;Multifactor authentication is a security measure recommended for all users and admins in Azure Virtual Desktop to improve deployment security.&lt;SEP&gt;Multifactor authentication provides an extra layer of security against unauthorized access using methods such as mobile push notifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570</data>
