<node id="Principle Of Least Privilege">
  <data key="d0">Principle Of Least Privilege</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The principle of least privilege is the starting point for defining access control, meaning granting just enough access at the asset level.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle of least privilege ensures that human and non-human accounts have only the minimum permissions necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;A security concept where access control policies grant the minimum scope needed for users to perform their duties.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle of least privilege ensures users have only the appropriate level of access needed for their role.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle of least privilege is a security concept that ensures users have only the minimum level of access required for their tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The principle of least privilege restricts access to resources using JEA and JIT methods to minimize misuse potential.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adb14c0fcfabd886fa4aa083b8012d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2</data>
