<node id="Conditional Access">
  <data key="d0">Conditional Access</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditional Access is a feature of Microsoft Entra ID (Azure Active Directory) that adds extra protection around sign-in events by applying context-based rules to access decisions. Rather than giving all identities the same level of access, Conditional Access takes into account all available data points—such as time, privilege, device, network, and location—to determine whether and how access should be granted.

Conditional Access covers users, groups, and workload identities, enforcing policies based on specified criteria aligned with operational needs and use case restrictions. As an IAM (Identity and Access Management) control applied to sensitive components, it represents a modern authentication approach that requires ongoing management to remain effective.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional Access policies apply security controls based on risk and context, requiring MFA for privileged Event Grid operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional Access is a Microsoft Entra ID feature for managing risks by evaluating user identity, sign-in method, and device before granting access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-654e7aada501f6fea6718cd59dbed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ea57e7a575650ba4d31b8ba51cf8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/harden-resources.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Just In Time">
  <data key="d0">Just In Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Just in Time (JIT) is an approach that provides required privileges only when they are needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Just in time (JIT) access is a method of granting permissions only when needed rather than as standing access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Just Enough Access">
  <data key="d0">Just Enough Access</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Just Enough Access (JEA) is an approach that provides only the required privileges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996400</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity Lifecycle Management">
  <data key="d0">Identity Lifecycle Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity lifecycle management is the process of managing digital identities from creation to decommission, including access reviews and governance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996401</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Passwordless Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Passwordless Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Passwordless authentication is a modern access protocol used to protect privileged access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Impact Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Critical Impact Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical impact accounts are administrative identities that carry the highest security risks due to their privileged access to broad sets of systems and applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity Governance">
  <data key="d0">Identity Governance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity governance is a process to manage the lifecycle of digital identities, high-privileged users, external/guest users, and workload users through access reviews.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-660c07f6382831457c45f8649ff82cf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra Connect Sync">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra Connect Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra Connect Sync is a tool for configuring filtering in hybrid identity environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Connect Sync handles synchronization between existing Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID, with default configuration blocking high-privilege account sync.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Identities">
  <data key="d0">Workload Identities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workload identities are a type of identity used in Azure Active Directory for non-human workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Workload identities are used by application services to authenticate themselves to other components in a solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Active Directory">
  <data key="d0">Azure Active Directory</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Active Directory is Microsoft's identity and access management service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Roles">
  <data key="d0">Custom Roles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom roles are configurable roles in Azure Active Directory for fine-grained access control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a17d2379a32b2d40cab90487cb72ecd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Principal">
  <data key="d0">Service Principal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A service principal is associated with an application and dictates its access scope, abstracted when using managed identities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Privileged Identity Management">
  <data key="d0">Privileged Identity Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Privileged Identity Management provides time-based and approval-based role activation for high-impact identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Privileged Identity Management is used to audit activity history for group assignments of privileged users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Authentication Library">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Authentication Library</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MSAL is used for authentication and authorization of custom applications with Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
