  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Identity">
  <data key="d0">Workload Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A workload identity is a system identity for an application or component used to authenticate itself to other services and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Workload identity enables an application to authenticate itself against other resources for inside-out access.&lt;SEP&gt;Workload identities are used to grant access to resources from deployment environments and can be handled by Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-385f36a776384c86dd2e520eb0f51b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ea57e7a575650ba4d31b8ba51cf8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996406</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
