<node id="Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication (AuthN) is a process that verifies that an identity is who or what it says it is.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication is the process of verifying a user's identity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization">
  <data key="d0">Authorization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Authorization (AuthZ) is a process that verifies whether an identity has permission to perform a requested action.&lt;SEP&gt;Authorization is the process of granting permissions based on identity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c20cbaa5ca63eea5db965095af5d2c3b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity Provider">
  <data key="d0">Identity Provider</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An identity provider (IdP) is a cloud-hosted service that stores and manages users as digital identities.&lt;SEP&gt;An identity provider (IdP) externalizes identity and access management, enhancing security through multifactor authentication and access logs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Principal">
  <data key="d0">Security Principal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A security principal is an identity that provides permissions, which can be a user, group, or service principal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Identity">
  <data key="d0">User Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A user identity is an identity for a person, such as an employee or external user.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996409</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Persona">
  <data key="d0">Persona</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A persona is a job function or title that has a set of responsibilities and actions within a workload.&lt;SEP&gt;A persona represents a responsible human or automated agent role that maps to team members' specializations and is used for accountability, access control, and work distribution in AI operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f04c6874b6ce40b7e121a05d7a90d38d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/personas.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003901</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role">
  <data key="d0">Role</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A role is a set of permissions that define what a user or group can do.&lt;SEP&gt;A role is a set of permissions needed to complete a job function, used to assign access in segmentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996804</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outside-In Access">
  <data key="d0">Outside-In Access</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Outside-in access refers to flows that reach the workload or its components from external users or systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inside-Out Access">
  <data key="d0">Inside-Out Access</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inside-out access refers to flows that reach out from the workload to other sources such as data platforms or third-party services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-037857f3ab661a8ce8ed7e958e0b34ea</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra ID Protection">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra ID Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra ID Protection helps detect, investigate, and remediate identity-based risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
