  <data key="d0">JIT And JEA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Just-in-Time (JIT) and Just-Enough-Access (JEA) provide traditional standing permissions for human operators.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/identity-access.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Directory">
  <data key="d0">Active Directory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Directory is an existing on-premises directory service whose high-privilege accounts should not be synchronized to Microsoft Entra ID.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory is used for SMB authentication and directory services integration with Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory provides SMB authentication and Kerberos support for Azure NetApp Files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0af9b59bcc2e38e219c04c0496ed334e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f</data>
