<node id="Security Operations Center">
  <data key="d0">Security Operations Center</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Operations Center (SOC), also known as SecOps, is a central security operation team responsible for detecting, prioritizing, and triaging potential attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security Operations Center (SOC) is involved in security-specific incident response procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triage">
  <data key="d0">Triage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Triage is an incident response operation that analyzes security issues and prioritizes their mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Triage is the process of assessing and prioritizing incidents to determine the appropriate response.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of analyzing and prioritizing incidents to determine severity, effect, and appropriate response actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
