  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIA">
  <data key="d0">CIA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CIA refers to confidentiality, integrity, and availability, the three core security properties used to assess incident impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/incident-response.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bridge Team">
  <data key="d0">Bridge Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The bridge team, also called the triage team, is responsible for coordinating incident investigation and communication.&lt;SEP&gt;The triage team that assembles to investigate an incident, consisting of relevant technical experts and decision-makers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="False Positive">
  <data key="d0">False Positive</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A false positive is an alert that indicates a security incident that did not actually happen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/incident-response.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Fidelity">
  <data key="d0">Alert Fidelity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert fidelity refers to the accuracy of data determining an alert, ranging from high-fidelity with actionable security context to low-fidelity with noise or lacking information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74c9c26213fc42a84efb674f80b70c8b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/incident-response.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
