<node id="Security Maturity Model">
  <data key="d0">Security Maturity Model</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The security maturity model provides a progressive path to strengthen workload security posture, structured into five distinct maturity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar-specific maturity model focused on security within the Well-Architected Framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7ba45bf48a024a996731f69cab5301</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level 1: Core Security">
  <data key="d0">Level 1: Core Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 1 establishes a minimum viable security posture as a foundation, focusing on security baseline, encryption, and identity management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption At Rest">
  <data key="d0">Encryption At Rest</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Encrypting data at rest ensures data confidentiality and integrity using strong encryption and strict access controls on data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption In Transit">
  <data key="d0">Encryption In Transit</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Encrypting data in transit protects workloads from interception, requiring TLS 1.2 as the minimum standard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bring Your Own Key">
  <data key="d0">Bring Your Own Key</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">BYOK allows users to manage their own encryption keys in Azure services instead of using Microsoft-managed keys, providing more control but adding operational burden.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TLS 1.2">
  <data key="d0">TLS 1.2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TLS 1.2 is a transport layer security protocol that is more secure and faster than its predecessors, TLS 1.0 and 1.1, supporting modern cryptographic algorithms. It is the required minimum version of Transport Layer Security for encrypting data in transit across all systems, recommended to prevent exploitation of legacy SSL/TLS vulnerabilities and protect against protocol downgrade attacks.

TLS 1.2 is widely mandated as the minimum version for secure client connections and inter-service communication across numerous Azure services, including Azure SQL Database, Event Grid, and Service Bus, ensuring message data and client connections are protected in transit.&lt;SEP&gt;Transport Layer Security version 1.2 is the encryption protocol used by Azure Virtual Desktop for all connections to infrastructure components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e0d4c6d0c4bc09abb77f7cb933aa9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653342d517c710c9f67df8e6155d05a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization And Authentication Controls">
  <data key="d0">Authorization And Authentication Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controls related to granting or denying access to resources based on user roles and specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996514</data>
