  <data key="d0">Vulnerability Scanning Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool used to identify vulnerable components in a workload as it matures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50e84f8f3385ed4e029dfd1f75a5fc3e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsegmentation">
  <data key="d0">Microsegmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsegmentation is a network security strategy that prevents lateral movement across workloads by separating components into protected subnets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Loss Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Data Loss Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DLP is a security strategy that identifies, monitors, and protects sensitive data from unauthorized access, misuse, or accidental disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;DLP is a security strategy that identifies, monitors, and protects sensitive data from unauthorized access or misuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c1925896ad2776a0d0431adee7f3d3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level 5">
  <data key="d0">Level 5</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 5 is the advanced defense tier of the security maturity model, focusing on enterprise-grade security solutions and advanced threat defense for highly mature organizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 5 of the maturity model focuses on achieving peak performance through experimentation, automation, and continuous optimization techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 5 focuses on sharing designs, successes, and failures across the organization and using automation to reduce friction beyond Level 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 5 of the maturity model focuses on transforming cost optimization into a competitive advantage through continuous innovation, maximizing ROI with predictable budgets and accurate forecasts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-734874c613782da336574a76536f1d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c08b70348e6bfa97e9d7c1d1701b024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e912a1ac7fa5ab0139e0fac99a203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9274b98dae68e1fda563c0a186872af</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Security Development Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Security Development Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft Security Development Lifecycle is a set of security practices for software development.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Security Development Lifecycle (SDL) recommends secure practices applicable to development lifecycles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fef76463ffa39e57a8a833790934275c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf9fd57985f14c81b7d1b9d2924d1bc</data>
