  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subnet">
  <data key="d0">Subnet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subnets are carved-out segments within a virtual network used to group resources within an isolation boundary with similar security assurances.&lt;SEP&gt;Subnets are subdivisions of virtual networks used to segment and collocate services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Security Group">
  <data key="d0">Network Security Group</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Network security groups are Azure resources used to set firewall rules for subnet traffic inspection.&lt;SEP&gt;A layer 3 and layer 4 firewall applied at the subnet or NIC level in Azure virtual networks, used to control inbound and outbound traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;NSG is a free resource that filters TCP/UDP inbound and outbound communication based on IP and port ranges within a VNet.&lt;SEP&gt;A Network Security Group (NSG) is used to further restrict traffic to only expected client origin IP addresses in API Management virtual network configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups provide granular control over which virtual networks can communicate with container apps.&lt;SEP&gt;NSG is used to filter traffic between Azure resources to mitigate potential security events.&lt;SEP&gt;NSG rules can be used in Azure Chaos Studio to simulate endpoint failures by blocking access to subnets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b82e5bd8bced74ea376399d3355126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4889043b463029eef941a26e276c8840</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Private Endpoint">
  <data key="d0">Private Endpoint</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A private endpoint is assigned a private IP address from a virtual network to secure access to PaaS services.&lt;SEP&gt;Private endpoints limit direct exposure to the public network and allow controlled access through a reverse proxy.&lt;SEP&gt;A private endpoint routes network traffic over the Microsoft backbone network instead of the public internet, eliminating risk exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;A private endpoint routes network traffic over the Microsoft backbone network instead of the public internet, eliminating public internet risk exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;A network configuration that limits access to a workspace to private IP addresses only, enhancing security and controlled access.&lt;SEP&gt;Private endpoints provide secure connectivity to various Azure resources including internal load balancers, enabling private access to SaaS solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e39ac746628d7273f799262e7cf7dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c50c3fc68e8ca3e2a2600f5ec515c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1a7707a8a1d8d9f53bc71b18814f3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Service Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A service-level firewall available for most Azure resources to set rules based on access patterns for internet-exposed services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47016d300e650b08a3402c1a274475c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996652</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
