<node id="Application Security Group">
  <data key="d0">Application Security Group</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A named group containing resources with similar inbound or outbound access needs, assignable as a destination type.&lt;SEP&gt;ASG is part of NSG that allows creating tags for traffic rules for easier management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b82e5bd8bced74ea376399d3355126</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateway is an Azure networking service designed for web traffic management and load balancing at the application layer (Layer 7), particularly for HTTP/HTTPS workloads. It supports key capabilities including TLS termination/offloading, autoscaling, health monitoring, routing, and load balancing for web applications. It handles security functions such as TLS termination and traffic inspection at the endpoint level.

Application Gateway integrates with Web Application Firewall (WAF), which can be enabled directly on it, as well as DDoS Protection and Azure Firewall to provide robust security for web applications in hub-and-spoke and Virtual WAN scenarios. It is commonly combined with API Management for improved API performance and is recommended for load balancing HTTP applications with firewall capabilities.

Application Gateway is deployed in a dedicated subnet with Network Security Group (NSG) and WAF controls, and can be used in private virtual networks and multiregion load balancing architectures. From an operational perspective, it can be stopped to save costs, monitored for capacity metrics, and configured with diagnostics, alerts, and autoscaling policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Gateway protects internet-facing workloads by creating separation between endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c53b990e9918af85864a95bf9284ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f471ce6b86ced91e851ed4cd06f0521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937b1809a20f2b2148f344a58b016317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df0cc69c8383501073ee148f940f5d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fa337fdf4c15ddf378bf74ac66c3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-257827ee036f98e6274522ad2bfee550&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4889043b463029eef941a26e276c8840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c2320d6f192d51ba7461cdb73ef6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca4d2bd438b809671ecf2d090095b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006021</data>
