</node>
<node id="Hub-Spoke">
  <data key="d0">Hub-Spoke</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub-spoke is a network topology that provides centralized firewall protection and optimizes costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36dd3a8f5a535bef38f7d594298d02cf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DDoS Protection">
  <data key="d0">Azure DDoS Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DDoS Protection is an Azure service that provides distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) protection for public endpoints and virtual networks. It helps protect resources such as Application Gateway instances with public IPs by guarding against DDoS attacks. The service offers simulation testing capabilities for denial-of-service attack scenarios.

Azure DDoS Protection operates through protection plans that can be associated with hub virtual networks to provide centralized DDoS protection management. These plans can be created and associated through Azure Firewall Manager, working alongside firewall policies. However, a notable limitation is that Azure DDoS Protection cannot be enabled on Azure Firewall public IPs within a Virtual WAN hub.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection is a standard plan providing advanced protection and detection capabilities against DDoS attacks for public IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection standard plan provides advanced protection and detection capabilities for public IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection provides advanced protection including detection capabilities that monitor endpoints for threats and abuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection protects public-facing spoke workloads at the virtual network or IP address level.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection is a security service that safeguards virtual networks against distributed denial-of-service attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DDoS Protection provides advanced DDoS protection by learning traffic patterns and adjusting protections accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9641143ef161c630f4c2735baa058dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa7e37862e9b9978a85e7dde37bac4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e4093031cc92a18b0a5ae7643e4edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df0cc69c8383501073ee148f940f5d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8f25dd2dc2bf1ed1488dc9092be0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11229197c05f5be9b778a1918888ee7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fa337fdf4c15ddf378bf74ac66c3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e496d3c1901ebb6e0f0add1d59b5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f878ef77f1b4e5dc16c41419b23ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608026926818db1b277afce5e06e8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cd6df2b9534dcc70f59a3fbb6607582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84edc61960c2c1e2ea0cf79280a5461f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004596</data>
