</node>
<node id="Network Filtering">
  <data key="d0">Network Filtering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network filtering is a mechanism that allows or blocks network traffic based on specified rules, verifying that traffic entering a boundary is expected, allowed, and safe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Network Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network transformation is a mechanism that mutates network packets at boundaries as a security measure to obscure them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="East-West Traffic">
  <data key="d0">East-West Traffic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">East-west traffic is network traffic that moves within a trusted boundary.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic that flows within a workload network when components communicate with each other.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="North-South Traffic">
  <data key="d0">North-South Traffic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">North-south traffic is network traffic that moves from a trusted boundary to external potentially hostile networks, and vice versa.&lt;SEP&gt;Traffic that flows between a workload network and external networks, crossing the edge of the network.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ingress Flow">
  <data key="d0">Ingress Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ingress flow is inbound workload traffic flowing toward a workload or its components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egress Flow">
  <data key="d0">Egress Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Egress flow is outbound workload traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hostile Network">
  <data key="d0">Hostile Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A hostile network is a network not deployed as part of a workload, considered a threat vector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reverse Proxy">
  <data key="d0">Reverse Proxy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A gateway function that acts as a transition point between public and private network boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A reverse proxy is a gateway that functions as a transition point between public and private network boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0824c72199637e43cfbbf3653d45df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3684f270a6e04d539183000fb990392a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Network">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Network is a fundamental networking service in Azure that serves as a building block for establishing private networks on the Azure platform. It enables resources to securely communicate with each other, the internet, and on-premises networks, providing centralized IP address management, integrated diagnostics, and capabilities including encryption, segmentation, and connectivity.

Azure Virtual Network offers robust traffic filtering features, allowing users to configure routing and network security groups to control traffic patterns for containment. It provides network isolation and security benefits, enabling applications to securely access resources and route traffic while controlling outbound traffic. It is commonly used to isolate virtual machines and scale sets by defining network security groups to filter traffic.

Azure Virtual Network supports network segmentation and isolation across multiple Azure services. It provides network isolation for App Service apps through virtual network injection, dedicated subnet deployment for SQL Managed Instance, and network-level isolation for Azure Databricks data plane resources. It also enables private communication between Azure resources, supports connecting Azure Virtual Desktop host pools to networks, and is often combined with API Management for enhanced networking scenarios.

Azure Virtual Network provides private IP address blocks for deploying resources with private connectivity, with resilience unaffected by single datacenter failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6aa7e37862e9b9978a85e7dde37bac4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50bf24a002558d213cd02700a64f5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c53b990e9918af85864a95bf9284ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cd6df2b9534dcc70f59a3fbb6607582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b3b849ac5683c426e666e8f3f3f48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161fa262de0d263c9842f3ec1f7a7795</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004985</data>
