<node id="Build And Deployment Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">Build And Deployment Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Build and deployment pipelines are prime targets for attackers who may tamper with them, inject malicious code, or access secrets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Least-Privilege">
  <data key="d0">Least-Privilege</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Least-privilege is an access control principle where access is granted on a need-to-know basis with minimal permissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Least-privilege is a security principle where users are granted only the minimum access necessary to perform their duties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Default To Deny">
  <data key="d0">Default To Deny</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Default to deny is a design principle where access is blocked unless explicitly allowed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-174b243fd3068f9f7f6fa881f576ccdd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
