</node>
<node id="Environment Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Environment Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environment isolation is the practice of strictly separating production and non-production systems to prevent breaches from spreading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abf9fd57985f14c81b7d1b9d2924d1bc</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/secure-development-lifecycle.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Plane Operations">
  <data key="d0">Control Plane Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Management of the resource itself, distinct from data plane operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Plane Operations">
  <data key="d0">Data Plane Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Access to the data stored by a resource, distinct from control plane operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Resource Tags">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tags used to annotate resource groups or subscriptions with owner team information.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure resource tags are metadata applied to resources to track which resources belong to which customer.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure resource tags are metadata key-value pairs applied to resources to identify and govern them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96969696039ca4d7daf8f0eaa36cb1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad653e4d2f68d336a1fa1654643a4bb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/governance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Virtual Networks">
  <data key="d0">Hub Virtual Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub virtual networks are shared networking components within an Azure estate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Owner Role">
  <data key="d0">Owner Role</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A highly privileged RBAC role that gives users the ability to grant other users access to a resource.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d3c29048704933cd594ead18773c494</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Groups">
  <data key="d0">Security Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security groups are used as a workaround for RBAC complexity by assigning roles to groups instead of individual identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Security groups are organizational units used to assign permissions and manage access for human and service principals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6503993c6e8852f14500c5e6630b88b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Function-Based Grouping">
  <data key="d0">Function-Based Grouping</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Function-based grouping organizes security groups by discrete work functions rather than team structure, maintaining strict least-privilege access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role-Based Grouping">
  <data key="d0">Role-Based Grouping</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Role-based grouping (Pattern 1) assigns security group membership based on responsibilities in the workload, aligned to job roles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NSGs">
  <data key="d0">NSGs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Security Groups (NSGs) are used to filter network traffic between segments in Azure virtual networks.&lt;SEP&gt;NSGs (Network Security Groups) are networking components that can block traffic from Load Balancer health probes or client IP addresses as an alternative to Admin State.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups provide subnet-level filtering in spoke virtual networks based on IP addresses, ports, and protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups filter traffic entering and leaving the network based on IP address and port ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups (NSGs) are Azure resources used to filter network traffic to and from Azure resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups (NSGs) are used to define traffic rules for network security management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b1ef27485e0c9c13eb1505e8179870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c00db143f490c3d917ea5c2345f79ef2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Networking Segmentation Pattern 1">
  <data key="d0">Networking Segmentation Pattern 1</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation within a single virtual network using subnets to mark boundaries, providing layer 3 level control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Networking Segmentation Pattern 2">
  <data key="d0">Networking Segmentation Pattern 2</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation where workload components are spread across multiple networks without peering, communicating through a public intermediary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASGs">
  <data key="d0">ASGs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Security Groups (ASGs) are used alongside NSGs to filter network traffic in Azure virtual networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Security Groups simplify management by abstracting underlying IP address ranges in network security rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Security Groups (ASGs) are used when defining traffic rules for NSGs instead of specific IP addresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b1ef27485e0c9c13eb1505e8179870</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Networking Segmentation Pattern 3">
  <data key="d0">Networking Segmentation Pattern 3</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern 3 uses Azure Network Security Perimeter to create logical boundaries around PaaS services, preventing data exfiltration without requiring individual private endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96035ef5f5894d52718d074319b896c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perimeter">
  <data key="d0">Perimeter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A perimeter is the trust boundary and entry edge around a segment where security controls are applied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Containment">
  <data key="d0">Containment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Containment is a technique to prevent lateral movement and contain the blast radius if an attacker gains access to a segment.&lt;SEP&gt;Containment is the practice of limiting incident impact to prevent it from affecting other components or systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The first step in incident remediation that isolates affected components to prevent the problem from spreading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c726f154bb635219bc21e5a4c3c1ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/incident-response.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Isolation is the practice of grouping entities with similar assurances together to protect them with a boundary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Segment">
  <data key="d0">Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A segment is a logical unit that is isolated from other entities and protected by a set of security measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity">
  <data key="d0">Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity is the primary security perimeter used to authenticate and authorize access across isolation boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3df9290c84fe42909028ddfaafd17299</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/security/segmentation.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776996804</data>
