<node id="Azure Load Testing">
  <data key="d0">Azure Load Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Load Testing is a fully managed load testing service designed to generate high-scale load by simulating traffic, load, and usage patterns for applications. It helps optimize application performance and scalability by reflecting actual production workloads and gathering workload data.

The service integrates with Apache JMeter and supports CI/CD integration, enabling automation and streamlining of different types of testing. Azure Load Testing provides dashboards with live updates and detailed resource metrics, and supports performance tests within Azure App Testing.

Azure Load Testing is used across a variety of scenarios, including verifying scaling rules and adjusting autoscaling policies, simulating realistic event volumes for testing delivery reliability, simulating realistic producer event rates, consumer patterns, and partition key distribution, and validating capacity under production-style workloads. It is also employed to simulate realistic Service Bus workloads to identify bottlenecks before production deployment, and to generate initial traffic to warm up Azure Firewall before performance tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7ad22ba75f55d75473c21aeba4f8611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997b67d2a5ddf57a24dd0380ce47e074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e4a31ea43efb7a100f1df033cb0e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c203348328e5589b8f4b6fa4101a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298abf3381d05efe7bed040fe109d8ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b1c021188faeb6dd44f9550bc2c4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd9ecc5b1e909344bcefaee765852bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db510f47656045373bcac562ba7e53ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd12866b1c0a9d8fe76b6447e59f118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/capacity-planning.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tools-processes.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
