<node id="Automatic Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic tuning is a feature in Azure SQL Database that continuously monitors and improves queries automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic tuning monitors queries, adapts to changing workloads, and applies tuning recommendations automatically using AI and machine learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic tuning is a SQL Database feature that enhances efficiency by automatically optimizing performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bbb7e81c733c8a34be73ab3d43902b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe464ce8a55b32a868b7ba10711df9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CI/CD Tools">
  <data key="d0">CI/CD Tools</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">CI/CD tools are used to automate the deployment process, test against endpoints, check HTTP statuses, and validate data quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Healing Systems">
  <data key="d0">Self-Healing Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-healing systems automate recovery processes for known performance issues by adjusting system configuration automatically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Database Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Database optimization involves identifying and implementing improvements to handle loads, deliver fast response times, and minimize resource utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Monitoring And Alerting">
  <data key="d0">Automated Monitoring And Alerting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated monitoring and alerting involves setting up systems to continuously monitor performance metrics and detect deviations or anomalies, triggering alerts when issues are detected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Diagnostics">
  <data key="d0">Automated Diagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated diagnostics are tools or scripts that analyze performance data and identify root causes of performance issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Remediation Actions">
  <data key="d0">Automated Remediation Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated remediation actions are predefined responses triggered when specific performance issues are detected, such as restarting services or clearing caches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48dc8704fc8585c17685d5d5ff321ca8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/continuous-performance-optimize.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Content Hosting">
  <data key="d0">Static Content Hosting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Static Content Hosting optimizes delivery of static content using a dedicated hosting platform, offloading from the application platform.&lt;SEP&gt;Static Content Hosting is a design pattern that optimizes delivery of static content by using a dedicated hosting platform, offloading responsibility from the application platform.&lt;SEP&gt;Static Content Hosting pattern optimizes delivery of static content using dedicated hosting platforms that are cheaper than dynamic application hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;Static content hosting delivers static content efficiently, avoiding expensive dynamic application hosts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec74bc9a6ceebb7c4ce58c9f06c2063c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Materialized View">
  <data key="d0">Materialized View</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Materialized View uses precomputed views of data to optimize retrieval, storing results of complex computations to reduce resource consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d81a147434c35f3d6af3a65d96c1c22</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Request-Reply">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Request-Reply</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that decouples request and reply phases to improve responsiveness and scalability, maximizing server-side concurrency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cache-Aside">
  <data key="d0">Cache-Aside</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that introduces an on-demand cache for frequently read data to improve overall system performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Choreography">
  <data key="d0">Choreography</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern using decentralized event-driven communication to coordinate distributed components, providing an alternative to centralized orchestration bottlenecks.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that coordinates autonomous distributed components using decentralized, event-driven communication, enabling frequent service updates with less overall system change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Competing Consumers">
  <data key="d0">Competing Consumers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern applying distributed concurrent processing to handle queue items with dynamic scaling based on queue depth.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing Consumers pattern applies distributed and concurrent processing to handle queue items, enabling scaling based on queue depth down to zero.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing consumers pattern applies distributed and concurrent processing to efficiently handle queued items.&lt;SEP&gt;Competing Consumers is a code optimization design pattern applied within Azure Databricks environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Resource Consolidation">
  <data key="d0">Compute Resource Consolidation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern that optimizes compute resources by increasing density and combining workloads on shared infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;A design pattern that optimizes compute resources by increasing density and combining multiple applications on shared infrastructure, simplifying management and observability.&lt;SEP&gt;Compute Resource Consolidation pattern optimizes compute resources by increasing density and combining multiple applications on shared infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;This pattern combines multiple applications on shared infrastructure to maximize resource utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Compute Resource Consolidation is a code optimization design pattern applied within Azure Databricks environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0773a066490ceb376c40ec81b1c605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fa8a30517c9b1ec527c6f5d09a0fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/design-patterns.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command And Query Responsibility Segregation">
  <data key="d0">Command And Query Responsibility Segregation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern (CQRS) separating read and write operations for targeted performance and scaling optimizations, especially for high read-to-write ratio applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f353c01b035545d08e4ab51fe6daecad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/design-patterns.md</data>
