<node id="Performance Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Performance Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance baselines provide reference points for comparing performance over time and identifying improvements or degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of metrics representing workload behavior under normal conditions as validated by testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance baseline is a reference point against which testing data is analyzed and compared using APM tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance baseline represents starting-point measurements against which future performance tests are compared.&lt;SEP&gt;Establishing a performance baseline provides insight into capabilities and helps identify performance constraints in Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d20a250447d571c0a31d1f1f211c8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5fd47376a7e9081496e03cedc06a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-997b67d2a5ddf57a24dd0380ce47e074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/performance-test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diminishing Returns">
  <data key="d0">Diminishing Returns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diminishing returns is the point where iterative improvements no longer justify the cost and burden of fixing inefficiencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f40a9cc5e9bacfbd14def915787060e9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency Pillar">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency Pillar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Performance Efficiency pillar is a component of the Well-Architected Framework focused on optimizing workload performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency pillar is a framework with multiple maturity levels focusing on optimizing workload performance through signals and feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency pillar is a framework component related to performance testing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency pillar is one of the pillars that must be balanced against cost optimization trade-offs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43be904f845543056b0462aeab67302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4aed87d4e81857a842b49249489eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cf91e067df302cf4a6958a130fa0fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4c20a753377d79a1b6e9a6ac4090a3</data>
