<node id="Data Compression">
  <data key="d0">Data Compression</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data compression using lossless and lossy techniques reduces data footprint, saving storage space and bandwidth and enabling faster data transfers.&lt;SEP&gt;Data compression is the action of reducing file size by minimizing redundant data.&lt;SEP&gt;A method to compress and bundle HTTP content and file data for fast transmission between clients and servers, optimizing network traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Data compression reduces the size of data to optimize storage space and improve workload performance efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique of reducing data size to minimize storage requirements and improve data transfer efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Data compression reduces the size of stored data, most effective in write-once, read-rarely scenarios and colder storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Data compression is a technique used to optimize application performance by reducing data size in network transfers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4d7f07b48cc1c474bedf5d938c8ae09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94fc40a37b0b592b4e03905809e7d296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c00db143f490c3d917ea5c2345f79ef2</data>
