<node id="Connection Pooling">
  <data key="d0">Connection Pooling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection Pooling is a technique that allows the reuse of established database or network connections instead of creating a new connection for every request. By maintaining a pool of ready-to-use connections, it significantly reduces the latency and overhead associated with repeatedly establishing and tearing down connections, enabling high throughput especially under high concurrency.

Connection Pooling is supported by Azure services for efficiently managing database connections, including SQL Database, and is also used as a client optimization technique for Service Bus message handling. Connection pooling isolation can ensure that resource-intensive tasks do not consume all available connections, helping mitigate cascading failures.

However, Connection Pooling can also introduce challenges such as pool fragmentation, which may degrade performance if not managed properly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e31fdc4d1c3251e67cb0588dd3047a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefafe3b76f15cde350013dbb7911e9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c50ccf987c588887cc7df000f1e99478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe464ce8a55b32a868b7ba10711df9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-code-infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
