</node>
<node id="HTTP/2">
  <data key="d0">HTTP/2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A modern network protocol that enables multiple requests over a single connection, reducing connection overhead.&lt;SEP&gt;A network protocol designed to improve performance by reducing latency and optimizing data transfer over HTTP/1.1.&lt;SEP&gt;HTTP/2 is a protocol that fully multiplexes connections, reuses connections, and compresses headers to improve efficiency over HTTP/1.1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c2638addf4f5d994287e1c06820ce5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c50ccf987c588887cc7df000f1e99478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90796296cec0f129315921be106646d</data>
