<node id="Data Performance Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Data Performance Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data performance monitoring involves collecting and analyzing performance metrics specific to data operations to proactively identify and mitigate potential bottlenecks.&lt;SEP&gt;Data performance monitoring is the practice of consistently tracking the efficiency of data stores, partitions, and indexes in real-time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Partitioning">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Partitioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Horizontal partitioning splits data based on rows or ranges of values (also known as sharding), with each partition containing a subset of rows.&lt;SEP&gt;Horizontal partitioning divides a dataset based on specific criteria such as ranges of values, with each partition containing a subset of data meeting defined criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Horizontal partitioning distributes data across multiple resources or servers for better scalability and performance, effective when workloads can be parallelized.&lt;SEP&gt;Horizontal partitioning (sharding) divides data into shards based on a key, spreading load across multiple computers to reduce contention and improve performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A partitioning strategy that divides data into multiple stores with identical schemas, where each partition (shard) contains a subset of rows based on partition key values.&lt;SEP&gt;A partitioning strategy that distributes data across multiple partitions using a shard key.&lt;SEP&gt;Horizontal partitioning (sharding) divides data across partitions with the same schema, making item location difficult but enabling rebalancing for even distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6542d2e0c59d483460cb92d7687c6c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c944e9a44adf39c12919b36fa366a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f5c02d75cf91d6692adb66113df89eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c0f1c2454a3cd326399dd189c571e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103386df6f9acd0832fa49dd897fcede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc8280bb50c2a5f4a589617c1bed437</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Query Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Database Query Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimizing database queries refines queries using techniques such as index hints and caching to increase efficiency and speed of data retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997223</data>
