<node id="N+1 Query Problem">
  <data key="d0">N+1 Query Problem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The N+1 query problem occurs when excessive roundtrips to the database are made; it is mitigated by using joins and batch fetching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Caching">
  <data key="d0">Query Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Query caching stores results of frequently run queries in memory to eliminate repeated execution and reduce processing overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-059c3b1921ce4b9169eff7763d1acd07</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CQRS Pattern">
  <data key="d0">CQRS Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Command and Query Responsibility Segregation pattern separates read and write operations for data stores.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern for separating read and write operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Partitioning">
  <data key="d0">Data Partitioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data Partitioning is a strategy for distributing data across multiple partitions or storage units to improve performance, scalability, and availability. It aims to reduce contention, improve throughput, and optimize query performance in distributed systems.

Data Partitioning covers several approaches, including horizontal, vertical, and functional partitioning, each with specific application design considerations. Strategies typically organize data based on commonly used filter columns, with guidelines recommending fewer than 10,000 partitions and at least 1 GB per partition.

While beneficial, Data Partitioning introduces challenges such as synchronization, failover complexity, querying across partitions, rebalancing, and handling uneven data growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ec3bae0c0f185d5df0733c73840934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f5c02d75cf91d6692adb66113df89eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c0f1c2454a3cd326399dd189c571e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-428d5f718f38d153cbe16fd48c1637de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e47e51139cb584d95de7bb450c2af708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/partition-data.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OLAP">
  <data key="d0">OLAP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Online analytical processing (OLAP) is a technology that organizes large business databases and supports complex analytical queries without affecting transactional systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Online Analytical Processing systems used for complex analytical processing, reporting, business intelligence, data mining, and decision support.&lt;SEP&gt;OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) is a data processing approach for analytical queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OLTP">
  <data key="d0">OLTP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Online transaction processing (OLTP) is a technology that records business interactions as they occur in day-to-day operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Online Transaction Processing systems used for real-time transactional processing, handling individual transactions efficiently for operational tasks like order processing and inventory management.&lt;SEP&gt;OLTP (Online Transaction Processing) is a data processing approach for transactional workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e1025a7954be69db6e0428a192ab050c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Memory Caching">
  <data key="d0">In-Memory Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">In-memory caching stores frequently accessed data in memory for fast retrieval, useful for data that is read frequently but changes infrequently.&lt;SEP&gt;In-memory caching stores frequently accessed data in memory for fast retrieval, useful for data that is expensive to compute and read frequently but doesn't change often.&lt;SEP&gt;A caching technique implemented within an application to utilize idle compute resources and increase compute density.&lt;SEP&gt;A caching technique implemented within an application that stores data in memory to utilize idle compute and reduce external data fetching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c50ccf987c588887cc7df000f1e99478</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Query Caching">
  <data key="d0">Database Query Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Database query caching caches results of database queries to avoid running the same query multiple times.&lt;SEP&gt;Database query caching caches results of database queries to avoid running the same query multiple times, useful for complex and time-consuming queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content Delivery Network Caching">
  <data key="d0">Content Delivery Network Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Content delivery network caching caches web content on distributed network servers to reduce latency, effective for static content like images, CSS, and JavaScript files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Read Replicas">
  <data key="d0">Read Replicas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Read replicas are multiple copies of a database that distribute read queries to minimize demand on the write database and improve performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas distribute read workloads across up to 10 instances using asynchronous binary log replication.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas are database copies in the same or cross regions used to offload read-heavy queries and reporting workloads from the primary server.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas incur independent charges at the same rates as the primary server in Azure Database for MySQL.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas serve analytical and reporting workloads, bill independently for compute and storage, and can be sized independently from the primary server.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas use asynchronous binary log replication to provide horizontal read scaling with measurable lag between source and replica.&lt;SEP&gt;Read replicas offload read queries from the primary server, freeing compute and I/O capacity for write operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Optimistic Concurrency">
  <data key="d0">Optimistic Concurrency</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimistic concurrency is an approach for updating databases using snapshots instead of traditional locking mechanisms, improving performance and scalability.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimistic concurrency handles concurrent updates by allowing multiple users to work concurrently, using version or timestamp to detect and resolve conflicts without locking.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimistic concurrency is an approach for updating databases using snapshots instead of traditional locking mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimistic concurrency is a measure to enable more throughput to databases when scaling horizontally.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimistic concurrency is an approach to eliminate data locking while maintaining data consistency, applicable to both relational and nonrelational databases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd9326bd28e1ca67beb40e575a0abd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c944e9a44adf39c12919b36fa366a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fb475b8b7efe4018b64a1ed512f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b047e8b449398992f0dfab15265a69c0</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/scale-partition.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL Optimization">
  <data key="d0">ETL Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ETL optimization streamlines extract, transform, and load processes to minimize processing time by making each step efficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parallel Processing">
  <data key="d0">Parallel Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Parallel processing distributes data processing tasks across multiple threads or nodes for concurrent workload processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Parallel processing is a method of distributing computational work across multiple CPUs, GPUs, or nodes to handle compute-intensive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809d253c9aab5017c77e2a8b92279866</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/get-started-overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Batch Processing">
  <data key="d0">Batch Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Batch processing groups similar tasks together to reduce overhead and overall processing time.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch processing groups multiple operations together in a single request to improve efficiency and reduce network overhead.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch processing reduces network round trips by sending or receiving multiple messages in single operations using ReceiveMessages() and SendMessages() methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch processing is a method of scheduling intensive workloads during low-carbon intensity periods to reduce emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch processing is an optimized data ingestion method that minimizes computational overhead and enhances sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Execution of large volumes of jobs with results delivered upon completion.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch Processing is an architectural pattern for executing large volumes of jobs with results delivered upon completion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5dafaf64829c3146ac17935b49a986e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c64e72596f12ff7c458fd34e5a4d481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d2aa553dc8052b724423e935c1fc7fe</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainable-ai-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Proximity">
  <data key="d0">Data Proximity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data proximity is the strategic placement of data closer to users or services that access it most frequently to ensure faster access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7bd352195eb26eade8cba187e9a01b8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexes">
  <data key="d0">Indexes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexes enhance data retrieval speed by allowing databases to find data using specific columns or fields, improving sorting and join operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lossless Compression">
  <data key="d0">Lossless Compression</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lossless compression algorithms reduce data size without losing any information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lossy Compression">
  <data key="d0">Lossy Compression</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lossy compression algorithms achieve high compression ratios by removing less important or redundant information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B-Tree Indexes">
  <data key="d0">B-Tree Indexes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">B-tree indexes are used for equality and range queries but may have high storage overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hash Indexes">
  <data key="d0">Hash Indexes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hash indexes are used for exact match queries but are not suitable for range queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Full-Text Indexes">
  <data key="d0">Full-Text Indexes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Full-text indexes are used for text search operations but may have high storage requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Archiving">
  <data key="d0">Archiving</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Archiving relocates older, less-frequently accessed data to more cost-effective storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997228</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Purging">
  <data key="d0">Purging</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Purging permanently removes redundant data from storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25cb48c49a01513d772a058997d07ef3</data>
