<node id="Relational Database">
  <data key="d0">Relational Database</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of database used to store structured, transactional data using normalized tables with relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;A relational database is a traditional database system that may be switched to alternatives for cost optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-data-performance.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NoSQL Database">
  <data key="d0">NoSQL Database</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of database used to store unstructured or semi-structured data using document structures or key-value pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;NoSQL database is suited for document-oriented data or data requiring flexible schemas.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of database suited for document-oriented data or flexible schemas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e6b92d448946b8b4857fbfb49acd5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
