<node id="Canary Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Canary Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment strategy that gradually rolls out new versions while monitoring for issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Canary deployment is a safe deployment pattern that provides flexibility through side-by-side deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Canary deployment is a progressive exposure approach using weighted load balancing to send a specific percentage of traffic to an origin for testing new features.&lt;SEP&gt;Canary deployment is a progressive exposure technique used with Azure Front Door's weighted load balancing to send a specific percentage of traffic to an origin for testing new features.&lt;SEP&gt;Canary deployments validate routing changes such as subscription filter modifications before full rollout in Service Bus infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4be12a3d391245ffca95ba2ca936932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe53a5474c5e4934795683b73b06789&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d314b16e3b2b8776b889c2beaec2890&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc6dd32c7c960a85b9a30c11bc43659</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prewarming">
  <data key="d0">Prewarming</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preparing a new environment by simulating production-like traffic to ensure readiness before cutover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4be12a3d391245ffca95ba2ca936932</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Place Upgrades">
  <data key="d0">In-Place Upgrades</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of upgrading a component or application without replacing it or migrating it to a new environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4be12a3d391245ffca95ba2ca936932</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997269</data>
