  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Operations">
  <data key="d0">Database Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Database operations refer to tasks like backups, schema changes, performance tuning, and monitoring that need optimization for maximum efficiency and minimal resource utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring And Debugging">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring And Debugging</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoring and debugging includes logging, telemetry, instrumentation, and distributed tracing that can affect performance if excessively or poorly implemented.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd9885ad1df3a42bbb9f25a554d6897e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/performance-efficiency/optimize-operational-tasks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Slots">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Slots</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment slots allow swapping app content and configuration between nonproduction and production environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment slots run in the same compute environment as the production instance, enabling blue-green deployments and release management.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment slots are a feature of Azure Functions that allow staging changes before production release, reducing risk of errors and enabling safe rollbacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2bb86f739c9edc6bd3bfbf22453a81a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85416f9f4269be56820f2abc15bfb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8fc58eb81af85bd1aa7f2b1f5ef9b</data>
