<node id="Control Plane">
  <data key="d0">Control Plane</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A control plane is a back-end system or suite of tools for managing applications and dependencies through a unified interface.&lt;SEP&gt;The control plane is managed by the Databricks platform and is isolated from the data plane, communicating securely to manage workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A control plane is a formalized solution or application responsible for managing customer lifecycle events, provisioning, and configuring infrastructure in SaaS solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;A control plane is a component built for complex requirements that uses Azure Resource Manager APIs directly to manage infrastructure.</data>
