<node id="Version Control">
  <data key="d0">Version Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Version control is used to maintain consistency in documentation and keep a record of updates, such as storing runbooks in a version-controlled repository.&lt;SEP&gt;Version control systems are used to store IaC templates, track changes, manage different versions, and foster collaboration among team members.&lt;SEP&gt;Version control is a cornerstone of DevOps for managing code assets, library packages, SDKs, container images, and model versions consistently across the SDLC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ede2f555755748b50d3eff6168ec5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d58b81465c40024b1e7d72578e9d17</data>
