</node>
<node id="Immutable Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Immutable Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure intended to be replaced with new infrastructure running new configuration with each deployment, not changed in place.&lt;SEP&gt;Immutable infrastructure involves redeploying resources with the latest configuration to replace those running the previous version.&lt;SEP&gt;Immutable infrastructure is a design approach where all systems in scope are replaced with updated configuration simultaneously and identically with each deployment, rather than being modified in place.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a87895e99b347e4b871e414149100339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mutable Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Mutable Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure intended to be changed in place, where deployments modify configuration rather than replacing infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutable infrastructure allows scoped updates on existing resource groups as the smallest viable change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a87895e99b347e4b871e414149100339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998187</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Module">
  <data key="d0">Module</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit of abstraction for dividing groups of resources to simplify complex deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a87895e99b347e4b871e414149100339</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997782</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immutable Deployment Model">
  <data key="d0">Immutable Deployment Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An immutable deployment model deploys new infrastructure rather than updating existing infrastructure in place, recommended for business-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop Landing Zone Accelerator">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop Landing Zone Accelerator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An example architecture for Virtual Desktop implementation deployable via ARM, Bicep, or Terraform files.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Virtual Desktop landing zone accelerator highlights necessary customizations for integrating Azure Virtual Desktop with Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3536c75ac3d6643bae44188fec4dab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0aeda7bb18ec43b01e80e8a4401d9b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004847</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modules">
  <data key="d0">Modules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Modules encapsulate complex configurations or combinations of resources to make infrastructure deployments repeatable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layered Approach">
  <data key="d0">Layered Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A layered approach separates IaC pipelines into layers aligned with resource deployment lifecycles, from low-touch to high-touch.&lt;SEP&gt;A layered approach reflects different lifecycles by keeping foundational layers static while application layers change more frequently, using separate deployment pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998186</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security As Code">
  <data key="d0">Security As Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security as code ensures security is part of the deployment pipeline, including vulnerability scanning and configuration hardening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Orphaned Resources">
  <data key="d0">Orphaned Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Orphaned resources are resources no longer needed by a workload that IaC tools cannot automatically remove, requiring a standardized strategy to scan for and delete them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Promotion Stack">
  <data key="d0">Code Promotion Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code promotion stack is a set of environments used to promote code through stages, deployed using standardized IaC templates with abstract parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-248e5ba1455ebb0b8f84cdf668b13e6f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/infrastructure-as-code-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997786</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UAT">
  <data key="d0">UAT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">User Acceptance Testing requires comparing implementation with users' expectations and getting their approval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40e4a31ea43efb7a100f1df033cb0e46</data>
