</node>
<node id="Level 4 Maturity">
  <data key="d0">Level 4 Maturity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 4 maturity focuses on gaining operational efficiency by evaluating engineering assets and processes and aligning tools with organizational standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Level 5 Maturity">
  <data key="d0">Level 5 Maturity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 5 maturity represents future adaptability, focusing on operating workloads at scale, modernizing culture, processes, tools, and technology through continuous improvement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NuGet Packages">
  <data key="d0">NuGet Packages</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NuGet packages are software modules that may require a quarantine process managed by an organization's security team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997889</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Service Capabilities">
  <data key="d0">Self-Service Capabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-service capabilities enable various job functions within a workload to operate independently.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-service capabilities are scripted solutions that team members can invoke to handle repetitive unplanned tasks, enhancing agility and autonomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f888e8f4cb50fcce1b0c57a123318181</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rearchitecture">
  <data key="d0">Rearchitecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rearchitecture involves identifying opportunities to redesign systems based on observed growth, new usage patterns, and future potential.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997890</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Call Engineers">
  <data key="d0">On-Call Engineers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">On-call engineers are dedicated roles set up to handle support responsibilities, reducing the support load on developers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Scanning">
  <data key="d0">Security Scanning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Security scanning is applied to generated artifacts including dependency checks and infrastructure-as-code scanning for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Security scanning is a centralized process that organizations can provide instead of teams managing their own scanning implementations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc830fbd68e22812a74bf3c788ef10f4</data>
