</node>
<node id="Playbooks">
  <data key="d0">Playbooks</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Playbooks are troubleshooting resources used to train vendors on handling workload support tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997891</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Developer Environments">
  <data key="d0">Developer Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Developer environments are created for each feature or change as a Level 5 strategy to reduce friction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f8d7568e4aed8a2c3665910aa5492c2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997892</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment strategy defines how and when changes are deployed to production, ensuring service availability and minimizing downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring Stack">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The monitoring stack involves collecting logs and metrics from workload components to provide functional and operational insights.&lt;SEP&gt;A monitoring stack runs in parallel to the functional stack, collecting and analyzing metrics, logs, traces, and events to provide visibility into workload behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44db748d8a4a0feea6626c78c05321a2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/observability.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brownfield Workloads">
  <data key="d0">Brownfield Workloads</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Brownfield workloads are existing workloads into which automation is incorporated early in their life cycle to improve efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997893</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rollback">
  <data key="d0">Rollback</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rollback is a provision within a deployment system to restore the system to a functional state if errors occur during deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Rollback is a mitigation strategy that reverts updated systems to the last-known-good configuration state.&lt;SEP&gt;Rollback is a mitigation strategy that reverts to the last-known-good version, considered but rejected in the example due to complex data and schema operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea5e8233e721a917652b3958170e098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Summarization Agents">
  <data key="d0">Summarization Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Summarization agents use a simple Copilot-style architecture with straightforward retrieval and response generation for synthesizing content across documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Summarization agents use a Copilot-style architecture to read and condense information from documents, reports, logs, or conversations into concise summaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a81a26ddd3f3a3848c76ca543d5b996</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997894</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation Agents">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recommendation agents rely on reasoning-oriented models capable of analyzing multiple data sources with cross-source correlation.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation agents analyze multiple data sources to detect patterns and provide context-aware recommendations for operational decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a81a26ddd3f3a3848c76ca543d5b996</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artifact Generation Agents">
  <data key="d0">Artifact Generation Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Artifact generation agents assist in generating code, infrastructure definitions, and tests, with outputs that may become part of production workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Artifact generation agents convert written requirements into executable code, infrastructure definitions, and automated tests while adhering to defined standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a81a26ddd3f3a3848c76ca543d5b996</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Policy Validation Agents">
  <data key="d0">Policy Validation Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Policy validation agents review code, configurations, and workflows against policies, standards, and design documents to enforce compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;AI agents that assist in reviewing and validating assets against policies and standards, supporting decisions and flagging deviations while humans retain final oversight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc830fbd68e22812a74bf3c788ef10f4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action Optimization Agents">
  <data key="d0">Action Optimization Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action optimization agents use insights across artifacts to route work and take action on decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Agents that extend beyond analysis by taking direct operational actions, requiring careful design, oversight, and human-in-the-loop workflows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc830fbd68e22812a74bf3c788ef10f4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997896</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GenAI">
  <data key="d0">GenAI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GenAI refers to generative AI solutions, both off-the-shelf and custom-built, used to reduce manual toil and improve operational productivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative AI (GenAI) refers to AI solutions built with foundation models that depend on diverse, high-quality data and scalable data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-499b8edccfe967f6e95130c69a3964d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pull Requests">
  <data key="d0">Pull Requests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pull requests are part of the standard developer lifecycle for integrating generated artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc830fbd68e22812a74bf3c788ef10f4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776997896</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
