  <data key="d5">1776999381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Test Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A high-level blueprint that guides overall testing approach, defining objectives, scope, methodologies, tools, roles, and responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Plan">
  <data key="d0">Test Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A detailed document that guides testing execution for a specific release, outlining scope, test cases, timelines, and entry/exit criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layered Test Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Layered Test Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy of structuring tests in layers to provide rapid feedback, earlier defect detection, and faster releases.&lt;SEP&gt;A layered test coverage strategy provides rapid feedback, earlier defect detection, and faster releases by structuring tests in layers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OWASP ZAP">
  <data key="d0">OWASP ZAP</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing tool used for security testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Testing In Production">
  <data key="d0">Testing In Production</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controlled testing performed in production environments with safeguards that limit user exposure and reduce risk to gather real user feedback and performance data.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in production is necessary for AI workloads due to their nondeterministic nature to ensure expected performance over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d58b81465c40024b1e7d72578e9d17</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003847</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canary Releases">
  <data key="d0">Canary Releases</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A progressive exposure strategy that releases updates to a small targeted group of users first to uncover problems before broader rollout.&lt;SEP&gt;Canary releases are an advanced deployment pattern supported by Kubernetes and ingress controllers for release engineering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95f95636f4fc764df073f790408dc229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2789d17a06aaa84a6ce5fba59172ad</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-kubernetes-service.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001879</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Pyramid">
  <data key="d0">Test Pyramid</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The test pyramid model illustrates a layered approach for test automation, distributing tests across unit, integration, and end-to-end layers to maximize coverage while minimizing execution time and maintenance costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration Testing">
  <data key="d0">Integration Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Integration testing validates interactions between components, APIs, contracts, and shared services at medium cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Integration testing is a testing approach recommended for API-driven workloads alongside contract testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Integration testing ensures application components operate individually and can interact with each other as expected.&lt;SEP&gt;Integration testing should be prioritized when deploying updates to online inferencing endpoints to ensure they don't negatively affect other services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d58b81465c40024b1e7d72578e9d17</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003848</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End-To-End Testing">
  <data key="d0">End-To-End Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end testing is emphasized for customer-facing workloads along with UI testing.&lt;SEP&gt;End-to-end testing confirms full workflow correctness across the entire system, simulating real-world scenarios with high cost but highest confidence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Testing">
  <data key="d0">Manual Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual testing validates scenarios requiring human judgment, exploratory learning, usability, and UX nuances with high cost and low scalability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Load And Performance Testing">
  <data key="d0">Load And Performance Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Load and performance testing validates performance, latency, throughput, and scalability under expected workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Testing">
  <data key="d0">Security Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Security testing should be prioritized at the beginning of the release process to prevent vulnerabilities and ensure safer deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Security testing identifies vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, and attack vectors throughout the development lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Security testing involves detailed test plans for detecting unethical behavior, integrating AI components, and conducting penetration tests or red team exercises.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f1e74a0c11b25222056af287680862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9a0e9b061e029f4a866b91345d9e7b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure Testing">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure testing involves validating infrastructure code by observing application behavior through deploying software and running tests against it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbdf289020cfbf6bc9f18cea2c3f4bf8</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Framework">
  <data key="d0">Test Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A test framework is the structure within which tests are organized, executed, and monitored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Data">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthetic data simulates authentic user scenarios while avoiding the complexity of production data handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthetic data is used to supplement limited real samples and validate end-to-end processing in testing scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mock Services">
  <data key="d0">Mock Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mock services simulate production service behaviors to validate scenarios without risking live operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mock services accurately simulate production service behaviors to validate scenarios effectively without risking live operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c203348328e5589b8f4b6fa4101a78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ephemeral Environments">
  <data key="d0">Ephemeral Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ephemeral environments are on-demand test environments created for specific test purposes and destroyed after use to reduce costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephemeral environments are on-demand environments created for specific test purposes and destroyed after use, reducing infrastructure costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephemeral environments are temporary environments for development, testing, and staging that are created and deleted as needed to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c203348328e5589b8f4b6fa4101a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Test Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Test coverage measures the extent of automation validation across code paths and user scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5f9d8aded9b458939437b400ad44c9</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998074</data>
