<node id="Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design patterns are industry-proven application patterns used to ensure applications are reliable, performant, and secure.&lt;SEP&gt;Reusable solutions that help developers solve recurring design problems with efficient, maintainable, and scalable code.&lt;SEP&gt;Design patterns are reusable solutions for common software design problems, with resources like documentation, tutorials, and sample code available for learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f73ba7b617cf9dce0d1fe9a51c2649a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16aecaf278f5a9e57cc05404dd1ae26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1608d8f18c85af394b2bd50413fdfd0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/tools-processes.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-code-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Chain">
  <data key="d0">Supply Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Supply chain refers to the organizational pipeline design for deploying and managing workload lifecycles, relying on collaboration across teams.&lt;SEP&gt;In cloud workloads, a supply chain is a standardized suite of tools and processes used to affect infrastructure and application change across environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Promotion Chain">
  <data key="d0">Code Promotion Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code promotion chain refers to the sequence of workload environments through which changes are tested and promoted before reaching production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f021372b9d4a41efe0a14847b5724b0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acceptance Testing">
  <data key="d0">Acceptance Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acceptance testing evaluates system compliance with business requirements and determines readiness for delivery to end users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shift-Left Principle">
  <data key="d0">Shift-Left Principle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The shift-left principle advocates testing early in the software development lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-63b22c0a62281685eeaf37e83bc431f1</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998185</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Progressive-Exposure Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Progressive-Exposure Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Progressive-exposure (canary) deployment reduces risk by deploying changes to small, controlled groups in stages before broad release.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e01f488d95dc27e4fa0c309fcbf165fd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/operational-excellence/workload-supply-chain.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998186</data>
