</node>
<node id="Billing Increment">
  <data key="d0">Billing Increment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing increment is a usage amount that incurs a cost (meter), such as a unit of time, number of instances, or size of data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Billing Factor">
  <data key="d0">Billing Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing factor is the type of usage that incurs costs, such as time, storage amount, data transfer amount, or number of requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meter">
  <data key="d0">Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A meter is another term for billing increment, representing the unit by which resource usage is measured and charged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Runtime">
  <data key="d0">Runtime</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Runtime is a billing factor referring to the duration a resource actively runs, typically measured in hours, days, or months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Transfer">
  <data key="d0">Data Transfer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data transfer is a billing factor referring to the movement of data into and out of a resource.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual CPUs">
  <data key="d0">Virtual CPUs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual CPUs (vCPUs) are a billing factor based on the number of vCPUs allocated to resources such as virtual machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specialized Services">
  <data key="d0">Specialized Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Specialized services are a billing factor referring to services or features used with other resources, such as specialized databases or AI services, which may have separate pricing models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uptime Guarantees">
  <data key="d0">Uptime Guarantees</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Uptime guarantees are service-level agreements (SLAs) on availability and reliability that can coincide with higher costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8d68f0cdc97e70397b1ec00eda7f2e3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/align-usage-to-billing-increments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Pricing Calculator">
  <data key="d0">Azure Pricing Calculator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Pricing Calculator is an online tool provided by Microsoft for estimating and modeling the costs of Azure services before implementation. It allows users to select and configure Azure services, test different configurations, payment plans, and billing increments, and evaluate approximate hourly or monthly costs of workloads.

The tool supports cost modeling for a wide range of Azure services, including App Service tiers, API Management service tiers, ExpressRoute, Load Balancer, SQL Database, Service Fabric clusters, Azure Local, and data storage scenarios. For specific services, it can estimate costs across multiple dimensions such as compute, storage, networking, IP addresses, hubs, connections, and data transfer volumes, including ingress and egress across various configurations. Users can convert anticipated traffic usage into cost estimates, making it valuable for planning and budgeting Azure deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure pricing calculator is a tool for estimating Azure costs before deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76c4bb7431f02f35a05848683404dfc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80555797ec0044df18cccee521a04c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78af010626eadf0be8c939d900c80b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df87985019f98b613c9173ac606646be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca94eb8d1a3fa16fe190b0f6eecd280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7918938c3b3fb0cddcc9e93b114d4a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d57d3c8e9b437c3bf033faee9829a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8650a6bc1260a7fa43030a811f587363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d73a470d503be7e3a2f2ef63b96ec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-661923999882010b2c5bc9a8ccb33fff</data>
