<node id="Azure Hybrid Benefit">
  <data key="d0">Azure Hybrid Benefit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Hybrid Benefit is a licensing program offered by Microsoft that allows customers to use their existing on-premises software licenses when running resources in Azure, resulting in discounted cloud pricing. It applies to Windows Server, Linux VMs, SQL Server, Azure Local workloads, and containerized applications running on-premises or at the edge.

The program requires Software Assurance-enabled licenses in many scenarios, such as exchanging SQL Server licenses to save up to 30% on licensing costs in SQL Database. It supports both cloud-migrated workloads and new cloud systems, helping organizations reduce costs across mission-critical deployments, nonproduction environments, and various other scenarios. Azure Hybrid Benefit is recognized as a key cost optimization practice within the Azure ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16a408cdd425591d8dd93b51902b6a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80555797ec0044df18cccee521a04c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99334db9b3c4c908652c875ca2926b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74a4365f57d52439ea79753f3bb9374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4c20a753377d79a1b6e9a6ac4090a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0410a251086c78865c685a5005e7ecae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbffb4e1f51b21a7612a357a00679dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c957da7c0dc63ec3f07d3774c278b886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f05e5f46b39ac0c01364030a2aca2729</data>
