</node>
<node id="Rate Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Rate Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A collaborative process between development and purchasing teams to identify opportunities for cost optimization and make informed decisions on billing plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The practice of finding and securing the most cost-efficient pricing options for cloud and software resources without modifying architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e259f9d5ef6cf3be37487cfef56d05dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62f6828365a1e0ab74dfd86571a41a19</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/get-best-rates.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commitment-Based Billing">
  <data key="d0">Commitment-Based Billing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pricing model where users commit to a certain capacity over time in exchange for significant discounts, with charges incurred whether resources are used or not.&lt;SEP&gt;Commitment-based billing is a billing model that may offer discounts for consistent loads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62f6828365a1e0ab74dfd86571a41a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd009330fd8bb700e86760925fa4ea4b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/get-best-rates.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumption-Based Billing">
  <data key="d0">Consumption-Based Billing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A pricing model where users pay based on actual resource consumption, also known as pay-as-you-go.&lt;SEP&gt;Consumption-based billing is a billing model recommended as a starting point to understand incurred costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62f6828365a1e0ab74dfd86571a41a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd009330fd8bb700e86760925fa4ea4b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/get-best-rates.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/maturity-model.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
