<node id="SQL Server">
  <data key="d0">SQL Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Server is a database technology and platform widely used across various deployment scenarios. It can be deployed on virtual machines, including Azure VMware Solution private cloud guest VMs, and potentially migrated to PaaS solutions for cost savings. Its licensing costs can be reduced using Azure Hybrid Benefit on Azure Local.

SQL Server supports features such as column stores (suitable for vertical partitioning with static column data), always-on availability groups for synchronous or asynchronous replication, transparent data encryption, and Activity Monitor. Its table partitioning concept differs from general data partitioning approaches.

SQL Server can be deployed with Azure NetApp Files volumes as SMB shares to reduce TCO. It is supported by Azure Backup for database backups, including through the Backint connector for SAP applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64d440b1a3c317835e0dd6ef617a4d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103386df6f9acd0832fa49dd897fcede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc8280bb50c2a5f4a589617c1bed437&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453</data>
