<node id="Release Gates">
  <data key="d0">Release Gates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Release gates serve as spending guardrails by establishing cost-related criteria that must be met before deployment passes through CI/CD pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Release gates are checkpoints or conditions that must be met before a release or deployment can proceed, used to ensure cost-effectiveness and alignment with optimization goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Release gates are checkpoints or conditions in a release pipeline that must be satisfied before deployment can proceed, ensuring cost-effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a9274b98dae68e1fda563c0a186872af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
