<node id="Archive Tier">
  <data key="d0">Archive Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The archive tier is the lowest-cost storage tier for long-term data retention, typically one year.&lt;SEP&gt;A storage tier in Azure Backup for long-term retention backup data that is rarely accessed and stored for compliance needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Archive tier is a storage tier for Azure Backup that supports low-cost storage of infrequently accessed data.&lt;SEP&gt;Archive tier offers the lowest storage cost but requires rehydration to access data, which takes time and incurs additional costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-580ec71ae333662d0e2d0544eb12f556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6fe01d5e4f3c9a2a28525facf5534c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
