  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data access tiers are Azure storage blob tiers that help optimize storage costs based on data access frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6fe01d5e4f3c9a2a28525facf5534c3</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Lifecycle Policies">
  <data key="d0">Data Lifecycle Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data lifecycle policies specify when and how data should be moved between storage tiers based on predefined criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Data Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data segmentation involves strategically organizing data into distinct segments to efficiently allocate storage resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Data segmentation addresses workload-specific requirements such as security and regulatory constraints that may prevent exporting data across regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Data segmentation involves maintaining separate pipelines and access controls for data sources with distinct security requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Data segmentation is the practice of separating data based on workload-specific requirements such as security or data freshness rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188c7778d5d303d397f8ab1d39a109c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88dee01d0a30636bf4119d50523dfef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96152a32ed0c284eafe7250fb96edb70</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Deduplication">
  <data key="d0">Data Deduplication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data deduplication eliminates redundant data by storing only unique data blocks, using hashing algorithms and data chunk comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Data deduplication uses hashing algorithms and comparison of data chunks to identify and eliminate duplicate data to save costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lakeflow Connect Free Tier">
  <data key="d0">Lakeflow Connect Free Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lakeflow Connect Free Tier in Azure Databricks provides 100 free DBUs per workspace per day for SaaS and database ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Connect Free Tier provides 100 free Databricks Units per workspace per day for data ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Connect Free Tier provides 100 free Databricks Units per workspace per day for data ingestion from SaaS applications and databases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Unity Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Unity Catalog is a centralized metadata catalog and governance framework within Azure Databricks. It provides comprehensive data governance capabilities including fine-grained access controls, permission inheritance, and permission management across analytics workloads.

Unity Catalog supports data discovery, lineage tracking, and cross-region metadata synchronization, enabling organizations to capture data lineage and monitor external locations. It offers audit logging through system tables, allowing detailed usage pattern analysis and the creation of chargeback models.

Unity Catalog governs data ingested through Lakeflow Connect Free Tier and provides centralized governance across Azure Databricks workspaces, including security features for fault tolerance and data access tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caf8d0c8419c804f864143fd95c9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4aa034c37c80a21f6fbf6660a82591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Storage">
  <data key="d0">Cold Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cold storage is used for data that applications access infrequently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hot Tier">
  <data key="d0">Hot Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hot tier is a storage tier for frequently accessed data, with a typical retention period of 30 days before moving to cooler tiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cool Tier">
  <data key="d0">Cool Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The cool tier is a mid-level storage tier with a typical retention period of 90 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Retention Policies">
  <data key="d0">Data Retention Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data retention policies ensure compliance with legal, regulatory, and business requirements by specifying how long data is kept.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2d4c7fc5a3047895102fdfbc0cc7e78</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Avro">
  <data key="d0">Avro</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Avro is a file format suited for write-heavy I/O patterns, with efficient serialization and deserialization, compatible with message buses like Kafka.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parquet">
  <data key="d0">Parquet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parquet is a columnar storage file format that excels in read-heavy I/O patterns and column-focused queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Parquet is an efficient columnar file format native to Databricks that leads to faster read times and lower data costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Parquet is a columnar data format that reduces storage and speeds up reads.&lt;SEP&gt;Parquet is a columnar file format used for analytical workloads with compression options like zstd and Snappy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000953</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ORC">
  <data key="d0">ORC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimized Row Columnar (ORC) is a columnar storage file format that excels in read-heavy I/O patterns and column-focused queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kafka">
  <data key="d0">Kafka</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Kafka is a message bus that produces a series of events and messages in quick succession.&lt;SEP&gt;Kafka is a streaming platform whose topic length can be used as a scaler by KEDA for event-based scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Kafka is a protocol compatible with Azure Event Hubs for streaming scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db510f47656045373bcac562ba7e53ca</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backup Compression">
  <data key="d0">Backup Compression</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Backup compression reduces the size of backup files during the backup process to save storage costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backup Storage Tiers">
  <data key="d0">Backup Storage Tiers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Backup storage tiers involve moving older backups to lower-cost storage options such as cold storage or archive storage to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f42998a4e0c9bc3045bdc13dd319dd6a</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998690</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Lifecycle Management">
  <data key="d0">Data Lifecycle Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data lifecycle management is the process of managing data from creation to deletion, including organizing, storing, protecting, and archiving based on value and usage patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Data lifecycle management (DLM) controls data growth from creation to deletion, including automated removal of intermediate copies and regulatory retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Data lifecycle management (DLM) involves policies for managing data through its lifecycle including tiering and retention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f675dff830aa38bf7b60ffd30f2363d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Prioritization">
  <data key="d0">Data Prioritization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data prioritization is the process of categorizing and assigning importance levels to data based on sensitivity and criticality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f675dff830aa38bf7b60ffd30f2363d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998690</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retention Policy">
  <data key="d0">Retention Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A retention policy specifies the duration for which data should be retained to meet legal, regulatory, or business requirements before deletion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f675dff830aa38bf7b60ffd30f2363d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Data Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data redundancy is the practice of storing duplicate copies of data across multiple storage systems to improve availability and fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f675dff830aa38bf7b60ffd30f2363d</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-data-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preproduction Environment">
  <data key="d0">Preproduction Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preproduction environments should emulate production environments with strategic tradeoffs for cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Preproduction environments are environments used before production for testing and validation, with recommendations for cost optimization and balancing similarity with production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal And Vertical Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal And Vertical Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Horizontal and vertical scaling are strategies for scaling resources efficiently to meet demand without over-provisioning in production environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c5fc827ca305a978ff51b6d10e1dd732</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998730</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU Emulation">
  <data key="d0">GPU Emulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GPU emulation is a cost-saving approach for preproduction tasks that don't require real GPU processing power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0410a251086c78865c685a5005e7ecae</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998731</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endpoint Emulation">
  <data key="d0">Endpoint Emulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Endpoint emulation uses mock endpoints to simulate responses of costly components without invoking them, helping optimize preproduction costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sampled Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Sampled Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sampled scaling selectively scales vital components rather than scaling all components to maximum capacity, balancing cost-effectiveness with risk minimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbad66d8b687b8c159df0a6efcb8ad93</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold DR Environment">
  <data key="d0">Cold DR Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cold DR environment has little or no infrastructure or running services, using infrastructure as code to deploy during disruptive events. Cost-effective but may have long recovery times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hot DR Environment">
  <data key="d0">Hot DR Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A hot DR environment runs all infrastructure and services, mirroring data in real time for near-instantaneous failover and minimal data loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm DR Environment">
  <data key="d0">Warm DR Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A warm DR environment is partially active and periodically syncs with the primary site, offering a middle ground between cold and hot approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preproduction Environments">
  <data key="d0">Preproduction Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preproduction environments include development, testing, and staging areas that simulate production while reducing unnecessary costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Environments that should closely mirror production environments to enable better testing and validation before deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ff8d586800116f4a9c0f2e6c0039f7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Assurance Environment">
  <data key="d0">Quality Assurance Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An environment dedicated to testing to identify and fix bugs before deploying to production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Environment">
  <data key="d0">Security Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An environment for security testing to ensure applications are secure against threats and vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Acceptance Testing Environment">
  <data key="d0">User Acceptance Testing Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An environment where end users and stakeholders test an application to validate functionality and requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Governance">
  <data key="d0">Governance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Governance involves limiting deployment options in preproduction environments to control expenses and mitigate risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Robust governance involves standardization to reduce errors and rework, ensuring consistent quality and cost optimization through automated compliance checks.&lt;SEP&gt;A design area focused on managing and regulating cloud service usage to establish a secure Azure environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A design area for managing and regulating cloud service usage to establish a secure Azure environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Governance is the set of controls, practices, and tools used to organize, control, and regulate cloud service usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83d5dd3a4439658c5b437672b1fb0375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb32778b5a44a1a37ca0f92518c49c6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a0beb0360defdd62600690749d5e142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c62ba342ae2202ab7183c0dd367378f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad653e4d2f68d336a1fa1654643a4bb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-environment-costs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-personnel-time.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/governance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Inventory">
  <data key="d0">Flow Inventory</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A flow inventory is a comprehensive list of all sequences of actions, data transitions, and system interactions within a workload, used as the first step to align investments with flow priority.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9c98557d8b38582c1462aa9d0fd3e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flow Prioritization">
  <data key="d0">Flow Prioritization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow prioritization is the process of classifying flows based on their influence on business outcomes, user experience implications, and resource consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9c98557d8b38582c1462aa9d0fd3e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-flow-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decouple">
  <data key="d0">Decouple</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Decoupling is the strategy of removing a flow from a shared resource and placing it into a separate resource.</data>
