  <data key="d2">Event-driven autoscaling dynamically adjusts resources based on specific events or triggers rather than traditional metrics like CPU or memory utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998880</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cooldown Period">
  <data key="d0">Cooldown Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cooldown period introduces a delay between scaling events to prevent excessive scaling activities triggered by temporary load spikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998881</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content Offloading">
  <data key="d0">Content Offloading</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Content offloading transfers content to external services or platforms to reduce workload on primary infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Content offloading is a strategy to offload content to external services or platforms to reduce workload on primary infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998881</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Priority Queues">
  <data key="d0">Priority Queues</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Priority queues are used to reduce demand by ordering requests based on priority to manage resource consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-066af31d500f1a0a71053da1bd80b73e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998882</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Supply">
  <data key="d0">Control Supply</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Control supply is a strategy of defining an upper limit on spending for a resource or service to control costs and ensure expenses don't exceed a certain level.&lt;SEP&gt;Control supply defines upper limits on spending for resources or services to ensure expenses stay within budget.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998882</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure HPC Cache">
  <data key="d0">Azure HPC Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure HPC Cache is a caching service provided by Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure HPC Cache is an Azure service for high-performance caching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9c864d1abe92319ff199943a677dc7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eb4bf3421da46d9aac57d5ba0a0c195</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998883</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Offloading">
  <data key="d0">Database Offloading</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Database offloading reduces load on the main application server by offloading database operations to separate servers or specialized services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998883</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cache Aside">
  <data key="d0">Cache Aside</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cache aside pattern checks the cache for data before querying the persistent data store, reducing demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998883</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reducing Demand">
  <data key="d0">Reducing Demand</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reducing demand implements strategies to minimize resource utilization and avoid overprovisioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-563595f22347b72716cb226e6b3627c4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Up">
  <data key="d0">Scale Up</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale up is a vertical scaling strategy that shifts to a higher SKU to provide more resources to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale In">
  <data key="d0">Scale In</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale in is a horizontal scaling strategy that removes instances to provide less resources to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Down">
  <data key="d0">Scale Down</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale down is a vertical scaling strategy that shifts to a lower SKU to provide less resources to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Usage Data">
  <data key="d0">Usage Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Usage data is either direct or indirect information about how much a task, service, or application is being used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Cost Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost metrics are numeric data related to workload cost, such as cost per hour, cost per transaction, or cost per unit of resource usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a2a48b425bd11c45a9970a1c6d7737</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/optimize-scaling-costs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998888</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Anomaly Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Cost Anomaly Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost anomaly alerts notify about unexpected cost variations that might indicate inefficiencies or abnormal spending patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998945</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commitment-Based Plan Utilization Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Commitment-Based Plan Utilization Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerts that monitor commitment-based plan usage to maximize the value of commitments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9780793a52d779d72d7dfc08b3276f92</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
