<node id="Spending Guardrails">
  <data key="d0">Spending Guardrails</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Spending guardrails are measures to control and manage costs within a specified budget, including release gates, governance policies, resource limits, and access controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Governance Policies">
  <data key="d0">Governance Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Governance policies are rules that enforce compliance and enable auditing of workload resources, acting as spending guardrails on resource types, configurations, tags, location, and data management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Limits">
  <data key="d0">Resource Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource limits are controls on the number, size, and duration of resources that can be provisioned to prevent excessive spending and optimize utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d57924d25d627fa240cecd66ef26712</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/cost-optimization/set-spending-guardrails.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776998952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Durable Functions">
  <data key="d0">Azure Durable Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Durable Functions enables orchestrating complex workflows and long-running stateful processes in a serverless environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Durable Functions orchestrate complex workflows and long-running processes with stateful workflows in a serverless environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464884618643684fc043c8a50e0bf16f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumption Plan">
  <data key="d0">Consumption Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The consumption plan is an Azure Functions hosting option suitable for short-duration background tasks triggered by events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumption plan is ideal for unpredictable workloads, charging only for operation time and resources consumed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consumption plan is a fully managed hosting plan for Azure Functions that doesn't support access to the associated App Service instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a75f6abfb52e7f12669ccabfaf886c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-functions.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Plan">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The dedicated plan is an Azure Functions hosting option suitable when workloads already run on dedicated infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dedicated (App Service) plan is an Azure Functions pricing plan suitable for predictable workloads with steady usage patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d47e196697e1f71a7cc7ba2d19f43</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-functions.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Windows Task Scheduler">
  <data key="d0">Windows Task Scheduler</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Windows Task Scheduler is used to run scripts and tasks on a schedule within Windows operating systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999044</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Server Agent">
  <data key="d0">SQL Server Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Server Agent runs scripts and tasks when SQL Server is installed on a VM.&lt;SEP&gt;SQL Server Agent is an instance-scoped feature supported by Azure SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002773</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Resource Manager Cmdlets">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Manager Cmdlets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Resource Manager cmdlets are used to monitor VM status and manage virtual machines running background tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Center Management Pack For Azure">
  <data key="d0">System Center Management Pack For Azure</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">System Center Management Pack for Azure collects data from instrumentation in tasks and the operating system in VMs.&lt;SEP&gt;A management pack that collects data from instrumentation and the operating system in VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7bf06da147fe51859af7fc046f4ec860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7424eb960d7c722faf499211634269a1</data>
