  <data key="d5">1776999210</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poison Message">
  <data key="d0">Poison Message</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Message that repeatedly causes processing failures, potentially blocking the queue and preventing processing of other messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WebJob">
  <data key="d0">WebJob</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure App Service feature that supports running scripts or programs as background tasks within the context of a web app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gatekeeper Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Gatekeeper Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gatekeeper is a pattern used to isolate background compute instances from the UI for security.&lt;SEP&gt;Pattern used to transfer sensitive data to an isolated background process that has access to protected storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0f7011b209ee2d53115a29ddfa186f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event-Driven Trigger">
  <data key="d0">Event-Driven Trigger</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigger mechanism where an event, typically a user action or workflow step, initiates a background task.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Schedule-Driven Trigger">
  <data key="d0">Schedule-Driven Trigger</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigger mechanism where a timer-based schedule invokes a background task on a recurring basis or for a single run.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web-Queue-Worker">
  <data key="d0">Web-Queue-Worker</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Architectural style where the UI or a job places a message in a queue that a background job monitors to detect and process new messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999050</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Message-Based Communication">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Message-Based Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Communication pattern where a background job monitors a queue, detects new messages, and uses message data as input for processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c3ed9c705aa5674f170118b9caf9fbf</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/background-jobs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999050</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
