  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Review">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Well-Architected Review is a self-assessment tool that helps workload teams examine a workload from the perspective of the Azure Well-Architected Framework, consisting of approximately 60 questions.&lt;SEP&gt;An assessment process for receiving, prioritizing, and integrating recommendations for continuous workload improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Well-Architected Review is an assessment tool for identifying and prioritizing opportunities to improve workload posture.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Azure Well-Architected Review is a free assessment tool consisting of questionnaires tied to pillar checklists to evaluate design choices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Well-Architected Review is an assessment tool that evaluates SAP workload reliability and provides specific recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a5d862a78e37f61b1525f212796615f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5505883d3947b5183a0241244e460f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d14511d72d14b9bf6ec7b7f61c0bc5c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/implementing-recommendations.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/pillars.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/what-is-well-architected-framework.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DevOps Tooling For Well-Architected Recommendation Process">
  <data key="d0">DevOps Tooling For Well-Architected Recommendation Process</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">DevOps Tooling for Well-Architected Recommendation Process provides example scripts for automating backlog integration of recommendations from the Well-Architected Review CSV into Azure DevOps or GitHub.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/implementing-recommendations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Learn">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Learn</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Learn is a platform whose profiles are tied to Well-Architected Review assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/implementing-recommendations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brownfield Workload">
  <data key="d0">Brownfield Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A brownfield workload is an existing workload that is already deployed and operational, requiring assessment as part of continuous improvement efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/implementing-recommendations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greenfield Workload">
  <data key="d0">Greenfield Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A greenfield workload is a new workload in the initial design phase, where assessment helps establish a baseline and guide design decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ae74d8c186fbc9d0dd83b114ed0e8e5</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/implementing-recommendations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fallback">
  <data key="d0">Fallback</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fallback is a mitigation strategy that removes updated systems from production traffic routing and directs all traffic to the stable stack.&lt;SEP&gt;Fallback is a mitigation strategy that redirects traffic to a stable environment rather than rolling back changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency deployment (hot fix) deploys a fix during rollout to address problems quickly while following safe deployment practices with accelerated timelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RCA Report">
  <data key="d0">RCA Report</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The RCA report is generated after incident resolution within SLA timeframe, documenting the root cause analysis findings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triage Team">
  <data key="d0">Triage Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The triage (bridge) team is assembled by the incident recipient with the right members to coordinate communication, progress tracking, and access to incident assets.&lt;SEP&gt;The triage team is responsible for investigating incidents and assessing impact, relying on documented architectural layouts and component-level details.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd8f7b0b2f8f309054b1fccac7b1fa</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Containment Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Containment Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Containment strategies isolate affected components and limit the blast radius of an incident, including blocking access, limiting reach, and maintaining degraded functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87618a32c6b3af420a6fe25de69e11bb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incident">
  <data key="d0">Incident</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An unplanned event that disrupts, degrades, or threatens to disrupt the normal operation of a system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Break-Glass Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Break-Glass Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency credentials with elevated privileges used during critical incidents, strictly controlled with clear usage guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergency credentials with clear rules on who can use them, when, and how, paired with emergency drills and tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Severity Level">
  <data key="d0">Severity Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A classification system (critical, high, medium, low) that determines the appropriate response level based on business impact and affected users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incident Response Manager">
  <data key="d0">Incident Response Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A role that owns the incident from detection through resolution and RCA, ensures processes are followed, decisions are made, and the right people are informed. Also designated as the authority to close an incident.&lt;SEP&gt;A role that owns the incident from detection through resolution and RCA, ensuring processes are followed and decisions are made.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrospective Leader">
  <data key="d0">Retrospective Leader</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A role that leads post-incident reviews, captures lessons learned, produces actionable reports, and ensures findings are applied.&lt;SEP&gt;A role that leads post-incident reviews, captures lessons learned, and produces actionable reports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last-Known-Good">
  <data key="d0">Last-Known-Good</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The last healthy state of the workload before an incident began, used as a reference point for rollback operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76e082c22642a698e3564a262d80083</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canary Rollout">
  <data key="d0">Canary Rollout</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Canary rollout is a deployment strategy where changes are gradually rolled out to subsets of users to detect problems early.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Failure Response">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Failure Response</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An example scenario describing how a workload team detects, mitigates, and resolves a deployment-related incident involving a search enhancement feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Incident Readiness Training">
  <data key="d0">Azure Incident Readiness Training</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure-related incident readiness training provided by Microsoft covering introduction to incident readiness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Flag">
  <data key="d0">Feature Flag</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature flag is a technique used to bypass problematic functions as a mitigation strategy during deployment incidents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Search Enhancement Feature">
  <data key="d0">Search Enhancement Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The search enhancement feature includes a new search API endpoint, updated database schema, redesigned UI search widget, and new caching logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03dd22646fb9b82dbaadbb44aa74a190</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Call Engineer">
  <data key="d0">On-Call Engineer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A role that actively mitigates and resolves incidents, follows responsibilities for different incident types, and collaborates with specialized teams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IcM Tool">
  <data key="d0">IcM Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An incident management tool that tracks progress, maintains accountability, centralizes activities for live site management and on-call rotations with a four-step workflow: create, acknowledge, mitigate, and resolve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineering Bridge">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Bridge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A triage team mobilized during incidents to evaluate impact and severity, consisting of the right members with agreed communication and progress tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da6af83acc232eee3f313065fe9b7723</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Monitor Agent">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor Agent is installed on VMs to pull local logs and deliver them to Azure Monitor, Microsoft Sentinel, and Microsoft Defender for Cloud.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor Agent is a software agent installed on VMs that pulls local logs and delivers them to Azure Monitor, Microsoft Sentinel, and Microsoft Defender for Cloud.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor Agent is used to onboard VMs to AVD Insights for monitoring VM health.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor Agent is used to ingest log data from compute resources, replacing the legacy Log Analytics agent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-520b008ac150d01d52152b172f0a59b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-776c12fee2375faef068c91c8f0e42d7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Hub">
  <data key="d0">Event Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Hub is recommended for SIEM or security integration use cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry Data Lifecycle Management">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry Data Lifecycle Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of managing retention policies for telemetry data, including short-term retention for raw debugging data and long-term storage for performance metrics and auditing records.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correlation">
  <data key="d0">Correlation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correlation is the process of linking telemetry data from multiple system layers to understand what is happening across the entire application environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aggregation">
  <data key="d0">Aggregation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of combining and consolidating telemetry data from multiple sources to create meaningful insights and reduce storage footprint.&lt;SEP&gt;Aggregation involves combining data from multiple sources, such as events with the same activity or transaction ID, removing duplicates, and filtering irrelevant data.&lt;SEP&gt;Aggregation is the process of combining data from multiple sources, removing duplicates, and filtering out irrelevant data to prepare for analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry Data Security">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry Data Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Telemetry data security involves protecting operational data against accidental deletion, controlling access with RBAC, enabling soft delete, applying resource locks, and encrypting sensitive data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999379</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Queue">
  <data key="d0">Message Queue</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A message queue provides at-least-once delivery semantics for telemetry data, ensuring data is not lost and allowing ingestion and storage to scale independently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Settings">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic settings must be enabled for each resource to route platform logs to a storage solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic settings are configurations for collecting only essential operational data from resource data sources, reducing costs by eliminating unnecessary data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0bd917d676e447b692a55c949aee0e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mindful practice of collecting and analyzing telemetry to understand system health and behavior, making the state of a system observable through measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;A design area for gaining insights into application behavior through resource utilization, health, availability, and capacity monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd2f8bec9d3a589a0de1d0f5ecb5745</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hot Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Hot Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis that processes telemetry immediately after generation for rapid detection and response.&lt;SEP&gt;Hot analysis processes telemetry immediately after it is generated for rapid detection and response in time-sensitive scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Warm Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis that occurs after telemetry is collected and lightly aggregated, correlating multiple telemetry sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm analysis occurs after telemetry is collected and lightly aggregated, involving correlation of multiple telemetry sources for near-real-time investigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Cold Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis working with large volumes of historical telemetry data on a scheduled or ad-hoc basis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold analysis works with large volumes of historical telemetry data on a scheduled or ad-hoc basis to identify long-term trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Activity ID">
  <data key="d0">Activity ID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A unique identifier assigned to each request and propagated across services to enable correlation of related telemetry data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-564e02afbba673b81e1950dcf16d845f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visualization">
  <data key="d0">Visualization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visualization converts complex telemetry into actionable insights using dashboards, charts, and reports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry Data">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Telemetry data includes logs, metrics, and traces that provide snapshots of activity across system layers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbdaa68e6dc2f42f64d0e7f513238530</data>
