<node id="Flow Design">
  <data key="d0">Flow Design</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow design is the process of designing a flow to meet technical targets, following best practices such as being scoped, logical, maintainable, defined, reliable, scalable, secure, efficient, and user-centric.&lt;SEP&gt;A three-step process for optimizing workloads through structured flow design aligned with business processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef06ef7197a8a530ba87de793b6cb9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a4bbe30fb21c1755cbcd0ff8a3c9e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/design-guides/optimize-workload-using-flows.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Use Case">
  <data key="d0">Use Case</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A use case defines the purpose, criticality, consumers, events, execution, and dependencies that guide functional design and set goals for flow design.&lt;SEP&gt;Defines the functional requirements of a flow, supporting one stage in a business process with attributes like purpose, criticality, and consumers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef06ef7197a8a530ba87de793b6cb9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f62c9cb7be167228d33fac3b26a501c</data>
