<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Desktop (AVD) is a cloud-based desktop and application virtualization service that runs on Microsoft Azure, providing a managed Microsoft control plane for virtual desktop infrastructure. It enables organizations to deploy, manage, and maintain virtual desktop workloads, giving users access to their desktops and applications from anywhere, on any device. AVD supports Windows 10/11 Enterprise multi-session remote desktops and offers features like pooled resources, personal desktops, autoscaling, and hybrid environments. It serves as a cost-effective modernization path for Remote Desktop Services by migrating end-user desktops to the cloud.

AVD manages session hosts, host pools, and application groups, with operators using scaling plans and load balancing algorithms to manage workloads. It operates within Azure capacity limits under a shared responsibility model between Microsoft and customers, requiring collaboration between platform and workload teams. The service encompasses performance, operational, and security considerations, including access control, diagnostics, and security monitoring capabilities. Its components require version compliance and regular updates.

For security, AVD uses TLS 1.2 for secure connections and supports hybrid identities, cloud-only identities, and various security configurations. It leverages FSLogix for user profile management and App Attach for application delivery to session hosts. AVD provides comprehensive networking guidance covering traffic optimization, network security, segmentation, multi-region connectivity, and hybrid networking, requiring real-time, low-latency network connectivity for a seamless user experience. It can be deployed on Azure Local and serves as an alternative to traditional VMs in policy-restricted environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e0bea5b8f0e427ffb4c77402adb2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-973e5b950ce99287babd4d9e8e310ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988833b417b706271b5f65bb2ca513c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113f1dee9dacbd713204570906b3c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec86357472a346e4f83fb7543b0e24c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0aeda7bb18ec43b01e80e8a4401d9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-291c7f730b8dea7d3fc0379e8208d526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5158a76c261c507648b548ec947486da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db16efb77d945a638ed3a142b84cba38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eb78b84d41322da30efb8dd70aafc73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37837339dd05d2a9f58b6dc734ebd967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9c715c42ddea999c4f406ee448b176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161fa262de0d263c9842f3ec1f7a7795&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb02bc2525ef384d46a37259cf6a9cf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b00f2a93a89bf2a6f52f33a9c1e0f13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0766d4ac6781acc119de13f144078bfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76733dbb26e72d185a328617ee81949b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dace10a501d3c2b544e137b224cd683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785fcaaef274ecc977b30c815a92374a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd</data>
