<node id="GenAIOps">
  <data key="d0">GenAIOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GenAIOps, or Generative Artificial Intelligence Operations, is a methodology and set of operational practices focused on the lifecycle management of generative AI solutions. It is considered a specialized subset of MLOps that extends beyond traditional machine learning operations to address the unique requirements of generative AI workloads.

GenAIOps encompasses practices for discovering, evaluating, integrating, and deploying generative AI models. Key activities include selecting the right model, prompt engineering, prompt iteration, fine-tuning pretrained models with enriched data, and incorporating domain-specific knowledge through techniques such as Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). These practices are integrated into broader DevOps and CI/CD processes.

GenAIOps also serves as a maturity framework, particularly within Azure Machine Learning, where maturity levels progress from basic model usage to structured deployment leveraging automated optimization techniques. It is relevant to SaaS businesses and organizations implementing generative AI strategies at scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20168b92f579ebd286ed6e8413a80537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d7c0f28c3ae2bf90186c890ee840779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f800b00991f43e7769f067d21a566bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140bb45f92c520fcbeae833dad674c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c563cf6a8147f2a681fea0529461445c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f0843affc0f5b75863b4bcdf11cf5f</data>
