<node id="Azure Disk Storage">
  <data key="d0">Azure Disk Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Disk Storage is a Microsoft Azure managed disk service that provides block-level storage volumes for use with Azure Virtual Machines. It encompasses multiple disk types across various performance tiers, including Premium SSD, Ultra Disk Storage, Standard SSD, and Standard HDD, with design trade-offs between performance and cost.

The service offers security, reliability, and encryption capabilities, along with various billing models. Azure Disk Storage is a crucial dependency for VM-based architectures and is covered in separate best practices guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab2911837499c055b346ca8d6a1cac17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e6162eae6d61a639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
