<node id="Responsible AI">
  <data key="d0">Responsible AI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Responsible AI is a comprehensive framework and set of principles aimed at ensuring the ethical, fair, transparent, and inclusive design, deployment, and use of AI systems. It serves as both a primary design driver and a referenced resource, addressing safety measures and controls alongside traditional application security considerations.

Responsible AI provides guidance for the responsible deployment of AI systems, including safeguards for agentic AI, content safety, and broader ethical considerations. It focuses on preventing manipulation, content toxicity, intellectual property infringement, and fabricated responses, while also addressing the ethical implications of handling sensitive data in AI training.

As a design area related to security principles, Responsible AI emphasizes user experience and the ethical implications of releasing AI solutions to the public. Its principles guide organizations to align AI usage with brand values and industry standards, ensuring that AI algorithms operate safely and avoid unintended harm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcbc73fa5b3fca3e1f52909f50221d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9a0e9b061e029f4a866b91345d9e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0144ba584fc445d0829602eb838085c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09c7d548eca9b203ee2a91331881fe03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96152a32ed0c284eafe7250fb96edb70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f0843affc0f5b75863b4bcdf11cf5f</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/responsible-ai.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/ai-strategy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Local is a Microsoft hybrid cloud platform that extends Azure to customer-owned infrastructure using Azure Arc, enabling modern and traditional applications to run consistently across distributed, edge, or on-premises locations. It provides high availability at the platform level with storage, compute, and network infrastructure supporting virtualized and containerized workload deployments, including VMs, Kubernetes clusters, and AKS integration.

Azure Local is a secure-by-default product with more than 300 security settings, incorporating identity controls, network filtering, BitLocker encryption, Application Control, SMB signing, Storage Spaces Direct, and drift protection controls. It is integrated with Azure services for monitoring, updating, and management, with guidance updated to reflect version 2311 covering security, monitoring, and licensing topics.

Azure Local is licensed on a per physical CPU core basis and supports hybrid cloud scenarios across diverse deployment models.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Local is a preview service that allows running Azure Virtual Desktop session hosts on-premises for hybrid environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0766d4ac6781acc119de13f144078bfb</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sustainable AI Design">
  <data key="d0">Sustainable AI Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New article providing guidance on building AI workloads sustainably by reducing energy consumption and carbon footprint on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable AI Design is a guide covering considerations and recommendations for designing sustainable AI workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable AI design incorporates environmental considerations into AI workload design to reduce energy consumption and carbon footprint.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4da5805c6af946f494849c13b188fd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5dafaf64829c3146ac17935b49a986e</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainable-ai-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005825</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grounding Data Design">
  <data key="d0">Grounding Data Design</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guidance on grounding data for AI workloads covering vector indexes, multi-media embeddings, and agentic solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Grounding Data Design is a referenced article describing principles of good data pipeline design for AI workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Grounding data design covers strategies to optimize searchability and retrieval for grounding data.&lt;SEP&gt;A design area document focused on grounding data design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c445903885a1763cd6ad5557106d024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0144ba584fc445d0829602eb838085c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c727fd4aca5ba57377185d29c2a3ab2b</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/whats-new.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform Teams">
  <data key="d0">Platform Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Platform teams host components or services that are too expensive for individual workload teams, dividing costs across workloads and providing self-service options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Teams">
  <data key="d0">Workload Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workload teams are individual teams responsible for specific workloads that partner with platform teams and share responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription-Vending Process">
  <data key="d0">Subscription-Vending Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A formal process through which platform teams offer subscriptions to workload teams as a self-service option.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-830fe53dca8ce291e75061d94230f1bd</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Teams">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Teams that provide support functions and governance for cloud workloads within an organization, focusing on organizational success.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776999987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Responsibility Model">
  <data key="d0">Shared Responsibility Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A model describing the division of responsibilities between workload teams and organizations for designing, implementing, and deploying workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The shared responsibility model defines responsibilities among cloud provider, customers, and the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;The shared responsibility model defines which Azure Virtual Desktop components Microsoft manages versus which the customer manages.&lt;SEP&gt;The shared responsibility model defines that organizations manage and operate workloads while Microsoft manages the physical and virtual infrastructure of Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A security model where Microsoft Azure and VMware share responsibility for certain security aspects of Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;The shared responsibility model for sustainability states that reducing emissions is a joint effort between the cloud provider and the customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06d07c7fd7e0ea2028615959913f9c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cb40dd3fd0df00b3000976f92afb432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161fa262de0d263c9842f3ec1f7a7795&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dad7224099dfb6b89e8724b6cc6f968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8b47369e36bfe734725b284a7694f4</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Landing Zone">
  <data key="d0">Application Landing Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An application landing zone is a collection of dedicated subscriptions to match the needs of a workload's resource organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Application landing zones are separate subscriptions intended for workload owners to deploy their VMware workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform Landing Zone">
  <data key="d0">Platform Landing Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Platform landing zones are a type of Azure landing zone available for standardization.&lt;SEP&gt;Platform landing zones are subscriptions owned by central teams providing foundational services like domain resolution, network connectivity, and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005270</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Operating Model">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Operating Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cloud operating model defines how an organization governs and operates its cloud platform and workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Common cloud operating models include decentralized, centralized, enterprise, and distributed, differing in level of ownership and governance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17e137434baf52b7c6f746bc411962c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198</data>
  <data key="d4">well-architected/workloads.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
