</node>
<node id="Staging Slot">
  <data key="d0">Staging Slot</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A staging slot is a pre-production environment in App Service used to validate app changes before swapping with the production slot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8b1c021188faeb6dd44f9550bc2c4fd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium V3">
  <data key="d0">Premium V3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium v3 is an App Service plan tier providing advanced scaling features and redundancy for production workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium v3 is an App Service pricing tier providing larger SKUs with increased memory, CPU capacity, more instances, and zone redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90796296cec0f129315921be106646d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Heal">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Heal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-heal is an App Service feature that automatically restarts applications based on defined conditions to resolve unexpected behaviors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IPv6">
  <data key="d0">IPv6</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IPv6 is a network protocol supported by App Service for inbound connectivity, which can overcome IPv4 address exhaustion issues.&lt;SEP&gt;IPv6 is recommended for environments with limited private IP address (RFC 1918) availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003343</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IPv4">
  <data key="d0">IPv4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IPv4 is a network protocol supported by App Service for inbound and outbound connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-369fa461119956df38997654d134395c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium V3 Tier">
  <data key="d0">Premium V3 Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium v3 tier is a high-capability App Service tier that supports Azure reservations and savings plans for dedicated compute.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e85416f9f4269be56820f2abc15bfb29</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium V3 App Service Plan">
  <data key="d0">Premium V3 App Service Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Premium v3 App Service plan provides advanced scaling features and ensures redundancy if failures occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARR Affinity">
  <data key="d0">ARR Affinity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Request Routing affinity creates sticky sessions that redirect users to the node that handled their previous requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Healing Rules">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Healing Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic healing rules trigger healing actions when thresholds like request count, slow requests, or memory limits are breached, enabling automatic proactive maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Check Feature">
  <data key="d0">Health Check Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The health check feature detects problems early and enables the load balancer to route traffic away from unhealthy instances to healthy nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Always On">
  <data key="d0">Always On</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Always On setting ensures that continuous and triggered WebJobs run reliably by preventing web apps from timing out after HTTP inactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Always On is an App Service setting that prevents applications from being automatically unloaded when idle, avoiding cold starts and request time-outs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90796296cec0f129315921be106646d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000130</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Service Environment">
  <data key="d0">App Service Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">App Service Environment is an Azure offering referenced occasionally to clarify features of core App Service offerings.&lt;SEP&gt;App Service Environment is a tier that provides a high degree of isolation with dedicated compute and networking.&lt;SEP&gt;App Service Environment provides better control over security and data protection through isolation, allowing independent scaling and limiting blast radius of breaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e035fd4bdb926eb43402af9b5f4b298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48af37296dffdbb0c217dfd4ed7f1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568f4a02582f7c3e1a2aba678f415b7c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000131</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Layer Security">
  <data key="d0">Transport Layer Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transport Layer Security (TLS) is an encryption protocol used for securing data in transit, with TLS 1.2 or higher recommended.&lt;SEP&gt;TLS is a protocol for secure data transmission, with clients required to use the latest version.&lt;SEP&gt;TLS is an encryption protocol for in-transit data protection, with TLS 1.2 enforced by default and TLS 1.3 supported on MySQL 8.0+.&lt;SEP&gt;TLS 1.2 is the minimum required version for all Event Grid communications including publishing and consuming events.&lt;SEP&gt;Transport Layer Security (TLS) is a protocol ensuring encrypted data exchanges between browsers, Azure Front Door, and origins.&lt;SEP&gt;TLS termination is a feature provided by Azure Front Door for secure communication handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.2 is the encryption protocol used by Azure Virtual Desktop for all connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608026926818db1b277afce5e06e8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dace10a501d3c2b544e137b224cd683</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005046</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Origin Resource Sharing">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Origin Resource Sharing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CORS policies restrict web app requests to allowed domains, headers, and other criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c</data>
