</node>
<node id="Azure Policies">
  <data key="d0">Azure Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure policies are used to enforce security configurations such as disabling unsecured protocols and enforcing CORS policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure provides built-in policies related to Azure NetApp Files that can audit security and configuration recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-980c7a5d8e921b4d4d355fea3481711c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/app-service-web-apps.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source Control Manager">
  <data key="d0">Source Control Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Source Control Manager (SCM) sites are part of App Service where local authentication and remote debugging can be disabled to reduce attack surface.</data>
