<node id="APIOps">
  <data key="d0">APIOps</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">APIOps is a tooling approach for automated API deployments and disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;APIOps is an automated API deployment tooling approach for managing API configurations and disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;APIOps is an automated API deployment process for achieving rigorous access control isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;APIOps is a method using GitOps and CI/CD to publish APIs and manage API configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;APIOps is an automated process for deploying and managing API configurations as an alternative to manual portal-based management.&lt;SEP&gt;APIOps is a method for automated API deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c53b990e9918af85864a95bf9284ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Developer Portal">
  <data key="d0">Developer Portal</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The developer portal is a component of API Management that can be disabled or restricted to reduce surface area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workspaces">
  <data key="d0">Workspaces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workspaces in API Management isolate unrelated APIs to minimize the impact of failures caused by misconfiguration or outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Workspaces in API Management segregate roles, networks, and gateways for multiple workload teams sharing a gateway.&lt;SEP&gt;Workspaces provide access control isolation for API Management instances hosting APIs for multiple teams.&lt;SEP&gt;Workspaces in API Management provide a federated model for serving APIs while providing team isolation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Named Values">
  <data key="d0">Named Values</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Named values are a built-in API Management capability for managing secret values and configuration data.&lt;SEP&gt;Named values expose Key Vault secrets to API Management policies and store nonsecret configuration values directly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth">
  <data key="d0">OAuth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth is an authorization protocol enabled through identity providers like Microsoft Entra ID for back-end API authorization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c7409b2f79632903a9d9de4c67055d6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnose And Solve Problems">
  <data key="d0">Diagnose And Solve Problems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnose and solve problems is a capability in the Azure portal for troubleshooting API Management issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnose and Solve Problems is a capability in the Azure portal for identifying and troubleshooting gateway performance and service availability issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="API Tracing">
  <data key="d0">API Tracing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">API tracing is a development tool that helps developers understand policy implementation within an API.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backends Feature">
  <data key="d0">Backends Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The backends feature in API Management allows defining back ends centrally and referencing them by ID in policy, supporting load-balanced backend pools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Status Blade">
  <data key="d0">Network Status Blade</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Network Status Blade is a tool in the Azure portal used to troubleshoot network connectivity for API Management instances in virtual networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfcc3c8f8098ec40d6c8eea6fb30a4a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Policy Regulatory Compliance">
  <data key="d0">Azure Policy Regulatory Compliance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Policy Regulatory Compliance controls should be evaluated and enabled for API Management workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Policy Regulatory Compliance controls help align API Management instances with desired security posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rate-Limit Policy">
  <data key="d0">Rate-Limit Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rate-limit policy is a cost optimization technique used to manage request loads in API Management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limit-Concurrency Policy">
  <data key="d0">Limit-Concurrency Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Limit-concurrency policy is a cost optimization technique used to manage request loads in API Management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Built-In Cache">
  <data key="d0">Built-In Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Built-in cache in API Management avoids costs of purchasing and maintaining an external Redis-compatible cache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscale Rules">
  <data key="d0">Autoscale Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscale rules are automated processes configured to reduce units when gateway capacity drops below defined thresholds, matching capacity to demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale rules increase or decrease the number of VM instances in a scale set based on demand to ensure sufficient resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-37b84c5a9a2c854b590a8a22c511c52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure API Center">
  <data key="d0">Azure API Center</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure API Center is a separate Azure service not covered by this guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure API Center is an Azure service that can integrate managed API analysis linting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000331</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium Tier">
  <data key="d0">Premium Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Premium tier of API Management supports availability zones, multiple gateway units, multiple regions, and workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Premium tier supports zone-level redundancy and auto-inflate for scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium tier provides dedicated messaging units with predictable capacity, auto-scaling, zone redundancy, and geo-replication capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Premium tier of Azure Service Bus supports higher throughput limits, larger payloads, auto-scaling of messaging units, availability zones, and geo-replication.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium tier of Service Bus provides dedicated messaging units, predictable costs, geo-replication, geo-disaster recovery, and zone redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium tier provides dedicated messaging units with predictable performance and guaranteed capacity for Service Bus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d10ef40f70919a984cf031275099f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e36fb889991403b16d790b11d406033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49c55356fee42f19cd603d7edc0b8b6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium V2 Tier">
  <data key="d0">Premium V2 Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Premium v2 tier supports most Premium tier features except multiple regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Component">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Component</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The gateway component is the data plane of API Management that proxies API requests from client applications to back-end APIs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard V2 Tier">
  <data key="d0">Standard V2 Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Standard v2 tier is one of the recommended production tiers for enterprise workloads in API Management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f6c0558e7d949b856127c014f04affd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000333</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defender For APIs">
  <data key="d0">Defender For APIs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Defender for APIs provides API security insights, recommendations, and threat detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth 2.0">
  <data key="d0">OAuth 2.0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth 2.0 is an authorization framework recommended for client authentication over preshared keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validate-Jwt">
  <data key="d0">Validate-Jwt</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Validate-jwt is an API policy for performing JWT validation as a security check at the gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ip-Filter">
  <data key="d0">Ip-Filter</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ip-filter is an API policy for filtering traffic by IP address at the gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Set-Header">
  <data key="d0">Set-Header</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Set-header is an API policy used to suppress HTTP headers from API responses to hide implementation details.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1851b3d40bd0c571dbe26a4fe3cd7a31</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiregion Topology">
  <data key="d0">Multiregion Topology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiregion topology supports resiliency against complete regional failures by deploying API Management across multiple regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OWASP API Security Top 10">
  <data key="d0">OWASP API Security Top 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">OWASP API security top 10 is a reference for mitigating common API security threats in API Management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Scale-Out">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Scale-Out</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic scale-out enables API Management to dynamically adjust capacity based on traffic demands to prevent failures from insufficient capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960ce6b41ae564fa5b6c6cd61ca41bea</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spectral">
  <data key="d0">Spectral</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Spectral is an open-source linter that can be integrated into API approval pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Hosted Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Self-Hosted Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-hosted gateway is an API Management deployment option that should be avoided if a Microsoft-hosted gateway unit works for the scenario.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-10a01f49cd31e39d688d04081e77099c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-api-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Monitor Network Insights">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor Network Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor Network Insights provides a comprehensive view of health and metrics for network resources including Application Gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f471ce6b86ced91e851ed4cd06f0521</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateway V2">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateway V2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateway v2 is a version of Application Gateway that supports autoscaling functionality and instance maintenance capability for rolling updates without dropping connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Gateway v2 is the newer SKU offering autoscaling, zone-redundancy, better TLS offload performance, and quicker deployment times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f471ce6b86ced91e851ed4cd06f0521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000408</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source Network Address Translation">
  <data key="d0">Source Network Address Translation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SNAT port limitations can affect back-end connections on Application Gateway, impacting requests per second when port limits are reached.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateway For Containers">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateway For Containers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateway for Containers supports overlay pod networking and enables scaling multiple AKS clusters sharing ingress while conserving IP space.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Gateway for Containers supports overlay pod networking with AKS, enabling scaling multiple clusters while conserving IP space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0d38621b3ffd595eb404a49344659d5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Gateway V1">
  <data key="d0">Application Gateway V1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Gateway v1 is an older version of Azure Application Gateway, not recommended for new deployments unless specifically required.&lt;SEP&gt;Application Gateway v1 is the older SKU that lacks autoscaling and other v2 capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30367ff0212e0532e6d7643671bf4b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7a6546681236542c47a1fdb89f50b5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TLS Termination">
  <data key="d0">TLS Termination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TLS termination on Application Gateway improves performance by eliminating re-authentication to each back end and simplifying certificate management.&lt;SEP&gt;Practice of terminating TLS at a border gateway to reduce CPU consumption and improve energy efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-937b1809a20f2b2148f344a58b016317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca4d2bd438b809671ecf2d090095b06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-application-gateway.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005707</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero Trust Network">
  <data key="d0">Zero Trust Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero Trust network is a security architecture for web applications using Azure Firewall and Application Gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df0cc69c8383501073ee148f940f5d11</data>
