  <data key="d5">1777000513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SFTP">
  <data key="d0">SFTP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SSH File Transfer Protocol support is an optional feature in Blob Storage that incurs hourly charges.&lt;SEP&gt;SSH File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) is an optional feature of Blob Storage that incurs additional metering costs.&lt;SEP&gt;SFTP is a file transfer protocol supported by Azure Storage that incurs an hourly cost when enabled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifecycle Management">
  <data key="d0">Lifecycle Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifecycle management policies move blobs to cost-efficient tiers based on usage metrics such as last accessed time.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifecycle management is a storage feature for managing data retention policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Access Tiers">
  <data key="d0">Access Tiers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Access tiers (hot, cold, archive) determine storage and transaction costs, with cooler tiers for less-accessed data.&lt;SEP&gt;Access tiers (hot, cool, cold, archive) allow cost optimization based on data access frequency, with cooler tiers offering lower storage costs but higher access costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cost Management">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cost Management</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cost Management provides cost analysis, budgets, and monitoring tools in the Azure portal.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cost Management is a tool for analyzing message volume patterns, operation counts, and configuring budget alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cost Management is a service for tracking and optimizing network spend related to Private Link and other networking features.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cost Management is a tool used to track and optimize hybrid network spending.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cost Management provides best practices for managing and reducing costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cost Management is a service that helps reduce HPC costs through monitoring and optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc6dd32c7c960a85b9a30c11bc43659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37837339dd05d2a9f58b6dc734ebd967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9c715c42ddea999c4f406ee448b176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e43dcd642e61ee23ed8647dbc84d2290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b14a078d2121adef2ae56cc9aaead82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006206</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storage Insights">
  <data key="d0">Storage Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage Insights helps identify storage accounts with no or low use.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage Insights is a tool used to identify storage accounts with no or low use.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage insights provides dashboards to monitor availability, performance, and resilience metrics of storage accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage insights provides a unified view of failures, performance, availability, and capacity for storage accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6949b9609e5ef191a10ce0e8da0a14</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Copilot">
  <data key="d0">Azure Copilot</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Copilot is used with Azure Storage Discovery to analyze redundancy configurations for optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Copilot provides Azure Storage Discovery to identify security threats such as anonymous access and account key access across storage accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Copilot assists with discovering storage estate insights and managing data redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Copilot works with Azure Storage Discovery to discover storage estate insights and manage data redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blob Index Tags">
  <data key="d0">Blob Index Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blob index tags are an optional feature in Blob Storage that incurs billing based on the number of index tags.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blob Inventory">
  <data key="d0">Blob Inventory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blob inventory is an optional feature that bills based on the number of objects scanned.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blob Soft Delete">
  <data key="d0">Blob Soft Delete</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blob soft delete enables a storage account to recover deleted blobs.&lt;SEP&gt;Blob soft delete is a feature that incurs additional transaction and capacity costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6432be253450a04b955049e15c85e38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Storage Actions">
  <data key="d0">Azure Storage Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Storage Actions enables automated data lifecycle management across storage accounts with regional availability for archiving, deletion, and tier transitions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage Actions provides regional automation for unified data lifecycle management across geographic regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000515</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifecycle Management Policy">
  <data key="d0">Lifecycle Management Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifecycle management policies are used to automatically delete or archive old blob versions and logs, and to transition objects to more cost-effective access tiers.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifecycle management policies automatically delete or set access tiers of blobs based on defined conditions to optimize cost efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-972be0b4bf11ea48bf7bc0f5604217e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000515</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storage SDKs">
  <data key="d0">Storage SDKs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage SDKs are Azure software development kits optimized for performance, providing mechanisms to fine-tune blob storage operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Acceleration">
  <data key="d0">Query Acceleration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Query acceleration filters out unwanted data during storage requests to avoid needless data transfer across the network.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifecycle Management Policies">
  <data key="d0">Lifecycle Management Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated lifecycle policies optimize costs by moving data to appropriate tiers based on age or access patterns, reducing manual operational overhead.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifecycle management policies optimize storage costs by moving data across Premium, Standard, Cold, and Archive tiers based on age and business requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c634b3a2b27e4b06ab4fb93df82c41da</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005926</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GZRS replicates data across availability zones and global regions, enabling read access from secondary regions during outages.&lt;SEP&gt;GZRS provides protection against regional outages with zone redundancy, at higher cost than LRS.&lt;SEP&gt;GZRS combines zone and geo redundancy; supported only by standard SMB accounts in Azure Files.&lt;SEP&gt;GZRS is an Azure Storage redundancy option combining zone and geo redundancy for data replication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LRS is the lowest-cost redundancy option, suitable for applications that can tolerate some data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Locally redundant storage (LRS) is a storage redundancy option used with same-zone HA that stores data within a single zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Locally redundant storage (LRS) is the most affordable redundancy level for Azure storage accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e39ac746628d7273f799262e7cf7dc3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor Storage Insights">
  <data key="d0">Monitor Storage Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitor Storage insights is a monitoring tool for identifying performance bottlenecks and throttling in storage accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa71b60fbaf9206cdd300b906d2e1868</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Service Health Dashboard">
  <data key="d0">Azure Service Health Dashboard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Service Health dashboard is used to monitor potential availability problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Service Health dashboard provides status information to monitor potential availability problems for Azure services.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Service Health dashboard is used to monitor potential availability problems for Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Content Delivery Network">
  <data key="d0">Azure Content Delivery Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Content Delivery Network is a service whose endpoints are considered internal dependencies for Blob Storage workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Content Delivery Network is an endpoint service identified as an internal dependency in failure mode analysis for Azure Files workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Content Delivery Network caches frequently accessed content at edge locations to improve responsiveness and reduce latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba915883bba414ecf1ca82b7ab6c12cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
