  <data key="d5">1777005353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Blob Storage Client Library">
  <data key="d0">Azure Blob Storage Client Library</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Blob Storage client library provides SDK functionality with built-in transient fault handling for manipulating containers and blobs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e409982ea62543ca5f8cfba60ee3111d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000521</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blob Inventory Reports">
  <data key="d0">Blob Inventory Reports</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blob inventory reports review retention, legal hold, encryption status, data size, age, and tier distribution of storage account contents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium Block Blob Storage">
  <data key="d0">Premium Block Blob Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium block blob storage accounts are recommended for workloads requiring high transaction rates, smaller objects, and low transaction latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c22ca64b05af7aae98b5daec0456ec48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For Storage">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for Storage is a security feature that detects threats by triggering alerts when anomalies in activity occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Storage detects potentially harmful attempts to access or exploit Azure file shares over SMB or FileREST protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender for Storage detects potentially harmful attempts to access or exploit Azure file shares over SMB or FileREST protocols, sending email alerts to subscription administrators.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001486</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immutability Policies">
  <data key="d0">Immutability Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Immutability policies protect critical blobs from being modified or deleted for legal, compliance, or business purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Immutability policies protect critical blob objects from being modified or deleted for legal, compliance, or business purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Access Signature">
  <data key="d0">Shared Access Signature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shared access signature (SAS) tokens provide delegated access to Azure Storage resources, with best practices including expiration policies and governance controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1af89a614a763c4c53d5180fa502d9bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GRS">
  <data key="d0">GRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-redundant storage (GRS) is a redundancy configuration that replicates data to a secondary region.&lt;SEP&gt;GRS (Geo-Redundant Storage) is a redundancy level requiring cross-region data synchronization.&lt;SEP&gt;GRS (Geo-Redundant Storage) is a redundancy configuration for Azure storage accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GZRS">
  <data key="d0">GZRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-zone-redundant storage (GZRS) is a redundancy configuration that replicates data across different availability zones and enables geo priority replication for optimal RPO.&lt;SEP&gt;GZRS (Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage) is a redundancy level requiring cross-region data synchronization.&lt;SEP&gt;GZRS (Geo-Zone-Redundant Storage) replicates data across availability zones and enables reading during outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LRS">
  <data key="d0">LRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LRS (Locally Redundant Storage) is a lower-cost redundancy level suitable for applications tolerating some data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Locally Redundant Storage is the default redundancy level for non-HA and same-zone HA deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfbc5259a1cb90df20b9d1680409b75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ZRS">
  <data key="d0">ZRS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) is a redundancy configuration that replicates across different availability zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone-Redundant Storage is the redundancy level used by zone-redundant HA deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;ZRS (Zone-Redundant Storage) replicates across availability zones for high availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Container Soft Delete">
  <data key="d0">Container Soft Delete</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Container soft delete enables a storage account to recover deleted containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Versioning">
  <data key="d0">Versioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Versioning automatically tracks changes made to blobs and allows restoring a blob to a previous state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vaulted Backup">
  <data key="d0">Vaulted Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vaulted backup protects block blob data from ransomware and other attacks by copying data to a Backup vault with retention up to 10 years.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last Synchronization Time">
  <data key="d0">Last Synchronization Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Last synchronization time is a property that helps estimate potential data loss by indicating when data was last written to the secondary region, applicable to GRS and GZRS configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Last synchronization time is a property used to estimate potential data loss before initiating a failover, indicating when data was last written to the secondary region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secure Transfer Required">
  <data key="d0">Secure Transfer Required</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secure transfer required is a setting that ensures all requests to a storage account must use secure connections, causing HTTP requests to fail.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863e2a07aedc1833ee7e4f6120b290a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-blob-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Sessions">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Sessions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic sessions execute untrusted or AI-generated code in secure, ephemeral sandboxes using Hyper-V isolation, with automatic destruction after use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyper-V Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Hyper-V Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyper-V isolation provides strong kernel-level separation between sessions to prevent malicious code from affecting hosts or other sessions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Envoy Proxy">
  <data key="d0">Envoy Proxy</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Envoy proxy redirects HTTP traffic to HTTPS with default configuration of allowInsecure: false.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MTLS">
  <data key="d0">MTLS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutual Transport Layer Security authenticates and encrypts traffic between services by verifying both parties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6442b7c1d4b778e4c37906350571fd8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Zone-Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Azure Zone-Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Zone-Redundant Storage (ZRS) provides high availability and durability by protecting against data loss from zone failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure zone-redundant storage (ZRS) provides high availability and durability of data by protecting against data loss from zone failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68def80a7a35bff6f8aac9812fc89a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OpenTelemetry Collector">
  <data key="d0">OpenTelemetry Collector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">OpenTelemetry collector provides comprehensive distributed tracing and metrics collection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resiliency Policies">
  <data key="d0">Resiliency Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resiliency policies include retries, timeouts, and circuit breakers to prevent and recover from service request failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium Ingress">
  <data key="d0">Premium Ingress</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium ingress provides dedicated resources, custom timeouts, and scaling settings for high-throughput workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium ingress allocates dedicated compute resources to the ingress proxy for latency-sensitive or high-throughput workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0f0a67e7828ea196dc49ba03dc0402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
