  <data key="d0">Dedicated GPU Workload Profiles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated GPU workload profiles provide consistent, low-latency GPU performance for sustained, latency-sensitive workloads such as AI training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c02fec47d3690eda5205a8e344d53952</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Savings Plan For Compute">
  <data key="d0">Azure Savings Plan For Compute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure savings plan for compute offers up to 17% savings compared to pay-as-you-go pricing through fixed hourly rate commitments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2561a2f86d2dab33aaf3dc641c06d2c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T4 GPUs">
  <data key="d0">T4 GPUs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">T4 GPUs are cost-effective GPUs suitable for inference and lightweight tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2561a2f86d2dab33aaf3dc641c06d2c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A100 GPUs">
  <data key="d0">A100 GPUs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A100 GPUs are reserved for large model training and high-compute scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2561a2f86d2dab33aaf3dc641c06d2c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OpenTelemetry Agent">
  <data key="d0">OpenTelemetry Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The managed OpenTelemetry agent emits standardized traces, metrics, and logs without requiring a custom collector, reducing operational overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eureka Server For Spring">
  <data key="d0">Eureka Server For Spring</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Eureka Server for Spring is a managed Java component in Container Apps for service discovery with built-in lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Config Server For Spring">
  <data key="d0">Config Server For Spring</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Config Server for Spring is a managed Java component in Container Apps for configuration management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a2ef717834626112dc2d5f7ce043852</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000627</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTTPS">
  <data key="d0">HTTPS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HTTPS is enforced to protect data in transit from network layer eavesdropping attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51d89d8bc1094d5427b9923c0759b965</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-container-apps.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant HA">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant HA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone-redundant high availability distributes primary and standby servers across different availability zones using zone-redundant storage, providing automatic failover within 60-120 seconds and zero RPO.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone-redundant high availability is an architecture that protects against single availability zone failures through automatic failover, achieving 60-120 second RTO and zero data loss for committed transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Zone-redundant high availability is a feature that provides reliability through redundancy across availability zones, costing double the compute cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Same-Zone HA">
  <data key="d0">Same-Zone HA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Same-zone HA protects against server-level failures using locally redundant storage but does not protect against zone outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MySQL Community Edition">
  <data key="d0">MySQL Community Edition</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MySQL Community Edition is the open-source database engine that Azure Database for MySQL is based on.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Purpose Tier">
  <data key="d0">General Purpose Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The General Purpose tier is a compute and service tier offered across multiple Azure database services, designed to provide balanced cost-performance for standard production workloads requiring consistent performance.

In Azure Database for MySQL, the General Purpose tier supports workloads needing high availability (HA), read replicas, and accelerated logs, offering balanced compute and memory resources for production environments. However, failovers in this tier involve cold-cache performance degradation, as the instance restarts on a new node without warm replicas.

In Azure SQL Managed Instance, the General Purpose tier tolerates higher storage latency and uses remote storage with file-size-dependent IOPS. It provides lower per-vCore TempDB allocation compared to higher tiers. This tier supports stop/start functionality, including stop/start schedules, and offers favorable Azure Hybrid Benefit conversion ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002766</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Memory Optimized Tier">
  <data key="d0">Memory Optimized Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Memory Optimized tier is a compute tier in Azure Database for MySQL required for workloads needing HA or read replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory Optimized is the highest-cost compute tier, designed for memory-intensive workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The Memory Optimized tier is a compute tier for workloads with consistently high memory pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Memory Optimized tier delivers higher memory-to-vCore ratios for cache-dependent and high-concurrency scenarios with lowest latency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Memory Optimized tier increases query throughput in high-concurrency scenarios at no extra cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-987318a54e0439c65ea9427adb8524a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b1775a768fc04ca64ed9caa4af5d16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storage Autogrow">
  <data key="d0">Storage Autogrow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage autogrow automatically increases capacity when free storage drops below a threshold, preventing the server from entering read-only mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage autogrow is a feature that automatically increases provisioned storage, which can cause cost increases without explicit user action.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage autogrow automatically increases storage capacity when utilization approaches the provisioned limit, preventing read-only mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage autogrow automatically increases storage capacity when utilization approaches the provisioned limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage autogrow prevents the server from entering read-only mode when capacity runs out.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Burstable Tier">
  <data key="d0">Burstable Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Burstable is the lowest-cost compute tier, suitable for intermittent workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The Burstable B-series tier is a compute tier for intermittent CPU demand workloads; it doesn't support HA or read replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Burstable tier is limited to development and testing environments due to CPU credit throttling and lack of HA and read replica support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="InnoDB Buffer Pool">
  <data key="d0">InnoDB Buffer Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">InnoDB buffer pool is a memory allocation that varies by compute size and determines cache efficiency for MySQL workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;InnoDB buffer pool determines how much working data is cached in memory, directly affecting cache hit ratio and query performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Performance Insight">
  <data key="d0">Query Performance Insight</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Query Performance Insight is a workbook providing query-level visibility for Azure Database for MySQL.&lt;SEP&gt;Query Performance Insight is a tool for optimizing queries, tables, and databases in SQL Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Query performance insight identifies top resource-consuming and long-running queries, providing metrics like CPU, duration, and implementation count.&lt;SEP&gt;Query Performance Insight identifies top resource-consuming and long-running queries in a workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Drift Detection">
  <data key="d0">Automated Drift Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated drift detection identifies unauthorized or accidental parameter modifications before they affect workload behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscale IOPS">
  <data key="d0">Autoscale IOPS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscale IOPS provides automatic I/O scaling based on demand without manual intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale IOPS dynamically scales I/O with demand to prevent storage throttling during workload spikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0dc99c95ce037733d84dabf2343a2974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure MySQL Flexible Server">
  <data key="d0">Azure MySQL Flexible Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure MySQL Flexible Server is a managed database service offering features like autoscale IOPS, read replicas, compute tier scaling, accelerated logs, and storage autogrow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accelerated Logs">
  <data key="d0">Accelerated Logs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Accelerated logs speed up transaction log operations by placing logs on high-performance storage, reducing commit latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ProxySQL">
  <data key="d0">ProxySQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ProxySQL is a connection proxy used to distribute read traffic automatically to read replicas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Tier Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Compute Tier Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Compute tier scaling adjusts server resources and requires a 60-to-120-second restart window.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81709438e911127c0b5e4af16cb8e572</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Database For MySQL Flexible Server">
  <data key="d0">Azure Database For MySQL Flexible Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Database for MySQL flexible server is a cloud database service that supports hosting multiple databases on a single server instance, with features like read replicas, HA, compute tiers, and stop/start capability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserved Instances">
  <data key="d0">Reserved Instances</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserved instances offer discounts for longer commitment terms compared to pay-as-you-go pricing.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved instances offer reduced compute costs through 1-year or 3-year commitments for predictable sustained usage, with vCore size flexibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved instances allow cost savings by committing to one-year or three-year terms for VMs with predictable pricing.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserved Instances allow advance purchase of compute capacity for one or three years to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f05e5f46b39ac0c01364030a2aca2729</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005878</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IOPS Autoscale">
  <data key="d0">IOPS Autoscale</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IOPS autoscale automatically adjusts IOPS consumption, potentially causing silent cost increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stop/Start Capability">
  <data key="d0">Stop/Start Capability</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The stop/start capability allows stopping nonproduction servers outside business hours to eliminate compute charges, with a 30-day maximum stop duration before automatic restart.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e273e45bd48c3fbe3a644e01b062e11a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Restore">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Restore</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-restore creates a new server from geo-redundant backups, with universal geo-restore supporting nonpaired regions. It does not support custom port configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-restore is a recovery method that restores database servers from backup data replicated to paired or nonpaired Azure regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-restore recovers a database from a service outage by restoring from geo-replicated backups to any SQL Database server in any Azure region.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-restore is a backup recovery capability reserved for full service outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Lockbox">
  <data key="d0">Customer Lockbox</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Lockbox controls Microsoft support access during support incidents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-403738333bd7842b48d9afbadf776957</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flyway">
  <data key="d0">Flyway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Flyway is a tool for version-controlling database schema changes in CI/CD pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b359b45da7d6b789373380187e0a7ede</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liquibase">
  <data key="d0">Liquibase</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquibase is a tool for version-controlling database schema changes in CI/CD pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b359b45da7d6b789373380187e0a7ede</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Near-Zero-Downtime Patching">
  <data key="d0">Near-Zero-Downtime Patching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Near-zero-downtime patching is a mechanism for applying maintenance updates with minimal disruption, requiring all tables to have primary keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b359b45da7d6b789373380187e0a7ede</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MySQL Flexible Server">
  <data key="d0">MySQL Flexible Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MySQL Flexible Server is an Azure database service with configurable security parameters, virtual network integration, private endpoints, and support for custom ports and encryption settings.&lt;SEP&gt;MySQL flexible server is an Azure database service supporting configurable HA, backup, compute tiers, and server parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARM Template">
  <data key="d0">ARM Template</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ARM templates are Azure Resource Manager templates used for infrastructure deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auditing Workbook">
  <data key="d0">Auditing Workbook</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The built-in Auditing workbook provides security event visualization for audit log data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Auditing workbook provides ready-made visualizations for audit event analysis on MySQL flexible server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Managed Maintenance Window">
  <data key="d0">Custom Managed Maintenance Window</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A policy allowing selection of preferred day and UTC start time for maintenance to minimize workload disruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Demand Backup">
  <data key="d0">On-Demand Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">On-demand backups create known-good rollback points before schema migrations or changes, with a 50-backup-per-server limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Management Lock">
  <data key="d0">Management Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CanNotDelete management locks prevent accidental deletion of production database servers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="REST API">
  <data key="d0">REST API</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">REST API is used alongside Azure CLI for automating configuration management and applying server parameter configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-249415e2f114bf589c9d5262bc0bf6bc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Innodb_Buffer_Pool_Size">
  <data key="d0">Innodb_Buffer_Pool_Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">innodb_buffer_pool_size is a parameter that should be maximized for the compute SKU to achieve the best cache hit ratio and page cache efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6b1775a768fc04ca64ed9caa4af5d16</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WordPress On Azure App Service">
  <data key="d0">WordPress On Azure App Service</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">WordPress on Azure App Service is an example architecture demonstrating key recommendations for Azure Database for MySQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e6b1775a768fc04ca64ed9caa4af5d16</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed HSM">
  <data key="d0">Managed HSM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Managed HSM is an alternative to Key Vault for managing encryption keys with hardware security module protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Managed HSM provides high-security key storage for organizations requiring enhanced key protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ca750e1276d5d236cc8c7095eaa1c8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer-Managed Key Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Customer-Managed Key Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer-managed key encryption provides full control over encryption key lifecycle including creation, rotation, and revocation for database encryption.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer-managed key encryption allows Premium tier users to control encryption key lifecycle using Azure Key Vault.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653342d517c710c9f67df8e6155d05a8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002480</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TLS 1.3">
  <data key="d0">TLS 1.3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TLS 1.3 is the strongest encryption protocol recommended for MySQL 8.0 servers to protect data in transit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Least Privilege Access">
  <data key="d0">Least Privilege Access</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Least privilege access is a security concept of assigning only the minimum privileges necessary for specific databases and tables.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity-Based Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Identity-Based Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Identity-based authentication replaces static passwords with short-lived tokens through Microsoft Entra ID managed identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Identity-based authentication provides superior security compared to storage account keys for accessing Azure file shares.&lt;SEP&gt;Identity-based authentication uses AES-256 Kerberos ticket encryption to authorize access to SMB Azure file shares, reducing reliance on storage account keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8a88ba4349c5c5150df583b3f68ce96</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audit Logging">
  <data key="d0">Audit Logging</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Audit logging tracks connection events, admin operations, DDL and DML statements, and table access for security monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b3fcfb30f28cfcb4e8d95e057040687</data>
