  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exponential Backoff">
  <data key="d0">Exponential Backoff</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Exponential backoff is a retry strategy for automatic connection retry during failover disruptions, maintenance, and scaling events.&lt;SEP&gt;Exponential backoff is a retry strategy starting at 30 seconds that prevents overwhelming downstream services during outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Exponential backoff is a retry policy strategy for handling transient consumer failures automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;Exponential backoff is a retry strategy optimized for consumer patterns to handle transient failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Exponential backoff is a retry logic pattern that absorbs transient connectivity disruptions during maintenance and failover events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MySQL Bug 102586">
  <data key="d0">MySQL Bug 102586</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">MySQL Bug 102586 causes HA standby desynchronization when multitable DELETE statements with CASCADE are used on HA-enabled servers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="InnoDB">
  <data key="d0">InnoDB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">InnoDB is the MySQL storage engine where explicit primary keys are required on all tables for efficient replication and failover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GIPK">
  <data key="d0">GIPK</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Generated Invisible Primary Key is a setting that automatically adds primary keys to tables lacking them, improving replication performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db2648910473195dad09b71af47dc280</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Availability">
  <data key="d0">High Availability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Availability doubles compute cost by deploying a standby replica with dedicated storage and compute.&lt;SEP&gt;High availability (HA) refers to ensuring continuous operation and minimal downtime for SaaS solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;High availability integrates redundancy and failover mechanisms to ensure uninterrupted operations.&lt;SEP&gt;High availability is a design principle ensuring applications remain operational during host failures through anti-affinity rules and stretched clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c2b90f75a5825a24b97092ce53a0d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-database-for-mysql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines provide data pipeline resilience with data expectations and fault tolerance capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines provide automatic error handling, data quality enforcement, and quality constraints for resilient data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines automatically handle transient failures, data quality violations, and infrastructure problems with built-in quality enforcement and retry capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines enforce built-in quality constraints during data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines automate data validation and pipeline quality assurance using data quality expectations and monitoring rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines simplify and automate the implementation of optimization recommendations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines are used to schedule regular optimization tasks in Azure Databricks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Loader">
  <data key="d0">Auto Loader</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Loader provides rescued data capabilities for data pipeline resilience in Azure Databricks.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Loader provides rescued data capabilities for handling errors in data pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Loader is a tool for monitoring schema evolution problems during data ingestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delta Lake">
  <data key="d0">Delta Lake</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Delta Lake is a storage layer technology that provides richer functionality for data stored in Delta format on data lake platforms. It offers data protection through ACID transactions, automatic versioning, time travel capabilities with retention policies for point-in-time recovery, and schema enforcement and evolution.

Delta Lake includes extensive optimization features such as OPTIMIZE commands, data compaction, Z-ORDER clustering, Bloom filters, table statistics, and VACUUM operations for efficient data management. It also supports exactly-once delivery, data versioning, and lineage tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks Asset Bundles">
  <data key="d0">Databricks Asset Bundles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks Asset Bundles are used for automated backup of source code, job definitions, and cluster configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Databricks Asset Bundles enable version control of notebook source code, job configurations, pipeline definitions, and infrastructure settings in Git repositories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Autoscaling">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Autoscaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster autoscaling uses dynamic node allocation to prevent resource exhaustion while maintaining cost efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster autoscaling dynamically adjusts node counts based on workload demand to reduce overprovisioning costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Pools">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster pools with prewarmed instances reduce cluster startup time from minutes to under 60 seconds.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster pools reduce startup times and optimize resource allocation for frequently used configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster pools reduce startup time from minutes to seconds while eliminating DBU charges for idle pool instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster pools provide prewarmed instances to reduce cluster startup time from 5-10 minutes to less than 30 seconds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless SQL Warehouses">
  <data key="d0">Serverless SQL Warehouses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless SQL warehouses provide automatic scaling with built-in high availability and eliminate cluster management overhead.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless SQL warehouses eliminate infrastructure management overhead and optimize costs through consumption-based billing for interactive SQL workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless SQL warehouses are deployed for BI and analytical workloads requiring interactive analytics with configurable sizing.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless SQL warehouses eliminate cluster management overhead and provide instant scaling for BI and analytical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structured Streaming Checkpoints">
  <data key="d0">Structured Streaming Checkpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured streaming checkpoints are used as part of advanced resilience strategies for data pipeline fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb68841440596ce96d4bd54899abbe7d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MLflow">
  <data key="d0">MLflow</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MLflow is an open-source framework and ML lifecycle tool for managing the end-to-end machine learning process. It provides experiment tracking (including code versions, environments, parameters, runs, and results), model registry, reproducibility, data and model versioning, and collaborative work capabilities.

MLflow is integrated with both Azure Machine Learning and Azure Databricks, falling within the Azure Databricks technology scope. It supports machine learning performance tuning, distributed training orchestration on GPU-enabled clusters, and integrates with the Azure Machine Learning managed feature store. Additionally, MLflow is used for model security validation within the secure development life cycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5cc325eb282741cd4c48968319d834f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ea600d3306dde466b8e4fa453de97e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88acce1b2be2296ca1e97b9e9e3c8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003795</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks">
  <data key="d0">Databricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks is a data and AI platform providing compute, storage, and analytics services.&lt;SEP&gt;Databricks is a data platform that supports model hosting and distributed data processing via Spark jobs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photon">
  <data key="d0">Photon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Photon is an acceleration engine providing vectorized query execution for efficient data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon is an acceleration engine that provides vectorized query execution capabilities to reduce compute time and costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon is an accelerated query engine that delivers better price performance for SQL workloads on serverless SQL warehouses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000938</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Policies">
  <data key="d0">Compute Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Compute policies enforce cost-effective configurations by restricting instance types and enforcing automatic termination settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless Jobs">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Jobs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless jobs eliminate idle time costs with consumption-based billing for variable and intermittent workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000939</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks Commit Units">
  <data key="d0">Databricks Commit Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks Commit Units (DBCU) are prepaid usage contracts offering discounts in exchange for usage commitments.&lt;SEP&gt;Databricks Commit Units (DBCU) are reserved capacity purchases for predictable workloads over one to three-year terms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f21b76f3eb7933c956cb0c1a98488ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000940</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks Repos">
  <data key="d0">Databricks Repos</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks Repos is a version control tool used in Azure Databricks CI/CD deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Databricks Repos enables Git integration for source control and collaborative development of notebooks and source code.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000941</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entra ID">
  <data key="d0">Entra ID</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Entra ID provides identity management and native integration with serverless workspaces for tenant users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks REST API">
  <data key="d0">Databricks REST API</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Databricks REST API is used with Azure Automation runbooks to establish automated backup procedures for workspace artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000942</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Rightsizing">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Rightsizing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster rightsizing is an automated solution using cluster metrics and Azure Monitor data to analyze utilization patterns and recommend optimal instance types and sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless Workspaces">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Workspaces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless workspaces are fully managed Azure Databricks workspace types with preconfigured serverless compute, default DBFS storage, and automatic Unity Catalog enablement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ec7a8b0cbc84ecca1daa616149db819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000946</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Principal Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Service Principal Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Service principal authentication eliminates dependencies on user credentials for automated processes and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Service principal authentication eliminates dependencies on user credentials for automated processes while providing access controls and audit trails.&lt;SEP&gt;Service principal authentication enables Azure Databricks integrations with external systems using managed identity and credential rotation policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7caf8d0c8419c804f864143fd95c9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d43601fe6822fd1a5a934f2ed75224</data>
