</node>
<node id="Spark">
  <data key="d0">Spark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Spark is a distributed computing engine used by Azure Databricks clusters, requiring performance tuning of executor memory, parallelism, and garbage collection.&lt;SEP&gt;Spark is a distributed processing engine that provides built-in caching mechanisms, partition pruning, and the Catalyst optimizer for query optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7caf8d0c8419c804f864143fd95c9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Hardening">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Hardening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster hardening includes SSH restriction, custom image scanning, and runtime security controls to reduce attack surfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless Compute">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Compute</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless compute uses consumption-based pricing, scales automatically, and reduces operational overhead for workloads with activity spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Serverless compute is an Azure Machine Learning option ideal for short, infrequent runs with standard or spot pricing options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19bbc6ffc74eee4a356518df32b00c13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f37224876d004b6edc267c88180a8c61</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks Units">
  <data key="d0">Databricks Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks Units (DBUs) are the unit of compute measurement in Databricks, with 100 free DBUs per workspace per day provided under the Lakeflow Connect Free Tier.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47ade5be5e93e797e6440422f4c49472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catalyst Optimizer">
  <data key="d0">Catalyst Optimizer</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalyst optimizer is a native Spark feature that dynamically optimizes joins and partitioning at runtime.&lt;SEP&gt;The Catalyst optimizer rewrites queries for efficiency in Spark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AQE">
  <data key="d0">AQE</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive Query Execution (AQE) adjusts query plans at runtime to handle data skew and improve joins.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive Query Execution (AQE) is a Spark runtime optimization capability that dynamically coalesces shuffle partitions, switches join strategies, and optimizes skewed joins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delta Cache">
  <data key="d0">Delta Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Delta Cache optimizes performance by caching data at the disk level across nodes in Azure Databricks.&lt;SEP&gt;Delta Cache uses local NVMe SSD storage to cache frequently accessed datasets, accelerating query performance by bypassing slower network storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structured Streaming">
  <data key="d0">Structured Streaming</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured streaming provides exactly-once processing guarantees with checkpoint-based recovery from cluster failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Structured Streaming is used for real-time data pipelines requiring low-latency and high-throughput performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Structured streaming in Azure Databricks supports configurable trigger intervals for real-time data processing with subsecond to micro-batch latency options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horovod">
  <data key="d0">Horovod</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Horovod is a distributed training tool integrated with Azure Databricks for machine learning workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa172784bde4c6d811c0a563536c6b8a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
