<node id="Instance Pools">
  <data key="d0">Instance Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Instance pools with multiple VM families provide allocation flexibility during capacity constraints and reduce provisioning failure risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Instance pools share underlying VM resources, which affects tenant isolation guarantees when consolidating SQL Managed Instance instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Instance pools consolidate multiple small SQL Managed Instance instances on shared compute to reduce per-instance overhead, restricted to the General Purpose tier.&lt;SEP&gt;Instance pools host multiple small managed instances sharing pre-provisioned compute, enabling smaller vCore configurations not available outside pools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9fa5913e5b110a5e9169b6c4527dd3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure REST APIs">
  <data key="d0">Azure REST APIs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure REST APIs are used to create automated workspace backup procedures for exporting configurations and metadata.</data>
