<node id="GPU-Enabled Clusters">
  <data key="d0">GPU-Enabled Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GPU-enabled clusters using NC, ND, or NV-series VMs accelerate deep learning model training by 10 to 100 times compared to CPU-only clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-12ef49ca366d153d40cdff6dc2237d82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000957</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Autoscaling Policies">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Autoscaling Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster autoscaling policies automatically adjust compute resources based on CPU utilization, memory usage, or job queue depth to balance performance and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Z-Ordering">
  <data key="d0">Z-Ordering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Z-ordering is a data clustering technique used with OPTIMIZE commands on Delta Lake tables to improve query performance based on frequently used filter and join columns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Photon Engine">
  <data key="d0">Photon Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Photon engine is a Databricks query engine that runs queries faster with built-in acceleration capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Photon engine accelerates SQL queries and DataFrame operations through native vectorized execution for analytical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid Clustering">
  <data key="d0">Liquid Clustering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid clustering is an alternative to traditional partitioning for tables with multiple partition candidates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zstd">
  <data key="d0">Zstd</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zstd is a compression algorithm that provides better compression ratios for cold data in Parquet file format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snappy">
  <data key="d0">Snappy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Snappy is a compression algorithm that provides faster decompression for frequently accessed datasets in Parquet file format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium SSD">
  <data key="d0">Premium SSD</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium SSD storage tiers provide up to 20,000 IOPS and submillisecond latency for Azure Databricks workloads requiring high performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD is a disk type that contributes to the highest VM uptime SLA.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD disks support reserved capacity to reduce total environment cost through prepayment.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD is an Azure disk type that supports reserved capacity for cost savings.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD is an Azure disk type recommended for VM OS disks, offering built-in redundancy and zone-redundant storage options.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD is a high-performance disk type offering customizable IOPS, throughput, built-in redundancy, and zone-redundant storage options with higher availability and lower latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSDs are recommended for production workloads requiring high performance, low latency, and an SLA in Azure Virtual Desktop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e6162eae6d61a639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spark Executor Memory Settings">
  <data key="d0">Spark Executor Memory Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Spark executor memory settings configure between 2 and 8 GB per executor and 2 to 5 cores per executor to balance parallelism and resource efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dd9d1b3dac2708d112ba207a146287c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Query Execution">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Query Execution</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive Query Execution (AQE) is a Spark feature that dynamically optimizes joins and partitioning at runtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks Unit">
  <data key="d0">Databricks Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks Unit (DBU) is an abstracted billing model based on compute usage in Azure Databricks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Job Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Job Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Job clusters are compute resources deployed for scheduled workloads that automatically end when jobs finish, reducing idle compute costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Termination">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Termination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic termination ends interactive clusters after appropriate timeout periods to eliminate costs from idle clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Databricks System Tables">
  <data key="d0">Databricks System Tables</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Databricks system tables track cluster usage and DBU consumption and can be queried to detect cost anomalies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ca9e9ecafaa14f1c2e106f58a475e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777000960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra Disk Storage">
  <data key="d0">Ultra Disk Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra Disk Storage is an Azure disk type that supports direct performance adjustments within a 24-hour period.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Disk Storage is a high-performance Azure disk type offering customizable IOPS and throughput, ideal for mission-critical workloads requiring lowest latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Disk Storage is a premium disk type with limited regional availability and specific VM type requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premium SSD V2">
  <data key="d0">Premium SSD V2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Premium SSD v2 is a high-performance disk type for Azure Virtual Machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD v2 is an Azure disk type supporting performance adjustments and Live Resize for dynamic capacity expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD v2 is a high-performance Azure disk type with customizable IOPS and throughput, suitable for data disks requiring low latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD v2 is a premium disk type with limited regional availability and specific VM type requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Premium SSD v2 provides better performance and scalability for VM storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard SSD">
  <data key="d0">Standard SSD</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard SSD is a cost-effective storage option suitable for development, testing, and workloads with moderate performance needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard HDD">
  <data key="d0">Standard HDD</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard HDD is a low-cost storage option suitable for backup, archival data, but unsuitable for performance-sensitive workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Machines Baseline Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Machines Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Machines baseline architecture is a foundational architecture that demonstrates key recommendations for Azure deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;A foundational architecture demonstrating key recommendations for Azure Virtual Machines deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8ab4a801cf288c76084ee5132b56b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Live Resize">
  <data key="d0">Live Resize</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Live Resize enables dynamic capacity expansion for Premium SSD v2 and Ultra NVMe disks without downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defender For Cloud">
  <data key="d0">Defender For Cloud</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Defender for Cloud is a Microsoft security solution designed to manage cyber threats, vulnerabilities, and security posture across cloud and hybrid environments. It provides Cloud Workload Protection capabilities for servers and offers a single pane of glass for security compliance management.

Defender for Cloud detects security threats and triggers alerts when anomalies in activity occur. It assesses compliance by providing recommendations showing compliance state for built-in policies, including those related to Azure Local. It measures the security posture of Azure Local machines and workloads, helping organizations strengthen their overall security.

Defender for Cloud enables visualization of network infrastructure and network security status across Azure virtual networks and virtual hubs. It is an integrated cloud service used with Azure Local that incurs additional costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Defender for Cloud provides security recommendations and alerts that can be automated via Azure policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure security service that integrates with Microsoft Defender for Endpoint.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef9765311dfd798d022450d45e1c01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5158a76c261c507648b548ec947486da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca4d2bd438b809671ecf2d090095b06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-firewall.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005706</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pricing Calculator">
  <data key="d0">Pricing Calculator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure pricing calculator is a tool to estimate and model environment costs.&lt;SEP&gt;The pricing calculator is an Azure tool used to estimate realistic costs for each tier of Azure Front Door.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pricing Calculator is an Azure tool used to estimate costs of virtual machines and other resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c9c22dcb398bdcbe4d02bc247b58ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-front-door.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disk Bursting">
  <data key="d0">Disk Bursting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Disk bursting is a feature that can improve disk performance without switching to another disk size or type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea53a0b406e3a5abb3d4cae35968d70</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001044</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Resource Manager Lock">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Manager Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A lock mechanism applied to disks to prevent accidental deletion and data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager lock helps prevent disks from being deleted to avoid data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager lock prevents accidental or malicious deletion of storage accounts, which can cause data loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e6162eae6d61a639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b291819acd1bfde1eed7819d1f9b371</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAS Tokens">
  <data key="d0">SAS Tokens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SAS tokens are shared access signature tokens used for authentication; Microsoft discourages their use and recommends setting expiration to 60 days or less.&lt;SEP&gt;SAS tokens are shared access signature tokens recommended with one-hour expiry and minimal permissions for Event Hubs authorization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ec11fc60af5bae9e6162eae6d61a639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6421530c72d2fa97eac8e07332f7bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Standard SSD">
  <data key="d0">Azure Standard SSD</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Standard SSD is one of the five Azure disk types available for virtual machine storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard SSD is a standard-performance managed disk type for session hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard SSD is a type of Azure managed disk offering moderate performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edb1f343516427f2303f45fae771d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Standard HDD">
  <data key="d0">Azure Standard HDD</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Standard HDD is one of the five Azure disk types, offering lower cost but lower performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard HDD is a basic managed disk type for session hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Standard HDD is a type of Azure managed disk offering basic performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edb1f343516427f2303f45fae771d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Azure Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Metrics is a monitoring tool used to identify disk throttling and performance bottlenecks in Azure environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001046</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Migrate And Modernize">
  <data key="d0">Azure Migrate And Modernize</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Migrate and Modernize evaluates on-premises or other cloud deployments and provides sizing suggestions for disks and VMs in Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001046</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Add-Azvhd">
  <data key="d0">Add-Azvhd</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Add-AzVHD is an Azure PowerShell command that automates VHD upload to managed disks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
