</node>
<node id="Disk Throttling">
  <data key="d0">Disk Throttling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disk throttling occurs when disk performance is limited, leading to suboptimal performance and increased latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Demand Bursting">
  <data key="d0">On-Demand Bursting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">On-demand bursting allows Premium SSD disks to handle short-term bursts of demand beyond their provisioned performance levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expand Without Downtime">
  <data key="d0">Expand Without Downtime</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Expand without downtime allows dynamic increase of storage capacity without deallocating attached VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b35a7e1a6cfd27f70308c05e1bbfe09e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ZRS Disks">
  <data key="d0">ZRS Disks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone-redundant storage disks that minimize the effect of availability zone failures and increase recoverability by allowing force-detach and reattach to different VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption At Host">
  <data key="d0">Encryption At Host</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end encryption that begins on the VM and flows through to attached disks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Site Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Site Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure managed solution for backup and disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Site Recovery is an Azure service used to replicate session hosts and set up virtual networks in failover regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-72c2b73044f2b48e2bd4429b378720d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Managed Disks">
  <data key="d0">Azure Managed Disks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure managed disks are block-level storage volumes managed by Azure that simplify storage management for Azure Virtual Machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure managed disks are virtual hard drives used by session hosts, available in Premium SSD, Standard SSD, and Standard HDD types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edb1f343516427f2303f45fae771d0c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Ultra Disk Storage">
  <data key="d0">Azure Ultra Disk Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Ultra Disk Storage is a high-performance disk type offering the highest uptime SLA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4075ae59294d213854a90d7e0f95059d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-disk-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription Filters">
  <data key="d0">Subscription Filters</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subscription filters reduce unnecessary processing by delivering only relevant events to consumers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Monitor Workbooks">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor Workbooks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor workbooks are used to create monitoring dashboards showing metrics like delivery success rates, retry counts, and processing latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor workbooks are used to create performance dashboards displaying latency trends, throughput rates, and processing time distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor Workbooks are used to develop operational runbooks documenting consumer group management, scaling steps, and troubleshooting procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor workbooks are used to develop operational runbooks for documenting procedures like consumer group management and troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db510f47656045373bcac562ba7e53ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9477f91dc0a48476ae389364456c73e9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-hubs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dead Letter Destinations">
  <data key="d0">Dead Letter Destinations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage locations for preserving undeliverable events, using Azure Storage queues or Azure Service Bus queues.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead letter destinations are configured storage locations for events that cannot be successfully delivered, with associated monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Grid">
  <data key="d0">Event Grid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Event Grid is a cloud-based messaging service designed for event-driven architectures, providing robust event routing, delivery, and management capabilities. It supports core constructs including topics, subscriptions, domains, and endpoints, enabling flexible event distribution across applications and services.

Event Grid offers features such as event batching, subscription filters, retry policies, dead letter destinations, and delivery monitoring. It supports security configurations including encryption, private endpoints, and other security controls. The service also provides geo-disaster recovery capabilities.

Azure Event Grid is available in multiple tiers, including Basic and Standard, each with different pricing models.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Grid is part of the Azure messaging ecosystem that integrates with Service Bus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7af6f86008720e63584837b73a9ec604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f08277df10a908d985f4ac74cf88b922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ea951af59993c2b22cf6dbc254d79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Schema Versioning">
  <data key="d0">Schema Versioning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Schema versioning is a practice for managing changes to event schemas across consumer deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drift Detection">
  <data key="d0">Drift Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Drift detection monitors deviations from desired subscription filters, retry policies, and security settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canary Event Publishing">
  <data key="d0">Canary Event Publishing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Canary event publishing is a production testing approach for validating event delivery and consumer health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a84d105f29ba765f53cc6dcefef77ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Batching">
  <data key="d0">Event Batching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Event batching delivers multiple events in single operations to reduce per-operation costs in Event Grid.&lt;SEP&gt;Event batching delivers multiple events in single operations to reduce per-operation costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Filtering">
  <data key="d0">Event Filtering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Event filtering applies filters at the subscription level to process only relevant events and eliminate costs of processing irrelevant events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Tags">
  <data key="d0">Resource Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource tags use consistent naming conventions for environment, application, business unit, cost center, and project to enable granular cost tracking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-420738f8bb67b56b01951ef9c163f45a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functions Premium Plans">
  <data key="d0">Functions Premium Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Functions premium plans provide automatic scaling capabilities for event consumer processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f08277df10a908d985f4ac74cf88b922</data>
