  <data key="d5">1777001157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Grid Data Sender">
  <data key="d0">Event Grid Data Sender</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Grid Data Sender is a built-in RBAC role assigned to applications that publish events to Event Grid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-935a5d6a7d3ef900c2c2a6bad10cdf79</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IP Address Filtering">
  <data key="d0">IP Address Filtering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">IP address filtering controls network access at the Event Grid topic level using allow lists and CIDR ranges, denying access by default.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Throughput Units">
  <data key="d0">Throughput Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Throughput units (TUs) in Event Grid Standard tier provide fixed capacity for sessions, message ingress, and topics with fixed hourly cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MQTT">
  <data key="d0">MQTT</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Message Queuing Telemetry Transport is a protocol used by Azure Event Grid for message delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;MQTT is a messaging protocol supported by Event Grid, with operations costing more than standard event operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3daa2e884924e39d9779d9c84c60b099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbb63c4dcd456a78e4886b5f325302</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resilience4j">
  <data key="d0">Resilience4j</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Resilience4j is a Java resilience library used to implement circuit breaker patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b6dcb04088b404ffb7108762ce20034</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-event-grid.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription Filtering">
  <data key="d0">Subscription Filtering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subscription filtering uses advanced syntax to deliver only relevant events, reducing traffic and processing overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b0629c90da136e31cc7058b5a6a724b</data>
