<node id="Multidimensional Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Multidimensional Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Multidimensional metrics provide real-time insights and alert configuration for Load Balancer monitoring and performance analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub-And-Spoke Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Hub-And-Spoke Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub-and-spoke architecture is a network topology where the hub is deployed first and changes less frequently than workloads in spoke networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Hub-and-spoke architecture is the networking topology used by Virtual WAN for scale and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cffe100ebb087468498365a5360ea32</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Event Schema">
  <data key="d0">Health Event Schema</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Health event schema is the schema used by Load Balancer resource logs to capture detailed records of events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session Persistence">
  <data key="d0">Session Persistence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session persistence directs requests from the same user to the same back-end server, optimizing performance but with reliability and load balancing tradeoffs.&lt;SEP&gt;Session persistence is a Load Balancer feature that consistently directs requests from the same client to the same back-end server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bac3ac1e7b8113e7254c6008979db0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001952</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inbound NAT Rules">
  <data key="d0">Inbound NAT Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Inbound NAT rules allow mapping IP addresses and ports to a back-end pool rather than to individual VMs, consolidating rules to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fe9f1b8e3eb203ebff19190e4bd21d4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
