  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Load Balancer SKU">
  <data key="d0">Standard Load Balancer SKU</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Standard Load Balancer SKU supports reliability features such as availability zones and multiregion load balancing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Standard Load Balancer SKU offers reliability features including availability zone support, multi-region traffic distribution, and larger back-end pool capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bffdea3a766285468bd7ae393d75002</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001954</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Global Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A global load balancer configuration uses a static anycast public IP to route client requests to the closest server instance across multiple regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UDP">
  <data key="d0">UDP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User Datagram Protocol (UDP) is a network protocol supported by Azure Load Balancer for Layer-4 load balancing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001955</data>
