</node>
<node id="TCP">
  <data key="d0">TCP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) is a network protocol supported by Azure Load Balancer for Layer-4 load balancing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127db8bd8dc9fb56e5514189bbd149e4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Tier">
  <data key="d0">Global Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The global tier in Standard Load Balancer uses geo-proximity distribution to serve user requests from the nearest region endpoint.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777001958</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Health">
  <data key="d0">Resource Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource health is a feature that monitors the health status of resources and informs about performance problems and outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource Health provides alerts for early warning of planned and unplanned events affecting SQL Managed Instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource Health provides alerts and events for monitoring Virtual WAN gateway connectivity and infrastructure status.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource Health is a category of alerting for Azure Virtual Desktop environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e2e1099d07e006869495c3c24dfc8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5158a76c261c507648b548ec947486da</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-load-balancer.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004902</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Control">
  <data key="d0">Application Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Control reduces the attack surface of Azure Local by controlling which drivers and apps are allowed to run.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMB Signing">
  <data key="d0">SMB Signing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SMB signing digitally signs SMB traffic to enhance data-in-transit protection and prevent relay attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMB Encryption">
  <data key="d0">SMB Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SMB encryption controls encryption of traffic between physical machines in an Azure Local instance on the storage network.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002055</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Arc">
  <data key="d0">Azure Arc</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Arc is a Microsoft service that extends Azure management capabilities to on-premises, multi-cloud, and edge environments. It is used by Azure Local to extend Azure capabilities to customer-owned infrastructure, providing management, monitoring, and operations that require outbound network access. Azure Arc has native integration in Azure Local edge products and is used to manage security configuration and compliance auditing for Azure Local, including built-in policy definitions for Arc-enabled workloads.

Azure Arc enables servers to be onboarded to Microsoft Sentinel and is part of Azure Local cost modeling. Beyond Azure Local, Azure Arc enables management of VMware infrastructure resources in Azure, including guest VMs running inside Azure VMware Solution private cloud, with support for guest management and Azure extension installation.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Arc extends Azure management capabilities to on-premises or multicloud environments, providing centralized server management and governance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d695b0d5275d5f3f66f5831b4118a711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
