</node>
<node id="Trusted Launch">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Launch</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trusted launch improves security of Gen 2 VMs using Secure Boot and virtual Trusted Platform Module.&lt;SEP&gt;Trusted Launch provides hardware-based security features including secure boot and virtual Trusted Platform Module (vTPM) for enhanced VM security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51f672aba79072f4ab0bff7c6abfa52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24da17048f52e4eee422a69ff4b58769</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storage Spaces Direct">
  <data key="d0">Storage Spaces Direct</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage Spaces Direct is a storage technology used within Azure Local for configuring volume fault tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage Spaces Direct is a storage technology in Azure Local that manages storage pools and enables in-place repair when physical disks fail.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Server Always On">
  <data key="d0">SQL Server Always On</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Server Always On is a high-availability pattern providing active/passive synchronous or asynchronous data replication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cce02fd292b03a1c7207cba11ed15e55</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002060</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ReFS">
  <data key="d0">ReFS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resilient File System (ReFS) is a file system that supports deduplication and compression features for storage optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DiskSpd">
  <data key="d0">DiskSpd</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">DiskSpd is a tool for testing workload storage performance using various command line parameters, measuring latency, throughput, and IOPs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMFleet">
  <data key="d0">VMFleet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMFleet is a tool for generating load and measuring the performance of a storage subsystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Way Mirroring">
  <data key="d0">Three-Way Mirroring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Three-way mirroring is a resiliency method for workload volumes requiring a minimum three-machine instance, providing maximum performance and resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All-Flash Storage">
  <data key="d0">All-Flash Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">All-flash (NVMe or SSD) based storage solutions designed for high-performance or low-latency workloads, maximizing storage efficiency by eliminating cache tiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insights">
  <data key="d0">Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insights is a monitoring feature for Azure Local that monitors performance of single or multiple instances simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdd0deaa1462aee92c407c1b8453db41</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Anti-Affinity Rules">
  <data key="d0">Workload Anti-Affinity Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Workload anti-affinity rules ensure VMs hosting multiple instances of the same service run on separate physical hosts, similar to availability sets in Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002066</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Way Mirror">
  <data key="d0">Three-Way Mirror</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Three-way mirror is a resiliency type for Azure Local instances with three or more machines, providing the highest resiliency and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-994006d21feeab794ea90c0dc1728c75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002066</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Update Manager">
  <data key="d0">Update Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Update Manager is a free tool for Azure Local instances and VMs for patching, updating, and other operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Update Manager is an Azure service for patching the Azure Local platform and managing OS, core agents, and services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002066</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AzureEdgeTelemetryAndDiagnostics">
  <data key="d0">AzureEdgeTelemetryAndDiagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AzureEdgeTelemetryAndDiagnostics is an extension installed by default on all Azure Local machines to share telemetry and diagnostic information securely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor Insights">
  <data key="d0">Monitor Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitor Insights enhances monitoring and alerting for Azure Local instances using native Azure capabilities, providing near real-time monitoring with customizable workbooks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Checker Tool">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Checker Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The environmental checker tool validates readiness of the target environment before deploying an Azure Local solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local Solution Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local Solution Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Local solution catalog provides the latest hardware OEM innovations for Azure Local instance deployments, including premium solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Windows Server Active Directory">
  <data key="d0">Windows Server Active Directory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Windows Server Active Directory is a prerequisite validated by the environmental checker tool for Azure Local deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Windows Server Active Directory is a directory service used for authentication and connection management with Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;Windows Server Active Directory is a directory service that integrates with Azure NetApp Files and is the only LDAP server supported by Azure NetApp Files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b09db71c55e81106668f400bcd89e89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Verification For VMs">
  <data key="d0">Azure Verification For VMs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure verification for VMs is a benefit enabling supported Azure-exclusive workloads to work outside the cloud, enabled by default on Azure Local 2311 or later.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002068</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Windows Server">
  <data key="d0">Windows Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Windows Server is a server operating system that can be licensed and activated on Azure Local VMs through subscription add-on or existing licenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002068</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local Solutions Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local Solutions Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Local Solutions Catalog is a certified list of validated machines, integrated systems, and premier solutions for Azure Local hardware.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bcc1cda0fd969bc80f928dbf3fb1acd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002068</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local Sizer Tool">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local Sizer Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Local sizer tool helps design and rightsize Azure Local instances during the design phase.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Local sizer tool is used during instance design phase to size instances based on workload capacity, performance, and resiliency requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002069</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Sovereignty">
  <data key="d0">Data Sovereignty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data sovereignty is a requirement that Azure Local helps address by keeping business systems and application data on-premises.&lt;SEP&gt;Data sovereignty refers to requirements ensuring data storage, processing, and access remain within specific jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local VMs">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local VMs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Local VMs are virtual machines deployed as workloads on the Azure Local platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4445edde79cb1986e3a57ab9302b4041</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Arc Jumpstart">
  <data key="d0">Azure Arc Jumpstart</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Arc Jumpstart is a resource for hands-on skilling, labs, training events, product demos, or proof-of-concept projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LocalBox">
  <data key="d0">LocalBox</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">LocalBox supports virtualized deployments of Azure Local for rapid testing and evaluation using nested virtualization in Azure VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Update Orchestrator">
  <data key="d0">Update Orchestrator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The update orchestrator is installed during initial Azure Local deployment and automates updates and management operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Local catalog lists validated hardware and integrated systems from OEM partner offerings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a6c7ad9dd0931003913cee8becffc2d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002070</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Local Baseline Reference Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Azure Local Baseline Reference Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A foundational architecture demonstrating key recommendations for Azure Local deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Planning">
  <data key="d0">Workload Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workload planning involves rightsizing capabilities and number of instance machines based on workload capacity requirements including vCPUs, memory, storage, and number of VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fda024896224771dc739306ae7edcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-local.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002071</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Storage Account">
  <data key="d0">Azure Storage Account</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Storage account is a storage resource that can receive exported data with immutability policies to protect against data tampering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commitment Tier">
  <data key="d0">Commitment Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Commitment tier is a billing model that offers lower rates in exchange for committing to a daily minimum of data collected in a Log Analytics workspace.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Export">
  <data key="d0">Data Export</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data export saves workspace data to alternate locations to protect against datacenter or region failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Data export sends data from a Log Analytics workspace to an Azure Storage account with immutability policies for compliance and long-term retention of audit data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transformation is a method to remove or obfuscate specific columns in collected data to maintain confidentiality on sensitive information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc4d1389b8b2d740cc491590de98ec6f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002157</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Analytics Workspace Insights">
  <data key="d0">Log Analytics Workspace Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Log Analytics Workspace Insights tracks ingestion volume, data caps, unresponsive log sources, and failed queries for workspace health monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics Workspace Insights is a tool for reviewing the amount of data collected in a workspace to identify trends and anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics Workspace Insights is a tool for tracking the health and performance of Log Analytics workspaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics Workspace Insights provides a unified view of usage, performance, health, agents, queries, and change log for Log Analytics workspaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f94f551ab29e43c1a22f727367fe189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ab50ed5aab47b600c04c6b913d6a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Collection Rules">
  <data key="d0">Data Collection Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data collection rules (DCRs) enable log multicasting to send critical data to multiple workspaces across different regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Data collection rules (DCRs) are configurations for collecting and routing monitoring data, designed with a single responsibility principle to minimize misconfiguration risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Collection Rules (DCRs) define what data to collect and how to transform it, ensuring only operationally valuable data is ingested.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Collection Rules (DCRs) define how data is collected and processed, specific to data source types within observability scopes.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Collection Rules (DCR) specify what data should be collected, how to transform it, and where to send it in Azure Monitor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f94f551ab29e43c1a22f727367fe189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8672b1e490ddaf66d06e5814d081ec72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Search Jobs">
  <data key="d0">Search Jobs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Search Jobs are asynchronous queries that run on any data in a Log Analytics workspace, including long-term retention data, creating new Analytics tables for further queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f94f551ab29e43c1a22f727367fe189</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Collection Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Data Collection Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Data collection endpoints (DCEs) are Azure resources that should be co-located with workload components and Log Analytics workspaces for optimal reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Collection Endpoints (DCEs) are deployed close to workloads to meet performance requirements for log data collection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f94f551ab29e43c1a22f727367fe189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8672b1e490ddaf66d06e5814d081ec72</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Multicasting">
  <data key="d0">Log Multicasting</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Log multicasting is a method to send critical data to multiple workspaces across different regions to ensure continuous access during regional failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Log multicasting is a method to send critical data to multiple workspaces across different regions to ensure workspace availability during regional failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8672b1e490ddaf66d06e5814d081ec72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federated Workspace Model">
  <data key="d0">Federated Workspace Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A federated workspace model uses multiple workspaces to provide high availability during regional failures for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b28f7bb04fd3a4329ab8ddf39e088c06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Query Auditing">
  <data key="d0">Log Query Auditing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Log query auditing tracks which users run queries in a workspace, recording details for each query to bolster security posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table Level RBAC">
  <data key="d0">Table Level RBAC</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Table level role-based access control grants users access to specific sets of tables across multiple resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ab1427ce079159adb889d9285c7e3c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Pricing">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Pricing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster pricing is a cost optimization method that aggregates ingestion volumes from multiple workspaces to achieve higher commitment tiers and reduce per-gigabyte ingestion costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Retention And Archiving">
  <data key="d0">Data Retention And Archiving</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data retention and archiving allows retaining data for up to seven years with occasional access through search jobs or data restoration, reducing long-term retention costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Summary Rules">
  <data key="d0">Summary Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Summary rules enable automated data summarization of high-volume log streams, reducing storage costs while maintaining analytical insights through aggregated datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Logs">
  <data key="d0">Basic Logs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basic logs configuration provides lower ingestion costs for tables used for debugging, troubleshooting, and auditing that are infrequently queried.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f85555293bf0c9da12094a059a2e42c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DCRs">
  <data key="d0">DCRs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data Collection Rules (DCRs) are configurations specific to data source types within observability scopes, separable by performance and events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f3e7854aa5a9772017d1a8685f93f69</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-log-analytics.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002171</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Model Registries">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Model Registries</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning model registries store and version machine learning models to track changes and maintain lineage with jobs and datasets used for training, supporting deployment strategies such as A/B releases, canary releases, and rollbacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Model Catalogs">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Model Catalogs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning model catalogs enable data science teams to discover, evaluate, and fine tune pretrained foundational machine learning models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Curated Environments">
  <data key="d0">Curated Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Curated environments are pre-created environments provided by Machine Learning that speed up deployment time, reduce latency, and improve training and deployment success rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Container For Pytorch">
  <data key="d0">Azure Container For Pytorch</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Container for PyTorch is a curated environment optimized for training large models on Machine Learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Compute Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Compute Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning compute clusters are Azure resources for training and batch inferencing workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine Learning compute clusters provide autoscaling capabilities and the ability to scale out workloads that support horizontal scaling for model training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Online Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Online endpoints are deployment targets for machine learning models that can be monitored and autoscaled via Azure Monitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Online endpoints are deployment targets for machine learning models that can be monitored and automatically scaled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Drift">
  <data key="d0">Data Drift</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data drift refers to changes in input data that can lead to a decline in a model's performance over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Data drift refers to changes in input data that can lead to a decline in model performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Data drift refers to changes in data distributions over time that need to be observed for maintaining model performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Data drift occurs when input data changes over time, making the model outdated.&lt;SEP&gt;Data drift refers to changes in data over time that can affect model accuracy and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-079fc4b2f13a7566fa50aa2ae024b4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88dee01d0a30636bf4119d50523dfef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Checkpointing">
  <data key="d0">Model Checkpointing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Model checkpointing periodically saves the state of a machine learning model during training for restoration in case of failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Compute Instances">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Compute Instances</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning compute instances are Azure resources used within Azure Machine Learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Online Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Managed Online Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Managed online endpoints are an inferencing option in Azure Machine Learning that supports release strategies like blue-green deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Virtual Machine Tier">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Virtual Machine Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dedicated virtual machine tier for compute clusters ensures batch jobs are not preempted, unlike low-priority virtual machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
