</node>
<node id="RAG">
  <data key="d0">RAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) is a technique for generative AI applications supported by Microsoft Foundry.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is a solution design for semantic retrieval using purpose-built vector indexes for grounding data.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is a design pattern used to manage complexity in workflows involving multiple AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is an AI technique that combines retrieval of grounding data with generative AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is an implementation approach where documents are chunked, paired with embeddings, and stored in an index for model consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is a solution design approach for refining data design through preprocessing, selecting embeddings, and chunking to create index-suitable data.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is a method that uses grounding data to enhance AI model responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89fc4e111ee01c8ccd6e29d9313ca90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd17378f06c53d63988ae606c0c8070e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/grounding-data-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/mlops-genaiops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003795</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Compute Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Compute clusters provide the ability to improve performance by scaling out workloads that support horizontal scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Compute clusters provide significant control over hardware and are tuned for parallel or distributed training in Azure Machine Learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e08b75063568eb6355420ca8b8527f53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f37224876d004b6edc267c88180a8c61</data>
