</node>
<node id="GPU">
  <data key="d0">GPU</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GPUs are better for models with high number of variables benefiting from higher parallelism, used in deep learning, image/video processing, and scientific simulations.&lt;SEP&gt;GPUs (Graphics Processing Units) are specialized hardware used in HPC for molecular modeling, AI training, and massively parallel calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd64e0b4a0a0a0b146d62e2b5b760fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809d253c9aab5017c77e2a8b92279866</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/get-started-overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Exfiltration Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Data Exfiltration Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data exfiltration prevention involves implementing measures to limit inbound and outbound requirements, such as creating service endpoint policies to filter egress virtual network traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd64e0b4a0a0a0b146d62e2b5b760fbc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Reserved VM Instances">
  <data key="d0">Azure Reserved VM Instances</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Reserved VM Instances allow prepayment for virtual machine usage over one to three years, providing discounts compared to pay-as-you-go pricing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca37c53f740f2b0fa041e3df2d737be8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Termination Policies">
  <data key="d0">Early Termination Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Early termination policies limit the duration of training runs or terminate nonperforming runs early to save costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca37c53f740f2b0fa041e3df2d737be8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low-Priority Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Low-Priority Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Low-priority virtual machines leverage surplus Azure capacity to provide large compute power at low cost for batch workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca37c53f740f2b0fa041e3df2d737be8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Catalogs And Registries">
  <data key="d0">Model Catalogs And Registries</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning model catalogs and registries store, version, and share machine learning assets, supporting A/B testing and deployment strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca37c53f740f2b0fa041e3df2d737be8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-machine-learning.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Tenant Customer-Managed Keys">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Tenant Customer-Managed Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A key management approach allowing organizations to manage encryption keys in their own tenant's Azure Key Vault even when the ANF account resides in a different Azure AD tenant.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-tenant customer-managed keys keep encryption keys under the customer's control in their tenant's Key Vault, even when the Azure NetApp Files account resides in another tenant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LDAP Over TLS">
  <data key="d0">LDAP Over TLS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAP over TLS is used for secure directory queries when integrating Azure NetApp Files with Active Directory.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAP over TLS provides secure directory queries when integrating with Active Directory.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAP over TLS secures communication between an Azure NetApp Files volume and the Windows Server Active Directory LDAP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AES-256 Encryption">
  <data key="d0">AES-256 Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AES-256 encryption is an industry-standard encryption method used by Azure NetApp Files via CryptoMod to generate encryption keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002356</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="File Access Logs">
  <data key="d0">File Access Logs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Logs capturing details of every file operation including user, file, time, and action on SMB, NFSv4.1, and dual-protocol volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;Logs providing file-level telemetry including user, operation, path, and timestamp for auditing and threat detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc4795580f532b2b4baa2c23d716389</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NTFS">
  <data key="d0">NTFS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New Technology File System (NTFS) is a security style used with SMB shares providing NTFS ACLs for granular file security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACLs">
  <data key="d0">ACLs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Access Control Lists used to limit access to necessary users.&lt;SEP&gt;Access control lists provide granular file security in NFSv4.1 and SMB environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c987aaa4d67de5353b754cdd58a2e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc4795580f532b2b4baa2c23d716389</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002358</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Vmware Solution">
  <data key="d0">Azure Vmware Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure VMware Solution is a cloud service that integrates with Azure NetApp Files to increase storage capacity without extra nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure VMware Solution is a cloud service that can be extended with Azure NetApp Files data stores to expand storage capacity beyond vSAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818813f6dc34b0174c539777eb18946d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002360</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAP">
  <data key="d0">SAP</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP is one of the world's leading producers of enterprise application software for business management and customer operations. The company develops a broad portfolio of applications and platforms, including SAP NetWeaver, SAP HANA, SAP Fiori, SAP Business Technology Platform, and tools like SAP Quick Sizer.

SAP workloads and applications are a major focus in the context of Azure platform optimization and design guidance. SAP workloads can be deployed on Azure infrastructure, leveraging services such as Azure NetApp Files to take advantage of high network throughput and reduce total cost of ownership (TCO). Additionally, the Microsoft Sentinel solution is specifically designed to protect SAP workloads running on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e43dcd642e61ee23ed8647dbc84d2290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f05e5f46b39ac0c01364030a2aca2729&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7d5e1cf32da816941912bb8333b6c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cda3aeb76002824742103c912685940&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b717f28742ad10a742194bed4e9e384e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277c3ba6003c8f8d8d862f28e5e221c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/get-started.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oracle">
  <data key="d0">Oracle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oracle is a vendor whose workloads are optimized for Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;Oracle database workloads can leverage Azure NetApp Files for higher network throughput and reduced TCO.&lt;SEP&gt;Oracle is an enterprise database workload supported by Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;Oracle is a database used by SAP Applications and supported by Azure Backup for native backups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93569c602aff04a9136b9c5a0562189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818813f6dc34b0174c539777eb18946d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005930</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Siemens Teamcenter">
  <data key="d0">Siemens Teamcenter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Siemens Teamcenter is a product lifecycle management (PLM) software that can use Azure NetApp Files as a storage solution for cost optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Region Replication">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Region Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-region replication minimizes data transfer by replicating only changed blocks across regions, creating a low restore point objective.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-region replication uses snapshot technology to replicate Azure NetApp Files instances across Azure regions for disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-region replication is a disaster recovery feature in Azure NetApp Files for replicating data across regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-region replication is a disaster recovery method in Azure NetApp Files that replicates data between regions without additional infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-region replication keeps backups of data stores in a globally redundant format for extra reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4057517613635840bc1340d6413748b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818813f6dc34b0174c539777eb18946d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Zone Replication">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Zone Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-zone replication minimizes data transfer and replicates only changed blocks across availability zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-zone replication replicates Azure NetApp Files instances across availability zones for local disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-zone replication replicates data between availability zones as a cost-optimized disaster recovery solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4057517613635840bc1340d6413748b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d9c66189ea1f2f564261486eac199f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Volume Shaping">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Volume Shaping</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic volume shaping provides nondisruptive volume resizing and service-level changes to meet performance requirements in real time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short-Term Clones">
  <data key="d0">Short-Term Clones</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Short-term clones create temporary, space-efficient volume copies for development, testing, and disaster recovery validation.&lt;SEP&gt;Short-term clones provide temporary volume copies with automatic cleanup capabilities for rapid, space-efficient testing and development workflows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1253bfacbc52856eb91edc734f4278e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93569c602aff04a9136b9c5a0562189</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Service Level">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Service Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible service level decouples storage capacity and throughput to eliminate overprovisioning and match throughput to workload needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible Service Level is a feature of Azure NetApp Files that allows on-the-fly throughput control for volumes without downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible Service Level (FSL) decouples storage capacity from throughput in Azure NetApp Files, allowing independent adjustment of volume throughput without increasing capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Flexible Service Level (FSL) allows fine-grained control over throughput, enabling users to dial performance up or down to optimize cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93569c602aff04a9136b9c5a0562189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002362</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure NetApp Files Performance Calculator">
  <data key="d0">Azure NetApp Files Performance Calculator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool for understanding how workload needs match with Azure NetApp Files capacity and service levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large Volumes">
  <data key="d0">Large Volumes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large volumes in Azure NetApp Files provide more capacity and performance but have minimum requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual QoS">
  <data key="d0">Manual QoS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual QoS allows configuring capacity pool performance independently from volume capacity, enabling high performance for small datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAP HANA">
  <data key="d0">SAP HANA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP HANA is an enterprise database workload supported by Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is an SAP in-memory database platform with high availability configurations on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is an in-memory database platform and an example of an OLTP workload.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is a database platform supported by Azure Backup through the Backint connector.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is a database system with specific storage configuration guidelines and backup support.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is a database platform supported by the SAP on Azure Deployment Automation Framework.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP HANA is an SAP database platform that supports SSO integration with Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93569c602aff04a9136b9c5a0562189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f05e5f46b39ac0c01364030a2aca2729&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7d5e1cf32da816941912bb8333b6c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35191f2c89cbaf908dd883ea878f01b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126bab5448fd1206151f95e91bdb3453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3990bf7b05c6dbb2810bbc7fcbbe492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cda3aeb76002824742103c912685940</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMB3 Encryption">
  <data key="d0">SMB3 Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SMB3 encryption is a security feature that Azure policies can enforce for Azure NetApp Files SMB volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;SMB3 encryption is a security requirement enforced by Azure policy for Azure NetApp Files SMB volumes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd1fa944006eb6acbe6c4bca0b730e7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f32a51ff5e5aa4e53c3b61b2c6b81b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LDAP">
  <data key="d0">LDAP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lightweight Directory Access Protocol is used for access authorization to Azure NetApp Files data.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAP is a general-purpose, network-based directory service used to locate network objects across diverse platforms, supporting millions of user and group objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4057517613635840bc1340d6413748b3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002364</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra Domain Services">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra Domain Services</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra Domain Services is used for access authorization to Azure NetApp Files data.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Domain Services is a domain service supported by Azure NetApp Files LDAP integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Domain Services is an identity service option for Azure Virtual Desktop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4057517613635840bc1340d6413748b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-netapp-files.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004854</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cool Access">
  <data key="d0">Cool Access</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cool access is an Azure NetApp Files feature that tiers infrequently accessed data to lower-cost Azure storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Cool access transparently tiers infrequently accessed data to lower-cost Azure storage, reducing storage costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cool access is a feature that transparently tiers infrequently accessed data blocks to lower-cost Azure storage to optimize costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45ad5e579cc0c475ae93c1c16691c70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818813f6dc34b0174c539777eb18946d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc7550f9959f9fd3d6c289785451692</data>
