<node id="Active Directory Domain Services">
  <data key="d0">Active Directory Domain Services</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) is used for access authorization to Azure NetApp Files.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) is an identity service option for Azure Virtual Desktop environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) provides domain joining for Azure Virtual Desktop VMs and must sync with Microsoft Entra ID.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) is a directory service for managing domains and forests in Windows environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) is used in multi-forest configurations for Azure Virtual Desktop.&lt;SEP&gt;AD DS is an identity service; standalone AD DS identities without Microsoft Entra ID are not supported for Azure Virtual Desktop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4057517613635840bc1340d6413748b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161fa262de0d263c9842f3ec1f7a7795&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0766d4ac6781acc119de13f144078bfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76733dbb26e72d185a328617ee81949b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020</data>
