<node id="Dead Letter Queues">
  <data key="d0">Dead Letter Queues</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dead letter queues isolate undeliverable or poison messages from the main message flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead letter queues prevent poison messages from blocking healthy message processing and support operational troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb40dfedb445538dcaca461fef2278f3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Replication">
  <data key="d0">Active Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active replication is a region-level redundancy pattern where the client sends every message to both regions, receivers listen on both, and messages require unique identifiers to discard duplicates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Passive Replication">
  <data key="d0">Passive Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Passive replication is a region-level redundancy pattern where the client sends to one region and falls back to the other on error, reducing duplicate messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e33a34bfd8e4ddf2903635a31b614a99</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002478</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
