  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Native Azure SDK">
  <data key="d0">Native Azure SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Native Azure SDK provides complete access to Service Bus features with Azure-specific optimizations and optimal performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e70d002685d5e46f8ea08751d291ae2b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Bus Premium Tier">
  <data key="d0">Service Bus Premium Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Premium tier of Service Bus provides dedicated messaging units with predictable performance, advanced features like larger message sizes, and auto-scaling capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Express Entities">
  <data key="d0">Express Entities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Express Entities store messages in memory for enhanced performance, configured through the EnableExpress property with trade-offs between performance and durability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002491</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session-Based Messaging">
  <data key="d0">Session-Based Messaging</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Session-based messaging ensures ordered processing for related messages but limits parallelism to one active receiver per session.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002491</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prefetch">
  <data key="d0">Prefetch</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Prefetch settings enable clients to receive multiple messages proactively, reducing the impact of network latency on message processing throughput.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-498530bb6096692fd24e326f3f0018c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002491</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PeekLock">
  <data key="d0">PeekLock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PeekLock mode ensures messages are not lost if a receiver fails by keeping messages available until lock expiration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b49c55356fee42f19cd603d7edc0b8b6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-bus.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002492</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Fabric">
  <data key="d0">Service Fabric</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Fabric is an Azure platform for deploying and managing microservices and clusters, with capabilities for networking, security, and cost optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Fabric is an Azure platform for deploying and managing microservices and containers, supporting clusters, health monitoring, and CI/CD deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Service Fabric is an Azure platform for deploying and managing microservices and container-based workloads, supporting multiple programming models and scaling mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d0c804921f6d35d43cf53a8ca5e01fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c34815c939645bbbdf7eeec0352ec98f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender Antivirus">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender Antivirus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender Antivirus is a security tool that can impact performance on Service Fabric Windows VMs.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender Antivirus is used for vulnerability detection with features like daily scans on Windows machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender Antivirus is a security tool used for daily scans on Windows machines to detect potential threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Defender Antivirus helps protect VMs in Azure Virtual Desktop environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d0c804921f6d35d43cf53a8ca5e01fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612bbe95aa1cd140db2ec8a1f9529c91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f0ffcfda5392d2501f62dadf04b020</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accelerated Networking">
  <data key="d0">Accelerated Networking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Accelerated networking enables a high-performance path that bypasses the host, reducing latency, jitter, and CPU usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Accelerated networking is a feature enabled on host machines to reduce latency and increase response time for SDK operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Accelerated networking enables SR-IOV to a VM, greatly improving networking performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Accelerated networking is a VM capability that improves throughput and reduces network latency for session hosts.&lt;SEP&gt;Accelerated Networking improves network performance by bypassing the physical switch, providing improved latency, jitter, and CPU utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d0c804921f6d35d43cf53a8ca5e01fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a2c3c1077bbf94e3d952e330c6f922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eb78b84d41322da30efb8dd70aafc73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea3b54c45d951e732cca09b525690b9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/networking-and-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005955</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliable Services">
  <data key="d0">Reliable Services</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reliable Services is a programming model in Service Fabric that keeps services active during system failures, network problems, or service malfunctions, preserving state for stateful services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af193ca86913bf526ac2830012c0e345</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
