</node>
<node id="Cluster">
  <data key="d0">Cluster</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A cluster is a network-connected set of virtual or physical machines onto which Service Fabric resources are deployed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af193ca86913bf526ac2830012c0e345</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Fabric Explorer">
  <data key="d0">Service Fabric Explorer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Fabric Explorer is a tool for managing Service Fabric clusters; cluster client certificates should not be distributed among its users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Access Control List">
  <data key="d0">Access Control List</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An ACL applied to client certificates provides an extra level of authentication for controlling access to Service Fabric clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Encipherment Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Data Encipherment Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A separate data encipherment certificate is used to encrypt values when distributing secrets via the Service Fabric Secret Store, isolating certificates to reduce risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Governance">
  <data key="d0">Resource Governance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource requests and limits govern resource usage across nodes in a Service Fabric cluster to prevent one service from consuming too many resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource governance involves implementing monitoring and enforcement to ensure tenant resource usage stays within expected limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cc3bfd562c976605e6ae1bf0c63a873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-service-fabric.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
