<node id="Serverless Tier">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Serverless tier automatically pauses and scales compute resources based on workload demand, billing per second of compute used, suitable for intermittent usage patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperscale Tier">
  <data key="d0">Hyperscale Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hyperscale tier uses storage snapshots for zero downtime and rapid recovery when the Business Critical tier isn't practical.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hyperscale tier provides cloud-native architecture with independently scalable compute and storage, supporting the widest variety of applications without extra SQL licensing costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a363f9bc0a4fd35ef60bc7f3c1bce53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c</data>
