<node id="Query Store">
  <data key="d0">Query Store</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The query store continuously collects detailed query information to simplify performance troubleshooting by diagnosing query plan changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Query Store is the primary tool for workload analysis and index optimization in SQL Managed Instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Query Store is the primary tool for identifying regressed queries and plan changes in SQL Managed Instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Query Store is a performance monitoring tool used to identify regressed queries and plan changes in SQL Managed Instance databases.&lt;SEP&gt;Query store tracks query performance over time, helping find longest running and most resource-intensive queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Memory Database Objects">
  <data key="d0">In-Memory Database Objects</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">In-memory technologies enhance workload performance for high-performance OLTP applications and real-time analytics, potentially reducing database costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADO.NET">
  <data key="d0">ADO.NET</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ADO.NET is a database driver that enables connection pooling by default for Azure SQL Database.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c70229b1bcbf083a0dcea43a7ae158bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Critical Tier">
  <data key="d0">Business Critical Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Business Critical tier offers the highest reliability guarantees for critical workloads in SQL Database.&lt;SEP&gt;The Business Critical tier is a service tier not supported by instance pools.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Critical tier is a service tier offering secondary replicas for read offload and higher TempDB allocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logical Server">
  <data key="d0">Logical Server</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A logical server manages databases in Azure SQL Database, with each single database having its own set of resources managed via a logical server.&lt;SEP&gt;A logical server is the level at which sign-ins, firewall rules, auditing rules, and threat detection policies are centrally administered for collections of databases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failover Groups">
  <data key="d0">Failover Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failover groups automate failover from primary to secondary database instances with read-write and read-only listener endpoints that remain unchanged during geo-failovers.&lt;SEP&gt;Failover groups are used alongside active geo-replication and zone-redundancy to enhance database availability in Azure SQL Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Failover groups provide geo-replication and automatic failover capabilities for Azure SQL Managed Instance.&lt;SEP&gt;Failover groups replicate all user databases as a unit to a geo-secondary instance in another region, providing cross-region disaster recovery with DNS-based endpoint redirection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7fca38ac08e844d0fae7a5f7036423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Database Firewall Rules">
  <data key="d0">SQL Database Firewall Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Database firewall rules can be configured at the database level and server level to control network access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Always Encrypted With Secure Enclaves">
  <data key="d0">Always Encrypted With Secure Enclaves</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Always Encrypted with secure enclaves extends Always Encrypted to protect highly sensitive information like credit card and social security numbers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51a42def26d6149ba32bd2654d702dd4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-database.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failover Group">
  <data key="d0">Failover Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failover groups provide disaster recovery capabilities with standby replicas that support failovers, backups, and maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standby Replica">
  <data key="d0">Standby Replica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A license-free standby replica is a secondary instance in a failover group used exclusively for disaster recovery, supporting failovers, backups, and maintenance but not production connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002762</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stop/Start Schedules">
  <data key="d0">Stop/Start Schedules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stop/start schedules allow stopping General Purpose instances during predictable idle periods to eliminate vCore and licensing charges while retaining data and backup storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0428e305303dcb842ea973ff0a9c850a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For SQL">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For SQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for SQL provides threat protection including vulnerability assessment, injection alerts, brute-force detection, and unusual access pattern alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002764</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TDE">
  <data key="d0">TDE</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparent Data Encryption protects data at rest using customer-managed keys stored in Azure Key Vault.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002765</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Agent">
  <data key="d0">SQL Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Agent is a SQL Managed Instance feature for job automation that requires risk assessment and should be disabled if unused to prevent privilege escalation.&lt;SEP&gt;SQL Agent is a built-in job scheduler in SQL Managed Instance for database maintenance and operational tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;SQL Agent is a native feature of SQL Managed Instance used for scheduling index maintenance, statistics updates, and consistency checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002767</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NSG Rules">
  <data key="d0">NSG Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Security Group rules control inbound traffic to the SQL Managed Instance subnet using a deny-by-default approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2db34598644f37a302573882b84524ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002768</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Management Views">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Management Views</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic management views (DMVs) are SQL-native diagnostics used for observability of SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="T-SQL">
  <data key="d0">T-SQL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">T-SQL compatibility differences must be validated before schema deployment to SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Events">
  <data key="d0">Extended Events</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Extended events are SQL-native diagnostics used alongside DMVs and Query Store for SQL Managed Instance observability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Cluster">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Cluster</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual cluster health indicators detect infrastructure-level problems affecting SQL Managed Instance availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defb38181cf95696eca523469c9e1024</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Server Enterprise Edition">
  <data key="d0">SQL Server Enterprise Edition</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Server Enterprise Edition is the database engine that Azure SQL Managed Instance is compatible with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002772</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Broker">
  <data key="d0">Service Broker</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Broker is an instance-scoped feature supported by Azure SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002773</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CLR Integration">
  <data key="d0">CLR Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common language runtime (CLR) integration is an instance-scoped feature supported by Azure SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77a08381ef2f6c3a3cbd1e048130bad2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002774</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maintenance Windows">
  <data key="d0">Maintenance Windows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maintenance windows shift planned failover events to predictable low-traffic periods to reduce impact on users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002775</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Redundant Backup Storage">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Redundant Backup Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-redundant backup storage maintains backup copies in a paired region, enabling recovery to any Azure region during a regional disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-redundant backup storage enables recovery to any Azure region during a regional disaster without depending on failover groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Instance Link">
  <data key="d0">Managed Instance Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Managed Instance link offers an alternative replication path for hybrid environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dffaff7bec32455c14addc7b21c4afa3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002776</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="License-Free Standby Replicas">
  <data key="d0">License-Free Standby Replicas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">License-free standby replicas are failover group secondaries designated for disaster recovery only, eliminating licensing charges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server Auditing">
  <data key="d0">Server Auditing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Server auditing captures sign-in activity and completed queries for SQL Managed Instance, supporting dual destinations and immutable storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stop/Start">
  <data key="d0">Stop/Start</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stop/start is a feature on General Purpose instances that eliminates compute and licensing charges during predictable idle periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99ff69f495aed35c047df8c9f7f551df</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TempDB">
  <data key="d0">TempDB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">TempDB is a shared temporary database resource in SQL Managed Instance with fixed allocation that cannot be modified.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Governor">
  <data key="d0">Resource Governor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource Governor controls CPU, memory, and I/O allocation across workloads sharing an instance to address noisy-neighbor risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In-Memory OLTP">
  <data key="d0">In-Memory OLTP</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">In-memory OLTP is a feature on the Business Critical tier for high-throughput workloads that eliminates latch contention and reduces CPU overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Next-Gen General Purpose">
  <data key="d0">Next-Gen General Purpose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Next-gen General Purpose is a service tier offering instance-level IOPS provisioning and flexible memory allocation independent from vCore count.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-gen General Purpose is an updated General Purpose tier where IOPS scale at the instance level based on reserved storage rather than per file.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redirect Connection Type">
  <data key="d0">Redirect Connection Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Redirect connection type routes traffic directly to the hosting node after initial authentication, reducing per-query latency for virtual network-local connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f2023b0dcac7ae7c7d25fc08064528b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Critical">
  <data key="d0">Business Critical</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business Critical is a service tier offering local storage, per-vCore IOPS provisioning, and a built-in readable secondary replica for read-only workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002778</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Purpose">
  <data key="d0">General Purpose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General Purpose is a service tier with file-size-dependent IOPS scaling and remote storage architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Database Projects">
  <data key="d0">SQL Database Projects</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL database projects validate T-SQL compatibility and identify unsupported syntax before production deployment targeting SQL Managed Instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-101349d8f262064be3735fbc48d13b8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002779</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Security Baseline For Azure SQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Security Baseline For Azure SQL</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure security baseline for Azure SQL provides foundational security controls for SQL Managed Instance configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8cca5d0852b439b0c20120d19e126b0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-sql-managed-instance.md</data>
