<node id="Subdomain Takeover">
  <data key="d0">Subdomain Takeover</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subdomain takeover occurs when a DNS record points to a deprovisioned Azure resource, allowing traffic redirection to malicious sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-257827ee036f98e6274522ad2bfee550</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002854</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic View">
  <data key="d0">Traffic View</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Traffic View is a dashboard feature showing client connection locations and latency, incurring extra costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-257827ee036f98e6274522ad2bfee550</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002854</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic Manager Profile">
  <data key="d0">Traffic Manager Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Traffic Manager profile is a core deployment component that specifies traffic-routing methods and can be combined for sophisticated routing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmission Control Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Transmission Control Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TCP is a protocol used by Traffic Manager to determine the availability of endpoints for non-HTTP applications.&lt;SEP&gt;TCP is used by Traffic Manager to determine endpoint availability for non-HTTP applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a76b7951c5b546531ebdfe1e8a4a70df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4889043b463029eef941a26e276c8840</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-traffic-manager.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic View Dashboard">
  <data key="d0">Traffic View Dashboard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Traffic view dashboard provides insights about client connection locations and associated latency for Traffic Manager profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;A dashboard for analyzing the performance of traffic in Traffic Manager.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2230ce3d7cb1e253eb90d2592e57fab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c2320d6f192d51ba7461cdb73ef6e1</data>
