  <data key="d0">RADIUS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Remote Authentication Dial-In User Service (RADIUS) authentication integrates with existing infrastructure for point-to-site VPN authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Security Baseline For Virtual WAN">
  <data key="d0">Azure Security Baseline For Virtual WAN</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure security baseline for Virtual WAN covers hub security, gateway configuration, routing security, and connection encryption controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de21122336bd114f1583106e238ec656</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Router">
  <data key="d0">Hub Router</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub router is a Virtual WAN component that routes inter-hub and spoke-to-spoke traffic with configurable routing infrastructure units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f3f86dbbc0e68845a4cfbd563dcaafe</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GCMAES256">
  <data key="d0">GCMAES256</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GCMAES256 is an IPsec encryption algorithm recommended for site-to-site VPN connections to reduce CPU overhead and maximize throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;GCMAES256 is a custom IPsec policy setting that reduces CPU overhead and supports higher throughput on VPN connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f3f86dbbc0e68845a4cfbd563dcaafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142487c37cb4da71ab0fecf01ad7e10b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Routing Preference">
  <data key="d0">Hub Routing Preference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub routing preference is a configuration setting that can be set to ExpressRoute, VPN Gateway, or AS Path for optimizing spoke-to-spoke traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f3f86dbbc0e68845a4cfbd563dcaafe</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Hub">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual hub is a component of Virtual WAN that has effective routes in routing tables and connects to on-premises and cloud resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-142487c37cb4da71ab0fecf01ad7e10b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual WAN Standard SKU">
  <data key="d0">Virtual WAN Standard SKU</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Virtual WAN Standard SKU provides zone redundancy, advanced routing, and hub-to-hub connectivity for production deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Continuity Testing">
  <data key="d0">Business Continuity Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Business continuity testing involves simulating region failures, circuit failures, parallel path scenarios, and BGP route advertisement during failover events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant SKU">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant SKU</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone-redundant SKU provides automatic distribution of gateway instances across availability zones for fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active configuration creates separate tunnels to each VPN gateway instance with BGP peering for immediate failover without convergence delay.&lt;SEP&gt;Active-active configuration allows critical application components to continue operating during datacenter failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global VPN Profile">
  <data key="d0">Global VPN Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Global VPN profile provides automatic hub selection for point-to-site connections, directing clients to the nearest available hub.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AS Path Prepending">
  <data key="d0">AS Path Prepending</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">AS path prepending is a BGP traffic engineering technique used to control traffic distribution across ExpressRoute circuits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Routing Infrastructure Units">
  <data key="d0">Hub Routing Infrastructure Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual hub routing infrastructure units should be set above baseline to accommodate growth and prevent the 25-minute scaling delay from affecting connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Scale Units">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Scale Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway scale units determine VPN and ExpressRoute gateway throughput capacity and require maintenance windows to change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-To-Site Address Pool">
  <data key="d0">Point-To-Site Address Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The point-to-site address pool should be sized to support double the expected user count to prevent exhaustion during gateway redistribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c60b5ebd31506f4de3e92091b80399f0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002991</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Routing Intent">
  <data key="d0">Routing Intent</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing intent automatically routes traffic through a security solution deployed in the virtual hub.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Route Tables">
  <data key="d0">Custom Route Tables</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom route tables match defined security zones to prevent unauthorized traffic between segmented zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777002992</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure VPN Client">
  <data key="d0">Azure VPN Client</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure VPN Client is deployed to user devices with a profile that authenticates through Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22d333e97696a760da77cbcd035a0d29</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/azure-virtual-wan.md</data>
