  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalized Ru Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Normalized Ru Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Normalized RU consumption is a metric measuring percentage usage of provisioned throughput on a database or container.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b18016c0695a884e7aacb8b1c571837</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For Azure Cosmos DB">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For Azure Cosmos DB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for Azure Cosmos DB detects attempts to exploit databases, including SQL injections and suspicious access patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4ef1aec0a62de4cc107952af4e1f676</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parameterized Queries">
  <data key="d0">Parameterized Queries</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Parameterized queries help protect against injection attacks and other security vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4ef1aec0a62de4cc107952af4e1f676</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Network Endpoints">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Network Endpoints</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual network service endpoints and rules limit access to Azure Cosmos DB accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4ef1aec0a62de4cc107952af4e1f676</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003074</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexing Policy">
  <data key="d0">Indexing Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexing policy in Azure Cosmos DB affects data storage cost and query performance, and should be considered alongside partition key selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Indexing policy in Azure Cosmos DB controls which paths are indexed, affecting RU consumption and query performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Indexing policy defines which fields are indexed in Azure Cosmos DB, affecting query performance and throughput costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4ef1aec0a62de4cc107952af4e1f676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e48c686ed9dcbf1ebc4bd457a81b5e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a99a5a991c44794d4415bc58af98647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003074</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmos DB SDK">
  <data key="d0">Cosmos DB SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cosmos DB SDK is a client library with built-in transient fault handling, retry logic, custom error handling, and diagnostics logging capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003075</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backup">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backup</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous backup enables point-in-time restore, recovery from accidental operations, and restoring deleted resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous backup is a backup configuration option in Azure Cosmos DB that supports point-in-time restore and recovery from accidental destructive operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c24295afcc6630eeee9c761977e6d4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple-Region Replication">
  <data key="d0">Multiple-Region Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple-region replication is a strategy for distributing Azure Cosmos DB accounts across multiple Azure regions to improve resilience and reduce latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9532ce6b51cab52bfc6f5e88ba579fc8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003076</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bulk Operations">
  <data key="d0">Bulk Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bulk operations involve multiple insert, replace, or upsert operations where disabling indexing can improve speed and resource utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89a2c3c1077bbf94e3d952e330c6f922</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003078</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subqueries">
  <data key="d0">Subqueries</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subqueries are used strategically to optimize queries by filtering arrays before joining them, increasing efficiency of self-join expressions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89a2c3c1077bbf94e3d952e330c6f922</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Managed Failover">
  <data key="d0">Service-Managed Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Service-managed failover allows Azure Cosmos DB to automatically change the write region of a multiple-region account to preserve availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90c24295afcc6630eeee9c761977e6d4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Level">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency levels in Azure Cosmos DB balance data consistency, availability, performance, and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e48c686ed9dcbf1ebc4bd457a81b5e7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/cosmos-db.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
