  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Index Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Index Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Index tuning analyzes tracked queries and provides recommendations for creating or dropping indexes to improve performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligent Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Intelligent Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligent tuning continuously monitors and dynamically adapts the database to the workload automatically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PgBouncer">
  <data key="d0">PgBouncer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PgBouncer is a connection pooling tool that optimizes database resource utilization and connection management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grafana Dashboards">
  <data key="d0">Grafana Dashboards</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Built-in Grafana dashboards in Azure portal show CPU usage, storage, active connections, and query throughput with zero-setup monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-330ebc42a023add05f25dea08e51afc6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Row-Level Security">
  <data key="d0">Row-Level Security</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Row-level security is a PostgreSQL feature allowing administrators to define policies controlling how specific rows of data display and operate for roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Row-level security is a method of enforcing authorization at the database row level, requiring user identity propagation to the data store.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Throttling">
  <data key="d0">Connection Throttling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Connection throttling limits repeated connection attempts from the same IP address to protect databases from malicious sign-in attempts and DDoS attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Managed Keys">
  <data key="d0">Customer Managed Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer managed keys (CMKs) provide full control of encryption key lifecycle including key rotation to align with corporate policies for data encryption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92a07b964260a4bef1cc690bb26c2030</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/postgresql.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Custom Script Extension">
  <data key="d0">Azure Custom Script Extension</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Custom Script Extension downloads and runs scripts on Virtual Machines for post-deployment configuration and management tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Custom Script Extension for Windows and Linux downloads and runs scripts on Virtual Machines for post-deployment configuration and management tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic VM Guest Patching">
  <data key="d0">Automatic VM Guest Patching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic VM guest patching provides timely rollout of critical patches and security patches for VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Compute Gallery">
  <data key="d0">Azure Compute Gallery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Compute Gallery enables automatic deployment of VM applications by defining them in a profile.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Compute Gallery is used to store and share golden images, supporting locally redundant and zone-redundant storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM Insights">
  <data key="d0">VM Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VM insights monitors health and performance of VMs and views trends from collected data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor Agent">
  <data key="d0">Monitor Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitor agent extension collects monitoring data from the guest OS using data collection rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Orchestration Mode">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Orchestration Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible orchestration mode spreads VM instances across fault domains and availability zones for high availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible orchestration mode allows managing VM instances at scale with options like spreading across fault domains and managing heterogeneous workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boot Diagnostics">
  <data key="d0">Boot Diagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Boot diagnostics is a feature for getting information as VMs boot and diagnosing boot failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Boot diagnostics provides information as VMs boot and diagnoses boot failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ac46b8199b0c3f4b8d2b71037af88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b386253cf68784da43f3bbb4fd519b</data>
