  <data key="d0">Virtual Machines Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual Machines baseline architecture is a foundational architecture demonstrating key recommendations for infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-612bbe95aa1cd140db2ec8a1f9529c91</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM SKUs">
  <data key="d0">VM SKUs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VM SKUs are approved virtual machine stock keeping units that ensure adherence to cost constraints and resource requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-612bbe95aa1cd140db2ec8a1f9529c91</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ephemeral OS Disks">
  <data key="d0">Ephemeral OS Disks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ephemeral OS disks localize disk access and avoid network hops, supporting state isolation and fault recovery for VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite Service-Level Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Composite Service-Level Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite SLOs are calculated based on Azure SLAs to set realistic expectations for VM performance and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-103d1a840787f3b63521ec34c09294d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Backup Instant Restore">
  <data key="d0">Azure Backup Instant Restore</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Backup Instant Restore is a backup capability for protecting VMs that cannot be easily rebuilt from IaC.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Backup Instant Restore is a feature for protecting VMs that cannot be easily rebuilt, using virtual machine snapshots in an Azure Recovery Services vault.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standby Pools">
  <data key="d0">Standby Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standby pools preallocate dormant instances ready to take over workloads during failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MaxSurge">
  <data key="d0">MaxSurge</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MaxSurge creates new instances in batches during upgrades, ensuring no downtime by deleting old instances after new ones are healthy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fault Domains">
  <data key="d0">Fault Domains</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fault domains isolate failures so that during maintenance, VM instances remain available in other domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault domains are logical groupings of resources within a stretched cluster that share a common physical fault domain, used to improve availability in failure scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Fault domains define how stretched clusters should respond in a failure scenario.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005140</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone Balancing">
  <data key="d0">Zone Balancing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone balancing equally spreads VM instances across availability zones to ensure sufficient instances remain if one zone goes down.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Lock">
  <data key="d0">Resource Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A ReadOnly resource lock prevents accidental stopping of always-on VMs through operator error in Azure portal or CLI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Repairs">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Repairs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic repairs on scale sets initiate recovery by replacing faulty instances when health endpoints report unhealthy status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b4044189e1ed4b14e738dc027893d75</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Recovery Services Vault">
  <data key="d0">Azure Recovery Services Vault</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Recovery Services vault stores virtual machine snapshots to implement RPO requirements for recovering disk state on faulted VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra Conditional Access">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra Conditional Access</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra Conditional Access restricts resource access based on conditions such as duration and minimum required permissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policies are configured by the platform team to help secure user access with multifactor authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004856</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Reservations">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Reservations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Capacity reservations reserve compute capacity within applicable SLAs with consumption-based billing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb860ff346987514c80ee21375c28eec</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spot Placement Score">
  <data key="d0">Spot Placement Score</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Spot Placement Score is a tool for making data-driven decisions about choosing the best regions and VM sizes to maximize availability and reduce capacity-related failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Spot Placement Score helps choose optimal regions and VM sizes to maximize availability and reduce capacity-related failures for Spot VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66547a86281f1ddd7468af1b4f756f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5</data>
