  <data key="d0">Azure Automation Start/Stop</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Automation Start/Stop is a low-cost automation feature for stopping VMs during off-hours to reduce idle instance costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Boost">
  <data key="d0">Azure Boost</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Boost offloads back-end virtualization processes to free up CPU resources for guest virtual machines, available only on specific VM sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52e7efe4d2287af32f723d20849c59c5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-machines.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
