  <data key="d2">Virtual Network Manager centrally manages connectivity based on rules, streamlining networking operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Network">
  <data key="d0">Hub Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hub network hosts shared services like Azure Firewall, ExpressRoute, and DNS, managed centrally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Network Manager IP Address Management">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Network Manager IP Address Management</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Network Manager IP address management provides centralized IP planning, visibility, and conflict detection across complex virtual network environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90098779392fd33c8719164d18403b49</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/service-guides/virtual-network.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003344</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Interface Cards">
  <data key="d0">Network Interface Cards</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Network interface cards (NICs) are Azure resources with SLA guarantees that connect virtual machines to virtual networks.</data>
