  <data key="d5">1777003798</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client Layer">
  <data key="d0">Client Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The client layer is the user interface layer where users experience intelligent capabilities, designed to be thin and delegate to other layers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Layer">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The intelligence layer handles routing, orchestration, and agent capabilities that coordinate AI operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inferencing Layer">
  <data key="d0">Inferencing Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The inferencing layer runs trained models to generate predictions or decisions based on data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Layer">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The knowledge layer provides grounding data, knowledge graphs, and retrieval services with data access policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tools Layer">
  <data key="d0">Tools Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The tools layer provides business APIs, external services, and action capabilities with standardized interfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inferencing Applications">
  <data key="d0">Inferencing Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inferencing applications perform single-step operations like classification, translation, or summarization with simpler architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence-Focused Applications">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence-Focused Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligence-focused applications involve more dynamic problem-solving capabilities beyond simple inferencing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI Gateway">
  <data key="d0">AI Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AI gateway provides authentication, quotas, safety, and routing between client and model serving layer.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI gateway provides authentication, quotas, safety, and routing between the client and the model serving layer in inferencing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;AI gateways provide gateway offloading, routing, and aggregation capabilities within workloads, addressing cross-cutting concerns like authentication, rate limiting, and model routing.&lt;SEP&gt;AI gateways provide gateway offloading, routing, and aggregation capabilities for policy enforcement in AI workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-24f18c621ebf65d4f1fbf92e2b662e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Layer Caching">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Layer Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-layer caching is a strategy to improve performance and reduce costs by caching at multiple levels of the application stack.&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-layer caching approach that implements caching at multiple levels of an application stack to improve performance and reduce costs in AI applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Result And Answer Caching">
  <data key="d0">Result And Answer Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching approach that reuses responses for identical or semantically similar queries to reduce model invocations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval And Grounding Snippet Caching">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval And Grounding Snippet Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching approach that caches frequently retrieved knowledge fragments and grounding data to avoid repeated database and search queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Output Caching">
  <data key="d0">Model Output Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching approach that caches intermediate model outputs for reuse across requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-To-Live Policies">
  <data key="d0">Time-To-Live Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TTL policies set appropriate expiration times for cached data based on data freshness requirements and content sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Orchestrator">
  <data key="d0">Orchestrator</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An orchestrator manages a workflow by coordinating communication among different components of an AI solution for predictable, compliance-driven, or performance-critical workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;The orchestrator is a code component that collects data from service calls for telemetry analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e4f16dff66fd138210770c89bf13e56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003632</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agent">
  <data key="d0">Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An agent wraps, extracts, and defines intelligent behavior in an application, providing context-bound functionality for multi-step reasoning, tool coordination, and adaptive behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Kernel">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Kernel</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Kernel is an orchestration framework that agents can work with.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Kernel is a custom hosting tool for AI orchestration.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft's Semantic Kernel is an agent framework used for orchestration with deterministic components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1840b694f5e40fc921e2e4772b238961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67c506626bcdefd4d8e43a813bed2c5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004003</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autogen">
  <data key="d0">Autogen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Autogen is an orchestration framework that agents can work with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Agent Framework">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Agent Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Agent Framework is an orchestration framework that agents can work with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Approaches">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Approaches</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid designs where orchestrators delegate specific subtasks to agents, combining structured workflows with flexible agent-based reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cache Invalidation">
  <data key="d0">Cache Invalidation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cache invalidation involves implementing triggers for data updates, model changes, and prompt modifications to ensure cached data remains current.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Leakage">
  <data key="d0">Data Leakage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data leakage is a security risk introduced by caching where cached data may be exposed to unauthorized users.&lt;SEP&gt;Data leakage occurs when future or label-derived information contaminates training data, potentially harming model performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agent State Persistence">
  <data key="d0">Agent State Persistence</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Agent state persistence is a design pattern for multi-turn conversations and long-running tasks where agents retain context across requests, sessions, or deployment cycles using durable storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e4237497869de86a9398c01400b4293</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Router">
  <data key="d0">Model Router</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model routers improve availability by routing requests to healthy models and can select the best model for a task, adding flexibility but introducing variability.&lt;SEP&gt;A model router is a component added to applications that routes requests between models, providing flexibility and cost optimization but adding non-deterministic behavior and complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event-Driven Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Event-Driven Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Event-driven architecture uses events to trigger actions, enabling decoupled components and real-time processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Event-driven architecture is a design pattern providing real-time responsiveness and efficient data processing for data-driven applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785e87e834f31a4dbca33b6d90c3cba1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Kernel SDK">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Kernel SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Kernel SDK is a software development kit that encourages microservices-based design where each agent or function is encapsulated within its own service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MCP">
  <data key="d0">MCP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP is a standard protocol used to wrap business capabilities as discoverable tool servers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OpenAPI">
  <data key="d0">OpenAPI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OpenAPI is a standardized interface format recommended for tools in AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;OpenAPI specifications are used to define tools for consistent interface documentation and validation with broad SDK support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c890e794024af9b99316b7007c076920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prompt Injection">
  <data key="d0">Prompt Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prompt injection is an attack that can manipulate AI behavior or extract sensitive information, requiring filtering and prevention safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-adaa1027480290045f9552546fffa81d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-design.md</data>
