  <data key="d0">Serve Layer APIs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serve layer APIs are production resources that require significantly more GPU-based compute power and larger container images than traditional APIs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Batch Inferencing">
  <data key="d0">Batch Inferencing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Batch inferencing is a method best hosted on platforms supporting transient usage where compute can be shut down when not in use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Inferencing">
  <data key="d0">Online Inferencing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Online inferencing is a method best hosted on platforms supporting elastic compute utilization that scales automatically based on load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traceability">
  <data key="d0">Traceability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Traceability is critical for maintaining model integrity, tracking version, deployer, deployment time, and data lineage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure OpenAI Batch API">
  <data key="d0">Azure OpenAI Batch API</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure OpenAI Batch API is recommended for batch inferencing of foundation models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noisy Neighbor Problem">
  <data key="d0">Noisy Neighbor Problem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The noisy neighbor problem affects serverless and PaaS services, leading to no throughput guarantees.&lt;SEP&gt;The noisy neighbor problem occurs when shared resources are excessively consumed by some tenants, degrading performance for others.&lt;SEP&gt;Noisy neighbor problems occur when shared resources cause performance issues between customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4040d041e59704b3306d1322e36844d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Framework AI Workload Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Framework AI Workload Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A review tool for self-assessing the readiness of AI workloads in production on Azure, organized around Well-Architected Framework pillars.</data>
