  <data key="d0">Baseline Microsoft Foundry Chat Reference Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A reference architecture describing design choices for a production-ready chat implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-48279cd8ae48ad0f168d69da13fbec3f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Search">
  <data key="d0">Vector Search</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vector search is a search capability that enables AI workloads to query vector data types for similarity-based retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;Vector search finds semantically similar data points using embeddings rather than exact keyword matches, essential for RAG and AI-driven workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Vector search is a search capability enabled by embeddings that allows semantic searches and comparisons of data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1615f9ff2ca4b3875210de37b97549d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19bad4c2dc835c16e4ab2cf4c0b9477</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/grounding-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ELT">
  <data key="d0">ELT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">ELT (Extract, Load, Transform) is a data pipeline method where transformation occurs after loading data into the target store.&lt;SEP&gt;ELT (Extract, Load, Transform) is a data processing method common for data lakes and big data tools.&lt;SEP&gt;ELT (Extract, Load, Transform) is a data processing pattern for data lakes where raw data is loaded first then transformed, often preferred for ML.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-714291704908e3bdade44c394b8075a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003554</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure AI Search">
  <data key="d0">Azure AI Search</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure AI Search supports enrichment pipelines during indexing, generating vector representations via embedding models and storing them in the index.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure AI Search is a Microsoft Platform as a Service (PaaS) offering used as a search index platform supporting vector search, filtering, and AI workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure AI Search is a Microsoft search service supporting vector search, semantic search, full-text search, multimodal data processing, automatic indexing, high availability, index aliasing, and document-level security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1615f9ff2ca4b3875210de37b97549d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Store">
  <data key="d0">Feature Store</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A feature store is an intermediate data layer that catalogs curated features with metadata such as lineage, generation time, and source for reuse across models.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature store is a centralized repository for maintaining "golden" training data that can be reused across multiple models or experiments, requiring proper access controls, encryption, and auditing.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature store contains features with predictive power, documented for AI workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature stores are centralized repositories for storing, managing, and serving engineered features for machine learning models, providing consistency across training and inference phases.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature store is a system for organizing, storing, and serving machine learning features, with recommendations to delete poor-performing features to reduce clutter and costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88acce1b2be2296ca1e97b9e9e3c8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572f3c246135d73811d52b8da63488e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96152a32ed0c284eafe7250fb96edb70</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EL">
  <data key="d0">EL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">EL (Extract and Load) is a data processing method used in RAG scenarios where documents are stored first and transformed later.&lt;SEP&gt;EL (Extract, Load) is a data processing pattern common in GenAI and RAG where documents are stored first and transformations happen downstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6717a8d0d4d23f93188603d15aa394ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Model Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model deployment is an approach where the model is trained using production data during development, requiring strong security controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Code Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Code deployment is an approach where the model is trained with non-production data and only uses real data once deployed to production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Inversion">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Inversion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Embedding inversion is a security risk where original text can be reconstructed from vector embeddings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0582c7a093b3909eeea812b8cd03ce7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
