<node id="Search Index">
  <data key="d0">Search Index</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A search index stores contextual or grounding data sent to a model's inference endpoint along with prompts, requiring low-latency real-time query support.&lt;SEP&gt;A search index stores contextual or grounding data sent to a model's inference endpoint, supporting real-time inferencing with high performance, vector search, filtering, and keyword indexing.&lt;SEP&gt;A search index is evaluated using metrics like query latency, throughput, and result accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;A search index is an externalized copy of data optimized for search and retrieval, used instead of querying directly from source systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A search index is an externalized data store used to make grounding data quickly searchable and retrievable rather than querying directly from source systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A search index is a data structure that organizes documents and fields to enable efficient querying, filtering, sorting, and retrieval of relevant information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c1615f9ff2ca4b3875210de37b97549d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49cbe51fefb78cfc1f460890101acf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e4f16dff66fd138210770c89bf13e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd17378f06c53d63988ae606c0c8070e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd21c65de17626ab06977604d71d47eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1743b32b112f4b0604908616e81188c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/grounding-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is an AI pattern that combines search index queries with model inference to generate grounded responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a method used to ground AI outputs in domain-specific data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c1615f9ff2ca4b3875210de37b97549d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd58a7646960270583df76ed6cf1f36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/ai-strategy.md</data>
