  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Decay">
  <data key="d0">Model Decay</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model Decay refers to the degradation of AI model performance and output quality over time, leading to inaccurate or irrelevant results. It occurs when models become stale due to changes in data, external factors, new use cases, or new data sources. This decline can manifest as data drift or concept drift, driven by both internal and external changes.

Model decay is a common challenge in AI systems, particularly when models trained on production data are not adequately monitored and retrained. Addressing model decay requires automated detection and mitigation strategies to maintain model reliability and accuracy over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Model decay refers to the degradation of model performance over time, which data maintenance aims to address.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcbc73fa5b3fca3e1f52909f50221d81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d7c0f28c3ae2bf90186c890ee840779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edb72d3cdc6179848ac635d4bf547fae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0144ba584fc445d0829602eb838085c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd01bdef0c5247574e6e62d31ab28944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140bb45f92c520fcbeae833dad674c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c727fd4aca5ba57377185d29c2a3ab2b</data>
