  <data key="d5">1777004002</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Training">
  <data key="d0">Model Training</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model training is the process of training AI models, with considerations for online and offline approaches affecting reliability and cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Model training involves selecting hyperparameters, temperatures, weights, and other parameters, with history documented to avoid repeating unsuccessful configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03df2eaa58b6c9bb42baf709c977fdda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572f3c246135d73811d52b8da63488e7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003850</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DataOps">
  <data key="d0">DataOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DataOps is an industry-proven methodology for data handling operations.&lt;SEP&gt;DataOps is a specialization of DevOps that focuses on managing the data lifecycle by streamlining ETL/ELT processes.&lt;SEP&gt;DataOps covers data aggregation, preprocessing, transformation, and normalization stages for training or enrichment purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;DataOps is a practice involving inner loop monitoring that measures proximity to acceptance quality bars and checks for anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;DataOps is the ingestion and preparation of data for AI workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d7c0f28c3ae2bf90186c890ee840779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e7187f5b4c0c71d8355bb2f3750ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f31ccebc2a168b87f30309e8394d245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f800b00991f43e7769f067d21a566bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a945886318d32ffa9cc3299a5304135e</data>
