  <data key="d5">1777003898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Drift">
  <data key="d0">Model Drift</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model drift is the deviation of model responses from expected results over time, requiring change management processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Model drift refers to the degradation of model performance over time, requiring change management processes for adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;Model drift occurs when a model's predictive power or relevance decays over time due to external changes such as shifts in user behavior or market dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d7c0f28c3ae2bf90186c890ee840779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f800b00991f43e7769f067d21a566bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad</data>
