<node id="Personas">
  <data key="d0">Personas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Personas represent subsets of humans and processes involved in the creation and operation of a workload, capturing roles, behaviors, and accountabilities. They are dynamic and goal-oriented, unlike static roles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-156d22032a6e46dc6dd3f14e97cd2338</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/personas.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003903</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agentic Personas">
  <data key="d0">Agentic Personas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agentic team roles requiring specialized persona management due to autonomous decision-making at runtime, unlike deterministic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-156d22032a6e46dc6dd3f14e97cd2338</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/personas.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003903</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Persona Permissions">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Persona Permissions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic persona permissions support flexible, workflow-aware access control including just-in-time provisioning and tool-specific access during different phases for agentic workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-156d22032a6e46dc6dd3f14e97cd2338</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/personas.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autonomous Agent Persona Accountability">
  <data key="d0">Autonomous Agent Persona Accountability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autonomous agent persona accountability involves maintaining clear accountability chains for agent decisions, including audit trails, human override capabilities, and escalation paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-156d22032a6e46dc6dd3f14e97cd2338</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/personas.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Azure Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Azure Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Azure Well-Architected Framework provides security principles focused on confidentiality and integrity for AI workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A framework providing best practices as a technical foundation for building and operating solutions on Azure, including sustainable workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09c7d548eca9b203ee2a91331881fe03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4458614e664da3e8fee92706ac5798b7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/responsible-ai.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-get-started.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Research Team">
  <data key="d0">Research Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The research team conducts risk discovery by consulting organizational guidelines, industry standards, laws, regulations, and known red-team tactics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09c7d548eca9b203ee2a91331881fe03</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/responsible-ai.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777003956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Policy Team">
  <data key="d0">Policy Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The policy team develops workload-specific policies incorporating guidelines from parent organizations and government regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09c7d548eca9b203ee2a91331881fe03</data>
