  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Machine Learning Model Monitoring provides automated monitoring by comparing real-time inference data with reference datasets to track drift and other performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30b28c47770b02897c940d0ac99d82ea</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004004</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concept Drift">
  <data key="d0">Concept Drift</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concept drift occurs when external conditions change, causing model predictions to no longer reflect reality.&lt;SEP&gt;Concept drift refers to changes in the underlying relationships that a model has learned, affecting model accuracy over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88dee01d0a30636bf4119d50523dfef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Feature Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature engineering involves data manipulation and reshaping source data, structured with good coding practices to support testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature engineering involves techniques like quality filtering, rescoping, deduplication, and standardized transformation to prepare predictive data for training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96152a32ed0c284eafe7250fb96edb70</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperparameter Testing">
  <data key="d0">Hyperparameter Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperparameter testing is an iterative process of tuning model parameters to meet accuracy goals, balancing accuracy with computational cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A/B Tests">
  <data key="d0">A/B Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A/B tests are used to evaluate new experiences and prevent quality regressions before full deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Live-Site Testing">
  <data key="d0">Live-Site Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Live-site testing extends functional testing into the live system, including scheduled tests for data volumes, duplicate detection, and data freshness validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL/ELT Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">ETL/ELT Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ETL/ELT pipelines are ingestion workflows tested end-to-end to ensure reliable data ingestion and high quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baselining Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Baselining Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A baselining strategy is applied during model training to measure and compare model quality using well-defined metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cff8026f25a4be62d5df6cf336623ae3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/test.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Foundation Model Fine-Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Foundation Model Fine-Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Foundation model fine-tuning adapts pre-trained model capabilities to specific domains or tasks using smaller but higher-quality training datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Domain-specific fine-tuning requires high-quality, task-relevant training examples representing specific patterns for the model to learn.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task-Specific Adaptation">
  <data key="d0">Task-Specific Adaptation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Task-specific adaptation focuses training data on particular capabilities or output formats such as structured outputs or specific instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Retention">
  <data key="d0">Data Retention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data retention involves decisions about keeping or deleting training data after model training, balancing retraining needs against storage costs and security concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Data retention involves planning policies for how long data is stored, balancing compliance needs with storage costs and management complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Data retention is a compliance consideration for SaaS solutions involving planning how long customer data is stored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Data Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data maintenance addresses model staleness over time through newer model adoption, trigger-based or routine retraining, data removal, and data retention strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Data maintenance involves copying data, building redundant pipelines, and running routine processes to address model decay and staleness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c727fd4aca5ba57377185d29c2a3ab2b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Mesh">
  <data key="d0">Data Mesh</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A data mesh is a data management approach that can streamline the adoption of new machine learning models alongside feature stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f1b29ba3c7b376f74d78cc48c0332ad</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/ai/training-data-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
