</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected SaaS Workload Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected SaaS Workload Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A review tool that independent software vendors can use to self-assess the readiness of their SaaS workload, providing technical recommendations and documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f8506bb4138ab3ab7a2de2f7558bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SaaS Workload Design Areas">
  <data key="d0">SaaS Workload Design Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Foundational design areas that help check design choices of a workload's architecture and operational approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f8506bb4138ab3ab7a2de2f7558bda4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Independent Software Vendors">
  <data key="d0">Independent Software Vendors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Independent software vendors (ISVs) are the target users of the Azure Well-Architected SaaS workload assessment for self-assessing their SaaS workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;ISVs are companies that build and sell software solutions, particularly SaaS products.&lt;SEP&gt;ISVs build and sell SaaS solutions to businesses (B2B) or consumers (B2C), hosting and maintaining their products.&lt;SEP&gt;Independent software vendors (ISVs) build and operate SaaS solutions for their customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f8506bb4138ab3ab7a2de2f7558bda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead72caffece10babff69d75d2a2b12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c62ba342ae2202ab7183c0dd367378f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b111334644545025473a63cd0bd3a289</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/incident-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Of Goods Sold">
  <data key="d0">Cost Of Goods Sold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">COGS is the direct cost of delivering a SaaS solution, often significantly composed of Azure spend.&lt;SEP&gt;COGS represents the costs associated with delivering SaaS, which vendors seek to reduce while scaling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-661923999882010b2c5bc9a8ccb33fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c62ba342ae2202ab7183c0dd367378f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/get-started.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tenancy Model">
  <data key="d0">Tenancy Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tenancy model defines how resources are deployed and shared across customers, affecting cost granularity.&lt;SEP&gt;The tenancy model determines whether resources are dedicated or shared among customers, affecting cost granularity.&lt;SEP&gt;A tenancy model determines resource sharing between customers in SaaS, ranging from single-tenant to fully multitenant models.&lt;SEP&gt;The tenancy model refers to the decision of how to host and segment database resources for customers in a SaaS solution.&lt;SEP&gt;The tenancy model determines how resources are shared or isolated among customers, balancing cost, management, and data isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;The tenancy model determines how customer lifecycle events are handled, ranging from fully multitenant shared resources to dedicated resources per customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-661923999882010b2c5bc9a8ccb33fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-720f5dd6d7dfc922834541dcd8b45b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead72caffece10babff69d75d2a2b12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7520ec32083d26a0b106d0af04f3ccd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/devops.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004394</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft AI Cloud Partner Program">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft AI Cloud Partner Program</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft AI Cloud Partner Program provides special subscriptions and credits for Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Service Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A service catalog lists specific Azure resources and resource SKUs that are part of an architecture, helping determine the total cost of a solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Points">
  <data key="d0">Scale Points</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale points are key metrics such as number of customers, users, and transactions that help forecast costs and plan for growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Dev/Test Pricing">
  <data key="d0">Azure Dev/Test Pricing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Dev/Test pricing offers reduced rates on certain Azure services for non-production use through separate dev/test subscriptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c288d93fcfdd99e1ec3771981b68f75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bin Packing">
  <data key="d0">Bin Packing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bin packing is an approach to share resources with limited capacity between customers in multitenant solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bin packing is a concept for understanding the capacity of each deployment stamp to determine when to deploy more.&lt;SEP&gt;Bin packing is a concept related to condensing tenants onto as few resources as possible for cost-effective scaling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-926d040bafb1c4ed2780ed2173357dfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b4c66eb667c03ba64de0007c8067a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/billing-cost-management.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stateless Workloads">
  <data key="d0">Stateless Workloads</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stateless workloads do not maintain session state, making it easier to run redundant copies in different locations for resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiregional Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Multiregional Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiregional architecture deploys applications across multiple regions to meet high uptime requirements and support geographically distributed users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Cost Of Ownership">
  <data key="d0">Total Cost Of Ownership</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Total cost of ownership (TCO) includes costs of operating a solution, crucial for planning pricing models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f6c3c95f26c867cee192fcc4d9d6f0e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/compute.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serverless Resource Model">
  <data key="d0">Serverless Resource Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serverless resource models automatically scale based on demand but may support fewer features and become cost-inefficient at scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DTU">
  <data key="d0">DTU</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Database throughput unit (DTU) is a synthetic resource consumption metric used in Azure SQL Database combining CPU, memory, storage, and IOPS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B2C">
  <data key="d0">B2C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business-to-consumer (B2C) solutions can store multiple customers' data in a single store with logical partitioning based on customer ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B2B">
  <data key="d0">B2B</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business-to-business (B2B) solutions that share components can use a single data store for specific parts while including customer IDs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004302</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscale Throughput">
  <data key="d0">Autoscale Throughput</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscale throughput allows dynamically adding or removing resources based on specified triggers in provisioned throughput models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc7b59ec61dfec2c82ddf6c12087f39d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SQL Database Advisor">
  <data key="d0">SQL Database Advisor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Database Advisor is a feature in Azure SQL Database that monitors for performance problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Tenant Data Leakage">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Tenant Data Leakage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-tenant data leakage is a security risk in multitenant environments where one tenant may access another tenant's data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47ab26c52b0edef6c01bfe85ba5744e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SaaS Solutions">
  <data key="d0">SaaS Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SaaS solutions are software-as-a-service offerings whose customers often have high expectations for availability and disaster recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Design">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Design</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active design with replication is the most resilient multiregion approach but is complex to build and requires conflict resolution for data synchronization delays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-passive architecture uses asynchronous data replication between regions for high resiliency but may result in some data loss during catastrophic outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Read-Only Replica">
  <data key="d0">Read-Only Replica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A read-only replica is a copy of a data store that can be provided to customers for direct access, reducing strain on production operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af77fdbd68a5283ca0d7625c8716f1b1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application-Tier Approach">
  <data key="d0">Application-Tier Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Application-tier approaches are methods for providing data access to customers through APIs, reports, or exports rather than direct database access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af77fdbd68a5283ca0d7625c8716f1b1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transactional Data Store">
  <data key="d0">Transactional Data Store</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transactional data stores are designed to support application operations with specific performance and access pattern needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-720f5dd6d7dfc922834541dcd8b45b10</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytical Data Store">
  <data key="d0">Analytical Data Store</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytical data stores are used for reporting and machine learning tasks, separate from transactional operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-720f5dd6d7dfc922834541dcd8b45b10</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/data.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Independent Software Vendor">
  <data key="d0">Independent Software Vendor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An independent software vendor (ISV) is responsible for managing customers' data in a SaaS context.</data>
