  <data key="d0">Scaling Plans</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Scaling plans in Virtual Desktop dynamically target host pool capacity based on schedules, manage load balancing behaviors by time of day, and handle user session lifecycle to balance experience, performance, and cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Scaling plans optimize host pool efficiency by adjusting capacity to match real-time demand, reducing unnecessary resource usage and improving cost management.&lt;SEP&gt;Scaling plans in Azure Virtual Desktop reduce costs by ensuring the correct number of session hosts are running when needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Scaling plans automatically adjust the number of VMs based on user demand and schedule to reduce costs and optimize resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762b78f72e74a93fafe604dbf5c648c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop Insights">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Desktop Insights captures scaling plan diagnostic logs and populates usage trends and operations data.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Desktop Insights is a dashboard built on Monitor workbooks that helps understand and configure monitoring for Azure Virtual Desktop environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Virtual Desktop Insights is a dashboard providing insights and visualizations for monitoring Azure Virtual Desktop environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5158a76c261c507648b548ec947486da</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004898</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Groups">
  <data key="d0">Application Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application groups in Azure Virtual Desktop manage and publish sets of applications or desktops to users, controlling access and organizing resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Desktop Application Groups">
  <data key="d0">Desktop Application Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Desktop application groups provide users access to a full Windows desktop from a session host, supported by both pooled and personal host pools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remoteapp Application Groups">
  <data key="d0">Remoteapp Application Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RemoteApp application groups provide users access to specific published applications, supported only by pooled host pools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breadth-First Load Balancing">
  <data key="d0">Breadth-First Load Balancing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Breadth-first load balancing distributes user sessions across session hosts by assigning users to the host with lowest usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Breadth-first load balancing spreads user sessions across available hosts, reducing impact if a session host goes offline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hibernation">
  <data key="d0">Hibernation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hibernation reduces VM startup delays and improves user experience while minimizing infrastructure costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Host Pools">
  <data key="d0">Host Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Host pools are collections of session hosts in Azure Virtual Desktop, including pooled and personal types.&lt;SEP&gt;Host pools are groupings of VMs in Azure Virtual Desktop that serve user sessions, configurable with different business continuity strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exclusion Tags">
  <data key="d0">Exclusion Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Exclusion tags are applied to faulty session hosts to prevent scaling plans from turning on unhealthy hosts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fc3321ebc08faa060fdaa8c0631ac64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004690</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSLogix">
  <data key="d0">FSLogix</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FSLogix is a profile management solution used with Azure Virtual Desktop that stores user profile data in pooled host pool environments. It requires optimal storage selection, as the distance between the host pool and storage location directly affects user experience. FSLogix profiles are hosted on Azure storage and can be monitored via operational and admin logs through Azure Storage solutions.

FSLogix provides a cloud cache feature that can sync and replicate user profiles across regions, supporting business continuity scenarios. The solution requires ongoing updates and management by the workload team to ensure proper functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;FSLogix is a profile management solution used in Azure Virtual Desktop, storing user profiles in VHD/VHDX files with specific IOPS requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;FSLogix is a component of Azure Virtual Desktop with its own release notes.&lt;SEP&gt;FSLogix is the recommended user profile solution for Azure Virtual Desktop, designed to roam profiles in remote computing environments using dynamically attached VHD and VHDX containers.&lt;SEP&gt;FSLogix is the recommended user profile solution for Azure Virtual Desktop, designed to roam profiles in remote computing environments using VHD and VHDX containers.&lt;SEP&gt;FSLogix provides profile container solutions for Azure Virtual Desktop, with storage considerations similar to App Attach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f5093839809e1ed5af9bc52a2f11883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113f1dee9dacbd713204570906b3c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-291c7f730b8dea7d3fc0379e8208d526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8759d38d5ccbdc62d8b354e52ff647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8542985fe4d9cc2800c19d4bee3d5e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db16efb77d945a638ed3a142b84cba38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb02bc2525ef384d46a37259cf6a9cf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b00f2a93a89bf2a6f52f33a9c1e0f13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785fcaaef274ecc977b30c815a92374a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Group">
  <data key="d0">Application Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application groups in Azure Virtual Desktop organize applications for user access, each linked to a single host pool.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Host Pool">
  <data key="d0">Host Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A host pool is a collection of session hosts (VMs) that serve user sessions, available in pooled and personal types.&lt;SEP&gt;A host pool is a collection of session hosts that serve virtual desktop or application sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;A host pool is a collection of VMs in Azure Virtual Desktop that serve as session hosts, subject to scaling limits and golden image updates.&lt;SEP&gt;A host pool is a collection of VMs in Azure Virtual Desktop that can be updated by deploying new VMs from golden images.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb02bc2525ef384d46a37259cf6a9cf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b00f2a93a89bf2a6f52f33a9c1e0f13</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session Host">
  <data key="d0">Session Host</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session hosts are VMs that serve user sessions in Azure Virtual Desktop, with performance affected by region, compute size, and storage.&lt;SEP&gt;A session host is a VM deployed within a host pool in Azure Virtual Desktop that serves user sessions and should be deployed in an availability zone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b00f2a93a89bf2a6f52f33a9c1e0f13</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/operations.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session Desktop">
  <data key="d0">Session Desktop</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session Desktop provides users with a full desktop environment with all applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RemoteApp">
  <data key="d0">RemoteApp</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RemoteApp delivers only required applications to users without a full desktop environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004691</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NV-Series">
  <data key="d0">NV-Series</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NV-series VMs are backed by NVIDIA Tesla M60 GPUs for graphics-intensive applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AVD Insights">
  <data key="d0">AVD Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AVD Insights is a monitoring solution for Azure Virtual Desktop that provides observability into VM health and operational stability.&lt;SEP&gt;AVD Insights is a monitoring tool used alongside Azure Log Analytics to track and monitor usage patterns of application groups in Azure Virtual Desktop.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004692</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NVIDIA Tesla M60">
  <data key="d0">NVIDIA Tesla M60</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NVIDIA Tesla M60 is a GPU that backs NV-series VMs for graphics-intensive workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Labels">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Labels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity labels are classifications assigned to application groups based on data type and business criticality to enforce appropriate access controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e6a367b5313dacf4139b0da89a311c1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breadth-First">
  <data key="d0">Breadth-First</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Breadth-first load balancing distributes user sessions across session hosts by assigning users to the host with the lowest usage, improving user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depth-First">
  <data key="d0">Depth-First</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Depth-first load balancing saturates one session host at a time before moving to others, ensuring efficient resource use and cost-effectiveness, especially in scale-down scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Host Pool">
  <data key="d0">Personal Host Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Personal host pools assign each user to a dedicated persistent VM, with fewer scaling considerations and focus on user experience and cost management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start VM On Connect">
  <data key="d0">Start VM On Connect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Start VM on Connect is a feature considered in personal host pool scaling strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b60d334dcab017475c35990888bb92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Host Pools">
  <data key="d0">Personal Host Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Personal host pools assign a user to a specific VM, maintaining application state over time with user profile data stored on the VM's OS disk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pooled Host Pools">
  <data key="d0">Pooled Host Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pooled host pools assign multiple users to various VMs, using FSLogix for profile data, providing communal remote experience at potentially lower cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004693</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Desktop Accelerator">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Desktop Accelerator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual Desktop Accelerator is a resource on GitHub for facilitating standardized AVD deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Windows 365">
  <data key="d0">Windows 365</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Windows 365 is a cloud-based desktop solution with fixed monthly cost and lower management overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depth-First Load Balancing">
  <data key="d0">Depth-First Load Balancing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Depth-first load balancing saturates one session host before assigning sessions to others, ensuring efficient resource use and cost-effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validation Host Pools">
  <data key="d0">Validation Host Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation host pools are used to test incoming AVD updates before broader rollout to ensure features are validated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b03bedb23d04a090f7869304a4613c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/application-delivery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop Workload Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop Workload Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A self-assessment review tool for checking the readiness and maturity of Azure Virtual Desktop workloads against best practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-988833b417b706271b5f65bb2ca513c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004724</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop Design Principles">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop Design Principles</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Virtual Desktop design principles are foundational design guidelines that form the basis of the assessment questions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-988833b417b706271b5f65bb2ca513c4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004725</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Gallery">
  <data key="d0">Compute Gallery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Compute Gallery is a regional resource used to store images, with recommendations to create secondary galleries for redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50815fe6bf25d27a5c4d85a90c7be6cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/business-continuity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777004753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Demand Capacity Reservation">
  <data key="d0">On-Demand Capacity Reservation</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">On-demand capacity reservation is an Azure feature that reserves compute capacity for disaster recovery scenarios, ensuring availability during regional outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e22de9abdb33acde406e3f7b3ab35a57</data>
