  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AD FS">
  <data key="d0">AD FS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS) is a federation service that can be used with hybrid identities but is not supported for certain Azure Virtual Desktop deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AD DS">
  <data key="d0">AD DS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) is a directory service for managing user identities that can be synced to Microsoft Entra ID.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub-Spoke Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Hub-Spoke Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hub-spoke architecture is a recommended network design that separates shared services from workload-specific resources for improved security.&lt;SEP&gt;Hub-spoke architecture separates shared services from workload-specific resources for improved security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6ef60fdfefa17516a41d6cfc052155</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud-Only Identity">
  <data key="d0">Cloud-Only Identity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cloud-only identity refers to users created and managed directly in Microsoft Entra ID for use with Microsoft Entra ID-joined VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c7f6d6f720349d226f2c7824d044fde</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005053</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region Selection">
  <data key="d0">Region Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Region selection is an important consideration when deploying Azure Virtual Desktop, affecting performance, latency, compliance, data residency, and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM And Disk Sizing">
  <data key="d0">VM And Disk Sizing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VM and disk sizing directly affects cost and end-user experience in Azure Virtual Desktop deployments, involving right-sizing VMs and selecting appropriate disk types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Virtual Desktop Metadata Store">
  <data key="d0">Azure Virtual Desktop Metadata Store</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The metadata store contains workspaces, host pools, app groups, and scaling plans, and is not always supported in the same region as session hosts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a87021e93b079d4a2aa659b18ba848</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MSIX">
  <data key="d0">MSIX</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MSIX is a container format used by App Attach to separate user data, the operating system, and apps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Universal Windows Platform">
  <data key="d0">Universal Windows Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Universal Windows Platform (UWP) is an app platform supported by App Attach.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed File System Namespace">
  <data key="d0">Distributed File System Namespace</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed File System (DFS) namespace is recommended to ensure App Attach file share paths are accessible in secondary failover locations for disaster recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84ef78f46fe9d8b133491676d4e97bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-virtual-desktop/storage.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vsan Stretched Cluster">
  <data key="d0">Vsan Stretched Cluster</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A vSAN stretched cluster spans across two availability zones to provide continuous availability during datacenter failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vsan Witness">
  <data key="d0">Vsan Witness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A vSAN witness resides in a third availability zone to support the stretched cluster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failure To Tolerate">
  <data key="d0">Failure To Tolerate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FTT policies control the number of failures a storage system can tolerate, affecting data resiliency and storage overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAID-1">
  <data key="d0">RAID-1</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RAID-1 is a storage layout used to tolerate at least one or more failures in the stretched cluster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005139</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure VMware Solution">
  <data key="d0">Azure VMware Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure VMware Solution is a Microsoft managed cloud service that enables organizations to migrate and run on-premises VMware vSphere workloads on Azure infrastructure, integrating VMware vSphere hypervisor with Azure dedicated BareMetal infrastructure. It provides a private cloud platform for hosting, deploying, and managing applications and workloads using virtual machines, including back-end APIs and applications, leveraging both VMware and Microsoft proprietary services.

The service offers comprehensive software-defined data center (SDDC) capabilities, including compute, storage, and networking, along with DNS and IP management features. It supports clustering and high availability through stretched cluster capabilities across availability zones. Azure VMware Solution integrates with various Azure services, VMware SDDC components, and monitoring tools, providing robust monitoring and security capabilities.

Infrastructure management encompasses backups, disaster recovery, operations management, incident response, and well-architected networking for connectivity, performance, and availability. The platform requires security measures for infrastructure, data, and applications, as well as tagging and compliance practices. It supports well-architected application design across reliability, security, cost optimization, performance efficiency, and operational excellence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85429190e4c4d18677d3b30fb9717ab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dad7224099dfb6b89e8724b6cc6f968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6209adb9655b3736e195cfd6bf95d4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32aeab96a805c5243f99de82ce31a9a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf05ce9803a3c657d2a88a0f28f474a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6302e71e0ce865b4ad1deecc215e545&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c45aa9611048afab38755ade22af2f4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15da9f5a57c9361e9e5487fa0eea82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35655a1a35d30fe6c5b864675c7afdb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfb7bf32559f95cd49b57ae0a4db207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd2f8bec9d3a589a0de1d0f5ecb5745&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/operations.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware Vsan">
  <data key="d0">VMware Vsan</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware vSAN is used with stretched clusters across availability zones for storage configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSAN is a storage solution providing datastore capabilities within Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ea85e904c2617bba6ba490ecb16f6e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Affinity Rules">
  <data key="d0">Affinity Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Affinity rules ensure VMs or groups of VMs are placed in separate hosts or fault domains to maximize availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Affinity and anti-affinity rules control VM placement across hosts for performance optimization, fault tolerance, and availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-passive configuration provides failover capability for critical application components during datacenter failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de655321a745d8c54849090ecd0165e8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM-VM Anti-Affinity Policies">
  <data key="d0">VM-VM Anti-Affinity Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM-VM anti-affinity policies prevent related VMs from being placed on the same host or fault domain to ensure redundancy and fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM-VM Affinity Policies">
  <data key="d0">VM-VM Affinity Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM-VM affinity rules place critical VMs in the same fault domain to ensure colocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VM-Host Affinity Policies">
  <data key="d0">VM-Host Affinity Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VM-host affinity policies ensure application tiers are deployed on the same host and within the same availability zone for performance isolation and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;VM-host affinity policies ensure application tiers are deployed on the same host and within the same availability zone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Tier Application">
  <data key="d0">Three-Tier Application</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A three-tier application architecture consisting of front-end web tier, business layer, and database layer, used as a use case for anti-affinity policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Performance Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance isolation is a requirement for resource-intensive workloads, achieved through VM-host affinity policies to dedicate specific hosts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6b0395ca88e97fa04e354f84b77afba</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005141</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware VSphere">
  <data key="d0">VMware VSphere</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware vSphere provides resource pools as an alternative solution for VM placement.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSphere is a virtualization platform providing features like resource allocation, VM templates, cloning, and dynamic resource allocation.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSphere is a hypervisor used in Azure VMware Solution for virtualization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfb7bf32559f95cd49b57ae0a4db207</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/overview.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stretched Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Stretched Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stretched clusters provide VMware clusters with high availability and disaster recovery capabilities across multiple geographically distributed datacenters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VSAN">
  <data key="d0">VSAN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virtual storage area network (vSAN) spans two datacenters in a stretched cluster setup and supports synchronous replication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TLS/SSL Termination">
  <data key="d0">TLS/SSL Termination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TLS/SSL termination offloads SSL processing from back-end VMs to Application Gateway to protect session data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005143</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VSAN Witness">
  <data key="d0">VSAN Witness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The vSAN witness resides in a third availability zone and serves as a quorum for split-brain scenarios in stretched cluster configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-108ead3dd7f225a59ab1119690c2ecfc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
