</node>
<node id="Software-Defined Datacenter">
  <data key="d0">Software-Defined Datacenter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The software-defined datacenter (SDDC) is a virtualized infrastructure approach used in Azure VMware Solution, with suppressed egress charges.&lt;SEP&gt;The software-defined datacenter (SDDC) is the environment within Azure VMware Solution where tier-1 routers provide routing capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6dad7224099dfb6b89e8724b6cc6f968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAID">
  <data key="d0">RAID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Redundant array of independent disks (RAID) is a fault-tolerant storage technology used to help ensure data integrity and availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Redundant array of independent disks (RAID) is a configuration that helps ensure data availability and protection against host and disk failures in vSAN storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6dad7224099dfb6b89e8724b6cc6f968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware Vrealize Operations">
  <data key="d0">VMware Vrealize Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware vRealize Operations is a tool used to benchmark environments and establish baseline performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PsPing">
  <data key="d0">PsPing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PsPing is a tool used for debugging and troubleshooting network performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SDDC">
  <data key="d0">SDDC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SDDC (Software-Defined Data Center) is the infrastructure environment where problems are identified, troubleshot, and fixed in Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Software-defined datacenter (SDDC) is the activation unit for Azure VMware Solution capacity including regions, nodes, and network settings.&lt;SEP&gt;SDDC (Software-Defined Data Center) is the environment where workloads run within Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Software-defined datacenter (SDDC) is a virtualized infrastructure unit in Azure VMware Solution across which traffic can be distributed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddb8ee34b6bdf35afe1e1325c627198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf05ce9803a3c657d2a88a0f28f474a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perfmon">
  <data key="d0">Perfmon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Perfmon is a performance monitoring utility used to establish baseline performance before migrating to Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iostat">
  <data key="d0">Iostat</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Iostat is a Linux utility used to establish baseline performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c67315c03619b3929955234658fb9266</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware SDDC">
  <data key="d0">VMware SDDC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware software-defined data center stack used for resilience, security, scalability, automation, and disaster recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware software-defined datacenter (SDDC) runs several VMware native components integrated with Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware ESXi">
  <data key="d0">VMware ESXi</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware ESXi is a hypervisor component of the VMware SDDC stack.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware ESXi is a hypervisor host used within Azure VMware Solution clusters to provide compute and local storage resources.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware ESXi hosts are infrastructure components managed by the platform team in Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware ESXi is a VMware solution component that generates logs collected by the VMware syslog service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32aeab96a805c5243f99de82ce31a9a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware VCenter Server">
  <data key="d0">VMware VCenter Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware vCenter Server is a management component of the VMware SDDC stack.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vCenter Server is a component managed by the platform team with administrative credentials in Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vCenter Server is a VMware solution component that generates logs collected by the VMware syslog service.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vCenter Server is a management platform for VMware environments with administrative accounts that require credential rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32aeab96a805c5243f99de82ce31a9a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/landing-zone-integration.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware NSX-T Data Center">
  <data key="d0">VMware NSX-T Data Center</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware NSX-T Data Center is a networking component of the VMware SDDC stack.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware NSX-T Data Center is a VMware solution component that generates logs collected by the VMware syslog service.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware NSX-T Data Center is used to create firewall rules and manage network segments for Azure VMware Solution workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware NSX-T Data Center is a networking and security platform used within Azure VMware Solution.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware NSX-T Data Center provides native micro-segmentation capabilities to restrict network communication between application components.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware NSX-T Data Center provides network segmentation, micro-segmentation, and distributed firewall capabilities for Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983e678073c39ad00690c826b108b77a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfb7bf32559f95cd49b57ae0a4db207&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88c271297891fe91c48171c10d75570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/monitoring.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VMware VSAN">
  <data key="d0">VMware VSAN</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VMware vSAN is a storage component of the VMware SDDC stack.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSAN is a distributed shared-storage infrastructure using local storage from ESXi hosts within an Azure VMware Solution cluster.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSAN is a VMware solution component that generates logs collected by the VMware syslog service.&lt;SEP&gt;VMware vSAN datastores can be encrypted with customer-managed keys to protect data at rest in Azure VMware Solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2316cc990e8eb48dc944c11d4a38990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da04e0b617f52da285d2c9c112bc493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2956238f945f53b269eebcd0c33b1c0f</data>
