  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scalable Design">
  <data key="d0">Scalable Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scalable design is a principle for sizing applications to handle peak workloads and operate with reduced functionality during outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failures To Tolerate">
  <data key="d0">Failures To Tolerate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failures to tolerate (FTT) is a level that determines desired resiliency for data protection in vSAN storage policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc9c17e8a9e3ca66742a781b355fe68c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/azure-vmware/infrastructure.md</data>
