  <data key="d0">Energy Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy Efficiency is a sustainability design principle established by the Green Software Foundation, focused on reducing unnecessary energy consumption in software systems and workloads. It emphasizes using the least amount of energy possible, minimizing energy waste in software applications. This principle is referenced in the context of workload optimization, guiding the design of greener, more sustainable software.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy efficiency is a sustainability design principle aligned with the Green Software Foundation.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy efficiency is a Green Software Foundation principle focused on reducing energy consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;A sustainability design principle aligned with the Green Software Foundation.&lt;SEP&gt;Energy efficiency is a sustainability design principle focused on reducing compute time and energy consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c191d35e97adae9dac9c5492df49a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0813e746db9803018f01837c963e4db3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b69de4dd949df6b1d5f8a06ccc255f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc7bbe0246f2fdb01b26dc432706f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca4d2bd438b809671ecf2d090095b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-776c12fee2375faef068c91c8f0e42d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d98ec414432be325b11ec7ac0d7f9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7b8a756934ab64251ea5a23e73f2de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66676114d38f71040fa212c5425b398e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hardware Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Hardware Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hardware Efficiency is a sustainability design principle established by the Green Software Foundation, focused on maximizing the utilization of existing and deployed hardware resources. The principle emphasizes optimizing hardware resource usage to reduce waste and improve overall sustainability. It also involves minimizing embodied carbon by supporting older devices and using the least amount of embodied carbon possible, thereby extending hardware lifecycles and reducing the environmental impact of manufacturing new equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hardware efficiency is a Green Software Foundation principle focused on minimizing hardware resource usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Hardware efficiency is a sustainability design principle focused on maximizing compute utilization and reducing idle resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0c191d35e97adae9dac9c5492df49a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b69de4dd949df6b1d5f8a06ccc255f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc7bbe0246f2fdb01b26dc432706f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca4d2bd438b809671ecf2d090095b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-776c12fee2375faef068c91c8f0e42d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a57afd24805552d7c2ea0ed4b6b7da2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7b8a756934ab64251ea5a23e73f2de</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-networking.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-storage.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Don't Repeat Yourself">
  <data key="d0">Don't Repeat Yourself</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DRY is an architectural principle that promotes reducing code duplication for efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server-Side Rendering">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Rendering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Server-side rendering processes UI on the server, beneficial when server power is cleaner or hardware is more efficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client-Side Rendering">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Rendering</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-side rendering pushes rendering responsibility to end-user devices, efficient when only rendering what's needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UX Design For Sustainability">
  <data key="d0">UX Design For Sustainability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">UX design for sustainability considers how design choices impact energy efficiency, network load, and compute resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Async Access Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Async Access Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Async access patterns involve queuing and buffering requests for batch processing to stabilize utilization and flatten consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dark Mode">
  <data key="d0">Dark Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dark mode is a UI feature with dark backgrounds that saves energy on displays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e29bd1c0f9b18d3b2102accfec264dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Native Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Native Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cloud-native design patterns are architectural patterns for building optimized cloud applications that reduce resource utilization and carbon emissions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sustainable Workload">
  <data key="d0">Sustainable Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A sustainable workload is an application design approach on Azure that considers climate impact and optimizes code and applications for sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;A sustainable workload is a cloud workload designed with considerations for reducing carbon emissions and improving energy and resource efficiency on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;A sustainable workload describes the practice of designing solutions that maximize utilization while minimizing waste, ultimately reducing the footprint on the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A sustainable workload on Azure incorporates security and sustainability principles to reduce carbon emissions and costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c764fb21384acf0511b788e916cf534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4458614e664da3e8fee92706ac5798b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-776c12fee2375faef068c91c8f0e42d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-get-started.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005716</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Code Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Code efficiency refers to optimizing application code to stabilize resource utilization and prevent unnecessary energy consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="API Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">API Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">API efficiency involves reducing chattiness, optimizing message encoding, and caching responses to minimize unnecessary load on systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777005502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backward Software Compatibility">
  <data key="d0">Backward Software Compatibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Backward software compatibility is the practice of supporting older browsers and operating systems to reuse existing hardware rather than requiring upgrades.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c722ba3139f83b2d92048e90bdfc365b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sustainability/sustainability-application-design.md</data>
