<node id="SAP Workload">
  <data key="d0">SAP Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP workloads are enterprise application workloads that place high demands on data platforms for performance, availability, and recoverability.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP workload refers to the computing and networking demands of SAP applications, requiring optimized networking for peak performance.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP workload refers to SAP systems running on Azure that require operational procedures, monitoring, and automation.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP workload refers to SAP application deployments on Azure that require reliability, security, cost optimization, performance efficiency, and operational excellence.&lt;SEP&gt;SAP workload refers to the deployment and operation of SAP applications, with best practices covering premigration to operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c634b3a2b27e4b06ab4fb93df82c41da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea3b54c45d951e732cca09b525690b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3990bf7b05c6dbb2810bbc7fcbbe492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d14511d72d14b9bf6ec7b7f61c0bc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277c3ba6003c8f8d8d862f28e5e221c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/networking-and-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-areas/operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/sap/get-started.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1777006074</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
