<node id="HPC">
  <data key="d0">HPC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-Performance Computing, a domain involving intensive computational workloads including data-intensive, compute-intensive, and hybrid scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;High Performance Computing workloads requiring efficient, scalable, reliable, and cost-aware design across compute, storage, networking, and job orchestration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f48d0d41fd8e386fc551c0a52af6a632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778fbb08fc2452f88b89df8ede476434</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/get-started-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/hpc/hpc-design-principles.md</data>
