<edge source="Azure" target="Availability Zones">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Availability Zones are a core infrastructure feature provided by Azure, consisting of isolated sets of datacenters within an Azure region. They deliver datacenter-level fault tolerance and resiliency by enabling zone-redundant configurations across nearly all Azure services. Azure regions support Availability Zones to enhance protection against datacenter failures, offering workload redundancy as a built-in resiliency capability. Availability Zones are also specifically recommended for scenarios such as SAP application server resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d9">fault tolerance,infrastructure,infrastructure component,infrastructure feature,infrastructure provision,platform capability,resiliency,resiliency infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7401b60ee469e374fd0c1ceb511518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e985b627cce63375e11a2952b871309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437b53743af22a4aaa11b22db9356761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7d5e1cf32da816941912bb8333b6c53</data>
