  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776995557</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reliability" target="Security">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reliability strategies such as replication and disaster recovery increase workload surface area, and incident response urgency may lead to security control bypasses, creating tradeoffs with security goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Security controls increase complexity and critical dependencies, creating tradeoffs with reliability goals including increased misconfiguration risk, disaster recovery complexity, and rate of change.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability strategies such as replication and disaster recovery increase workload surface area, and incident response urgency may lead to security control bypasses, creating tradeoffs with security goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Security controls increase complexity and critical dependencies, creating tradeoffs with reliability goals including increased misconfiguration risk, disaster recovery complexity, and rate of change.</data>
  <data key="d9">complexity,control bypass,dependencies,patching,surface area,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776996868</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reliability" target="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Cost Optimization and Reliability represents a fundamental tradeoff in system design. Increasing reliability often requires additional resources and investments that directly conflict with cost optimization goals. Reliability strategies such as replication, over-provisioning, and observability introduce redundancy and operational overhead that raise costs. Similarly, reliability requirements like monitoring, testing, on-call rotations, and support contracts incur significant additional expenses.

Conversely, cost optimization decisions can negatively impact reliability by reducing resiliency, limiting recovery strategies, and increasing system complexity. Organizations must carefully balance these competing priorities, making deliberate tradeoff decisions between minimizing costs and maintaining acceptable levels of reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">increased costs,operational investment,redundancy,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cb40dd3fd0df00b3000976f92afb432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f818319705988a5625ea0e36f168cb</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1777004361</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reliability" target="Operational Excellence">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reliability increases workload complexity, which increases operational elements and complicates monitoring, tracing, and documentation efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Excellence practices can increase complexity and destabilizing activities, creating tradeoffs with Reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability increases workload complexity, which increases operational elements and complicates monitoring, tracing, and documentation efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Excellence practices can increase complexity and destabilizing activities, creating tradeoffs with Reliability.</data>
  <data key="d9">complexity,increased complexity,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776998151</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reliability" target="Performance Efficiency">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reliability patterns like replication and resource balancing introduce latency and over-provisioning that counter performance efficiency goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance efficiency decisions such as reduced replication, increased density, and increased complexity can negatively impact reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability patterns like replication and resource balancing introduce latency and over-provisioning that counter performance efficiency goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance efficiency decisions such as reduced replication, increased density, and increased complexity can negatively impact reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication for reliability can lead to higher latency and lower throughput, trading off performance efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d9">increased latency,over-provisioning,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cb40dd3fd0df00b3000976f92afb432</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1777004362</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Reliability" target="Data Replication">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Data replication is a reliability pattern used to survive replica malfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Data replication is a reliability pattern used to survive replica malfunction.</data>
