<edge source="Performance Efficiency" target="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cost Optimization and Performance Efficiency share a complex relationship characterized by both synergies and tradeoffs. Cost Optimization often improves Performance Efficiency, as reducing waste and streamlining resources can lead to better-performing systems. However, cost-saving measures can also hinder performance targets and ongoing performance optimization, creating tensions that must be carefully managed.

Key tradeoffs between Cost Optimization and Performance Efficiency arise around supply-demand balance, component count, and investment alignment. In areas such as database management and workload design, balancing cost with performance involves specific trade-off decisions, including index design and table partitioning. Achieving the right balance requires deliberate evaluation of where cost reductions support performance goals and where they may compromise them.</data>
  <data key="d9">alignment,optimization,trade-off,tradeoff</data>
