<edge source="Security" target="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Cost Optimization and Security represents a fundamental tradeoff in system design. Security measures increase costs through premium SKUs, additional infrastructure, log storage, resource consumption, and operational processes. Conversely, pursuing cost optimization can lead to reduced security controls, weakening overall security posture. Designing and operating secure solutions can be expensive, requiring organizations to balance reliability and security investments against business requirements and cost efficiency goals.</data>
  <data key="d9">additional infrastructure,design tradeoffs,increased costs,increased demand,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f818319705988a5625ea0e36f168cb</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/saas/design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1777004367</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Security" target="Replication">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Replication increases the workload surface area, which conflicts with the security goal of minimizing attack vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Replication increases the workload surface area, which conflicts with the security goal of minimizing attack vectors.</data>
  <data key="d9">surface area increase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776996076</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Security" target="Disaster Recovery">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Disaster recovery solutions increase surface area and require implementation of additional security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Security controls affect recovery time objectives and must be included in disaster recovery plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery solutions increase surface area and require implementation of additional security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Security controls affect recovery time objectives and must be included in disaster recovery plans.</data>
